window.RSI_DATA={"updated_at":"2026-10-20 10:41 CST","papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25906","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25906v1","title":"An Analysis of Semantic and Spatio-Temporal Co-evolution for Edge Classification on Dynamic Text-Attributed Graphs","authors":"Tyler Bonnet; Marek Rei","affiliations":"","abstract":"Dynamic edge classification on text-attributed Web graphs, such as review networks, community forums, and news-derived knowledge graphs, requires high quality, adaptive semantic representations in the context of network evolution. Existing dynamic graph architectures typically initialize text feature vectors with pretrained language models and hold them static during training to preserve their semantic structure, forgoing the potential benefits of allowing them to co-evolve with network topology. In this work, we investigate the effects of enabling such co-evolution with a unified text-graph alignment framework that integrates a lightweight Transformer adapter to update token-level text representations via spatio-temporal gradients from a contrastive pretraining objective. To prevent detrimental semantic distortion, a language model maintenance objective anchors the evolving text embeddings to their original semantic structure. Evaluations on the Dynamic Text-Attributed Graph Benchmark demonstrate that this anchored text-graph co-evolution consistently improves upon the edge classification performance of frozen-text baselines across diverse Web-related domains. Representational analyses reveal that the framework reduces anisotropy, improving the linear separability of text embeddings, and effectively encodes structural and temporal information into the semantic space. A computational efficiency analysis confirms that this beneficial semantic and spatio-temporal co-evolution is achieved without incurring the prohibitive computational overhead typical of end-to-end joint training.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25858","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25858v1","title":"Are Self-Evolving Agents Continual Learners?","authors":"Xiaoyin Chen; Yizheng Huang; Yinglun Xu; Ziyun Zhao; Emmett McQuinn; Julie Liu; Hope Yao","affiliations":"","abstract":"Large language model agents are often deployed in environments where new knowledge, tools, and workflows keep arriving. Such an agent is therefore expected to adapt continually, learning new tasks as they arrive without forgetting earlier ones. This resembles the continual learning problem, but at a pace that conventional gradient updates cannot sustain. Nonparametric self-evolving agents are a natural alternative: they adapt by rewriting their own harness, such as prompts, memory, and skills, from task feedback while the model weights stay frozen. We study whether such agents are effective continual learners across four drifting task streams that shift in topic, workflow, or domain (built from BIRD, BFCL, and ScienceWorld). Evaluating three representative methods spanning experience retrieval and self-modification (ReasoningBank, GEPA, and Meta-Harness), we find that although self-evolution improves aggregate performance on most streams, higher plasticity consistently comes at the cost of stability. Specifically, self-modifying methods apply global edits to a shared prompt or workspace, interfering with unseen tasks and overwriting earlier knowledge as the stream shifts. Conversely, similarity-based memory retrieval localizes updates across distant domains, but still retrieves foreign memories on unseen tasks and suffers from retrieval collision when similar queries require conflicting workflows. These findings show that current self-evolving agents remain incomplete continual learners.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25847","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25847v1","title":"ACE-Trader: Adversarial Co-Evolution for Generator-Critic Trading Systems","authors":"Chang Zhou; Jiarun Zhou; Xingtong Yu; Hong Cheng; Hui Zhang; Xinming Zhang","affiliations":"","abstract":"Generator--critic trading systems pair an LLM-based trader that makes trading decisions with a red team agent that evaluates these decisions and provides feedback for revision. However, improving individual trading decisions does not ensure that both agents learn from experience and improve together over time. This raises an important question: how can the trader and red-Team select useful experience and learn from each other's evolving behavior? On one hand, experience that benefits decisions under one market condition may become ineffective or harmful under another. On the other hand, trading outcomes reflect both agents' actions, making it difficult to derive appropriate experience for each role. In this work, we propose ACE-Trader, an adversarial co-evolution trading framework. Specifically, we first develop separate context-dependent memory selectors that learn to identify useful experience for the current trading decision. Both selectors receive shared feedback from net-return differences between complete memory-assisted and memory-free trading pipelines, with online updates emphasizing recent outcomes. We further design a co-evolution mechanism that links role-specific memories through shared trading records. We use these records to evaluate the Red-Team's risk assessments and the effects of the Trader's revisions against realized market outcomes, then derive experience for their respective memories. By linking this experience to the corresponding records, we enable the Trader to improve its proposals based on prior critiques and the Red-Team to adjust its review focus as the Trader's behavior changes. Experiments on U.S. stock trading show that ACE-Trader outperforms all 22 active baselines in cumulative return and achieves the highest Sharpe ratio and lowest maximum drawdown across both active methods and passive benchmarks.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-19","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25119","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25119v1","title":"Memory as Belief: Bayesian Evolution of Memory for Self-Evolving LLM Agents","authors":"Yiming Xu; Qian Yang; Zihan Chen; Yuefei Wu; Wenhan Zeng; Bin Shi; Bo Dong","affiliations":"","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents increasingly rely on external memory to accumulate past experiences for continual adaptation. However, effectively reusing memory requires accurately assessing its value, as retrieved experiences may become unreliable when transferred across task contexts. Despite its importance, memory valuation remains largely underexplored, with existing methods relying on historical retrieval success rates that overlook the context dependency of memory usefulness and the varying reliability of estimates under different amounts of evidence. Inspired by the Bayesian brain hypothesis, we propose BEAM (Bayesian-style Evolutionary Agentic Memory), a framework that reformulates memory value evaluation as a parameterized cognitive inference process, where memory value is represented as a context-conditioned dynamic belief rather than a passive historical statistic. Specifically, BEAM infers memory value beliefs from current task contexts and continuously calibrates them using execution feedback as empirical evidence, transforming memory from passive storage into an adaptive cognitive mechanism for continual self-evolution. Extensive experiments across reasoning and code generation benchmarks demonstrate that BEAM consistently improves memory utilization and enables continual self-evolution of LLM agents.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25114","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25114v1","title":"Compile Once, Run Cheap: Frozen, Portable Skills for Embodied Agents, and What Recursive Self-Improvement Adds","authors":"Jingwen Bai; Guochao Bai; Canbo Zhang; Shuangqi Li; Minchao Hu; Weichun Huang; Shuang Liu","affiliations":"","abstract":"Embodied AI lacks the data-rich pretraining that gave language models their agents and skills, so new manipulation capability costs demonstrations per task or a frontier model in every episode. We study a third route: a strong general model acts only as an offline author that writes, runs, diagnoses and repairs a manipulation skill in simulation until it passes an exam on layouts drawn after freezing; the frozen skill then runs as code alone or under a cheap caller that reads only its description. We call this skill-level recursive self-improvement Skill-RSI and specify a compile protocol (isolated, audited author; hidden validation layouts; no-feedback and inherit-only controls; tamper-evident ledger) and a reuse protocol that runs the identical files with executors from another model family. On 7 RoboTwin 2.0 tasks with cluttered tables, Claude Code compiled 4 tasks into 7 frozen skills, 5 from a first draft needing only qualification, at USD 4.29-8.22 of author cost each (USD 55 per skill counting the 13 failed campaigns). The other three tasks did not compile in 18 campaigns, including five with GPT-6 and a pre-registered 150-layout run: on the hardest task every campaign scored 78-95 of 100 but had 3-16 safety aborts, failing the gate of 95% success with zero aborts; a 100-episode exam bounds an abort rate only to 3.6%. On hidden layouts, repair that inherits the previous version beat from-scratch rewriting in 8 of 8 controlled campaigns (sign test p = 0.004); an inherit-only lineage attributes most of the gap to inheritance, with development feedback adding a little (3 of 3, p = 0.125). Write-once campaigns found no detectable first-draft effect of practice (minimum detectable effect 14 points). The frozen skills kept 148/150 successes on new layouts with no model and 147/150 with a DeepSeek-flash caller at USD 0.00028-0.00054 per episode; no direct-control baseline was run.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25078","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25078v1","title":"CoEvo-RSI: When Harnesses Evolve, Which Models Should Follow?","authors":"Jiaqi Su; Guibin Zhang; Jie-Jing Shao; Cong Pang; Tiankuo Yao; Ivor Tsang; Haiyan Yin; Shuicheng Yan","affiliations":"","abstract":"Model--harness co-evolution has emerged as a prominent paradigm for recursive self-improving (RSI) agents, jointly evolving their execution scaffolds and intrinsic capabilities. We study the persistent yet often overlooked brain--body mismatch problem in this paradigm, where an evolving harness (body) demands behaviors its model (brain) has not learned or restricts capabilities it already possesses. We introduce CoEvo-RSI, a RSI framework that advances model--harness co-evolution through agent-driven, bidirectional historical inheritance. Drawing on a shared evolutionary archive and execution feedback, a meta-agent coordinates harness development from historical designs with model checkpoint selection or merging and subsequent adaptation under the selected harness, aligning inherited capabilities with evolving execution requirements to reduce brain--body mismatch. Using only supervised fine-tuning (SFT) on its own rejection-sampled trajectories, CoEvo-RSI makes Qwen3.5-9B competitive with larger models across diverse vertical applications, including multi-agent failure attribution, role-aware text-to-SQL, and smart-home instruction following. It surpasses DeepSeek-V4-Pro on TraceElephant (+14.16 agent accuracy) and GLM-5.3 on HomeBench VM (+4.90 success rate), underscoring the need for brain--body alignment and the potential of bidirectional historical inheritance to advance agent co-evolution.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.25012","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.25012v1","title":"Conjugate Compilation: Self-Improving Agentic Co-Compilation for Speculative Decoding","authors":"Annabelle Sujun Tang; Rohan Mahapatra; Christopher Priebe; Hanyang Xu; Manya Ghobadi; Christopher Rossbach; Hadi Esmaeilzadeh","affiliations":"","abstract":"As LLM adoption surges, scaling model serving requires unlocking stranded GPU capacity alongside deploying more GPUs. Speculative decoding brings two models into the serving process: a small draft model proposes tokens that a larger target model verifies. Yet compiling these models individually leaves their shared execution outside the compiler's optimization boundary. We introduce CONJUGATE COMPILATION, which reframes speculative decoding as a cross-model compilation problem and jointly optimizes the draft and target models within their shared execution rather than treating each in isolation. Our key insight is that cross-model compilation should be informed by the measured performance of the co-located shared execution it produces: an optimization that improves a kernel in isolation need not improve the models when they execute together. To expand cross-model opportunities, we devise operand layouts that interleave blocks from both models within common tiles, co-locating GEMM and non-GEMM work while preserving their mathematics. We realize CONJUGATE COMPILATION through a self-improving agentic search system in which an LLM edits cross-model optimization plans using the compiler and GPU execution as its environment. Each proposed plan is compiled and evaluated through its co-located shared execution, whose measured score, together with kernel-level verdicts and compiler feedback, informs subsequent proposals, while Monte Carlo tree search accumulates rewards to guide exploration. Across six single-GPU speculative-decoding configurations on NVIDIA B300 and RTX 5090 GPUs, CONJUGATE COMPILATION achieves a geometric-mean per-round speedup of 1.37x over conventional execution. Interleaved kernels raise this speedup to 1.45x, reaching 1.59x in the best case. CONJUGATE COMPILATION also improves GPU utilization on average by 1.46x on RTX 5090 and 1.50x on B300.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24944","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24944v1","title":"Epi: Towards a Persistent, Self-Improving Agent for Autonomous Research","authors":"Yue Huang; Zhangchen Xu; Xiaonan Luo; Zheyuan Liu; Lichi Li; Yiping Wang; Peiyang Song; Eric Gabriel Ramos; Enze Xie; Olexandr Isayev; Paul Liang; Nouha Dziri; Huan Sun; Jianfeng Gao; Ying Liu; Misha Sra; Xiangliang Zhang; Alex Pentland; Zichen Chen","affiliations":"","abstract":"We present Épi, an autonomous research agent that sustains investigations across model sessions and evolves its methods through accumulated experience. Épi combines persistent research history, hierarchical memory, branching and independent review to maintain research continuity, learn from experiments, and explore and revisit alternative approaches. Its experiments run across session boundaries, and a fixed verifier evaluates their outputs. Épi produced 120 record-setting results, comprising 20 numerical bound records across 12 families and 100 construction records across eight families. These include an approximately 84-fold narrower interval for the $n$-queens constant and a more than 3.6-million-fold narrower rigorous interval for the quartic Feigenbaum attractor dimension. Exact dual certificates establish that the Cohn-Elkies linear-programming bound cannot be sharp in dimensions 10 and 11. Beyond numerical improvements, Épi gives a computer-assisted proof of Tuza's conjecture for split graphs with an eight-vertex clique part and at most three triangle-active neighborhood types, with arbitrary multiplicities. We extend this research process to algorithmic coding with Épi-turbo, a lightweight configuration that develops executable solvers for tasks including vehicle routing, scheduling and production planning. On 30 FrontierOR tasks, Épi-turbo achieves a 5.4% higher total benchmark score than Codex at 64% of its model cost, using the same underlying model and reasoning effort. Épi is designed to support human understanding by connecting computational results to explicit methods and mathematical arguments that researchers can examine and build upon.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-18","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24896","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24896v1","title":"Peer Pressure: Execution-Verified Co-Evolution of Attacker and Defender Populations for Code Security","authors":"Khushbu Pahwa; Yubin Ge; Daniele Bonadiman; Xiaofei Ma; Yi Zhang","affiliations":"","abstract":"LLM code agents increasingly ship code with little oversight, yet defenders trained on static vulnerability datasets fall behind adapting adversaries. We co-train attacker and defender instead, and let execution decide every reward: an attacker (Red) edits a real repository and earns nothing unless its patch applies, builds, passes the tests, completes its development task and reproduces a real exploit in an isolated container, whose path also labels the entry point, the critical operation and the trace between them. Peer-Relative Policy Optimization (PRPO) makes both sides populations of LoRA adapters over one frozen base and credits each against same-role peers that faced an identical condition, placing the population inside the policy-gradient baseline rather than the opponent pool, with a tournament preserving diversity. Matching cancels the condition's difficulty: at equal coverage it is worth 2.3 points of balanced accuracy over a baseline computed on other conditions, and it matches a within-policy control at half the verifier spend. PRPO's 7B diff reviewer reaches 64.8% balanced accuracy on four unseen applications in three untrained languages, 5.5 points above supervised security fine-tuning and 4.4 above a frozen frontier reviewer (Claude Opus 4.8), which it leads by 15.8 on the application it trains on. Its 9B repository agent recovers 23 of 172 held-out VulnGym advisories, against 10 after supervised fine-tuning and 7 for the same backbone untrained under the same scaffold, and locates 17 of 43 reachable entry points against 13 for mini-swe-agent with GLM-5.2. Run unchanged on jailbreak defense, the same algorithm matches or exceeds WildGuard's static F1 at equal corpus and model size. Under a judge distinct from its training oracle it cuts attack success from 36.0% to 4.6%, against WildGuard's 8.9%.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24630","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24630v1","title":"Selm: Self-Evolving Library Management for Multi-Skill Agent Optimization","authors":"Mengxi Hu; Yuxuan Hu; Jinbo Su; Ke Wang; Honghao Shi; Wenli Wu; Cuiping Li; Hong Chen; Jing Zhang","affiliations":"","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents increasingly use skills as a lightweight way to acquire task-specific knowledge. Recent work enables skills to evolve from task trajectories. However, these methods often lack systematic management of evolved skills, making it difficult for agents to reuse and accumulate skills across domains, thus limiting performance on subsequent tasks.To reliably accumulate, reuse, and maintain useful skills across tasks, we present SELM (Self-Evolving Library Management), a framework that formulates skill evolution as library-level management. SELM jointly manages skill retrieval, updating, and lifecycle by maintaining skill confidence and utility signals. It introduces utility-aware retrieval to select useful skills, a Map-Reduce framework to generate targeted updates from task-specific experience, and lifecycle controls to retain or remove skills based on their effectiveness. These mechanisms enable the skill library to continuously accumulate useful experience while preserving and pruning skills across tasks, improving agent performance on complex tasks across diverse domains. We evaluate SELM on four agent benchmarks covering diverse tasks and execution environments, and SELM consistently outperforms in most settings.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24464","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24464v1","title":"Learning to Compose: Recursive Self-Improvement of Shared Executable Stacks for Zero-Shot Long-Horizon Robot Manipulation","authors":"Yangzhi Chen; Feiran Liu; Zishuo Wang; Zijian Jin; Xin Zhu; Lecheng Ruan; Wenjuan Han","affiliations":"","abstract":"Individually competent robot skills can fail when composed: tools may lack a required capability, completion signals may misrepresent physical progress, and one skill may leave a state that violates its successor's prerequisites. We introduce Recursia, a recursive self-improvement framework that treats the shared executable stack, rather than individual task programs, as the persistent unit of improvement. The stack integrates tools, skills with execution contracts, handoffs, and verifiers. Source-side execution traces guide failure attribution and the generation of missing tools or repairs to existing shared components. Generality checks, mechanism tests, and paired selection and regression gates determine which changes become the next parent. The resulting stack is frozen and reused through declarative task adapters, allowing source-derived changes to support new compositions without target-side code repair. Experiments cover LIBERO-Pro Long simulation and a physical Franka FR3 equipped with a Franka Hand. In simulation, Recursia improves success over ASPIRE by 5.8 percentage points under Pos perturbations and 15.1 points under Task perturbations. Across three physical compositional target tasks, it improves mean success over the Skill Document Only baseline by 40 percentage points. Analyses of constituent execution, candidate rejection, and inference drivers distinguish local mechanism improvements from complete task success and characterize the cost of feedback-conditioned orchestration. These results examine shared executable interfaces as a concrete mechanism for compositional transfer in robot programming.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24454","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24454v1","title":"MELD: Recursive Self-Improvement via Hierarchical Coordination for Multi-Agent Scientific Discovery","authors":"Sizhe Tang; Zuyuan Zhang; Zeyu Fang; Tian Lan","affiliations":"","abstract":"Multi-agent scientific discovery with large language models raises a coupled learning problem: research assignments determine both which experiments are pursued and the experiences from which agents adapt. We introduce MELD, a unified hierarchical test-time training framework that jointly adapts a team-level Coordinator policy and agent-level individual Scientist policies within a single discovery process. The Coordinator generates a joint portfolio of search branches and research directives over a shared derivation tree, while Scientists develop hypotheses and execution plans implemented by a shared frozen Executor. Both levels receive alternating GRPO-style parameter updates under a shared smooth best-of-budget objective, allowing team organization and individual research behavior to co-evolve in a recursive self-improvement loop. Our analysis establishes objective alignment for the hierarchy, characterizes conditions for coordination gains over independent parallel discovery and the first-order benefit of private adaptation, and derives a finite-budget regret bound for adapted models. On 22 MLGym and MLE-bench tasks, MELD is best on 20 of them and achieves the highest aggregate normalized scores on MLGym, using a 4B backbone for coordination and research. Most baselines use proprietary Scientists, and all systems share one frozen Executor.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24453","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24453v1","title":"Hippo: Training-Free Agent Self-Evolution via Hippocampal Replay","authors":"Yutong Song; Jiang Wu; Yuxuan Ren; Tony Qin; Baoyuan Wang","affiliations":"","abstract":"Motivated by recursive self-improvement (RSI), we study how LLM agents can learn through external memory without updating model parameters. Extracting useful experience from a single attempt is difficult: flawed reasoning can produce success, while poor execution can obscure a sound strategy. Preserving its value over time is also difficult: our accumulation baseline without consolidation initially improves but eventually performs below a no-memory baseline. Our key idea is to compare attempts at the same task to identify reusable decisions and refine when they apply. We introduce Hippo, a memory framework inspired by selective hippocampal encoding and replay that learns from these comparisons when shortcomings are diagnosed. It compares the resulting experience with existing memory to merge overlaps and resolve conflicts through explicit applicability conditions. This allows prior guidance to be revised without storing every lesson as a separate entry. Experiments on SWE-bench Verified, WebArena, and Mind2Web show performance gains in all three settings and substantially fewer retained experiences than the accumulation baseline. The gains extend across the evaluated base models of varying capabilities, indicating that memory-based adaptation remains useful even for highly capable models.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-17","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.24177","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.24177v1","title":"Self-Improving Video-to-Action Models","authors":"Hyunwoo Ryu; Eric Ming Chen; Max Wilcoxson; Vincent Sitzmann","affiliations":"","abstract":"Video generative models are an emerging tool for embodied agents: they can serve as scalable visual planners, generating videos that depict how to complete previously unseen tasks. However, executing these plans typically requires a video-to-action or \"inverse dynamics\" model trained on large, human-collected video-action datasets, severely limiting scalability. We introduce Mirror, a self-supervised approach that learns video-to-action mappings through environment interactions, without prior action data or hand-crafted rewards. Mirror learns by attempting to follow a visual plan by executing its best guess of the underlying actions in the environment. Mirror then trains on the resulting video-action pairs, incrementally self-improving and following the visual planner more closely. Across Atari, OGBench, and DeepMind Control, Mirror outperforms leading learning-from-observation methods with learned video plans, and achieves near-expert performance with oracle plans. On Minecraft BASALT, it outperforms methods with access to expert actions or hand-engineered task knowledge. In Minecraft survival, it is the first method to acquire an iron pickaxe through self-improvement alone, without rewards or expert action labels. In the offline setting, with expert action labels but no environment interaction, it sets a new state of the art in obtaining diamonds. Our results suggest that advances in video models can translate into increasingly capable agents without a corresponding need for hand-crafted rewards or large collections of expert action data.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-20"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23599","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23599v1","title":"From Trajectories to Differentiated Skills: Cognitive Differentiation for Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Yewei Zhao; Derong Xu; Wei Chen; Yin Xu; Peilun Zhou; Xiaohan Wang; Guojun Yin; Wei Lin; Mingjun Xiao","affiliations":"University of Science and Technology of China；Meituan；City University of Hong Kong","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents tackle complex tasks through reasoning and interaction with external environments. Agent skills provide persistent, transferable capabilities that guide task planning, inform contextual decisions, support tool use, and enable executable procedures. Yet existing skill-evolution methods largely organize knowledge around skill artifacts, overlooking the functional heterogeneity within individual skills and its implications for knowledge maintenance and use. Inspired by cognitive science, we propose Cognitive Differentiation in Skill Evolution (CDSE), which evolves a unified skill through four functionally distinct yet coordinated components: Meta, Experience, Tool, and Script. CDSE extracts evidence-grounded semantic gradients from successful and failed trajectories, consolidates them by functional role, and applies component-specific updates and validation with cross-component coordination and adaptive invocation. An analysis of 500 top-ranked skill packages shows that 96.8% contain knowledge spanning at least two functional roles. Across six benchmarks, three agent models, and two execution harnesses, CDSE achieves the highest scores in all 36 settings, improving over the Base agent by 7.6 percentage points and the strongest competing method in each setting by 2.6 points on average. Ablation studies further support the importance of functional differentiation and adaptive invocation.","tldr":"背景与问题：一条轨迹可能同时暴露规划失误、工具误用和可自动化操作；把它们统一写进技能文档，不能决定该如何验证、维护或何时调用。\n\n方法：CDSE从成功与失败轨迹提取带证据的行为修改建议，按其作用分配维护方式：一般规则与局部经验保留适用条件，可执行程序须经过测试。协调冲突后重写调用描述，让更新后的技能影响后续执行，模型与协议保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准、三模型、两harness的测试表均领先，平均比各设置最强竞争方法高2.6个百分点。训练与测试分开，但完整消融及演化总成本未见，不能单靠总体排名确认功能拆分的独立贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，有意义的是更新的功能决定验证合同，而非认知类比本身。多轮可重复整理固定轨迹，因此轮次增长不代表新增交互学习，更不说明技能更新器本身递归变强。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 执行证据驱动改进","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称按功能差异组织技能更新，而非只按文档或包边界存储。本文证据显示，已评分轨迹产生带证据的行为建议，按功能维护、协调和验证后更新外部技能；模型与更新协议固定，多轮还可重复使用固定轨迹集。相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）按技能—流程—原则的抽象层级组织经验，本篇按控制、情境经验、工具指导和程序的执行功能分配维护责任。编辑推断：不只是模块改名，但独立收益仍需完整消融和预算核验；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23574","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23574v1","title":"Darwin-Claw: Environment-Adaptive Experience Consolidation for Recursively Self-Evolving Agents","authors":"Mingze Yin; Xiaohan Wang; Dian Li; Longfei Luo; Jiahong Yan; Yiheng Zhu; Chang-Yu Hsieh","affiliations":"Zhejiang University；Tencent；Zhongguancun Academy","abstract":"While Large Language Model (LLM) agents have demonstrated remarkable capabilities across complex tasks, they predominantly operate in isolated sessions, lacking the ability to continually learn from historical interactions or adapt to user-specific environments. Existing self-evolution paradigms often indiscriminately inject raw interaction trajectories into memory or skill modules, leading to obscured behavioral patterns and compromised update controllability. Furthermore, as foundational LLM reasoning improves, the bottleneck for agentic evolution shifts from accumulating generic knowledge to effectively managing situational experience. To address this, we propose Darwin-Claw, an environment-adaptive self-evolving framework that systematically distills episodic experiences to drive the comprehensive evolution of operational skills and durable memory. Theoretically grounded in an iterative agent-actor and evolver-critic co-adaptation, Darwin-Claw introduces a Hierarchical Experience Consolidation System that extracts fine-grained error attributions and generalizes them into dynamically updated prototype vectors. This structured situational experience serves as interaction patches for context-sensitive perception and explicit optimization signals for skill refinement. Practically, Darwin-Claw is a readily deployable, automated framework compatible with mainstream agent systems without requiring manual curation. Extensive experiments on WildClawBench demonstrate that Darwin-Claw yields substantial performance improvements, establishing a controllable and stable pathway for the continual, user-centric adaptation of autonomous agents in real-world ecosystems.","tldr":"背景与问题：把用户交互原样塞进记忆或技能，会混淆环境限制与通用操作经验，也难判断哪些补丁应保留、哪些已过时。\n\n方法：Darwin-Claw把有学习信号的轨迹整理成带触发条件的经验单元，写入相关技能；后续轨迹提供效果与无效调用变化，控制试用、晋级和淘汰。LLM判断新轨迹是否相关及改善是否来自经验，底层模型参数不变。\n\n结果与结论：自主后训练场景中，相对只传递上下文报告，技能方案的六项平均分由28.42%升至31.91%。但具体模型—任务组合仍有退化，WildClawBench的完整数值表和消融未见，稳定性主张证据不足。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，限定经验容量与撤销低效补丁比持续追加更可控；但轨迹后的LLM归因不能替代同条件有无记忆对照。还需区分研究目标模型变强与负责优化的agent技能真正获得迁移。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称把情境经验、技能与长期记忆连接成可控的整体递归演化。本文证据显示，LLM筛选及归因产生经验单元，后续轨迹的效果与效率估计控制试用、晋级和淘汰；骨干不更新。相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）分层检索、去重及反向经验提示，本篇突出用户环境触发条件、技能内补丁和生命周期竞争。编辑推断：部署机制有细化，但LLM判断因果贡献不等于受控因果识别，且原型向量叙述与可见实现细节衔接不足；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23344","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23344v1","title":"Language Models Learn to Improve Language Models","authors":"Minhua Lin; Zijun Wang; Zewen Liu; Zhaotian Weng; Bing He; Zhan Shi; Benoit Dumoulin; Xiang Zhang; Suhang Wang; Hanqing Lu","affiliations":"The Pennsylvania State University；UC Santa Cruz；Emory University；UC Santa Barbara；Amazon","abstract":"Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly used to automate AI research, including language-model (LM) development, offering a potential path toward recursive self-improvement. However, turning experimental feedback into a learned ability to propose effective improvements across models faces two challenges. First, training such an ability with real feedback is expensive: reinforcement learning (RL) requires evaluating tens of thousands of proposals, each potentially requiring a full model-training run. Even at ten GPU-hours per run, reward collection alone would consume hundreds of thousands of GPU-hours, motivating a cheaper surrogate. Second, surrogate feedback can become unreliable as policy optimization favors overestimated proposals when the proposal distribution shifts. To address these challenges, we propose LM2LM, which trains LLMs with RL to generate effective LM improvement proposals. To provide scalable feedback, we use a research world model (RWM), a frozen LLM that predicts proposal gains from real experimental records provided in context, as the reward model for RL. To maintain feedback reliability, we periodically execute current-policy proposals ranked highly by the RWM and add their measured outcomes to its context. Across eight autoregressive and diffusion LM development environments, real-execution evaluations on held-out tasks show that LM2LM enables Qwen3.8-27B to outperform GPT-6-sol, even when GPT-6-sol is given 300 real experimental records in context, while requiring 33% lower data-generation cost. LM2LM also generalizes to a model family unseen during training.","tldr":"背景与问题：训练研究提案者若逐个运行模型实验，反馈成本过高；改用预测收益后，策略又会集中到预测器高估的方案，使代理奖励上涨而真实收益不涨。\n\n方法：LM2LM用读取真实实验记录的冻结LLM预测收益，训练提案者；定期真实执行当前策略中预测高分的提案，把测量结果补入预测器上下文。提案者权重改变、反馈记录刷新，校准专门针对优化偏爱的区域。\n\n结果与结论：留出任务采用真实执行评价，摘要称优于带实验记录的强模型，数据生成成本低33%。可见案例中，静态记录方案不断强化有害改动，加入真实负结果后该改动比例下降；但主结果表与完整成本口径被截断。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，预测器离线准确不足以支撑在线优化，最需要复测的恰是策略追逐的高分点。证据支持定向纠偏，不证明全空间校准；这里学到改进其他模型的能力，尚非研究者自主改造自身训练算法。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"研究世界模型; 预算受限研究搜索; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称用研究世界模型的预测奖励训练LM改进提案者，并以当前策略的高分提案真实执行持续校准。本文证据明确：提案者权重更新，RWM权重冻结但上下文实验记录更新，真实收益纠正代理高估；并有静态记录退化案例。相对研究世界模型（arxiv:2610.12235）用记录改善候选预测和选择，本篇进一步训练提案生成策略，并针对优化造成的分布变化校准；相对MLExpert（arxiv:2610.22344）直接用执行窗口反馈训练，本篇以代理奖励降低真实执行需求。编辑推断：机制推进明确，但没有提案者自我替换或外层算法自改写证据；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22984","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22984v1","title":"Self-Evolving Agents Can Repair Failures but Struggle to Generalize from Them","authors":"Weixiang Zhao; Yichen Zhang; Yanyan Zhao; Jinming Bai; Bin Liang; Ruifeng Xu; Bing Qin; Ting Liu","affiliations":"Harbin Institute of Technology, Harbin；Harbin Institute of Technology, Shenzhen；The Chinese University of Hong Kong","abstract":"Experience-driven self-evolution offers a promising path for large language model (LLM) agents to continually improve through interaction. Yet existing approaches often rely on successful trajectories or external evaluation signals, leaving unclear whether agents can evolve when such positive anchors are unavailable. We study this question through Cold-Start Failure-Only Evolution (CFOE), where agents start without accumulated experience and learn only from failed interactions without privileged guidance. Across three self-evolving paradigms, multiple LLM backbones, and four interactive environments, we uncover a consistent repair-generalization gap: failure-derived experience can help repair previously failed tasks, but rarely yields sustained improvements on unseen tasks. Further analysis shows that agents often misinterpret failures, while even verified-correct experience remains difficult to transfer. Relaxing CFOE reveals that verifier feedback and additional interaction provide limited gains, whereas successful trajectories substantially improve transfer. These findings suggest that current self-evolving agents are better at repairing observed failures than building generalizable capabilities from failure.","tldr":"背景与问题：很多经验演化方法依赖成功轨迹或验证反馈；若agent空库起步、反复失败又不知道真实评分，能否仅靠反思获得可迁移能力仍不清楚。\n\n方法：论文由控制器只让失败轨迹触发外部记忆、技能或harness更新，隐藏评分且不告知失败筛选。分别测源任务重试恢复与固定未见任务表现，再筛出人工确认正确的经验，并放宽成功轨迹、反馈或额外交互条件。\n\n结果与结论：多个框架与环境中，源任务可部分修复，未见任务却少有持续改善。仅保留正确经验后，五种配置中四种的最终留出成绩仍不高于无经验基线，表明诊断错误不是唯一瓶颈。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应把经验正确性、同题可用性和跨题可迁移性分开验收。成功轨迹带来更强迁移，但成功与失败任务流分别采样，包含难度和内容差异；结果不能推出失败经验普遍无用。","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 经验迁移; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-19","novelty_summary":"作者声称揭示无正向锚点时的修补—泛化缺口。本文证据为冻结骨干、空经验起步、只允许失败轨迹进入更新，控制器保留验证标签，agent与更新器不可见；独立目标集评估时冻结经验，还人工筛查正确经验。相对MC-EvoBench（arxiv:2610.13829）隔离环境状态与经验来源，本篇隔离失败经验的监督条件；相对MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492）训练经验获取能力，本篇审计现有方法在无成功和显式评估反馈条件下的局限。编辑推断：补强既有迁移主题，但成功与失败流分别采样，不能纯归因为轨迹成败；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22791","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22791v1","title":"Self-Evolving Coding Agents via Harness-Policy Optimization","authors":"Zhepei Wei; Wenlin Yao; Baolin Peng; Danqing Wang; Qianhui Wu; Hao Cheng; Yu Meng; Jianfeng Gao","affiliations":"","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents have shown promising potential in coding tasks, and their performance is jointly determined by the policy model and the harness that mediates their interaction with the environment. Indeed, harness and policy are mutually reinforcing and evolving only one component is suboptimal---a harness tuned for one checkpoint may not target the failure modes of an updated policy, while policy learning remains limited to the trajectories elicited by a fixed harness. In light of this, we propose Self-HPO, a recursive self-improving framework for coding agents that alternates harness and policy optimization, using the evolving policy as its own harness proposer. Specifically, in each round, the current policy first analyzes its own failures and proposes new harness candidates (H-step). The policy is then updated through reinforcement learning (RL) under the selected harness (P-step), and hard tasks identified during training form the next harness search set, keeping harness optimization targeted to the policy's evolving failure modes. Across three coding benchmarks, Self-HPO consistently outperforms harness-only and policy-only baselines, improving Qwen3.5-35B-A3B's average resolve rate from 57.8% to 64.8%, with gains generalizing to out-of-distribution settings. Further analysis shows that both optimized components retain gains even when paired with their base counterparts, while their joint gain exceeds the sum of their individual gains. Self-HPO also improves reliability (Pass@1) and expands the capability frontier (Pass@k) over the base agent. Additionally, we show that with a stronger external model (e.g., Opus 4.8) as the harness proposer, the same framework yields a further performance boost.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-16","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-19"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22740","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22740v1","title":"R$^2$Orch: Recursive Self-Improvement for Agent Orchestration via Self-Play within a Skill-Internalization Loop","authors":"Mingda Zhang; Yun Huang; Qiang Huang; Yanjin Li; Rui Qian; Qichao Zhao; Tiesunlong Shen; Na Zhao; Jian Wang; Xiaoying Tang","affiliations":"","abstract":"In recent years, agentic orchestration has been widely applied to solve complex human tasks. However, existing orchestration learning still faces key challenges, including hand-designed curricula, advantage collapse when a task's rollouts all reach the same outcome, and unreliable evaluation signals that judge each skill by one noisy score. To address these challenges, we propose R$^2$Orch, a new paradigm of Recursive Self-Play Orchestration: an inner loop of self-play that improves the orchestrator on self-chosen tasks, and an outer loop that improves how the inner loop improves. To support this paradigm, we introduce Recursive Learnability, a training objective that rewards a Proposer for choosing tasks whose rollouts keep reaching different outcomes as skills are withdrawn. Built on this objective, we further propose Skill Withdrawal, in which the outer loop withdraws each skill once a controlled evaluation within self-play shows that the orchestrator performs as well without it. Moreover, the two loops form one cycle: failures are distilled into skills, skills into parameters, and withdrawals lead the Proposer to new failures, so the orchestrator moves toward zero-skill deployment. Experimental results on twelve datasets show that R$^2$Orch consistently outperforms baselines across question answering, math, code, and interactive tasks.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-19"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22599","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22599v1","title":"Can LLMs predict the outcomes of machine learning experiments?","authors":"Ayush Bansal; Aldo Pareja; Sean Klein; Serge Didenko; Artem Lukoianov","affiliations":"","abstract":"Recent advances in AI make Recursive Self-Improvement (RSI) increasingly plausible. Large Language Models (LLMs) can already propose, select, and run Machine Learning (ML) experiments. However, the space of possible design choices in ML is vast. An LLM that proposes an experiment needs a reliable intuition of whether it is worth running given the timing constraints of long training runs. In this work, we measure such intuition in current frontier LLMs by evaluating how accurately they predict the impact of self-generated ML experiment ideas before these are put into training runs. To this end, we construct a dataset of 288 LLM-proposed ideas on eight MLE-bench tasks. We then prompt five frontier LLMs (GPT-6 Astra, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Fable 5.1, Kimi K3, and GLM-5.3) to predict the impact of each idea and compare their predictions with the actual outcomes after training. We report four main findings. First, LLM predictions are substantially better than random chance but far from accurate: even the best model, Claude Opus 5.5, explains only half of the variance in outcomes (R^2 = 0.49). Second, we notice that all tested models systematically underestimate the magnitude of the changes. Third, prediction quality varies widely across tasks. Finally, the choice of the coding harness that actually implements the ideas has little effect on outcomes, and we find no evidence of self-preference. Higher reasoning settings and additional context lead to modest gains. Overall, our results show that current LLMs have useful but limited intuition about which ML ideas will work. We release our dataset to support further study.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-19"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22466","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22466v1","title":"Harness-Delta Attribution: Dissecting Gains From Harness Evolution","authors":"Wenxuan Ding; Qin Lu; Changlong Yu; Sha Li; Shuowei Jin; Xin Liu; Zhenyu Shi; Greg Durrett","affiliations":"","abstract":"Harness evolution automatically optimizes the prompts, skills, tools, and orchestration code around a fixed-weight model, offering a way to improve agentic systems without updating model weights. The agent harness is iteratively optimized to achieve higher performance on the search set. But how much of this gain reflects benchmark-specific overfitting or additional inference-time compute, and how much may generalize beyond the search set? In this work, we introduce Harness-Delta Attribution (HDA), an evaluation protocol that dissects an evolution gain into artifact-driven overfitting, gains explained by test-time scaling, and the remainder, which gives an upper bound on residual generalizable improvement. We apply HDA to 11 executor models and three harness-evolution frameworks across math, coding, creativity, and agentic tasks. In 21 of these settings that show statistically significant search-set gains, we find that a large share of the improvement is explained by overfitting or test-time scaling. Specifically, among these 21 settings, overfitting and test-time scaling account for 54% and 14% of the gain on average; their combined share exceeds 50% in 14 settings. The residual and held-out transfer vary substantially across tasks, models, and frameworks. Importantly, search-set gains often fail to transfer to held-out tasks, and provide limited evidence that they will persist under practical distribution shifts. Moreover, validation-based signals are insufficient to prevent overfitting. These results motivate attribution-aware evaluation in future harness evolution research.","tldr":"","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"","added_on":"2026-10-19"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22362","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22362v1","title":"CoDA: Co-Evolution of Data Engines and Action Policies","authors":"Tianjiao Yu; Zhilin Ou; Yifan Shen; Xinzhuo Li; Yuanzhe Liu; Onkar Kishor Susladkar; Fan Wang; Ismini Lourentzou","affiliations":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign；The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen；Amazon","abstract":"Generative simulation can automate robot environment construction, but physically valid environments are not necessarily useful for training. The challenge is to identify environments that address a policy's failures and supervision that helps it overcome them. We introduce CoDA, a framework in which a simulation data engine and an action policy co-evolve through a shared heterogeneous memory of environment construction, policy failures, and learning progress. The memory compiles validated diagnoses from a vision-language critic into generation programs that recreate difficulties and training programs that help the policy overcome them. We further propose Text2potential to convert these diagnoses into staged potentials for action-chunk value learning, providing dense supervision for policy updates while preserving the task's optimal policy under standard shaping assumptions. Measured learning progress guides further generation and program refinement. Across four manipulation task families, CoDA improves out-of-distribution success from 5.3% after supervised fine-tuning to 27.6%, exceeding the strongest closed-loop baseline by 9.5 percentage points with the same generation budget. On LIBERO-Pro, 15 rounds of generation and training raise success from 25% to 84% under position perturbations and from 1% to 76% under instruction perturbations.","tldr":"背景与问题：物理上有效的仿真场景未必值得训练；只按成功率生成难题，分不清当前短板究竟可学，还是继续投入也无收益。\n\n方法：CoDA 用轨迹诊断提出困难因素，再比较定向扰动与其他因素扰动，验证诊断后存入共享记忆。同一困难生成针对性场景和密集势函数；机器可检查的任务成功条件保持独立，训练后的实际进步指导下一轮生成。\n\n结果与结论：四类操作任务中，同接受环境预算下，分布外成功率为27.6%，高于成功率引导生成的18.1%。这支持超越标量难度的反馈有价值，但不代表总计算成本相等，实机迁移仍未建立。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键不只是找失败，而是验证失败原因并测量能否学会。生成引擎靠记忆适配、策略靠梯度学习，两者共演化不等于生成算法自身变强；势函数保留最优策略也依赖标准塑形假设。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称让数据引擎与动作策略共同演化；本文证据显示，引擎通过记忆与程序检索在上下文中适配，动作策略通过梯度更新，训练前后成功率变化再决定后续生成。相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）共同训练合成器与推理器，本篇增加场景因素干预验证，并把同一诊断编译为环境与势函数，不能等同为生成器权重共同学习。编辑推断：具体推进在于联结可学性、失败归因和训练监督；尚未证明编译与调度机制自身递归增强，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22344","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22344v1","title":"MLExpert: Towards a Generalist Agentic Model for Autonomous Machine Learning Engineering","authors":"Shangheng Du; Jinxin Shi; Shuaiyu Zhang; Yiming Wu; Junpeng Zhao; Shiyang Feng; Xin Li; Liang He; Xiangchao Yan; Bo Zhang","affiliations":"Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory；East China Normal University","abstract":"Large language models (LLMs) are expanding from assisting scientific research and engineering to autonomously developing and improving AI systems, advancing AI for AI (AI4AI) as a pathway toward recursive self-improvement (RSI). Workflow-driven machine learning engineering (MLE) systems provide a practical path toward this pursuit through complex orchestration that manages long-horizon experimentation, while recent MLE systems adopt model-directed interaction, allowing models to autonomously organize experiments and adapt optimization strategies based on execution feedback. However, feedback from each experiment reflects several preceding decisions, and a long MLE run contains many such costly experiments. Training must therefore select useful supervision from long interaction trajectories and learn from intermediate outcomes. We propose a post-training method for autonomous long-horizon MLE optimization and apply it to train MLExpert, a 35B Mixture-of-Experts agentic model. We design the Kaggle-MLE Factory to construct executable tasks and an interaction harness for model-directed experimentation. Hierarchical agentic SFT transfers general tool-use and coding capabilities to MLE through outcome-guided supervision. Windowed Interaction RL (WIRL) treats the multi-turn decisions between successive experiment results as an execution window and assigns it a shared outcome-based reward. Asynchronous collection and policy correction support policy updates before the trajectory ends. On MLE-Bench Lite, MLExpert improves the average medal rate of the base model from 37.9% to 72.7%, achieving performance comparable to larger frontier models such as Kimi-K3 and GLM-5.3. Further experiments show that MLExpert improves performance on NatureBench Lite, agent scaffold optimization, and algorithm optimization, suggesting that the learned optimization capability generalizes to other tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器学习实验返回结果前，agent 已作出多轮分析和代码修改；等整段研究结束才训练，既浪费中间反馈，也难把结果归给相关决策。\n\n方法：MLExpert 先从按结果筛选的轨迹学习，再把相邻实验结果之间的决策视为一个窗口，用实验结果及局部进步共同奖励窗口内行为。实验完成即可异步更新，不必等待整个任务结束，并修正采样策略与训练策略的差异。\n\n结果与结论：MLE-Bench Lite 平均获牌率从基座的37.9%升至72.7%；算法优化迁移中也有收益，但部分任务持平或退化。窗口共享奖励并未实现窗口内部的精细归因。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献是让研究者从真实实验节奏学习，而非证明研究流程递归自造。脚手架优化实验中，进一步强化学习同时增加调用量，准确率收益不能全解释为调用效率提高。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 自进化策略训练; 长程交互学习","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称训练自主组织长程机器学习实验的模型；本文证据为按实验结果划分交互窗口、共享结果奖励并修正异步策略偏移，以及后训练和迁移实验。相对 Athanor（arxiv:2610.21055）让固定研究者运行训练研究，本篇直接训练研究决策者；相对 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）的工作流搜索—微调循环，本篇重点是实验间决策的信用分配。编辑推断：学到优化能力属于 RSI 的能力基础，但材料没有展示更新后的研究者反过来改进自身训练方法。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22192","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22192v1","title":"Terminal-RSI: Recursive Self-Improving Terminal Agents via Recursive Self-Rewrite and Policy-Refine","authors":"Junyao Yang; Zongxia Li; Yucheng Shi; Zhongzhi Li; Ruhan Wang; Ruiwen Zhou; Haitao Mi; Shuicheng Yan; Leowei Liang","affiliations":"Tencent Hy Frontier；National University of Singapore；University of Maryland, College Park；University of Georgia；Indiana University","abstract":"Converting verifier outcomes into useful policy updates and partial progress into complete task resolution is crucial for terminal agents. We present Terminal-RSI, which alternates Recursive Self-Rewrite (RSR) of verified trajectories with critic-inheriting Recursive Policy-Refine (RPR). We formulate Turn-Boundary Skip-Observation GAE (TB-GAE) to retain token-specific baselines while applying decay across interaction turns. Family Dense Reward (FDR) calibrates semantic progress across task families; Success-Prioritized Reward (SPR) separates strict success from bounded partial credit. A Warm-up Critic Model, recursive critic handoff, and stage-specific learning rates coordinate the two refinement phases. The five-stage sequence from Qwen3.8-27B base model through RSR-1, RPR-1, RSR-2, and RPR-2 yields Terminal-RSI-27B: 19.84% on Terminal-Bench 4.0, 86.52% on Terminal-Bench 2.1, 16.95% on Terminal-Bench 3.0, and 79.00% on Terminal-Bench Hard. On LHTB, process reward rises from 0.21 to 0.37 and strict completion from 0/46 to 5/46; SWR100 success doubles from 3.00% to 6.00%. By recursively coupling verified trajectory rewriting with critic-inheriting policy refinement, each retained stage consolidates discovered behaviors and progressively advances the agent from partial local repairs to strict terminal verification.","tldr":"背景与问题：终端任务的冗长日志会让按 token 衰减的信用偏离实际决策距离；监督重写改变策略后，旧价值估计也可能失准。通过局部检查更不等于完成整个任务。\n\n方法：Terminal-RSI 交替学习经验证的重写轨迹与强化学习精炼，保留价值网络但在新阶段重新校准；信用按交互轮衰减，并限制失败轨迹的部分奖励，避免局部进展压过严格完成。\n\n结果与结论：长程终端测试的严格完成从0/46增至5/46，说明收益不只体现在过程奖励；但绝对完成率仍低。阶段还同时改变数据、奖励和学习率，现有曲线不能单独归因于价值继承。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得借鉴的是把检查覆盖、塑形奖励和终局成功分开报告。这里递归的是训练数据与策略继承，并无证据说明信用分配算法自身学会了如何改进；被丢弃分支也反对单调变强的叙事。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"失败驱动的递归更新; 长程交互学习; 终端智能体","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称递归耦合轨迹重写与策略精炼；本文证据显示成功执行轨迹用于监督更新，价值网络跨监督阶段继承并重新校准，奖励将部分进展置于严格成功之下。相对 ReTerm（arxiv:2610.18484）从失败状态分叉学习恢复，本篇强调监督转换后的价值漂移和跨交互轮信用衰减；相对 CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）的运行时匹配，本篇关注 actor—critic 交接。编辑推断：多轮权重训练成立，但保留阶段曲线不能证明各组件因果作用或优化器自身递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21791","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21791v1","title":"RSIFlow: Adaptive Self-Improvement Workflows with an Evolving Meta-Agent","authors":"Huan Zhang; Mingju Chen; Dongxu Zhou; Can Lv; Sen Cui; Faguo Wu; Shiji Zhou","affiliations":"Beihang University；Tsinghua University；Beijing Academy of Artificial Intelligence (BAAI)","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents have demonstrated strong capabilities in complex tasks, including code generation, tool use, and multi-hop question answering. Existing self-improvement methods enhance agent performance through model optimization, harness evolution, and executable artifact refinement, while recursive self-improvement (RSI) further extends optimization to the improvement mechanisms themselves. However, adapting self-improvement workflows to evolving performance bottlenecks while improving workflow orchestration through execution feedback remains a key challenge. We propose \\textbf{RSIFlow}, a \\textbf{R}ecursive \\textbf{S}elf-\\textbf{I}mprovement framework that integrates adaptive work\\textbf{flow} orchestration with meta-agent capability evolution. RSIFlow diagnoses performance bottlenecks from task-agent trajectories and environmental feedback to dynamically select component-specific improvement workflows. The meta-agent then distills workflow outcomes into component-specific skills and cross-component principles, evolving its own harness to improve subsequent workflow orchestration. Experiments across six benchmarks and two backbone models show that RSIFlow achieves the SOTA average performance on all benchmarks. Ablation studies further demonstrate the contributions of adaptive workflow orchestration and meta-harness evolution. Code is available at https://github.com/1HUAN1/RSI-Flow.","tldr":"背景与问题：改权重、改 harness 或修任务产物各自有效，却未必对应当前瓶颈；固定的干预选择方式也不会自动从过去的改进尝试中受益。\n\n方法：RSIFlow 根据轨迹和环境反馈选择一个组件更新，固定其余组件比较候选。之后把成功、失败及回归提炼为带适用条件的技能和跨组件原则，修改元 agent 的接口与指令，让下一轮诊断和选择使用这些经验。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准、两种骨干的12种设置中，11种领先所比较基线。材料称消融支持自适应编排和元 harness 演化，但消融表被截断，无法核对独立贡献及完整成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，比最终任务分数更关键的是元经验能否在相同预算下改善下一次干预。方法确实改变了改进者的外部状态，但五轮结果尚不能证明持续加速；还应区分任务产物修补与可迁移能力增长。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 失败诊断; 跨任务迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称同时适应任务瓶颈和演化工作流编排能力；本文证据显示同父系统、同批任务下选择组件更新，将尝试结果提炼为技能和原则并改写元 harness，元模型权重固定。相对 SIA（arxiv:2605.27276）的反馈选干预，本篇让选择所用的外部程序与经验持续改变；相对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461），元级可编辑并非首次，本篇细化为组件选择与证据化经验维护。编辑推断：这是已有元改进范式的具体推进；截断处缺少完整消融数值和预算，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21646","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21646v1","title":"The Self-Improvement Problem","authors":"Brian B. Moser; Stanislav Frolov; Tobias C. Nauen; Federico Raue; Andreas Dengel","affiliations":"German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence (DFKI)；RPTU Kaiserslautern-Landau","abstract":"With the rise of large language models, agentic systems are becoming increasingly autonomous, as they write code, call tools, revise prompts, and propose modifications to their own components. This autonomy raises a fundamental question for safe self-improvement: can an automated gate like a reward model or an automated reviewer reliably decide whether a proposed update should be accepted? The difficulty is structural. The gate must be a terminating, computable procedure, while the property we ultimately care about, namely whether an update is a genuine semantic improvement, depends on potentially unbounded program behavior. We formalize this mismatch by modeling agents as programs and defining improvement in terms of a semantic score that need not be computable. We study two evaluation abstractions. The first is a certifier that approves or rejects an update. The second is a search procedure that, given access to a proposal generator, attempts to output some improving candidate if one exists. We show that, in the fully general setting, no terminating procedure can simultaneously guarantee reliability (never accepting a non-improvement) and non-conservatism (never missing an available improvement): self-referential constructions can force any such gate or searcher to fail. Randomized gates with bounded error face the same limit. We then identify a standard decidable regime used in practice (bounded evaluation and a finite proposal budget) under which exhaustive simulation yields a terminating search procedure with the desired guarantees. We also show the limit of this recovery: a chain of accepted updates can raise the bounded score in every round while the true score falls. Our results draw a boundary between unbounded, universal settings where correctness guarantees collapse and bounded settings where they can be recovered by design.","tldr":"背景与问题：自修改系统希望自动门控既不放过坏更新，也不阻止好更新；但门控必须停机，真正的行为改进却可能依赖无界运行，二者要求并不相容。\n\n方法：论文把 agent 与候选更新表示为程序，分别研究判断单次更新和从提案中寻找改进。利用自指构造证明普遍可靠且完备的停机程序不存在，再限制评估时域与提案数量，恢复相对于有界分数的可判定保证。\n\n结果与结论：可见证明支持认证器的不可能性；材料还给出搜索及随机门控的对应结果，并构造代理每轮上升、真实目标反而下降的更新链。这不是现实系统失败率的测量。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，工程意义是声明保证究竟针对哪个有限目标，而非宣布自改进不可行。经典不可判定性不能替代统计审计；有限测试恢复的正确性也不能自动覆盖未测输入和长期目标。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 验证理论; 选择误差","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称形式化验证门控自改进的可靠性与进展保证边界；本文证据包含可见的对角构造、认证与搜索的区分，以及有界代理恢复保证的条件。相对 arxiv:2610.10611 研究固定验证协议下的复杂性类别，本篇讨论无界语义改进的不可判定性与代理连续上升时的真实目标漂移。编辑推断：贡献是将经典可计算性限制落实为门控合同，不是新的不可计算性技术，也不是现实奖励投机必然发生的经验结论。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21492","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21492v1","title":"MetaExp: Learning to Self-Improve through Experience via Verifiable Cross-Task Environment Scaling","authors":"Renhao Li; Xinjie Shen; Yang Su; Jianhong Tu; Derek F. Wong; Dayiheng Liu; Min Yang","affiliations":"University of Macau；Shenzhen Institute of Advanced Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences；Georgia Institute of Technology；Alibaba Token Hub, Alibaba Group","abstract":"Language-model agents can accumulate interaction feedback, but reliably turning that feedback into reusable experience remains challenging. Existing methods either optimize external experience scaffolds or train experience-related behavior on specific task distributions, leaving open whether experience learning itself can become a transferable model capability. Training such a capability calls for supervision beyond isolated tasks, which mainly support in-episode problem solving rather than revealing what knowledge remains useful across episodes. In this work, we introduce MetaExp, a scalable framework that trains this capability through verifiable task families with controlled cross-task structure. Each family preserves a reusable factor while varying task-specific realizations, enabling transfer without direct solution reuse. We propose two complementary designs: Shared-Tool families keep black-box tools fixed across tasks to elicit operational experience, while Shared-Workflow families preserve latent procedures across changing realizations to elicit procedural experience. We scale environments under both designs, collect and filter sequential interaction trajectories, and fine-tune Qwen3.5-122B-A10B on 4,956 trajectories from 1,000 task families. With parameters frozen during downstream evolution, MetaExp improves by +8.5 points on SpreadsheetBench, peaks at +2.3 on APEX-Agents, and improves by +14.8 on AutomationBench. The gains persist under domain-excluded training, supporting experience learning as a transferable capability for continued non-parametric improvement after deployment.","tldr":"背景与问题：会解任务不等于会从任务中积累经验；独立任务训练难以告诉模型哪些知识应跨回合保留，部署时加记忆甚至可能使表现下降。\n\n方法：MetaExp 构造共享工具或潜在流程、但具体答案不能直接复用的任务族，用连续求解和反馈后修订技能的轨迹训练模型。测试时参数冻结、经验库清空，从新分布逐步积累技能，再在不参与更新的固定目标集测量收益。训练反馈以执行检查为主，模型复核失败项。\n\n结果与结论：SpreadsheetBench 中经验积累带来8.5分增长，匹配基座在同协议下反降2.2分；排除相关训练领域后仍有收益，支持经验学习不只是携带目标领域知识。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，较有力的变化是把初始解题水平与经验带来的增量拆开。训练过滤仍主要确认当前任务成功，尚未直接验证每次技能修改能改善后续任务；经验积累也不等于更新算法持续递归增强。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"经验迁移; 自进化策略训练; RSI 评测与迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称经验学习可训练为跨分布能力；本文证据显示用保留共同因素的任务族监督求解及经验更新，部署时冻结参数、空库起步，并在独立目标集冻结经验评估。相对 STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）设计固定骨干的记忆结构，本篇训练产生和使用经验的模型行为；相对 SGUID（arxiv:2610.12367）筛选技能蒸馏，本篇在新分布上不再更新参数。编辑推断：区分经验学习能力与携带经验是具体推进，但训练未直接按经验更新的下游增益筛选。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21055","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21055v1","title":"Athanor: An Agent-Native System for Autonomous Post-Training Research","authors":"Yufa Zhou; Yichen Wang; Jiakun Fan; Ziqi Shu; Zhichao Liu; Anru R. Zhang; Neiwen Ling; Zijun Wei","affiliations":"ByteDance；Duke University；The University of Chicago；Virginia Tech","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement, in which AI systems build stronger AI systems, is one promising route to superintelligence. We study a weaker form that can be measured today: frontier agents post-training a small raw base model with public data, as a test of their research potential. We build Athanor, an open agent-native system for autonomous post-training research (AutoPostTrain) on real GPUs. We give the agents full research autonomy, low-friction engineering tools, and efficient starter code. The agents carry out the research themselves: they read datasets and evaluation results, build their training data, write and modify training algorithms, tune hyperparameters, and analyze the results to decide what to try next. They work in a sandbox and cannot use external teacher models. Athanor's services supply frozen evaluation, managed jobs, decontaminated data, a persistent research record, and a held-out suite the agents are unaware of. In a 104-hour campaign, a team of four Claude Opus 5.5 agents, each on an eight-GPU node and given no research advice, improves Qwen3-4B-Base from 15.9 to 67.3 on a six-task development suite and from 9.2 to 48.2 on a held-out suite, against 66.5 and 47.9 for the official Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507. To our knowledge, this is the first demonstration that a team of frontier agents can autonomously post-train a raw base model into a cross-domain generalist model that matches or surpasses the official instruct version on average. The campaign's full record shows that the agents reach this level by recombining known methods and each other's models: SFT on public reasoning data, RL with a rollout change one agent introduced, weight merges across agents, and rounds of self-distillation. With execution handled, today's agents already have the engineering and research ability to conquer this task. We hope Athanor provides a foundation for scaling autonomous AI research.","tldr":"背景与问题：自主后训练不仅要提出配方，还要完成耗时且易失败的 GPU 实验，同时防止开发集搜索和数据污染冒充通用能力增长。\n\n方法：Athanor 将作业、数据去污染和固定评估做成服务，把研究记录与模型谱系持久化；四个固定前沿 agent 自选数据、算法和模型组合，训练另一个基础模型。最终隐藏套件不向研究者开放，也不允许调用外部教师模型。\n\n结果与结论：104小时活动后，隐藏套件均分为48.2，官方指令版为47.9，支持接近其平均水平，而非可靠超越。论文区分活动期间协议与事后统一重测，结果不能混为同一条曲线。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这说明低摩擦执行设施能支撑已知方法的自主重组，但尚无基础设施消融证明它是决定性瓶颈。单次活动也未显示研究者自身变强，运营者仍承担节点恢复等基础设施职责。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 预算受限研究搜索; 自主后训练","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称首次由前沿 agent 团队自主后训练出平均匹敌官方指令版的跨域模型；本文证据为单次104小时研究活动、固定评估服务、隐藏套件和训练谱系记录，并未核验首创性。相对 RSIGym（arxiv:2610.10310）提供多轨研究服务，本篇聚焦真实 GPU 上单个通用检查点的后训练及封存评估；相对 MLExpert（arxiv:2610.22344），研究者模型未被训练。编辑推断：这是自主 AI 研发的具体实证，不是研究者自我替换或改进器递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21040","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21040v1","title":"Recursive Reward Improvement via Adversarial Meta-Prompt Evolution","authors":"Wei Dai; Qianchu Liu; Guanghui Qin; Xing Han; Tristan Naumann; Paul Pu Liang; Sheng Zhang","affiliations":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology；Microsoft Research；Johns Hopkins University","abstract":"Recursive Self-Improvement (RSI) has gained wide attention for its ability to work with limited data. In a proposer-solver loop, a proposer model writes training tasks and a solver model learns to solve them through reinforcement learning. Such loops have succeeded in mathematics and coding, where every answer can be checked automatically. Open-ended expert tasks, like clinical report generations, have no answer key, which makes simple question-answer generation not viable. Here the proposer must also write a rubric that lists the content an answer should include and the errors it should avoid. However, the unique challenge behind model-written rubric is the comprehensiveness of it. For naively generated rubric, solvers tend to exploit it, naming the expected topics without the substance behind them, which corrupts the learning process. To solve this problem, we introduce RRI, Recursive Reward Improvement, which uses a reward hacking adversary to supervise the reward. Before the solver trains on a generated task, an adversary writes an answer that games its rubric while being as useless as possible, the same model writes an honest answer without seeing the rubric, and up to two repair steps revise the rubric to make the honest answer win. The exploits found also rewrite how future tasks and rubrics are generated. On HealthBench Professional, RRI improves the adjusted score over the Generation Only self-improvement baseline by 10.9 points at 9B and 12.4 at 27B, and by 10.3 points without any external model. In particular, the gains are largest on difficult and writing tasks. We show that the 27B model trained on the HealthBench Professional description improves by 6.6 points on PRBench Hard and 8.0 on ProfBench without seeing a task from either. We further analyze the exploitable points of model-generated question-rubric pairs to facilitate future research on open-ended self-play.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放式专家任务缺少答案键，模型自写评分准则容易奖励关键词覆盖而非实质内容；求解器会把这些漏洞放大成训练方向。\n\n方法：RRI 从检索资料生成任务与准则，先写故意钻评分漏洞的答案，再与同一模型不看准则写出的诚实答案比较，由模型 judge 评分并指导修补。漏洞还改写未来任务和准则的生成指令，求解器用修补后的奖励学习。\n\n结果与结论：9B 设置相对只生成任务的基线提高10.9分，但相对已共演化任务与奖励的基线，攻击修补额外贡献为2.7分。修补次数受限，仍能被攻破的任务也进入训练，不能称为可靠奖励认证。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，主张应落在减少已发现的可利用性，而非无参考地建立真值。诚实答案和 judge 仍可能共享错误；专业基准收益不代表临床有效性，后续应独立测量修补后的排序可靠性。","published_at":"2026-10-15","topics":"评估器递归改进; 奖励投机与安全; 自适应课程与数据合成","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称用奖励投机监督任务、奖励与求解器共同改进；本文证据为攻击—诚实答案对照、准则修补、生成提示更新，以及相对无攻击共演化的增量对照。相对 UCoE（arxiv:2610.17609）以已知偏好响应对筛选可执行验证器，本篇修补逐任务 rubric 并用于权重训练；相对 arxiv:2610.11464 的锚点选择，本篇依赖模型生成对照与同源判断。编辑推断：外层生成规则确实改变，但判断器权重固定，残余漏洞仍被接纳，不能视为奖励已被认证。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20845","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20845v1","title":"Evolving Together, Failing Apart: The Skill-Policy Co-evolution Trap in Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Yujie Feng; Xiaobin Wang; Jinluan Yang; Xiaonan Shi; Pengjun Xie; Philip S. Yu; Xiaoming Wu; Jieping Ye","affiliations":"Alibaba Token Hub, Alibaba Group；The Hong Kong Polytechnic University；University of Illinois at Chicago","abstract":"Skill-policy co-evolution, in which an agent's policy model and its skill bank improve each other during training, is a promising paradigm for self-improving agents. Current evaluations score the co-evolved policy on the final bank it trained with (the delivered bank). After deployment, however, skills may be rewritten, added or removed more frequently than the policy model is retrained, leaving the policy to operate on a drifted skill bank that neither the training objective nor existing evaluation protocols address. In this paper, we first establish, through theoretical and empirical analysis, that the fragility hidden by this blind spot is not incidental. The acceptance rule these methods share (cooperative acceptance) ties a policy's competence to the bank it co-evolved with, leaving it fragile once skills drift, regardless of the implementation; empirically, sensitivity to skill drift grows as co-evolution training proceeds. We therefore introduce the CO-evolution Drift Audit (CODA), a deployment-oriented evaluation protocol that simulates skill drift and, alongside success rate under worst-case drift, introduces two new metrics: a consistency rate under meaning-preserving edits and a resistance rate to corrupted skills. Across four co-evolution methods and five benchmarks (six settings), worst-case success is 5-13 points below the peak measured for each delivered pair, erasing 52-93% of the delivered bank's gain over the no-skill baseline. CODA thus reframes the target of co-evolution, from peak performance on the co-evolved bank to the ability to harness skills however they evolve, and provides a shared standard against which future methods can be audited.","tldr":"背景与问题：技能—策略共演化通常只测最终配对；部署后技能库比权重更新更频繁，原配高分可能掩盖对特定措辞和内容的依赖。\n\n方法：论文固定任务和策略，在固定检索下分别改写技能措辞、删除必要步骤或注入误导，并另测增删技能与撤库。沿训练检查点追踪敏感性，再以任务成功、语义一致性和抗损坏性审计交付系统；语义保持改写另经模型及部分人工检查。\n\n结果与结论：四种方法、六种设置中，所测最差成功率比原配低5—13个百分点；五种设置的内容漂移敏感性随训练增加。理论依赖理想选择与候选覆盖，不意味着任意共演化必然退化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共演化应优化技能变化下的可靠使用，而非只优化原配峰值。意义保持改写也会造成损失，说明问题不全是技能变坏；但所测最差值不是所有部署变化的全局最坏保证。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 自改进稳定性; 模型—数据共演化","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称共演化接受偏好造成技能漂移脆弱性；本文证据包括固定检索下的内容扰动、训练阶段曲线和四方法六设置审计。理论依赖理想化候选最优选择及覆盖，不证明所有共演化必然严重退化。相对 CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）研究训练与部署 harness 不匹配，本篇隔离技能文本变化；相对 SGUID（arxiv:2610.12367）筛选蒸馏价值，本篇审计交付后漂移。编辑推断：这是对既有迁移评测的具体扩展，而非已提出鲁棒训练解法。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20809","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20809v1","title":"A Self-Improving Agent that Grows its Own DSL: Oracle-Free Operator Induction for Exact Question Answering","authors":"Yun-Shiuan Chuang; Yirou Ge; Yixi Li; Yiming Bian; Zijie Pan; Jenna L. Ballard; Uma Kona; Linsey Pang; Prakhar Mehrotra","affiliations":"PayPal AI","abstract":"A self-improving agent has to decide which new skills to keep, and in practice it keeps whatever earns a high reward, convinces a judge model, or compresses its library, even when the skill is wrong. That is fine until the answers have to be exactly right: over a table of transactions, a total is either right or wrong. We ask a harder question: can an agent grow what it can compute with no reward, no judge, and no answer key, and still be exactly right? A single frozen model runs two nested loops over a small, exact domain-specific language (DSL). The inner loop answers new questions only when two independently written expressions agree on every record. The outer loop discovers its own missing capability and authors an operator for it, admitted only when an independent second implementation agrees and the result obeys a conservation law, all without ground truth. The inner loop roughly triples the answerable-question set, and the outer loop self-extends on disjoint starting sets, inventing operators outside the starting closure; a no-induction control answers none of the new questions. The admission rule is empirically sound: it rejects 138 of 138 buggy operator variants under an independent reference, even one written by a different model family, where the admit-if-it-runs, self-consistency, and compression signals the field relies on admit most of them. Unmodified, the same mechanism self-extends on two further domains with unrelated schemas, business-ledger and clinical-encounter question answering, growing their answerable sets more than tenfold and nearly twentyfold. The loop transfers across model families too: run with further proposers, the gate stays sound and independent families self-extend comparably, with only the induction yield tracking each proposer's DSL fluency.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定小型领域语言只能回答已有算子可组合的问题；让 agent 自写新算子又会引入计算错误，运行成功或模型自信不足以决定保留。\n\n方法：冻结模型先用独立表达式的一致结果扩展问题覆盖，再针对反复出现的能力缺口生成算子。新算子需通过第二实现的差分测试和基于可信原语的守恒关系检查，获准后进入后续组合；解释器与准入规则保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：独立参考条件下，门控拒绝全部138个错误变体；人为让两实现共享错误时仍会漏放。团队盲评中仅89%的问题表达式忠实于问题，说明算得一致不代表理解正确。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可信扩展需要同时检查执行关系与问题语义。无 oracle 指在线准入不看答案键，不代表实验没有外部金标准；有限输入上的一致性也不是所有输入正确的形式证明。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"执行证据驱动改进; 可执行记忆与规则; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称无奖励、judge 和答案键地扩展自身领域语言；本文证据为固定模型提出算子，差分与守恒检查准入，新算子进入后续生成，以及无归纳控制和错误变体实验。相对 Memento 3（arxiv:2610.11794）更新环境规则和模型代码，本篇扩大计算词汇；相对 arxiv:2610.21646 的普遍认证限制，本篇主动限制语言、输入和验证范围，两者不矛盾。编辑推断：能力扩展来自可执行工具库，而非模型权重或准入算法自我提升；自然语言语义仍有缺口。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20474","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20474v1","title":"AdaRSI: On-Demand Recursive Self-Improvement for Embodied Agents","authors":"Peidong Wang; Ying Chang; Zhiming Ma; Xiaocui Yang; Shi Feng; Daqi Liu; Yuzhe Yang; Xu Cao; Chuang Wang; Jian Su; Daling Wang","affiliations":"Northeastern University；AgiBot；University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","abstract":"Pretrained vision-language-action models (VLAs) often fail midway through unseen long-horizon tasks. Recursive self-improvement (RSI) offers a remedy, but embodied RSI methods either refine the harness around a frozen executor and so cannot add a missing motion, or train the executor on persistent failures without asking whether a failure lies in how the executor is called or in what it can do. We ask when a self-improving embodied system should change the weights of its executor, and propose AdaRSI, an on-demand RSI framework for embodied agents. A coding agent first improves its skills and harness, then attributes persistent failures by retrying failing sub-steps from saved states, and fine-tunes only the sub-steps that remain unreliable, with demonstrations it collects itself and experience carried over from earlier tasks. On all 50 target tasks of RoboCasa365, with GR00T N1.5 as the executor and no human demonstrations, AdaRSI improves the VLA on all three suites and raises its success on unseen composite tasks from 4.6% to 13.8%. Compared with fine-tuning every sub-step, it reaches slightly higher success while using only 28% of the GPU time and 22% of the self-collected demonstrations, and fine-tuning without a harness trains more yet gains far less.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人子步骤失败可能是调用姿态或指令不当，也可能是执行器不会所需动作；直接微调所有失败既浪费数据，也可能损坏原本可用的能力。\n\n方法：AdaRSI 先修 harness，再从保存状态重试不同调用方式，只为仍不可靠的子步骤自采示范并微调。示范来自成功 rollout 或读取特权状态的脚本；训练起点取自实际到达状态，新策略经比较后仅在受益位置推荐使用。\n\n结果与结论：未见组合任务中，相对 harness-only 的9.9%，完整系统达到13.8%。同预算下只挑最低成功率步骤训练没有额外收益，支持训练状态与归因的重要性；结果限于仿真及单一执行器。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，harness 不只是廉价替代品，还决定训练数据来自哪些状态。保存状态重试提供受控干预，但有限重试找不到有效调用，并不严格证明动作不可实现；跨任务经验也尚未独立证明调度能力递归增强。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"harness—权重协同; 失败诊断; 具身 RSI","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称按失败归因决定何时更新执行器；本文证据为同状态更换调用方式、只训练残余不可靠子步骤、保留原策略默认，以及与低成功率选训练对象和全训练的对照。相对 arxiv:2610.11655 已提出先诊断再选择 harness 或权重，本篇不是首次提出干预分工，而是将其落实到具身子步骤、训练起始状态及按需调用。相对 EmbodiedRSI（arxiv:2610.10498）演化代码技能，本篇新增低层策略训练。编辑推断：支持成本有效的选择性适配，尚未隔离证明改进调度自身跨任务增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20431","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20431v1","title":"SwarmRSI: Recursive Self-Improvement through Evolving Scientific Agent Swarm","authors":"Qianru Meng; Xi Zhang; Konstantinos Papakostas; Congfeng Cao; Wenxiang Hu; Tianyi Lu; Xiao Zhang; Lun Zhou; Zaiqiao Meng; Zhaochun Ren; Xiaohui Yan; Yougang Lyu","affiliations":"Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd.；Leiden University；University of Groningen","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) in scientific research aims to improve agents' research capabilities through their own experimental experience. Scientific agent swarms can combine evidence and implementations from different research directions to guide their agents' subsequent experiments. However, poor experimental results can leave unclear whether to revise a hypothesis or its implementation, while overall program scores can hide components useful to other agents. To address these challenges, we introduce SwarmRSI, a framework that evolves scientific agent swarms for recursive self-improvement. We devise Feedback-Guided Swarm Mutation to refine hypotheses and their implementations using experimental feedback from other agents. We also propose Complementary Swarm Recombination to reuse retained hypotheses and complementary program components across agents, allowing partial results to support new research. Recursive Swarm Evolution integrates both mechanisms into a feedback loop, using new experimental evidence to guide subsequent research. Experiments on OpenProblems, NatureBench and MLE-Bench Lite demonstrate SwarmRSI's state-of-the-art (SOTA) performance. Further evaluations show that accumulated research experience improves performance on held-out tasks. Biologists also reproduce its programs for follow-up biological analyses.","tldr":"背景与问题：科学实验失败不说明假设错还是实现错；按整体得分淘汰程序，还会丢掉对其他研究分支有用的局部组件。\n\n方法：SwarmRSI 将假设、程序、执行证据与未解决需求写入共享图，用其他分支反馈决定改研究方向还是修实现。保留假设可迁到另一程序上验证，互补组件也可重组；每次执行及评分结果进入下一轮继承状态。\n\n结果与结论：NatureBench 上删除程序修订后，匹配既有最佳结果的比例从44.4%降至31.1%，支持实现修复有贡献。跨任务经验结果仍受源任务数量混淆，生物学家复用程序不等于复现整套方法。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，负结果应保留可复用结构，而非只有一个失败标签。但重组后得分上升不能证明原科学假设成立；固定搜索规则下状态越来越丰富，也不能直接当作改进算法自身递归变强。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 实验经验复用; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过演化可继承研究状态实现科学群体自改进；本文证据为执行反馈区分假设与实现修改、跨分支重用组件、共享图和选择机制的消融。相对 AReaL-RSI（arxiv:2610.18083）更新研究方向与带条件经验，本篇重点是明确的假设—程序关联及重组；相对 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）训练共享模型，本篇循环的改变对象是研究状态，未展示骨干训练或调度算法自重写。编辑推断：属于经验驱动研究搜索推进，而非递归研究者能力已被认证。生物学家复用两个程序不等于独立复现整体 RSI 效果。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20312","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20312v1","title":"Reflect After Failure: Brain-Inspired Self-Evolving Agents for Embodied Spatial Intelligence","authors":"Xin Li; Xiaohuan Gu; Yifan Wang; Shaobin Ling; Tianli Shi; Jingao Xu; Zhimeng Yin; Dapeng Wu; Yun Wang","affiliations":"City University of Hong Kong；East China Normal University；University of Electronic Science and Technology of China；The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen；The University of Hong Kong","abstract":"Vision-Language Models (VLMs) have made substantial progress in spatial reasoning, and self-evolving agents further extend these capabilities to embodied environments by learning from interactions. However, current self-evolution remains particularly challenging in embodied spatial tasks, complex and multi-step decisions from partial visual evidence making it difficult to determine why an execution fails. The failure may stem from misperception, insufficient exploration, or incorrect planning, yet execution feedback alone rarely reveals which component is responsible. As a result, simply accumulating interaction experience can reinforce ineffective strategies. To address this, we propose HiMeco, a brain-inspired self-evolving agent for embodied spatial intelligence, inspired by metacognitive monitoring and hippocampal memory consolidation. Through Hippocampal-Metacognitive Reflection, HiMeco diagnoses failures in perception-exploration-planning (PEP), then compares execution attempts to derive reusable strategies and guidance for avoiding recurring errors. It also abstracts interaction programs into parameterized skills, using evidence contracts and execution-based validation to determine their retention and reuse. These strategies and skills guide subsequent interactions, with memory updated only between rounds and model parameters kept frozen. HiMeco achieves state-of-the-art performance on ESI-Bench, and it also improves accuracy on EmbSpatial-Bench by 3.94 percentage points without evolution.","tldr":"背景与问题：空间任务只能看到部分环境，答错可能来自看错、探索不够或规划失误；不区分原因就总结经验，容易固化错误策略。\n\n方法：HiMeco 在执行结束后利用轨迹、答案真值与特权仿真信息诊断三类问题，比较多次尝试并提炼适用策略。程序片段抽象成参数化技能后，经证据合同和实际调用验证再保留；模型冻结，记忆只在轮间更新。\n\n结果与结论：材料称其在 ESI-Bench 领先，但结果表和关键消融未提供。EmbSpatial-Bench 的3.94个百分点收益发生在没有演化时，不能据此证明记忆更新有效。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应优先核查去掉分类诊断后是否仍能取得同样收益，而非接受脑机制类比。诊断分数不是校准概率，离线特权信息也是重要监督来源；推广到无真值或真实机器人反馈时，归因可靠性尚未确定。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"失败诊断; 经验迁移; 具身 RSI","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称将元认知诊断与记忆巩固用于具身空间自演化；本文证据显示借助真值、特权仿真元数据及冻结审计模型诊断，再以执行结果和证据合同维护策略与技能，权重和轮内记忆固定。相对 EmbodiedRSI（arxiv:2610.10498）主动选择区分假设的实验，本篇侧重事后感知—探索—规划归因；相对 MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492），本篇不训练经验更新行为。编辑推断：脑启发命名本身不是机制创新，截断材料未提供诊断必要性的完整消融效果。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20294","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20294v1","title":"MMLA-RSI: Recursive Self-Improvement through RTT and RTMA","authors":"Junyi Zou; Avrova Donz","affiliations":"MMLA-org；Communication University of China (CUC)","abstract":"An agent can improve its behavior within an unresolved problem by changing how it acts and which experience it retains. We propose MMLA-RSI, a recursive self-improvement scheme with two implementations in Memory-Mediated Learning Architecture: Reasoning-Time Training (RTT) changes the policy state $Φ$, while Reasoning-Time Memory Adaptation (RTMA) changes authoritative memory $M$. Each route also makes its adaptation method an object of improvement. A current numerical updater trains the policy proposing its successor; a current memory manager chooses the records available to the process proposing its successor. An independently admitted successor takes over the same role in the next generation. We give bounded executable rule languages, shared task/proposal interfaces, and one algorithm for either route or their composition. The RTT instance changes scalar schedules in a clipped-momentum update. The RTMA instance chooses NULL or a complete-row write with possible eviction. A fixed interpreter, trusted committer, and independent evaluator bound what can change. State versions, read closures, and conditional properties describe causal execution, accepted transitions, and finite work. Existing numerical-component studies motivate the construction. In four-candidate program selection, retaining LARC feedback updates reduces expected error by 24.65 and 36.65 percentage points for two trained initializations. In chronological continuous-integration replay, feedback binding is positive while retention increases loss. Completed SQL studies improve substantially over an unadapted substrate but do not establish the required additional online benefit. These results characterize their declared components. The two recursive routes and their joint realization are specified here; their beneficial recursive chains and discovery efficiency remain to be evaluated.","tldr":"背景与问题：改变策略状态或写入记忆，只能说明发生适配；要证明递归改进，还须显示当前适配规则参与产生更好的继任规则，并由后者继续承担同一角色。\n\n方法：MMLA-RSI 分别规定数值更新器和记忆管理器的继任流程：前者训练提出后继的策略，后者选择该过程能读取的记录。候选锁定后由独立评估器准入，固定解释器和可信提交器限制可改范围，并记录更新先于新尝试的证据。\n\n结果与结论：现有组件研究有正有负：程序选择受益，连续集成回放保留状态却增加损失，SQL 未证实额外在线收益。论文明确表示，有益递归链及发现效率尚未评估。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，其价值在于把功能参与、任务收益和搜索效率分开。固定随机带下输出改变也不必然证明动作分布改变；这些证据要求比组件增益更接近真正递归主张，但目前仍是待验证方案。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; Harness 递归演化; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称在数值更新器与记忆管理器两条路径中，让当前规则参与产生继任规则并独立准入。本文证据支持状态、读依赖、事件顺序和受限规则语言的规格说明，组件实验不构成有益递归链。相对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461）的可编辑元程序，本篇细化为有界更新规则及记忆提交规则；相对 RSIFlow（arxiv:2610.21791）的元 harness 经验更新，本篇要求继任者接替同一学习角色。编辑推断：可作为可检验协议关注，不能按已实现递归收益入账。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20665","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20665v1","title":"The World Won't Wait: Evaluating and Teaching Agents Under a Live Clock","authors":"Ningxin Pan; Hanyu Li; Yeqing Shen; Ning Ding; Yehui Tang; Wentao Zhang","affiliations":"Peking University；Samsung Research, Beijing, China","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents can solve complex interactive tasks, yet reasoning and tool calls take time. In continuously changing environments, an otherwise correct action may arrive too late. We introduce RealtimeBench, with 180 tasks across six game types, to evaluate agents while games continue running during inference. Paired evaluations show that GPT-6.1-sol outperforms the faster Jev when games are paused, but falls behind when they keep running. We propose Two-Timescale Offline Recursive Self-Improvement (TORSI): a slow teacher studies failures and tests corrections in paused games between attempts, then writes reusable instructions for a fast student. The student acts without teacher calls during gameplay, and validation scores determine which updates are adopted. Two rounds raise Jev's average test score from 13.51 to 24.19 on a 0--100 progress scale, improving all six game types. The instructions also improve average scores for three other models without retuning. These findings point toward real-time intelligence: enabling powerful LLM agents to remain effective in a continuously changing world by organizing deliberation, learning, and action across timescales.","tldr":"背景与问题：游戏在推理期间继续运行时，正确动作也可能来得太晚；暂停评测会掩盖这一点，在线调用更强教师反而可能破坏控制。\n\n方法：TORSI 让快学生独立行动，慢教师在回合之间读取失败，从保存状态练习替代动作，再让学生按真实延迟检验指导。只有在独立验证任务上改善的指导才替换旧版，下一轮处理更新后的残余失败，双方权重和行动接口不变。\n\n结果与结论：两轮后按游戏分别选出的指导，使测试平均进度分从13.51升至24.19；这不是统一采用第二轮候选的结果。消融显示仅写指导或缺少任一侧练习均不足以取得完整收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，慢推理适合用于控制间隙的学习，而非每次动作决策。证据限于文本状态接口、六类游戏和两轮，进度分不等于通关率；这里变强的是指导，不是教师或教学算法自身。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"Harness 递归演化; RSI 评测与迁移; 实时智能体","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称用双时间尺度离线教学支持实时自改进；本文证据为暂停与实时配对评测、教师和学生离线练习消融、验证门控指导更新及两轮结果。相对 Continual Harness（arxiv:2605.09998）在不重置任务中在线修改 harness，本篇把修改移至回合之间以避免教师延迟进入控制；相对 AHE（arxiv:2604.25850）的一般轨迹驱动修改，本篇保留学生接口，仅更新实时动作指导。编辑推断：是实时场景下的经验化指导改进，未证实教师更新机制自身递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19799","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19799v1","title":"Evolve Together, Fall into Place: How Social Scaffolding Shapes Self-Evolving Multi-Agent Systems","authors":"Seojin Hwang; Youngmin Choi; Hwanhee Lee","affiliations":"Chung-Ang University","abstract":"Recent work lets LLM agents evolve their own harness, up to the team itself. Yet in human groups, the same abilities achieve different outcomes under different social conditions. Borrowing the notion of scaffolding from developmental psychology, we investigate whether the social scaffolding of a self-evolving multi-agent system (MAS), namely its team composition and structure of interdependence (e.g., collaboration, conformity, or competition), shapes how the team evolves. We present AGORA (Agents Growing through Organization and Relational Arrangements), a framework that varies the two axes independently across three evolution mechanisms. Across web search, codebase understanding, and document QA, we find that (1) evolution alone rarely helps, while the right scaffolding surpasses a strong agent evolved alone by up to 25 points; (2) it does so by moving authority to the most capable member while the others step back; and (3) this member, having grown within the team, outperforms the same model alone. Designing a self-evolving MAS thus requires designing its social scaffolding, which shapes not only how its agents learn, but who gets to lead.","tldr":"背景与问题：让团队反复修改技能和角色，不保证合作会改善；弱主席可能压制强成员，增加角色也可能只增加等待。论文把团队组成与决策权限作为独立变量，而非默认有效的背景。\n\n方法：固定个体演化机制，改变成员能力配比及信息共享、修改提案和决策规则；执行轨迹与同伴备忘进入下一轮，团队修改经验证集阻止明显退化。权重不变，部分技能和记忆更新由固定强模型完成。\n\n结果与结论：网页搜索中，合适配置较独自演化的强代理最高多25分；但另一模型家族未稳定重现该优势，角色扩张还伴随超时。领导集中并非普遍有效的组织规律。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得检验的是强成员能否获得有效经验并减少协调损耗，而非多代理是否天然更强。竞争条件直接安排按分数轮换主席，不能把全部权力转移解释成演化涌现。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 经验迁移; RSI 评测与迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称社会支架决定多智能体演化效果及领导权分配。本文证据：冻结权重，分别更新技能、记忆或提示，再根据同伴备忘修改团队；反馈包括自反思、任务评分和验证门控。相对 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）搜索工作流后微调共享权重，本篇控制团队能力组合与相互依赖规则，研究外部状态演化，没有匹配性能比较。编辑推断：组织条件的受控研究是具体推进，但竞争条件直接规定按分数轮换主席，领导权迁移不能全部算作自发发现；固定强模型承担部分更新，也不证明改进者递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19725","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19725v2","title":"TimeRSI: Towards Self-Improved Agentic Deployment for Time-Series Foundation Models","authors":"Haoxin Liu; Deqing Fu; Lucheng Fu; Yiqiao Jin; Rushi Qiang; Harshavardhan Kamarthi; B. Aditya Prakash","affiliations":"Georgia Institute of Technology；University of Southern California；Samay AI","abstract":"Time-series foundation models provide strong zero-shot forecast, but deployment for real-world applications still requires task-specific designs for model inputs and outputs. Direct inference can leave domain knowledge and recurring forecast errors unaddressed, while tailored pipelines require substantial human expertise and effort. We introduce TimeRSI, a self-improving agentic deployment system around frozen forecasting models. A coding agent translates task descriptions into executable pipeline changes. It tests each revision on historical forecasting windows and uses observed errors to guide subsequent revisions. During deployment, an adaptive selector chooses among the resulting pipelines using completed forecasts under similar conditions. Across 198 tasks on TIME and fev-bench, TimeRSI outperforms all submissions on six point and probabilistic forecasting metrics. Controlled comparisons support the value of feedback-guided revision over non-iterative pipeline search. Further experiments verify the generalization with different coding agents and forecasting models. Code is available at https://github.com/haoxin1998/TimeRSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：冻结时序模型不会自动利用节假日等任务知识，也不会自行修正重复误差；人工设计流水线昂贵，而平均最好的方案未必适合每个预测窗口。\n\n方法：编码代理在早期历史窗口执行候选代码，用预测误差和日志指导下一次修订，再用较晚窗口筛选部署方案。部署时根据相似且结果已完整揭晓的历史窗口选择流水线；此时代码固定，仅选择依据更新。\n\n结果与结论：198项任务中，同候选数的非迭代搜索弱于直接推理，反馈修订则改善结果；TIME 的平均绝对缩放误差相对降低1.52%。更换编码代理和预测骨干仍有收益，但候选数匹配未控制全部成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键不是多生成方案，而是让实际误差否定看似合理的领域改动。历史误差能指导部署工程，却不能保证分布突变后的收益，更未证明编码代理自身越来越会优化。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 反馈驱动更新; 跨任务迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称以 RSI 自动改进冻结预测模型的部署。本文证据：编码代理用历史窗口误差修改输入输出流水线，较晚历史时段用于选择候选；部署时只更新选择依据，不再修改代码。相对 Meta-Harness（arxiv:2603.28052）从代码、分数和轨迹搜索 harness，本篇加入按预测条件匹配历史表现的部署选择，并区分适配窗口与选择窗口。编辑推断：是任务专用流水线搜索的具体扩展，改进对象不是编码代理或其优化算法；同候选数对照不等于同总计算量。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19591","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19591v1","title":"L3M: A Verifiable Harness and Runtime for Self-Extending and Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Carson Eisenach; Robert Joseph George; Vincent Quenneville-Belair; Kate Gwimm; Dean Foster","affiliations":"Amazon","abstract":"The lasting gains in AI have come from methods that absorb more computation, and language models already scale computation within a call. Useful work, though, happens across calls: over hours or days, through tools and external systems, among many agents and the humans they work for, and increasingly through code the agents write themselves. Whether that work compounds is enabled by the harness around it, and the harness faces a constraint the model does not: of the three participants in such a computation, the human, the model and code, only the human's attention does not scale, so the computation can grow only if the human is not in every loop. L3M is a runtime built on that premise, written in Lean 4 so that one language implements the harness, states its invariants, and is the language agents extend it in. One computation spans humans, agents, models and code, and all of its state lives in Git: a rich state trajectory -- rather than a chat conversation -- is an object the runtime can resume, rewind, fork, compare and merge. Waiting, communication, delegation and undo are primitives, not patterns the model reasons through each time. When an agent works out a procedure, it can write it once as a sealed Lean program whose type is its permission request, and the harness offers it back as a tool -- machinery for the model to use. To take the human out of the loop, L3M uses reversibility to decide where that is safe: a tool's review tier follows from how far its effects can be undone, so agents act freely where the runtime can recover. Because the machinery can change, the properties that make this safe are stated as kernel-checked theorems about the code that runs. On Terminal-Bench, an untuned L3M reaches about two thirds of its (unsafe) shell-equipped pass rate using only safe (not needing human review) tools.","tldr":"背景与问题：长期代理若每次等待、协调和恢复都依赖模型推理与人工审批，计算扩张会受人的注意力限制；允许代理写新工具，又可能扩大其操作权限。\n\n方法：L3M 把状态和轨迹持久化，并允许代理将重复程序封装为新工具。程序类型声明所需权限，运行时限制其不超过既有授权；可恢复或权限已限定的操作减少审批，部分检查由 Lean 内核验证。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称仅用无需人工审查的工具，可达到带不安全 shell 配置约三分之二的通过率；可见片段缺少完整实验表，不能据此判断自扩展的独立收益。定理也依赖编译、提供者和操作系统等可信部分。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献是让能力增长与权限增长脱钩，而非认证代理会正确自改进。回滚本地文件不能撤回已经发出的外部请求，安全主张必须逐项对应可恢复范围和可信假设。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; Harness 递归演化; 预算与权限审计","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称提供可验证的自扩展运行时。本文证据：代理可把程序变成后续工具，类型声明权限需求，内核检查部分运行时代码性质；可撤销性与预先限定的能力决定审查层级。相对 Self-Evolving Agent Harness（arxiv:2610.18813）的修改对象及准入分类，本篇给出具体实现和不变量；相对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461）允许修改元程序，本篇重点是限制扩展权限，而非提高修改算法。编辑推断：执行结果、类型检查及审查支持扩展准入，但缺少多轮自扩展收益归因；局部安全性质不能覆盖可信编译、系统服务及程序语义正确性。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19581","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19581v1","title":"XferAgent: Cross-Agent Experience Transfer for Self-Improving LLM Agents","authors":"Weihao Li; Jun Bai; Shijie Chen; Qincheng Lu; Xinyu Wang; Ziyang Song","affiliations":"McGill University；Northwestern University；Mila – Quebec AI Institute；Ohio University","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents can reuse experience from prior task executions to improve performance on subsequent tasks. Although existing methods enable cross-agent experience sharing, differences in agents' execution histories and task requirements make shared experiences difficult to reuse effectively. We propose XferAgent, a framework for cross-agent experience transfer that organizes reusable experience in local and shared experience graphs. XferAgent reconciles compatible contributions from heterogeneous agents while avoiding unreliable merges. For each new task, it selects shared experiences and integrates them with the target agent's local experience to support task execution. Experiments across diverse task domains show improvements over representative memory-based methods and effective experience transfer between heterogeneous agent frameworks. Cumulative task success also increases over successive task passes as agents update and reuse their experiences.","tldr":"背景与问题：别的代理学到的经验可能有用，却未必适配接收者的工具和执行历史；只共享语义相似条目，容易合并不兼容经验或重复注入无效指导。\n\n方法：系统分别维护本地与共享经验图，保留来源并避免有歧义的合并。新任务结合相关性、其他代理的使用结果与本地结果选择经验；任务评分随后更新使用统计，并将新轨迹提炼成下一轮经验。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称跨任务和异构框架迁移优于记忆基线，但主要结果表未包含在片段中。跨框架实验增加贡献者时，也同步增加源任务总暴露量，不能将收益全部归于代理多样性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，迁移价值必须由接收者校准，不能直接照搬贡献者的成功率。不过给所有已注入经验记同一个任务结果，仍无法区分谁真正有用；重复任务的累计成功也不等于未见任务泛化。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; RSI 评测与迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称改善异构代理间经验迁移。本文证据：本地和共享图保存成功或失败经验，按相似性及匹配歧义合并，结合其他代理与本地使用结果排序；任务结束后更新被注入经验的统计并写入新经验。相对 STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）处理分层抽象、遗忘及方向混淆，本篇侧重跨代理来源和本地—共享效用融合；相对 MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492），本篇不训练经验学习行为。编辑推断：闭环更新记忆和效用估计，不更新合并或检索算法；使用后成功只是关联反馈，不等于经验的因果贡献。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19424","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19424v1","title":"VideoHarness-SRSI: Structured Recursive Self-Improvement for Video Understanding Harness","authors":"Zihao Lin; Haoyu Dong; Haobo Xu; Chi-Chih Chang; Xuying Ning; Yinglong Xia; Shuang Yang; Zhuokai Zhao; Xinying Song; Dongfang Liu; Lifu Huang; Yang Song; Qifan Wang","affiliations":"University of California, Davis；Meta MRS Research；Duke University；University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign；Cornell University；Purdue University","abstract":"LLM system capabilities depend not only on model parameters but also on the executable harnesses that organize information acquisition, tool use, reasoning, and memory. Recursive harness evolution can automate their design, but how it can reliably discover generalizable systems from limited, noisy, and repeatedly reused feedback remains unclear. We study this question in agentic video understanding, where rich multimodal evidence and coupled mechanisms make harness optimization challenging. We first introduce VideoHarness-BRSI, a recursive self-improvement framework that evolves video harnesses around a frozen vision-language model. Analyzing over 4,000 evolved candidates, we find it competitive with hand-engineered systems but identify three interconnected failure modes: validation overfitting, search-budget dilution, and the early-experience trap. We trace all three to a common root: the same imperfect validation evidence drives both harness revisions and the proposer's search strategy. We therefore propose VideoHarness-SRSI, an evidence-governed framework in which every search decision rests on evidence that is transferable, sufficient, and gathered before the search commits. It restricts the proposer to content-free feedback, informs exploration with instrumented warm-up experiments, and develops mechanisms in isolated probe-race branches before factorial composition and joint refinement. Across four video understanding benchmarks, VideoHarness-SRSI improves the equally weighted mean held-out score by 6.2% relative to VideoHarness-BRSI and reduces the mean validation-test gap by 37.9%. Reliable harness evolution thus depends on how search is organized and informed, not only on how well it optimizes validation performance.","tldr":"背景与问题：有限验证集同时决定保留哪个 harness、下一步探索什么；视频和题目细节会诱导样本特化，早期噪声还可能让提案者过早放弃有效机制。\n\n方法：固定视觉语言模型，只向提案者开放汇总分数和不含验证内容的执行统计。先做受控预实验，再让机制在独立分支积累证据，最后测试组合及相互作用，减少一次联合修改导致的归因混淆。\n\n结果与结论：四个视频基准上，相对基础演化流程，平均留出得分相对提高6.2%，验证—测试差距缩小37.9%。内容暴露对照支持过拟合诊断，但片段不足以核对完整消融和总成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，更多反馈并非总是更好：能解释已见题目的信息，也能帮助记住验证集。真正应优化的是证据对未见任务的预测力；屏蔽内容仍不能自动消除反复查询汇总分数带来的选择偏差。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"Harness 递归演化; RSI 评测与迁移; 选择误差","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过证据治理提高视频 harness 演化的泛化性。本文证据：固定视觉语言骨干，限制提案者接触验证内容，先以受控试验探索机制，再隔离演化并检验组合；候选和评估记录影响后续搜索。相对 Meta-Harness（arxiv:2603.28052）强调读取完整历史代码和轨迹，本篇识别内容暴露可能产生的过拟合，并改变反馈接口及搜索组织。编辑推断：这是对既有 harness 搜索的实质修正，但设计更好的固定搜索流程，不等于搜索器自身递归进化；截断材料不足以核对完整预算和消融。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19422","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19422v1","title":"AgentSafeEvo: Adversarial Co-Evolution for LLM Agent Safety","authors":"Chenxu Wang; Xiaoyu Wen; Han Qi; Ziyuan Zhou; Cheng Jin; Chaochao Lu; Qiaosheng Zhang","affiliations":"Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory；Fudan University；Shanghai Jiaotong University；Zhejiang University","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents accomplish complex tasks through multi-turn interactions with external tools. However, malicious content embedded in user queries, tool descriptions, or environment observations can manipulate their decisions and induce unsafe actions. Adversarial co-evolution has emerged as an effective approach to strengthening LLM safety, but existing work primarily focuses on language-level safety or indirect prompt injection in web tasks. In this paper, we introduce AgentSafeEvo, a co-evolutionary reinforcement learning framework for agent safety built on an attacker-defender game spanning diverse tasks and attack types. The attacker learns to construct adversarial agent tasks that expose weaknesses in the defender's tool use, while the defender learns to complete tasks safely under these attacks. We further introduce learnability-guided task weighting, which uses within-task defender-reward variability to adjust each task's contribution to attacker and defender updates. Extensive experiments on agent safety and general capability benchmarks demonstrate that our method improves adversarial robustness while maintaining general agent capabilities.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定攻击集不会随防御者变强而暴露新弱点；工具代理还会从请求、工具说明和环境观察受到攻击，仅训练安全措辞不足以保证安全行动。\n\n方法：攻击者学习构造完整对抗任务，防御者学习在其中完成合法要求。固定模型分别判断轨迹安全性和效用，反馈更新双方；对同任务多次执行中结果差异较大的任务加权，避免只追求让防御者全败。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称安全鲁棒性改善且保持一般能力；片段提供四类安全基准与通用能力协议，但主要结果和加权消融被省略，无法核对幅度及独立贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可学习攻击应产生可区分的行为后果，而非单纯最难。不过奖励变化也可能来自评判噪声；训练依赖模型判断，尚需独立检查安全评分、合法任务完成与过度拒绝之间的关系。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"递归安全改进; 红队反馈; 自适应课程与数据合成","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称将对抗共演化扩展至多类工具交互任务。本文证据：攻击者生成用户请求、工具定义与观察，防御者执行；固定模型判断安全与合法任务完成情况，双方据此强化学习，组内奖励变化用于任务加权。相对 ReSI（arxiv:2610.12233）红队探测后筛选训练配方，本篇直接训练攻击任务生成者和防御策略；相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）的可教性共训练，本篇采用对抗目标和安全—效用模型奖励。编辑推断：经验生成器参与学习，但奖励波动只是可学习性代理，其校准及奖励投机防护在可见片段中未充分建立。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19386","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.19386v1","title":"STRATA: Self-Maintaining Structured Experience Graphs for Self-Evolving Language Agents","authors":"Guanhua Zhu; Hanwen Li; Zhi Wei; Mengnan Du; Chenxi Yuan","affiliations":"New Jersey Institute of Technology；The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen","abstract":"Large language model (LLM) agents can self-evolve at test time by accumulating experience: retrieving relevant memories before acting and writing new lessons back afterwards. Yet most are single-level: trajectories, distilled workflows and reasoning items all land in one undifferentiated pool indexed by embedding similarity, with no typed abstraction hierarchy. They never forget or deduplicate, and are prone to negative transfer, where a superficially similar but directionally opposite experience is recalled and its concrete steps are copied verbatim, actively harming the agent. We introduce STRATA, a structured, outcome-grounded, self-maintaining memory that organizes experience into a three-layer graph of atomic skills and code snippets, task workflows and generalized meta-frameworks, connected by typed edges. STRATA maintains itself through five mechanisms sharing one similarity geometry: a multi-dimensional similarity that scores retrieval by operation and target; a typed reflector crystallizing procedures from successes and pitfalls from failures; community detection that induces meta-frameworks; pressure-triggered garbage collection with articulation-point protection; and contrast edges that flag confusable, direction-opposite experiences. Across four interactive benchmarks (AppWorld, WebArena, ALFWorld, ScienceWorld), two frozen backbones and seven baselines, STRATA attains the best average score while simultaneously using the lowest latency and fewest environment steps of any memory-augmented method, and 44% fewer lines of injected memory than the most context-hungry baseline. We isolate two failure modes of prior memories: single-level memory degrades sharply as the task set grows, and single-level concrete memories suffer catastrophic negative transfer, which contrast edges repair, lifting ScienceWorld from 78.7 to 96.7 within the same system.","tldr":"背景与问题：把具体操作、任务流程和一般原则混在相似度记忆池里，会随规模增长稀释检索；更危险的是，表面相似但方向相反的程序可能被直接执行。\n\n方法：冻结模型，将经验组织成技能、流程和抽象原则，并按任务结果写回：成功产生可复用程序，失败只添加避坑提示。检索同时关注操作与目标，召回相反经验时明确警告，定期压缩和删除冗余流程。\n\n结果与结论：四个互动基准、两个骨干上，摘要称平均表现及效率优于记忆基线；ScienceWorld 同系统加入对比关系后，得分从78.7升至96.7。完整消融表缺失，尚不能核对各机制贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，经验被执行时，错误召回的代价高于一般检索问答。方向识别因此可能比继续扩库更关键；但当前对比关系依赖固定反义操作词表，开放语义下能否覆盖混淆尚未验证。","published_at":"2026-10-14","topics":"经验迁移; 外部记忆与规则更新; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称以分层、可维护经验图减少记忆扩张和负迁移。本文证据：冻结骨干，成功轨迹形成程序，失败只附警示；抽象、合并和删除改变后续检索，并以固定反向操作词表建立对比边。相对 XferAgent（arxiv:2610.19581）侧重异构代理的共享统计，本篇处理经验库的层次与反向程序混淆；相对 MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492）训练经验行为，本篇主要修改外部结构。编辑推断：同系统方向混淆修复比总体排名更能定位贡献，但维护规则固定，不能称为记忆管理器递归增强。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18868","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18868v1","title":"Tev: Scaling Long-Horizon Agentic Environments with Dense Progress Rewards","authors":"Wenbo Hu; Shraman Pramanick; Krishna Kumar Singh; Nanyun Peng; Kai-Wei Chang; Yong Jae Lee","affiliations":"Adobe Research；University of California, Los Angeles","abstract":"Long-horizon agents have drawn growing attention for their ability to work autonomously -- from hours to days -- on economically valuable tasks, a capability essential to automated discovery and recursive self-improvement (RSI). Yet open-source models still struggle on long-horizon tasks, largely for lack of both training data and a working recipe, and scaling both is hard: long, complex tasks are difficult to curate and verify, and their rewards are sparse. We address both. First, we introduce Tev-Gym, the first long-horizon agent training dataset with verifiable, dense, progressive rewards -- 1,170 verified task environments across 7 domains. It is built on a latent-world-first approach that first constructs a latent world: a complete and correct hidden specification of the task domain, workflow, and expected state after each step. Each task is then progressively rendered from this specification into an agent-facing environment, enabling controllable complexity and a natural progress metric. Second, we turn this metric into a training recipe: via progress-potential reward shaping (PPRS), we convert progress into a dense per-step reward that improves training efficiency and makes otherwise-intractable tasks trainable. Training with this recipe yields Tev-27B, which achieves substantial gains on the Agents' Last Exam computing and math sciences domains (ALE-CM), matching GPT-6 Astra and Claude Opus 5 at Pass@5. Despite training only on ALE-related data, it generalizes to the Terminal-Bench (TB) 3.0 and 4.0 subsets, surpassing GLM 5.2 and Gemini 3.7 Flash, and reaches Claude Opus 4.8-level performance on middle-horizon tasks such as TB 2.1.","tldr":"背景与问题：长程任务里，同组轨迹经常全部失败，终局二元奖励无法区分接近完成和毫无进展，导致组相对强化学习缺少梯度。\n\n方法：先构造已知正确的潜在世界，再从同一世界生成受损输入、目标和阶段检查，按工作区正确程度计进度。训练奖励额外保留最终进度，使未完成轨迹也能产生差异；它不是保证原最优策略不变的传统塑形。\n\n结果与结论：训练所得27B模型在指定长程计算与数学任务上，Pass@5 相对基座提高65%；还报告终端子集迁移。可见材料未给出主要训练消融，不能将全部收益归于稠密奖励。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共同真值来源有助于避免分别生成任务和检查器造成的工件失配。但代理目标仍被改变，部分进度奖励可能影响策略取舍；这属于训练基础，而非已展示的递归自改进。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 长程交互学习; 奖励信号","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称构建首个带可验证稠密进度奖励的长程训练集。本文证据：从预先确定的潜在世界生成任务、真值和阶段检查，再用最终进度补充终局奖励。相对 AutoEnvScaling（arxiv:2610.14163）让 solver 轨迹指导下一轮环境构建，本篇强调共同真值锚点和固定生成程序；相对 RewardWeaver（arxiv:2610.10120）动态选择过程奖励，本篇使用预定义可执行进度。编辑推断：是 RSI 的训练基础设施，而非环境或训练器自改进闭环，尚未展示生成策略随学习者反馈更新。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18845","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18845v2","title":"The Last Remote Sensing Model Built by Humans? Casting Any Earth Observation Task as Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Sijie Zhao; Zeqi Zhou; Heli Qi; Xuanchao Fu; Zhuo Zheng; Junshi Xia; Junjue Wang; Weihao Xuan; Naoto Yokoya","affiliations":"The University of Tokyo；RIKEN；Stanford University","abstract":"Earth observation (EO) models are still built by hand. For each new task, experts design a training recipe and tune it against a benchmark. We show that this loop can be handed to an agent. Any verifiable task can be cast as a harness and a verifier, where the harness defines what the agent may use and the verifier defines what counts as success. Every EO task can be made verifiable, through labeled benchmarks, independent sensors, physical models or the repeated observation of the same place. Given only these two components, a general-purpose coding agent builds the EO model and improves it recursively on its own outputs. Settings long treated as separate research problems, from learning with a handful of labels to adapting across domains, become choices of harness and verifier. On six EO benchmarks spanning optical, SAR and multispectral time-series imagery, with outputs that range from land-cover maps and ship instances to canopy heights and answers about large images, agent-built models surpass the state of the art on every one, and on land-cover mapping, they do so from 11% of the training labels. This establishes a new paradigm for EO, in which people design harnesses and verifiers and agents build the models, so EO models improve as agents do.","tldr":"背景与问题：新遥感任务往往需要专家重选模型和训练配方，少标签设置尤其依赖工程经验；论文试图把设计工作交给能运行实验的编码代理。\n\n方法：人固定可用数据、模型与预算，用封闭验证器只返回分数；代理自行写训练代码，并将已训练模型的预测或检查点用于后继模型，按分数选择保留。最终模型另在隐藏测试集评估。\n\n结果与结论：材料称六个遥感基准均超过所列已有方法，部分任务只需少量训练标签；每次运行上限为四张GB200、12小时。实验验证器仍使用基准标签，不能据此证明所有遥感任务都有可靠验证方式。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，减少训练标注不等于消除监督需求，部分成本转移到了验证标签与任务接口。递归发生在目标模型的自训练谱系，尚无证据表明编码代理或产生改进的规则也持续变强。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"RSI 研究环境与评测; 自主后训练; 反馈驱动更新","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称任何地球观测任务都可转为 harness 与 verifier，并由代理递归构建模型。本文证据：编码代理在封闭环境内写训练代码，以隐藏验证分数筛选，并利用此前模型预测、检查点或校准输出训练后继。相对 Athanor（arxiv:2610.21055）的自主语言模型后训练，本篇扩展到多传感器遥感及标签预算；相对 TimeRSI（arxiv:2610.19725）只改冻结骨干的部署，本篇多数任务允许训练目标模型。编辑推断：自训练谱系明确，但研究者自身未被更新；独立传感器和物理验证主要是论述，实验反馈仍来自基准标签。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18842","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18842v1","title":"Who Improves the Robot? Toward Physical Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Hai Zhou; Fan Yang; Zeyi Chen; Lejun Zhang; Chenyang Fu; Jianping Li; Jiayi Zhu; Xianyang Liu; Yingxuan Yang; Lili Meng; Lu Wang; Xinyang Han; Jiankai Sun; Weirui Ye; Guanchu Wang; Wanhua Li; Ming Zhou; Boyi Li; Ming Jin; Kun Shao; Muhao Chen; Guang Chen; Lei Ma; Joey Tianyi Zhou; Costas Spanos; Xia Hu; Mac Schwager; Weinan Zhang; Qian Feng; Shangding Gu","affiliations":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University；Google；Microsoft；University of California, Berkeley；Stanford University；Massachusetts Institute of Technology；Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory；Nanyang Technological University；Nvidia；Virginia Tech；Xiaomi；University of California, Davis；Tongji University；University of Tokyo；Singapore Management University；Technical University of Munich","abstract":"Robots are increasingly autonomous in task execution, yet their improvement remains largely human-driven. This study investigates Physical Recursive Self-Improvement (Physical RSI), in which physical experience guides lasting updates to both a robot's capabilities and its improvement procedure, making subsequent improvement more effective across tasks. Physical RSI faces challenges from noisy observations, continuous dynamics, costly trials, and irreversible consequences. We present an L0-L5 framework that differentiates capability-level from meta-level updates and within-task from across-task gains, reserving L5 for independently verified recursive gain. We study existing methods around harness adaptation and model training, alongside safety and control mechanisms that govern execution and successive updates. Our analysis reveals that, despite substantial progress in self-improvement, the surveyed literature does not yet demonstrate Physical RSI as defined by our framework. We identify research priorities in reliable feedback, causal attribution, safety preservation, and benchmarking, outlining a path toward robots that autonomously improve how they learn while ensuring safety. The GitHub repository for Physical RSI is available at https://github.com/SAIL-Research-Lab/Physical-RSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人能自主执行，不代表能自主改进；即使技能越积越多，也可能只是固定更新流程不断运行，而非学习过程本身变得更有效。\n\n方法：论文将执行系统与改进程序分开，用L0—L5区分能力更新、元级更新及跨任务收益。最高等级要求从相同起点和经验出发，在匹配预算下由独立评估比较新旧改进程序；物理反馈可来自真实交互或物理仿真。\n\n结果与结论：这是一项框架与综述工作，不提供达到最高等级的新系统。其判断是所审阅文献尚未满足该定义的物理 RSI 证据要求，不能扩展成对全部机器人研究的否定。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，递归主张最关键的对照是“更新后的改进程序能否产生更好的后续改进”，而非机器人最终更强。独立评测还须防止标准随轮次改变，否则所谓递归增益可能只是目标漂移。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 具身 RSI; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称建立 Physical RSI 的定义、分级和独立评测框架。本文证据是任务执行系统与改进程序的区分，以及从同一代系统、同一经验和同预算比较新旧改进程序的要求，不是已实现递归收益的实验。相对 MC-EvoBench（arxiv:2610.13829）隔离经验迁移混淆，本篇进一步要求元级更新及其后续收益；相对 Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461）可编辑元程序，本篇强调物理证据、跨任务和独立评价。编辑推断：贡献主要是审计标准，不能把其综述范围内未发现证据写成物理 RSI 不可能。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18813","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18813v1","title":"Self-Evolving Agent Harness","authors":"Chuyang Wei; Haoxiang Guan; Minghang Zhu; Kexin Zhou; Jiyan He; Xiren Zhou; Huanhuan Chen; Yifei Shen","affiliations":"Zhongguancun Academy；University of Science and Technology of China；Zhongguancun Institute of Artificial Intelligence","abstract":"Harness self-evolution revises an agent's software scaffolding, including prompts, memory, workflows, and executable components, while keeping model weights fixed. We formalize a feedback-driven process in which accepted revisions persist across runs. The framework separates update targets from proposal and admission mechanisms. It distinguishes changes to interpreted state from revisions to tools and code, repository-level control logic, and plugin composition. We characterize search through evolutionary optimization and examine its reliability through continual PAC-learning. Under explicit assumptions, the analysis yields an expected generalization bound, a retention bound conditional on historical regression budgets, and a high-probability admission rule using fresh, independent validation data. We examine how persistent harness revisions affect knowledge sharing and organizational workflows, with implications for scientific reliability, physical safety, and institutional accountability. Cases from prior work illustrate model--harness co-design, distributed execution, and plugin reuse. Reliable deployment requires continual validation as task distributions and evaluators change, with independent safeguards for learning, runtime privileges, and consequential actions. We provide a comprehensive 66-page discussion of related work, theory, algorithms, evaluation, applications, and the broader impact of Harness RSI, together with continuously updated code and supplementary materials, at https://github.com/zgcagi/Harness-RSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：提示、记忆、工具实现和运行时控制都可能被称为 harness 演化，但修改边界及风险不同；仅有修订过程，也不代表产生了可保留的性能收益。\n\n方法：论文按被继承的状态分类，分开描述修改对象、候选生成和准入。模型固定，执行反馈驱动候选，获准版本跨运行加载；摘要再提出依赖明确假设的泛化、回归保留及独立验证准入界。\n\n结果与结论：可见正文主要是定义、分类和引用案例，并非新的匹配实验。所给文本虽未标截断，却未包含摘要承诺的理论正文，因此不能核验定理条件；插件成本案例还明确存在两套统计不一致。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，最有用的区分是“发生演化”和“经比较证明改进”。修改解释态、可执行代码与更新算法应分别记账；独立验证数据的理论要求，也不能直接套到反复复用同一验证集的搜索。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"Harness 递归演化; RSI 可证伪性与治理; 验证理论","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称提供持久 harness 演化的操作分类及条件理论。本文证据明确区分修改对象、提案和准入，并指出更新机制自身修改是额外递归层；反馈可来自环境、自动评估或人类。相对 Self-Harness（arxiv:2606.09498）的失败挖掘—提案—回归测试实现，本篇是抽象归纳，不是新实验系统；相对 arxiv:2610.10611 的有界验证类分析，本篇摘要提出稳定性和独立验证样本下的统计保证。编辑推断：理论正文未出现在提供文本中，无法核查假设或证明；引用案例不能记作本文新实验。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18792","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18792v1","title":"SEAR: Self-Evolving Agentic Robotics","authors":"Xinyi Wang; Bangzheng Li; Hanyu Wang; Lin Zhang; Andrea Yaoyun Cui; Zhenggang Tang; Shyamal Buch; Dejia Xu","affiliations":"Luma AI","abstract":"Frontier language-model agents can now improve robots on their own: they write control code, test it, and keep what works as skills and memories for the next task. We introduce SEAR (Self-Evolving Agentic Robotics), a framework and benchmark built around two questions. Is the agent really learning, or just trying more often? And does what it learns still help on new tasks, in a new simulator, and on a real robot? The framework runs an agent in three modes: it writes code that becomes the policy (code-as-policy), acts live in the control loop (agent-as-policy), or works as a researcher that fine-tunes a vision-language-action model (auto-research). The benchmark adds controls that separate retained experience from repeated attempts, familiar tasks, privileged simulator state, larger budgets, and luck. Across seven frontier language models, 330 simulated and five physical tasks, and over four years of agent runtime, we highlight three findings. First, the learning curve of a robotic agent depends both on the overall time budget and the task difficulty relative to model capability. Harder tasks make longer sessions worthwhile; on easier tasks, re-rolling short attempts does just as well. Second, control code and shared routines transfer across tasks and simulators, while task-specific solutions do not. On a real robot, we observe a performance gap between agent-designed practice and novel human-designed scenes. Third, different models evolve more effectively in different ways. Some do best acting live, others writing code first. And a text-only model keeps pace with a comparable multimodal one: perception helps with error assessment, but agentic reasoning and tool use can matter more. We release the benchmark and codebase to support future research.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人成功率随时间上升，可能只是多次重试、熟悉初始状态或更大预算，不能直接证明保留了可迁移能力。\n\n方法：SEAR 将写控制程序、在线行动和自主微调纳入同一框架；用空技能库、同总预算短重启和隐藏初始状态评分分离继承与重采样。跨任务只保留代码技能和文字记忆，自动研究产生的权重不延续。\n\n结果与结论：RoboLab 中，一个模型无库成功率46.9%，继承自身库反而退化，改用其他模型的库则达60.6%。经验质量而非有无经验决定收益；硬件上练习成功也高于新场景表现。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，是否值得持续修改，取决于首次成功时间能否落在短尝试预算内，不能只按任务难度决定。封闭评分仍发现资产文件泄露等漏洞，且模型与工具绑定，跨模型排名并非纯模型能力比较。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"RSI 评测与迁移; 具身持续学习评测; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称用统一框架审计机器人代理是否真正学习及迁移。本文证据：代码策略、在线代理和自主微调三模式，封闭评判、匹配开发时间、空库和分预算重启对照；跨任务继承技能与记忆，而不继承自动研究模式的权重及数据。相对 MC-EvoBench（arxiv:2610.13829）在 Minecraft 隔离状态混淆，本篇扩展到机器人策略、多模拟器和硬件；相对 EmbodiedRSI（arxiv:2610.10498）提出主动实验机制，本篇重点在归因协议。编辑推断：为既有迁移审计提供更广的具体实证，但完整共演化循环仍列为提案。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18484","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18484v2","title":"ReTerm: Recovery Training for Self-Improving Terminal Agents","authors":"Wei Xie; Kaituo Feng; Shiming Fu; Yong Liu; Xiangyu Yue; Shuangjia Zheng","affiliations":"Fudan University；MMLab, The Chinese University of Hong Kong；Shanghai Jiao Tong University","abstract":"Terminal agents have shown strong abilities in complex coding tasks. However, they often struggle to recover from errors during long-running execution (e.g., command errors, faulty implementations), eventually leading to task failures. To this end, we present ReTerm, a self-improving terminal agent trained by learning how to recover from its own failed terminal tasks. To support its training, we construct a customized data pipeline and produce ReTerm-10K, a high-quality dataset that provides effective recovery demonstrations for SFT cold start. Furthermore, we propose ReTerm-GRPO, an online RL algorithm that forks from the agent's own failure states to generate multiple independent self-recovery attempts. By learning from whether these attempts successfully complete the task, the agent self-improves through its own recovery experience. Built on Qwen3.5-9B, our ReTerm-9B achieves 34.8% Pass@1 on Terminal-Bench 2.0, improving over the base model by 14.6 points. Further analysis shows that our method achieves consistently higher recovery rates across diverse error categories compared with standard GRPO training. All code, data and model are released at https://github.com/twothsnd/ReTerm.","tldr":"背景与问题：终端代理执行错误后会改变文件和环境，重新从干净状态训练未必教会它恢复；人工注入的错误又可能偏离当前策略真正会犯的错。\n\n方法：先保存学生失败后的环境快照，让强教师生成经验证的恢复示范。在线训练再从当前策略产生的失败状态分叉多次续做，用最终任务验证结果比较恢复行为；近期失败进入队列，随策略变化刷新训练起点。\n\n结果与结论：Terminal-Bench 2.0 的Pass@1 达34.8%，较基座多14.6个百分点；材料称各错误类别恢复率优于普通GRPO。该总增益同时包含教师示范与强化学习，片段缺少完整消融和成本对照。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败不只是负样本，也是可复用的训练初始状态。其价值取决于能否准确恢复环境；这训练的是纠错策略，不代表更新算法自身进化，也不能由恢复旧任务直接推断未见故障泛化。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"失败驱动的递归更新; 自进化策略训练; 终端智能体","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称从代理自身失败状态学习恢复。本文证据：强教师从学生失败快照生成通过验证的冷启动轨迹；在线阶段当前策略从同一失败状态分叉，以任务验证结果训练恢复行为，近期失败队列影响后续学习。相对 CoTrace（arxiv:2610.10426）把失败主要用于 harness 修订、匹配成功轨迹用于训练，本篇直接将失败后的恢复状态作为策略训练分布。编辑推断：是失败驱动训练的具体推进，训练器本身固定；总分增长包含教师 SFT 和在线 RL，不应全部归于分叉机制。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18355","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18355v2","title":"ABot-ER: Unified Embodied Reasoning through Agentic Data-Model Co-Evolution","authors":"Qiuyu Ding; Heng-Da Xu; Changda Xia; Jiajun Shen; Zihao Guan; Zhengchen Yuan; Jianfang Zhang; Di Yang; Jiayi Tian; Yuting Xu; Fei Wang; Shiao Liu; Wei Zhang; Xiaolong Wu; Wenbin Tang; Zedong Chu; Mu Xu","affiliations":"","abstract":"We introduce ABot Embodied Reasoning (ABot-ER), a unified embodied reasoning foundation model that breaks the tension between breadth and depth in embodied reasoning. Embodied intelligence demands the joint mastery of perception, planning, and execution, yet reconciling generality with specialization across this spectrum remains an open challenge. Within a single unified model, ABot-ER commands specialist-level depth across all three competencies, spanning spatial, scene, and temporal reasoning in perception; long-horizon action organization in planning; and point grounding and affordance in execution. The Agentic Data-Model Self-Evolution Engine continuously adapts data strategies to the model's evolving capability state. The Task-Conditioned Adaptive Training Strategy uses task tokens to activate lightweight low-rank residuals over a shared backbone, separating updates from heterogeneous output formats while retaining shared embodied knowledge. Across a systematic evaluation on twelve benchmarks covering three core competencies and five capability dimensions, ABot-ER achieves state-of-the-art overall performance across perception, planning, and execution within a unified parametric framework, demonstrating that breadth and depth can coexist in unified embodied reasoning.","tldr":"背景与问题：具身感知、规划与交互定位进步速度不同，固定数据比例会偏离当前短板；语义和动作空间输出共享参数，还可能互相干扰。\n\n方法：评估结果触发能力诊断，修订监督内容与混合比例，经固定规则筛选后训练并再评估；任务条件残差分担异构输出需求。改变的是语料和权重，数据准入规则及学习算法本身不随轮次学习。\n\n结果与结论：材料称十二个基准的各能力汇总领先；更关键的是，最终语料单次训练能匹敌六轮模型，累计后训练量仅五分之一。历史包含重启、跳过检查点和污染修复，不是一条连续增强链。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，证据更支持发现了可复用的数据配方，而非每轮继承权重不可替代。应分开计算数据清洗、预算扩大和反馈适配的贡献；交互定位得分也不能等同真实机器人运动控制能力。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 具身 RSI","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称数据—模型共演化缓解能力差异和异构任务干扰。本文证据：能力诊断驱动数据内容及混合比例修订，固定门控筛选，模型训练结果进入下轮；任务条件残差提供输出类型专用容量。相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）用同批交互更新合成器和求解器，本篇没有训练数据修订者；相对 ClawLoop（arxiv:2610.14118），同属诊断驱动任务调整，但面向具身监督数据。编辑推断：最终语料单次训练匹敌多轮结果，支持数据配方价值，不能证明连续权重递归必要性；历史还包含污染修复、重启及分支。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18097","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18097v1","title":"APT: Feedback-Driven Agentic Post-Training for Text-to-Image Generation","authors":"Sirui Zhang; Fangyun Wei; Dong Chen; Jinjing Zhao; Yitong Wang; Yunuo Chen; Baining Guo; Zheng-Jun Zha","affiliations":"University of Science and Technology of China；Microsoft Research Asia；University of Sydney；Fudan University；Shanghai Jiao Tong University","abstract":"Post-training is crucial for improving text-to-image models, yet existing pipelines typically rely on manually curated training data and fixed training distributions. We introduce APT (Agentic Post-Training), a fully automated framework that adaptively post-trains a base model according to its evolving capability profile. APT coordinates three agents to construct evaluation sets from user requirements, diagnose model-specific strengths and failure modes, and generate reinforcement learning data with an adaptive prompt distribution that emphasizes underperforming capabilities. By repeatedly evaluating, diagnosing, and updating the generator, APT lets the current model's behavior shape its next training tasks, forming a feedback loop inspired by recursive self-improvement. For general-purpose settings without user-specified evaluation scenarios, we further develop an evaluation harness that enables broad and diverse evaluation set generation. Experiments across multiple base models, benchmarks, and generation architectures demonstrate that APT is model-agnostic, benchmark-agnostic, architecture-agnostic, and fully automated.","tldr":"背景与问题：不同图像模型的计数、文字和空间关系短板不同，统一人工训练集未必适配；模型变强后，训练优先级也应重新判断。\n\n方法：预先生成固定的提示—评分准则诊断集，用同一视觉语言评估器诊断与给训练奖励。数据代理据当前失败生成下一轮提示，主要针对弱项，也保留其他能力；强化学习更新图像模型后再次诊断。\n\n结果与结论：Lens 上，保留反馈循环的GenEval 为0.859，去掉后为0.844，但OneIG均值持平；只练难项在后者甚至更高。实验支持部分收益，不能据此宣称反馈循环或混合采样在所有指标上必要。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，自适应训练价值应由跨指标权衡检验，而非自动化程度代替证据。诊断与奖励共用评估器，可能共同放大其盲点；这里更新的是生成器和课程，不是诊断者或教学策略本身。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 诊断反馈闭环","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称让图像生成器的能力变化指导自动后训练。本文证据：固定诊断集、固定视觉语言评估器生成短板反馈，数据代理调整下一轮提示分布，强化学习更新生成器。相对 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）共同训练合成与求解策略，本篇生成和诊断代理固定；相对 ABot-ER（arxiv:2610.18355）诊断驱动具身监督语料修订，本篇使用模型评分的图像奖励。编辑推断：是自适应课程向图像后训练的扩展，非改进算法递归增强；循环消融收益不一致，同源诊断和奖励的误差校准及抗投机证据不足。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18083","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18083v1","title":"AReaL-RSI: Adaptive Scaling and Coordination of Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Wenhao Zhou; Jiajun Song; Haitao Wang; Zipeng Qiu; Yingqi Peng; Ruida Xu; Jiale Li; Wenshuang Li; Shusheng Xu; Wei Dong; Hao Dai; Tongkai Yang; Yi Gao; Binhang Yuan","affiliations":"Ant Group；Zhejiang University；HKUST","abstract":"Scaling recursive self-improvement requires additional computation to produce useful research progress in reaching persistent objectives. Intuitively, more researcher agents can explore more hypotheses, but early evaluation scores might misrepresent their promise, shared findings could lose their applicability conditions, and useful procedures could remain confined to completed investigations. In this paper, we present AReaL-RSI, a framework for organizing a persistent research team of agents without updating backbone LLM weights. We formulate the scaling problem in terms of evaluated outcomes and whole-system resource expenditure. Concretely, a leader agent selects task-appropriate research orientations and guides ongoing investigations; conditional memory sharing distinguishes unresolved problems from supported findings and enables recipient adaptation. During recursive evolution, after each campaign, evidence-based review revises researcher orientation, knowledge, and skills for later campaigns. Experiments compare AReaL-RSI with Codex-Goal on downstream harness optimization, GPU kernel optimization, and AI research tasks using two backbones. Under the reported resource allocations, AReaL-RSI improves Terminal Bench performance by 2.2 percentage points for each backbone and increases mean KernelBench speedup by 32.2-36.8%; further scalability comparisons favor the design of AReaL-RSI over native scaling: combining experience sharing with specialized researcher roles yields 1.9-27.5% lower kernel latency than independent exploration and 1.3-33.9% lower latency than sharing alone across all seven comparable task-backbone pairs.","tldr":"背景与问题：增加研究agent不一定增加有效进展：早期低分可能掩盖好想法，广播未确认诊断会使探索同质化，单次成功也不会自动变成下一次研究的方法。\n\n方法：AReaL-RSI让leader依据实验记录协调持续研究者，共享时保留发现的条件与不确定性，限制未解决问题的主动传播。活动结束后再把证据提炼成研究方向、知识和技能，供后续团队使用；骨干与leader策略不变。\n\n结果与结论：给定资源配置下，相对Codex-Goal，两种骨干的Terminal Bench成绩均增加2.2个百分点；内核实验中，分工加共享优于独立探索和仅共享。主要实验段落缺失，无法完整核对成本与跨活动继承收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键区别是共享有适用条件的证据，而非共享全部历史。正面标签的程序检查只确认来源，不认证结论；harness发布也不要求未来任务增益，因此配置可继承不能直接算作研究程序已变强。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 预算受限研究搜索; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过团队协调、条件式经验共享和跨活动研究者harness修订组织RSI扩展。本文证据表明，实验记录驱动研究方向、知识与技能更新，但leader策略及编排不变；发布检查不要求执行脚本或证明未来收益。相对RSIFlow（arxiv:2610.21791）修改元harness以改善干预编排，本篇主要改变研究者配置与团队内信息传播；相对Hyperagents（arxiv:2603.19461），并未开放修改元级程序。编辑推断：这是协调与经验继承的具体推进，不是协调器自身递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17718","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.17718v1","title":"ECG-RSI: Recursive Self-Improvement through Targeted Electrocardiogram Waveform Evolution","authors":"Xiaoliang Wang; Zhuo Chen; Chuanyang Zheng; Jiangwei Lao; Quanbin Wang; Honglin Lin; Jiajia Liu; Zhihong Lu; Hao Jin; Jian Wang; Lijun Wu","affiliations":"","abstract":"Electrocardiogram (ECG) models need supervision that targets evolving weaknesses and remains faithful to waveform evidence. We introduce ECG-RSI, a recursive self-improvement framework combining verified waveform synthesis with feedback-guided intervention search. Signal remeasurement verifies waveform edits; construction errors guide generator repair, while learner errors motivate interventions compared on a separate selection set. Across seven benchmarks, three rounds raise Qwen3.5-35B-A3B's mean question-answering accuracy from 34.57% to 56.04% and mean classification F1 from 24.27 to 34.03. Across the retained trajectory, the preferred supervision shifts from direct reinforcement to confusion-focused contrasts. Continued feedback correction yields diminishing external gains. These results motivate separating error diagnosis from intervention selection and checking whether gains on the feedback set transfer to independent benchmarks.","tldr":"背景与问题：心电模型的弱点会随训练变化，但定向生成波形可能同时改变其他特征，使问题、答案与实际信号不符；只追着反馈错误补数据也可能过拟合。\n\n方法：ECG-RSI先按目标特征编辑训练波形，再复测目标与受保护特征，合格后才生成监督。构造错误用于修补生成规则，学习者错误用于提出不同数据配方；同父模型训练出的分支在独立选择集比较，获选分支进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：三轮后，四项问答平均准确率由34.57%升至56.04%；保留路径的监督重心转向易混类别对比，但继续纠错的外部收益递减。可见附录另列一组三种子分数，口径未充分说明，不能与主结果混算。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，错误诊断只能提出干预，不能证明该干预有教学价值。独立选择与外部评测使这一区分可检验；波形复测仍依赖特征提取与问答审查，不能等同临床有效性认证。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 失败诊断","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称以波形复测和学习者反馈共同驱动数据生成与模型演化。本文证据区分生成错误修补、学习者弱点诊断及独立选择，获选模型与数据进入下一轮；直接强化指增加薄弱类别监督，并非强化学习。相对SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）以作答结果训练合成策略，本篇通过受约束信号编辑、复测和生成规则修补约束监督，并比较同父模型的数据配方。编辑推断：推进在领域证据约束与干预选择分离，不能据此证明生成算法自身持续增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17609","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.17609v1","title":"Verifier-Harness Co-Evolution for Training-Free Self-Improvement on Open-Ended Tasks","authors":"Tianyi Xu; Yaolun Zhang; Yiran Wu; Joe Nguyen; Shengyu Dai; Saba Moeinizade; Zhenwen Shao; Qingyun Wu; Huazheng Wang","affiliations":"Oregon State University；Pennsylvania State University；Johnson & Johnson；AG2 AI","abstract":"Training-free self-improvement lets an agent use feedback to revise the response it is about to return and to update the harness state that shapes how it handles later tasks. On open-ended tasks that feedback rarely comes from reference answers or executable tests, so the agent has to rely on a model-based verifier. When the verifier is wrong, the current response can get worse, and misleading experience can persist across the task stream. A verifier that never changes also grows stale as the agent's responses improve and task demands shift. We introduce Unified Co-Evolution (UCoE), a training-free method that evolves an executable verifier program together with the agent's harness state while all model parameters stay fixed. UCoE synthesizes candidate verifier programs and tests them on response contrasts, pairs of responses that differ in one declared property and have a known preferred side. It selects the candidate whose discrimination on its weakest contrast family is highest, a quantity we call driving capacity. The selected verifier diagnoses one weakness in each draft, guides a single repair, decides which response is served, and determines whether the accepted repair may enter the harness state. As tasks complete, their diagnostics seed new candidate verifiers, which must beat the current verifier on the same contrasts before adoption. Across six open-ended benchmarks, UCoE averages 59.00% preference against matched direct generation with Qwen3-8B and 57.19% with Qwen3.8-27B, margins of 9.00 and 7.19 percentage points. On three verifiable benchmarks, the same method raises the mean from 36.06% for direct generation to 38.48%. Code is available at https://github.com/tianyi0216/Unified-Co-Evolution.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放任务没有答案或可执行测试，错误verifier不仅会把当前回答改坏，还会把误导经验写入后续harness；固定评分标准又可能随任务变化失效。\n\n方法：UCoE构造只破坏一个属性的回答对，选择最弱属性族上辨别力最高的评分程序。该程序指导局部修补、选择交付回答并控制经验写入；完成任务的诊断再提出新程序，经对比测试后替换旧版，所有模型参数固定。\n\n结果与结论：六个开放基准上，两种骨干相对匹配直接生成的平均偏好率为59.00%和57.19%。可见引言明确称多数收益来自当前任务修补，不能把总体优势全部归于跨任务共演化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，评分器应按能否辨别关键退化来选，而非只看平均准确率。但合成退化的偏好方向不等于自然修订的真实优劣；重复使用对比集也留下选择过拟合风险，理论不覆盖任意开放任务。","published_at":"2026-10-13","topics":"评估器递归改进; Harness 递归演化; 无真值反馈","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称在固定模型参数下共同演化可执行verifier与harness状态。本文证据显示，反馈来自固定模型评分及单属性退化构造的回答对；任务诊断产生新评分程序，程序又控制回答与经验准入。相对RHO（arxiv:2606.05922）使用自偏好选harness，本篇把评分准则与聚合程序纳入更新，并以最弱对比族表现门控。编辑推断：这是反馈机制可测试化的推进，但诊断程序和底层模型未演化，主要收益来自当题修补；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17114","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.17114v1","title":"D-World: An Explicit World-Language-Action Model with Recursive Self-Improvement under Dual Control","authors":"Xuan Wen; Baichao Wang","affiliations":"Geek+","abstract":"Frontier large language models (LLMs) now reason about space well enough to program robots, yet the world models behind robot policies are implicit, held in network weights or predicted video, and cannot be inspected or corrected directly. We present D-World, an explicit world-language-action model built on the Sense, Plan and Act decomposition. A perception agent writes the scene as an executable digital twin using generated vision and geometry code. A planning agent searches for actions in simulation and, after each executed action chunk, revises the twin's object states and named physical parameters against what the robot measured. A parameter revision is accepted only if replaying the latest chunk does not increase any measured residual beyond its tolerance, and every chunk is checked in the updated twin before it runs. Structural mismatches return to perception for reconstruction. We call this measurement-grounded cycle of correction and revision recursive self-improvement (RSI), in which the LLM stays frozen while the world it acts in improves. We model the choice of actions that both advance the task and expose model error as a dual control problem and show that the cost of incorporating evidence into the twin sets the threshold at which probing pays, so cheap local revision counteracts the turn-off of cautious controllers. Each episode runs a real-to-sim-to-real loop, and its recorded twins can be refitted and re-rendered offline into higher-fidelity environments for post-training. Because perception and planning communicate only through the twin and language, either can be replaced by a learned model, and since inference dominates the loop, the loop speeds up with faster models. On a dual-arm robot, towel and toaster tasks show local revisions, such as one reducing the bread's rendered-depth residual from 22.4 to 1.5 mm, that let execution continue without reconstruction.","tldr":"背景与问题：隐式机器人世界模型预测出错时，难把偏差定位到可修正量；每次重建场景又很昂贵，过度谨慎还会阻止获得辨识模型所需的接触证据。\n\n方法：D-World让冻结LLM编写可执行数字孪生，用实机执行后的测量修订对象状态和物理参数。参数修改须在最新动作段回放中不显著恶化已测残差，下一段动作再经更新后的仿真检查；结构错误则触发重建。\n\n结果与结论：双臂机器人的毛巾与烤面包任务展示局部修订后继续执行，其中面包深度残差由22.4降至1.5毫米。材料没有提供完整成功率、重建成本和受控消融，案例不能证明普遍收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可编辑参数使误差成为行动依据，但本质仍含系统辨识。门控只约束最新可测证据，早期残差不否决更新，仿真通过也不认证实机安全；离线后训练用途尚不能算已验证闭环。","published_at":"2026-10-12","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 预测误差反馈; 具身 RSI","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称用物理测量修订显式数字孪生，实现回合内RSI。本文证据显示改变的是对象状态与物理参数，反馈是实机测量残差，更新后的孪生影响下一段规划；LLM与修订规则不变。相对Memento 3（arxiv:2610.11794）的规则—代码及历史转移回放，本篇采用真实机器人测量、局部参数修订和最新动作段非回归门控。编辑推断：这是显式世界模型适配的具身扩展，核心参数更新也属于系统辨识，不是改进器递归优化；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16523","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.16523v1","title":"EAU: Environment-Agent-User Co-evolution for Training User-Centric Agents","authors":"Min Cai; Dan Zhang; Gao Xing; Libin Ma; Zhaohui Xu; Xi Ye","affiliations":"University of Alberta；National University of Singapore；Kuaishou Technology；Independent Researcher；Alberta Machine Intelligence Institute (Amii)","abstract":"Training LLM agents to interact with users over multiple turns is challenging because the learning signal depends not only on the agent, but also on the user simulator and environment, which jointly shape the agent's experience. Simulated users can be stochastic or inconsistent, while environments may contain unreliable tools, incomplete state coverage, and incorrect verifiers. Prior work mainly addresses the resulting instability through reward shaping or denser supervision, while treating these components as fixed. We instead introduce EAU, a meta-agent framework for environment--agent--user co-evolution. During training, EAU monitors trajectories, tool traces, rewards, and training statistics; diagnoses failures and uninformative interactions; and proposes targeted modifications to the user simulator, environment, reward design, and RL configuration. Validated changes are hot-swapped into the ongoing run, allowing the training setup to evolve together with the policy. These adaptations also persist across runs, so later training can build on previously discovered improvements rather than restarting from a fixed setup. We enable this process through an editable symbolic representation of user and environment dynamics, while the agent remains a neural LLM optimized with RL. Across three interactive-agent benchmarks and two backbone models, EAU consistently outperforms prior RL methods, improving the overall score over the strongest baseline by 14.7--15.0% and increasing successful task completion on ColBench by up to 36.7%, showing that co-evolving the training system with the policy can substantially improve multi-turn RL.","tldr":"背景与问题：多轮用户互动的坏训练信号未必来自策略：模拟用户可能泄露信息，工具或验证器可能出错。只做奖励塑形，无法修复产生这些轨迹的上游过程。\n\n方法：EAU让元agent读取训练轨迹与统计，诊断问题后修改用户规则、交互条件、奖励或训练配置；通过有限完整性检查的变更可在训练中热替换。策略继续按固定RL算法学习，已发现的干预经验跨运行保存。\n\n结果与结论：摘要在三个基准、两种骨干上给出相对最强基线14.7%—15.0%的总体增益。主要结果表被截断；附录说明不少基线来自既有报告，而PPO与EAU自行评测，因此并非全部统一重跑。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，把故障归因到训练系统而非一律归因策略，是有价值的改动。但运行内修补、奖励变化与超参数调整混合发生，需要核对各自增益和总预算；环境可编辑不等于元优化机制也在变强。","published_at":"2026-10-12","topics":"失败驱动的递归更新; 自适应过程奖励; 长程交互学习","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称让用户模拟器、环境和策略共同演化。本文证据显示，元agent依训练日志及轨迹修改符号用户规则、奖励和可调配置，策略通过固定RL算法更新，干预经验跨运行保留。相对RewardWeaver（arxiv:2610.10120）调整固定语义过程奖励的分配，本篇扩展到上游交互生成条件，并支持运行内热替换。编辑推断：贡献在在线训练系统干预，不应将程序化环境适配表述为三个模型共同学习，也未证明元agent或训练算法递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16491","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.16491v1","title":"Drafting Agents, Not Just Tokens: Speculative Recursive Self-Improvement for Agentic Systems","authors":"Xin Xu; Ke Cheng; Hao Wang; Yangru Huang; Yanghao Xiao; Zhichao Chen; Zhisheng Zhong; Xun Liu; Yi Li; Qian Li; Haibin Lv; Jun Zhang; Jie Jiang; Zhouchen Lin","affiliations":"","abstract":"Improving an agent through successive revisions requires balancing exploration and evaluation under a limited budget. A narrow search can miss useful sequences of edits, while fully evaluating every intermediate version can exhaust the budget before those sequences yield a verified improvement. We introduce Speculative Recursive Self-Improvement (SpecRSI), which drafts executable successor agents before their predecessors are fully evaluated, while requiring complete verification before adoption. Verification-Aware Tree Search (VATS) allocates the budget between further edits and outstanding checks using the predicted verified return of a continuation. Group Verification Optimization (GVO) learns the improver from completed searches while keeping the real evaluator fixed. In the main scientific comparison, terminal gains exceed Janus by 33.3%--40.0%. Additional evaluations show that SpecRSI outperforms Janus in all 50 scientific backbone--task pairs and exceeds MetaRSI-v1 by 1.85%--2.38% in macro-average system score across twenty backbones. Coding-validation success reaches 69.4% versus HGM's 64.3% at a 20.8% lower target-cost index.","tldr":"背景与问题：每改一版就完整评估，会把预算耗在尚未产生价值的中间状态；只预测当前候选质量，又忽略它还需多少编辑和检查才能成为可采用改进。\n\n方法：SpecRSI允许从未完成评估的版本继续起草，但采用前必须取得完整真实检查。搜索根据后续编辑与验证的预期净收益分配预算；外层用整次搜索的已验证收益减全部成本，训练下一轮改进者，真实评估合同不变。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出编码验证成功率69.4%，对照HGM为64.3%，目标成本指标也下降；但可见图注另显示，相对MetaRSI-v1，目标成本更低时总成本指标略高，不能概括为全面省算力。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，改进者应学习哪些尚未成功的编辑值得继续验证，而非只模仿成功补丁。完整搜索信用回应了这一点；预测器仍可能浪费不可追回的预算，且固定外层算法不意味着改进过程无限自举。","published_at":"2026-10-12","topics":"预算受限研究搜索; 自进化策略训练; Harness 递归演化","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过先起草后验证与完整搜索反馈训练改进者，提高预算内可验证收益。本文证据区分候选执行检查和预测净收益的评分器：只有前者产生准入证据，完整搜索的收益及全部成本训练起草、调度与评分组件。相对Evo²（arxiv:2610.13025）用编辑及反思的局部执行收益训练改进者，本篇将后续编辑、互补检查及整次搜索成本纳入信用；相对EvoX（arxiv:2602.23413）演化搜索策略，本篇具体学习编辑—验证调度。编辑推断：推进明确，但外层更新规则固定，不能称无限层级递归；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16078","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.16078v1","title":"Heterogeneous Agentic Coevolution","authors":"Wenqian Ye; Ziwei Guan; Zi Yang; Shivani Modi; Cici Cong Wu; Yunlong He; Yuxin Chen; Zhengyu Zhang; Liang Luo; Venkatesh Ranganathan; Jianhui Sun; Yantao Yao; Wenlin Chen; Buyun Zhang; Ellie Dingqiao Wen; Henry Kautz; Aidong Zhang","affiliations":"Meta AI；University of Virginia","abstract":"Recent advances in self-improving LLM agents have demonstrated the potential of AI systems that drive their own intelligence. However, many domain-specific applications rely on specialized foundation models that possess strong domain expertise but remain dependent on human-designed improvements. Extending recursive self-improvement to these models presents a key challenge: as a specialist improves, the strategies used to advance it must also adapt. To address this challenge, we propose Heterogeneous Agentic CoEvolution (HACE), a framework that jointly evolves specialized foundation models and LLM agents through reciprocal learning. HACE improves the specialist through supervised learning while training the agent with on-policy reinforced self-training, guided by verified performance gains on the current specialist. The agent's exploration, in turn, informs subsequent specialist training, enabling both models to adapt to each other's progress. To sustain this reciprocal learning, HACE further employs evolutionary search to optimize their interaction harness, adapting how the models exchange information and select training experiences as their capabilities evolve. We evaluate HACE across three challenging domains: recommendation systems, protein function prediction in biology, and crystal stability prediction in material discovery. We show that HACE outperforms the evaluated self-improving methods on the primary task metrics across all three domains. These results shed light on heterogeneous coevolution as a universal approach to improving specialized foundation models through reciprocal interaction with a learning agent.","tldr":"背景与问题：领域专家继续监督训练已达平台时，通用agent仍可能在部分实例上提供帮助；但专家变强后，旧agent策略与交互方式可能不再提供增量。\n\n方法：HACE用任务标签检验agent是否在当前实例上优于专家，探索结果决定专家重点训练哪些样本，专家仍学原始标签。候选专家与harness联合比较后，再收集相对保留专家有正贡献的新回答训练agent，改变下一轮可用贡献。\n\n结果与结论：材料称在推荐、蛋白功能和晶体稳定性预测中优于所比较自改进方法，起点为已收敛专家。主要结果表缺失；蛋白任务实际只更新预测头，不能统称所有领域基础模型权重均被改进。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，平均更弱的agent也可能凭局部互补性帮助专家，关键是验证哪些实例值得投入。这里监督来自原始标签而非纯自生知识；总体联合得分还需拆分专家、agent与harness各自的独立贡献。","published_at":"2026-10-12","topics":"模型—harness 共演化; 自进化策略训练; 模型—数据共演化","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称联合演化领域专家、LLM agent与交互harness。本文证据显示，原始标签验证agent相对当前专家的贡献，探索结果选择专家训练实例，保留专家—harness组合后重新收集正贡献回答训练agent。相对Co-Harness（arxiv:2607.22688）用改进harness产生轨迹训练agent，本篇另加入异构领域专家及双向经验选择；相对SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）合成器—求解器共训练，本篇不是造新任务，而是在有标签池中重分配训练。编辑推断：异构互惠学习有具体机制，但仍依赖外部标签，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15964","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15964v1","title":"Small but Mighty: Test Suites as Improvement Signals for Self-Evolving Agents","authors":"Yutong Cheng; Wei Cheng; Wenchao Yu; Dawei Zhou; Haifeng Chen","affiliations":"Virginia Tech；NEC Laboratories America","abstract":"A self-evolving agent rewrites its own harness and must decide which rewrites to keep, so its improvement signal is the check a rewrite has to pass. Verifying a rewrite by agent rollout is expensive and subjective, while executable checks such as the repository's own tests are too sparse to catch behavior-changing rewrites, rejecting only a quarter of them. We instead take test feedback as the executable signal, and search for test suites that are both small and strong with a quality-diversity evolutionary algorithm, so that the signal is dense and informative. TeSearch treats suite size as a behavior descriptor, so that quality is pursued at every size and a small, strong suite is reachable, and learns a transition kernel during the search that denoises the LLM as an actuator on that descriptor. Across 129 real-world modules and three backbones, TeSearch delivers the highest-quality suites of any method compared, LLM-driven evolutionary search included, and the smallest of any LLM-based one. Used as the improvement signal of a self-evolving agent, it rejects 59.9% of behavior-changing rewrites against 25.3% for the repository's tests, at a 4.0% false-alarm rate and 3.5 s per decision. The code and data are available at https://github.com/ccsnow127/TeSearch.","tldr":"背景与问题：agent重写harness后，端到端rollout昂贵，原仓库测试又漏掉大量行为变化；更大的生成测试集虽可能更强，却会增加每次准入成本。\n\n方法：TeSearch按测试集大小分区竞争，在每种规模内优化覆盖与变异检测，避免小而强的候选被大集合挤掉；实际生成数量反过来校准搜索。得到的测试集作为harness改写的可执行回归门控。\n\n结果与结论：在mini-swe-agent的470个核验改写上，行为变化拒绝率为59.9%，仓库测试为25.3%；代价是误拒部分等价改写。这里测的是构造改写的行为保持，不是多轮自改进后的任务成功率。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，回归检查是保住已有能力的护栏，不是改进价值本身。若目标本就需要改变行为，强制保持旧实现还可能阻止好更新；后续应把保持合同与允许变化的功能目标分开测试。","published_at":"2026-10-11","topics":"评估器递归改进; 验证理论; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称优化自演化agent的可执行改写信号。本文证据是按覆盖率与变异杀伤率搜索小测试集，再对人工核验标签的harness改写做准入评测，反馈来自执行而非模型偏好。相对Self-Harness（arxiv:2606.09498）用既定回归测试筛编辑，本篇优化测试本身；相对UCoE（arxiv:2610.17609）在线演化模型评分程序，本篇交付固定测试集，没有展示测试随agent长期共演化。编辑推断：这是回归门控质量的推进，不是已证明的任务收益或递归链；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15772","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15772v1","title":"RSIPO: Recursive Self-Improving Policy Optimization for Agentic Reinforcement Learning via Skill-Policy Co-Evolution","authors":"Fan Zhang; Hao Wu; Jinyang Wu; Hongyu Qu; Zheng Lian; Xiao Luo; Yefeng Zheng; Bo Zhang; Haoxuan Li; Pheng-Ann Heng","affiliations":"THU；NUS；Tongji University；UW-Madison；Westlake University；CUHK；Shanghai AI Laboratory；PKU","abstract":"Recent focus in agentic reinforcement learning (RL) seeks to improve credit assignment in long-horizon tasks. One promising direction combines reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards (RLVR) and on-policy self-distillation (OPSD), integrating trajectory-level advantages with dense token-level supervision. This line of work often conditions a teacher model on privileged context, such as agentic skills, to score tokens generated by the student policy. Despite their progress, they largely overlook the on-policy evolution of agentic skills and the reliability of teacher supervision. Towards this end, we introduce Recursive Self-Improving Policy Optimization (RSIPO), a self-evolving agentic RL framework that enables agentic skills and the policy model to co-evolve throughout the training process. Specifically, RSIPO enables the policy itself to extract skills from completed trajectories and explicitly optimizes its skill-generation capability through trajectory replay. It further employs empirical Bayes shrinkage to dynamically calibrate the student's trust in teacher scores, accounting for the fact that skill-enhanced teacher guidance can sometimes be less reliable. Experiments with Qwen-family models on embodied interaction and search-based agentic tasks demonstrate that RSIPO outperforms all the compared baseline approaches. With Qwen2.5-7B as the base model, RSIPO achieves an average success rate of 98.6\\% on ALFWorld, yielding absolute improvements of 2.5\\% and 17.4\\% over the second-best baseline and standard GRPO, respectively.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定技能库或离线技能生成器会落后于训练中的策略；给教师增加技能也不保证它比学生可靠，统一蒸馏可能强化错误指导。\n\n方法：RSIPO让当前策略从自身轨迹写技能，在同起点回放中与随机留出的无技能轨迹比较执行收益。收益奖励技能生成，噪声校准后的收益则调节学生对技能教师的信任；更新策略再产生下一批轨迹，测试不提供技能。\n\n结果与结论：Qwen2.5-7B在ALFWorld成功率为98.6%，比次优基线高2.5个百分点。但附录显示3B模型在搜索任务只排第二，不能照摘要推广为所有配置均领先；完整成本和消融表未见。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，技能相关不等于具有教学价值，实际回放比教师自信更合适。收益来自同任务重放，还需防止答案泄漏与起点不一致；初始化也使用外部LLM技能监督，不能称全程无教师。","published_at":"2026-10-11","topics":"技能蒸馏; 自进化策略训练; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称以技能—策略共演化及教师信任校准改进agentic RL。本文证据以同起点技能回放相对随机控制组的执行收益奖励技能生成，并对噪声收益收缩后调整蒸馏权重；策略更新又改变后续技能。相对SGUID（arxiv:2610.12367）筛选持续有效的技能蒸馏信号，本篇直接训练技能生成行为并动态校准教师；相对MetaExp（arxiv:2610.21492），本篇技能用于训练期监督，测试不提供技能。编辑推断：教学价值进入生成目标是具体推进，但回放衡量同任务帮助，跨任务技能价值未直接认证；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15708","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15708v1","title":"SpecForge: Recursive Self-Improvement for Coding Agents via Behavioral Specifications","authors":"Yutong Cheng; Haifeng Chen; Peng Gao; Wei Cheng","affiliations":"Virginia Tech；NEC Laboratories America","abstract":"Coding agents based on frozen language models can improve their performance by refining the external context they rely on, without updating model weights. We study recursive self-improvement through behavioral specifications: natural-language code documentation that describes the behavior of program entities and guides agents in generating correct code. We formulate a self-improvement loop in which an agent generates code from its current specifications, evaluates it with execution-verified tests, and refines the specifications based on observed failures. The improved specifications then guide subsequent generation, progressively improving the agent's understanding of the codebase. However, recursive refinement is challenging because program entities are interdependent. Improving the specification of one entity can inadvertently degrade the correctness of others, a phenomenon we call output coupling. This creates a whack-a-mole effect in which local improvements cause regressions elsewhere, preventing consistent progress. We introduce SpecForge, a multi-frontier tree search framework that addresses this challenge with three mechanisms: (i) Pareto-guided state selection preserves complementary specification states and prevents premature commitment; (ii) dependency-constrained entity selection prioritizes callee-before-caller refinement; and (iii) error-diversified expansion explores multiple refinements using different subsets of test failures. On DevEval+, SpecForge achieves the best performance across five backbone models, including a 94.9% solve rate with Claude-4.5-Sonnet and a 5.7-percentage-point average improvement over the strongest baseline. The improved specifications also make the agent better at tasks outside the loop: they transfer to cross-language translation and to new-feature implementation, where they outperform the benchmark-provided requirement documents.","tldr":"背景与问题：代码实体相互依赖，修好一个函数的规格可能改变整个模块生成，使其他函数退化；沿单条修订路径容易反复丢失已有成果。\n\n方法：SpecForge用从规格重建代码后的测试失败修改行为描述，而非直接积累代码补丁。搜索保留各实体上互有优势的规格状态，并优先修订被调用者，减少依赖错误造成的误导；新状态重新生成和测试整个模块。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出五种骨干上平均比最强基线高5.7个百分点，并称规格可迁移到跨语言翻译和新功能实现。主要实验段落未提供，尚不能核对迁移效果量及完整预算。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，外部知识的质量可用其能否支持行为重建衡量，而非文档相似度。不过测试来自已有参考实现，验证的是捕捉现有行为；这不自动证明新需求正确性，也不证明搜索器自身越来越会优化。","published_at":"2026-10-11","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 执行证据驱动改进; 跨任务迁移","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过行为规格的递归修订改善编码agent。本文证据显示，参考实现生成并执行验证的测试评价从规格重建的代码，失败修订规格，保留规格状态影响下一轮；模型和搜索规则固定。相对Self-Harness（arxiv:2606.09498）直接改运行harness，本篇改代码库行为知识；相对TeSearch（arxiv:2610.15964）优化测试信号，本篇把测试作为既定反馈，并处理规格间依赖和生成干扰。编辑推断：这是外部知识优化的结构化推进，不代表模型参数中的能力或优化器递归增强；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15244","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15244v1","title":"EvolvAttack: Backdooring self Evolving VLM Agents","authors":"Chuan Zou; Yang Xiang; Zexin Li; Xiaonan Luo; Simin Chen","affiliations":"University of Pennsylvania；Brown University；Nanyang Technological University；University of Notre Dame；George Mason University","abstract":"Self-evolving mechanisms let vision-language model (VLM) agents continually adapt through evolving memory, but they also allow malicious behavior to emerge only after deployment. We introduce a new attack surface, the self-evolving backdoor, whose payload stays dormant in the initial agent and is progressively activated as the agent evolves. Unlike conventional backdoors, which can be exposed by testing triggered inputs on a static model, our attack requires both a visual trigger and a sufficiently evolved memory state; static scanning with clean memory thus yields near-zero attack success and may deem the agent benign. We realize this through memory-aware backdoor training, which couples trigger activation with the agent's evolving memory while preserving benign behavior unless the trigger co-occurs with payload-related memory. Across three VLM backbones, four agent pipelines, and recency-, semantic-, and reward-based memory evolution, the attack preserves normal functionality and stays nearly inactive before evolution (0.5% attack success rate), yet exceeds 95% attack success within 100 interactions, revealing a stealthy threat unique to self-evolving agents.","tldr":"背景与问题：只在初始记忆下扫描视觉触发器，可能漏掉依赖后续经验状态才激活的后门；部署时权重不变也不保证行为安全不变。\n\n方法：EvolvAttack通过部署前投毒训练预置联合条件：触发图像与载荷相关记忆同时存在才稳定输出恶意行为。早期罕见输出被正常记忆机制写回，后续检索再提高激活机会，形成放大；攻击者部署后不直接修改记忆或权重。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称攻击成功率从演化前0.5%升至百次交互内超过95%。但可见消融中，补充空记忆训练覆盖会降低攻击效果，说明静态隐蔽性与动态强度受具体训练覆盖影响。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，安全审计对象应是带写回的交互轨迹，而非单个权重快照。这是预植后门借记忆放大的证据，不能表述为普通经验学习自然生成恶意；真实部署风险还取决于触发暴露与记忆准入。","published_at":"2026-10-11","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 外部记忆与规则更新; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-18","novelty_summary":"作者声称发现依赖演化记忆的延迟视觉后门。本文证据显示，部署前投毒训练预置视觉触发器与载荷记忆的联合激活，部署后标准写回和检索放大罕见载荷输出；并非正常自改进凭空产生恶意目标。相对STRATA（arxiv:2610.19386）研究无攻击情况下的经验负迁移，本篇展示被预植机制利用的记忆反馈放大。编辑推断：这是自演化安全审计的重要补充，但corpus缺少相关后门工作的充分原始材料，不能核验作者的首次主张；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15084","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.15084v1","title":"Self-Evolving Visual Agent via Margin Reward","authors":"Wenxi Yang; Yuzhong Zhao; Baochang Zhang; Yunfan Liu; Qixiang Ye","affiliations":"中国科学院大学；微软亚洲研究院；北京航空航天大学","abstract":"Visual agents that interleave reasoning with tool invocation have posed a promising direction for multimodal tasks. However, learning effective tool invocation usually relies on curated question-answer pairs or expert demonstrations at scale, which are expensive to acquire. In this study, we propose Marvo, a simple-yet-effective self-evolution approach that enables learning tool invocation from unlabeled images. Marvo consists of two agents: (1) a challenger that generates question-answer pairs from unlabeled images, and (2) a solver that learns tool invocation by solving questions through reinforcement learning. To encourage effective tool invocation, a good training question should be difficult enough to warrant tool use, yet remain within the solver's capabilities. To this end, we introduce a margin reward to the challenger, defined as solver's performance difference with and without access to tools. With the margin reward, we create an adaptive curriculum that encourages the solver to learn effective tool invocation. Across benchmarks covering agentic reasoning, visual search, mathematical, and general real-world reasoning, Marvo improves average accuracy by up to 7.1\\% --- demonstrating margin reward as a preferred way to scale question complexity without human supervision.","tldr":"背景与问题：视觉工具调用训练常依赖昂贵的标注问答或专家演示；仅按不确定性出题，也不能保证工具确实有用。方法：challenger 从无标注图像造题，solver 通过强化学习作答；solver 有无工具时的表现差作为出题反馈，使课程追踪工具的实际边际收益。结果与结论：作者报告覆盖 11,691 题的多基准评估中，Qwen2.5-VL-7B 平均准确率提高 7.1%；所给全文片段还报告八轮扩展中题目质量与表现后期下降。Insights：这提示课程信号应对准待学能力的边际贡献，而不是难度本身；依据是工具增益奖励及后期标签质量同步下滑。结论限于所测视觉任务，作者实验未经独立复现。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 工具调用学习; 强化学习自改进","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称以 solver 有无工具时的表现差，训练 challenger 生成值得调用工具且可解的问题；反馈经 challenger 生成题目进入 solver 强化学习，构成数据—模型闭环。本文证据包括多基准作者实验，并在所给全文片段中报告与 R-Zero 的匹配轮次比较；差异是以工具边际效用而非单纯不确定性指导出题。材料未支持领域级优先性，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14843","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14843v1","title":"Pre-Registered Genesis Accounting for Recursive Self-Improvement: First Audited Operator-Genesis Events in a Physics-Discovery Runtime","authors":"Wenbin Mao; Pei Zou","affiliations":"HoomanBio AI Lab；Huaman Biotechnology（北京）有限公司","abstract":"Claims of recursive self-improvement are easy to make and hard to falsify: did improvement come from re-using designer-provided mechanisms, or from mechanisms the system authored itself? We introduce a pre-registered, two-tier accounting: M1 counts machine-generated content instances within a designer-provided vocabulary, while M2 counts machine-authored mechanism types (new operators registered into the runtime's own vocabulary, with a held-out-validation certificate). We report the first audited M2 genesis events. In the primary event, depth-limited compositional search over elementary operators, judged by held-out R^2 on real NIST hydrogen Balmer measurements, produced the operator sq(inv(n)) = 1/n^2 -- the Rydberg-level form -- which no standard-library transform could express (held-out R^2: -0.546 best standard transform vs. 1.0000000 composed). A protocol flaw (independent variable built by inverting the very law under test) was caught in audit and repaired via an independent-label protocol; extrapolation to unseen levels (n=8,9 trained on n\u003c=7) attains relative error ~10^-6, four to six orders beyond the best standard operator. A second event independently recovered sqrt(inv(a)) -- Kepler's velocity law -- from JPL ephemeris vectors. Also incorporated: an audited compounding channel (first domain-level measurement: 1.109x accuracy ratio on a real held-out domain) and blind, decurated genesis exams whose honest tally is zero. The Kepler event passes line audit; the hydrogen gap reproduces on He II; the certificate is threshold-stable. Against eleven prior systems, the contribution is the measurement and governance of machine-authored mechanisms, not the search algorithm or rediscovered physics. Limitations: exams were curated by agents who knew the textbook answer, triggers manual, grammar observer-injected; both events demonstrate capability to author, not yet autonomous genesis.","tldr":"背景与问题：性能提升可能来自复用设计者提供的机制，也可能来自系统写出新机制；若不区分来源，RSI 声称难以证伪。方法：预注册区分机制实例与新算子，要求候选通过留出数据证书后才登记，并进入可复用注册表。结果与结论：作者报告氢谱与开普勒两次算子生成；氢谱协议修复循环性漏洞后，未见能级外推相对误差约为 10⁻⁶。盲选考试至今为零，事件触发仍需人工。Insights：这提示 RSI 应分别记录机制来源、验证与复用；依据是协议审计和诚实报告的零 tally。边界明确：结果支持受限语法下的机制生成能力，不证明系统能自主启动或持续进化。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 机制生成与记账; 科学发现","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称贡献是预注册 M1/M2 记账、机制必要性证书和持久注册表，而非新搜索算法或新物理定律；机制候选经留出数据验证后登记，并可供后续发现复用。本文证据包括氢谱与开普勒算子事件、协议循环性漏洞的审计修复和有限复合测量；盲选考试 tally 为零。作者将工作与十一种既有系统定位比较，但其排他性主张受检索覆盖限制。编辑判断：这是治理和测量提案，尚非自主递归改进证据；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14828","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14828v1","title":"EvoCowork: A Benchmark for Real-World Office Tasks","authors":"Zhou Liu; Xingyan Chen; ZhaoYang Han; Zewei Pan; Zeli Su; Ningxin Pan; Xue Hu; Kaixiong Ting; Wentao Zhang","affiliations":"北京大学；中山大学；上海交通大学；中央民族大学；北京航空航天大学；中国科学技术大学","abstract":"Office workflows are a demanding testbed for self-improving agents because their deliverables must be correct, natively editable, and mutually consistent. A central question is whether gains on feedback tasks reflect reusable procedures rather than task-specific fixes. We introduce EvoCowork, a 240-task benchmark for evaluating harness-level recursive self-improvement across four office modalities, with model weights held fixed. The benchmark covers presentations, documents, spreadsheets, and cross-office workflows, and scores submitted artifacts for content, native structure, formulas, cross-file consistency, and visual quality where needed. Its protocol separates feedback, revision selection, and final testing: methods learn from single-modality tasks, then are evaluated on unseen single-modality tasks and cross-office workflows under a shared initial harness and explicit budgets. In static evaluations of two models and four harnesses, the best configuration scores 42.25 overall and 30.62 on cross-office tasks. Starting from the same MSA harness with GLM 5.3, ACE and AHE improve in-domain scores by 4.90 and 2.64 points, respectively, but change cross-office scores by only +0.03 and -1.72. Thus, gains on the file types that provide feedback do not necessarily transfer to coordinated workflows. EvoCowork makes this distinction explicit while recording the capability, transfer, and cost of harness evolution. Code and task packages: https://github.com/DeepThinkingZhouLiu/cowork-evolution-benchmark.","tldr":"背景与问题：办公工作流要求文档、表格和演示文件既正确、可编辑又彼此一致；单一文件类型上的修补成功，不代表形成可复用流程。方法：构建四类办公任务基准，对产物内容、原生结构、公式和跨文件一致性评分，并将反馈集、选择集与最终测试分离，控制初始 harness 与预算。结果与结论：在 GLM 5.3 与共同初始 harness 下，ACE/AHE 域内分别提高 4.90/2.64 分，跨办公任务却只变化 +0.03/-1.72 分。作者据此指出，域内收益不保证协调工作流迁移。Insights：这提示迁移目标应直接进入 RSI 测试，而不能用总体分数替代；依据是单模态与跨文件结果分化。边界是离线办公产物、有限配置及有限方法运行。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"Harness 演化评测; 跨任务迁移; 办公智能体","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出 240 任务办公基准，评分覆盖原生文件结构、内容与跨文件一致性，并将反馈、修订选择和最终测试分开。本文证据显示 ACE/AHE 域内增益没有转为跨办公增益。与 AHE（arxiv:2604.25850）的关系是评测补充：该基准直接测试单模态反馈向跨文件工作流的迁移，而非提出新的演化机制；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14730","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14730v1","title":"Self-improving data synthesis can scale embedding models across domains and tasks","authors":"Zucan Lyu; Rui Tang; Jianlyu Chen; Peisheng Jin; Zheng Liu; Defu Lian","affiliations":"中国科学技术大学；认知智能全国重点实验室","abstract":"Adapting embedding models to new tasks requires training data that reflect task-specific information needs and relevance criteria. However, manual data design is costly and difficult to scale. Here we introduce SYNTRA, a novel retrieval data synthesis method whose self-improvement loop iteratively refines reusable synthesis instructions using feedback on trial outputs. This process requires only an unlabelled corpus and a few relevant query-document pairs. Experiments across 24 retrieval datasets spanning 15 domains demonstrate the effectiveness of the synthesized data. These data also improve widely used, strong embedding models on tasks with and without existing labelled training sets. Self-improvement enhances retrieval on all six evaluated tasks, outperforming human calibration on four. Moreover, retrieval performance continues to improve on MS MARCO as we scale the training dataset to 32 times its initial size. Overall, with minimal human intervention, SYNTRA enables scalable adaptation of embedding models across domains and tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：检索嵌入需要训练数据符合具体领域和相关性标准；人工设计查询、标签与合成指令难以随任务扩展。方法：系统从少量相关查询—文档示例推断任务要求，在小样本试产出上获取诊断反馈并修订共享合成指令，再用改进后的指令大规模生成数据。结果与结论：作者报告覆盖 24 个检索集、15 个领域；六项任务的自改进均提升训练数据效果，其中四项超过人工校准，MS MARCO 数据扩至初始规模 32 倍时性能仍提升。Insights：这提示递归改进对象也可以是产生训练经验的规则，而不只是模型参数；依据是指令修订与下游检索结果相联系。材料未提供独立复现，少量示例依赖、标签质量与长程闭环稳定性仍待验证。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 检索模型适配; 反馈驱动更新","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称根据试产出反馈迭代修订可复用的数据合成指令，再批量生成检索训练数据。本文证据为 24 个数据集、15 个领域的作者实验及六项任务上的自改进比较。与 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）都使训练经验适应学习者，但 SYNTRA 改写合成指令并训练嵌入模型，SynCo 联合优化合成器与推理器；二者未直接比较。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14625","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14625v1","title":"From Existing Methods to New Research Ideas: Two Perspectives on Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Leijun Zhou; Yanke Yu; Zhihao Liu; Qu Xiang; Tiancheng Hu; Yiru Dong; Yihan Wu; Yangxi Xiang; Xuejun Wu; Xi Chen; Buyue Qian; Yaowei Zheng; Junhao Hu","affiliations":"PrismShadow；北京大学；浙江大学；纽约大学","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) offers a route to AI systems that participate in their own continued development. Recent methods allow language agents to retain changes to their parameters, memory, skills, and code for subsequent execution and improvement. We examine how these methods can inform new research ideas through two complementary perspectives. First, we introduce a unified taxonomy with nine design dimensions organized into four groups: update targets, update organization, update schedule and scope, feedback and selection. This taxonomy places existing methods in a shared design space, where examining individual dimensions and their interactions can inspire new research ideas. Second, we examine how existing RSI methods draw on traditional deep learning, for example through optimization, regularization, data augmentation, continual learning, and adversarial learning. We develop further ideas by examining more specific learning mechanisms and drawing on evolutionary computation. We also review how existing benchmarks assess self-improvement under online, offline, and offline-to-online settings. Together, these perspectives help researchers develop new RSI research ideas from existing designs and learning mechanisms. RSI papers and resources are available at https://prism-shadow.github.io/awesome-rsi/.","tldr":"背景与问题：RSI 工作涉及不同更新对象、反馈与保留机制，宽泛分类难以揭示设计差异及其交互。方法：论文提出九维设计空间，并从优化、正则化、数据增强、持续学习与进化计算等机制中归纳可能的研究方向，同时梳理在线与离线评测。结果与结论：材料支持其分类框架和研究议程；没有本文系统的递归改进实验或性能结果。Insights：这提示比较 RSI 时可分别追问改什么、谁提出、依据何种反馈保留；这是框架可能提供的分析工具，材料未证明它本身改善系统或研究产出。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"RSI 评测与方法分类; 研究议程","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称用九维分类框架整理 RSI 设计，并从传统学习机制与进化计算提出研究构想；反馈来自文献及基准分析，不存在本文自身的改进对象—反馈—保留递归闭环。现有材料为综述全文片段，但未提供系统性与既有综述的匹配比较；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14495","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14495v1","title":"Reels-RSI: Program-Level Self-Improvement for Code-Rendered Explainer Videos","authors":"Wei Lin","affiliations":"Agentic Loops X","abstract":"Explainer videos -- a worked geometry problem, why the sky is blue, how a dynasty fell -- are usually one more target for pixel video generation. We argue they are a different kind of artifact: a program (script, storyboard and per-frame animation code) that a deterministic renderer turns into frames. A program can be read, diffed, tested and audited; pixels can only be watched. Reels-RSI is an open-source reel director for any agent harness; its self-improvement happens at the program level rather than in weights or prompts. Every revision pass is logged with a code snapshot; a retrospective pairs each check finding with the diff that fixed it and proposes lessons; a lesson that a static check can catch is compiled into a rule with a must-fail and a must-pass example, so the memory is unit-tested; and a rule learned today runs over everything made before it. A bounded, benchmark-gated step lets an agent rewrite the director's playbook, kept only when blind pairwise judgments on held-out topics prefer it; nothing enters memory without a human decision. Across 111 reels -- a field study, two playbook evolutions, a 2x2 memory ablation, a weaker director, a 48-reel learning curve and a judge-reliability study -- we find that the rule learned in the field caught four latent defects in frames authored before it existed and none after; that rules are an audit for a strong director (eight unguarded reels, no violation) and a guard for a weaker one (thirty violations unguarded versus five); that lessons shorten revision loops but do not compound or move the judge; and that the first rewrite's 11--1 verdict was a position bias in our vote design (judges pick the second-shown reel 62--81% of the time), masking scripts that traded thirteen facts for craft. We document four failure modes of the preference signal, which check caught each, and the fixes. Code, rules, lessons and data are public.","tldr":"背景与问题：解释视频既要视觉呈现，也要事实、推导和动画正确；只看像素难定位程序缺陷，偏好评审还可能把展示偏差当成改进。方法：把作品作为可读、可测试的程序记录；复盘将检查发现与修复差异配对，可静态检测的经验编译成带正反例的规则，并回查旧作品；playbook 更新需盲评且经人批准。结果与结论：作者报告一条规则在旧作品中发现四处潜在缺陷；研究也揭示盲评有明显顺序偏差。经验缩短修订循环，但没有形成累积改进或改变 judge。Insights：这提示可执行产物有助于把经验变成可审计检查，但偏好评分不能单独决定记忆保留；依据是回溯发现与位置偏差。证据限于单系统、有限作品和人工门控。","published_at":"2026-10-10","topics":"可执行记忆与规则; Harness 演化评测; 反馈偏差","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称将视频作品表示为可执行程序，把可静态检查的经验编译成带正反例的规则，并以盲评门控 playbook 改写。本文证据包括旧作品回溯审计及偏好评估的位置偏差；记忆保留仍需人工决策，且作者报告 lessons 不会复合。未与 corpus 中具体方法作匹配比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14224","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14224v1","title":"Harness^2: Recursive Agent Harnessing for an Open World","authors":"Ruiyao Xu; Yanfei Chen; Zhongying CuiZhu; Bhavana Dalvi Mishra; Yifei Ming; Han Yu; Rujun Han; Chen-Yu Lee; Tomas Pfister","affiliations":"Google Cloud AI Research；西北大学","abstract":"LLM agents' capabilities depend not only on their underlying models but also on their execution harnesses. Recursive self-improvement (RSI) offers a promising approach to automatically evolve these harnesses. However, deploying RSI in open-world settings still faces two critical challenges. First, open-world tasks are typically unseen during the harness design phase and novel at test time, leaving no ground-truth verifiers to reliably guide online harness edits. Second, the RSI process remains highly task-specific and fails to generalize to novel scenarios. We introduce Harness^2, a plug-and-play, recursive agent harnessing framework that addresses these challenges through two connected levels of recursion. Task-level recursion refines the current task's harness using a contrastive Propose-Probe-Compose step that reliably guides edits without ground-truth verifiers, and can be scaled further via parallel or sequential recursion. Harnessing-level recursion then extracts experience from these edits to update a continual improvement harness, enabling the agent to better adapt to future tasks. Across three professional benchmarks and four model-harness configurations, a single step consistently improves GLM-5 and Gemini 3.5 Flash over their base harnesses, yielding gains of up to 11.5 points on WorkBuddy-Bench, 4.5 points on JobBench, and 11.8 percentage points on LAB, with further gains as the task-level recursion budget increases.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放世界任务往往没有真值 verifier，按单一任务改出的 harness 又未必适用于后续新任务；直接继承任务专用修改还可能放大噪声。方法：先提出编辑并在相同任务和条件下探测行为变化，再据对比证据组合修改；随后从编辑过程提取适用条件与经验，更新未来任务的改进 harness。结果与结论：作者报告单步在多个专业基准和配置上有增益，增加任务级递归预算也带来提升。行为差异可帮助选择编辑，但不等于验证任务正确性。Insights：这提示应分别衡量“当前任务改得怎样”与“下一次是否更会改”；依据是双层循环及跨任务经验设计。证据限于特定基准、模型和预算，尚非独立复现。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"Harness 递归演化; 跨任务迁移; 无真值反馈","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称将无真值条件下的任务内对比探测，与跨任务积累可复用改进经验连接成两层递归。本文证据包括三项专业基准、四种模型—harness 配置及递归预算实验。与 Meta-Harness（arxiv:2603.28052）相比，本篇不仅搜索当前任务 harness，还将改进过程经验用于未来 harnessing；不是匹配性能比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14163","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14163v1","title":"AutoEnvScaling: Automating the Data Flywheel with Terminal Agents","authors":"Simon Yu; Baolin Peng; Bo Liu; Zhengyan Shi; Zhaoyang Wang; Hao Cheng; Qianhui Wu; Wenlin Yao; Natasha Jaques; Weiyan Shi; Jianfeng Gao","affiliations":"东北大学；微软研究院；华盛顿大学；北卡罗来纳大学教堂山分校","abstract":"Terminal agents solve tasks in software engineering and scientific research by executing commands in a terminal. Training them via reinforcement learning (RL) requires diverse and verifiable environments, but these environments are still mostly designed by human researchers, so their supply grows only as fast as researchers can work. We introduce AutoEnvScaling, which treats environment design as a terminal task and uses agents to automate the data flywheel. A proposer agent builds new RL environments from the rollouts of the solver being trained, and the solver's new rollouts guide the next round. By turning environment generation into a terminal task, AutoEnvScaling increases the valid-environment rate by up to 25 times compared to prompt-only generation, at up to 75% lower cost per valid environment. We show that training Qwen3.5-35B-A3B on AutoEnvScaling environments from GPT-5.6-sol improves its Terminal-Bench 2.1 score by 4.3 points over the matched Tmax baseline. The broader goal of AutoEnvScaling is to enable recursive self-improvement (RSI): by making both environment generation and solving terminal tasks, it lets one model co-evolve in both roles. We show that Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, acting in both roles, gains 12.2 points on Terminal-Bench 2.1 and raises its Terminal-Bench 4.0 score from 1.6 to 3.2. The pipeline also generalizes across agentic domains, generating environments for software engineering, computer use, professional work, and GPU kernel programming. Overall, these results show a path toward agents building their own training environments, reducing human reliance and taking a core step toward RSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：终端 agent 的强化学习依赖多样且可验证的环境；人工设计限制供给，固定任务池也会随 solver 进步而失去训练价值。方法：proposer 阅读 solver 轨迹，在沙箱终端中编写、运行和修复环境；环境通过有效性与难度校准后入池，solver 的新表现再指导下一轮生成，形成数据飞轮。结果与结论：作者报告相较纯提示生成，有效环境率最高提升 25 倍、单个有效环境成本最高降低 75%；同一模型兼任 proposer 与 solver 时，Terminal-Bench 2.1 提升 12.2 分。Insights：这提示训练经验生成本身可成为 agent 能力的一部分；依据是环境构建与 solver 学习相互反馈。边界是生成者也参与构造测试，仍需审查测试漏洞、长期稳定性与外部分布迁移。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"自适应课程与环境生成; 数据—模型共演化; 终端智能体","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称将环境设计变为终端任务，让 proposer 阅读 solver 轨迹、构建并校准训练环境，solver 新轨迹再指导下一轮；开放权重设置中同一模型可承担两角色。本文报告有效环境率、成本与 Terminal-Bench 作者实验。与 ClawLoop（arxiv:2610.14118）同属训练任务闭环，但前者聚焦完整终端环境的构建和校准；无直接比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13829","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13829v1","title":"MC-EvoBench: Auditing Experience-Driven Self-Improvement in Minecraft Agents","authors":"Jingwei Song; Zhisheng Chen; Bingfan Zeng; Jing Tang; Yubo Hou; Jinhao Jing; Zhengwei Xie; Linfeng Zhang","affiliations":"上海交通大学；中国科学院大学；华南理工大学；华中科技大学；北京航空航天大学；香港中文大学（深圳）；中国科学技术大学","abstract":"A central challenge in embodied recursive self-improvement is enabling agents to convert interaction history into capabilities that persist beyond one world and transfer to later tasks. A saved memory or successful final action does not by itself establish that a reusable capability was acquired; evaluation must separate capability change from carried-over resources, unequal source exposure, and early execution failures. We construct MC-EvoBench as a controlled Minecraft benchmark with a fixed catalog of 19 registered evolution chains, including 12 primary evaluation chains and seven calibration or probe chains, together with three graph-aligned paired probe families for transfer. The benchmark represents each task as a task-state graph, defines stage-level environment verifiers, assigns matched source and target roles, resets the target world, and permits only a declared agent artifact to cross the source-target boundary. For each probe, no-prior, related, unrelated, and shuffled source conditions are evaluated under matched environment-step budgets and five seeds; we report TSR, WGP, and VMP and retain provenance records. The benchmark reveals a consistent direct-capability gap between controller and planner-backed variants, while related experience yields no stable transfer: it does not improve either tool probe, its small wood-species gain hinges on one seed, and all intervals include zero. Stage audits further show that early wood-collection and crafting bottlenecks often leave later capabilities unobserved. MC-EvoBench thus offers a controlled testbed for durable, transferable embodied capabilities. Code and data are available at https://github.com/xzw-ustc/mc-bench-open-source","tldr":"背景与问题：保存记忆或在一次任务中成功，不足以证明获得可迁移能力；后续表现可能受携带资源、源任务暴露量和早期执行失败影响。方法：用任务状态图和阶段验证器记录进度，重置目标世界与库存，只让声明的 agent 工件跨任务；在匹配预算下比较相关、不相关、打乱经验与无经验条件。结果与结论：作者报告控制器的直接能力优于规划器变体，但相关经验未显示稳定迁移，微小收益受单个种子影响且区间含零；早期采集、制作瓶颈还会使后续能力未被观察。Insights：这提示具身 RSI 的首要难点是把能力变化与环境状态、执行机会分开归因；依据是严格重置后仍无稳定迁移。结论限于 Minecraft 探针和所测代理，不能外推到所有具身环境。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"具身持续学习评测; 经验迁移; 能力归因","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出 Minecraft 经验迁移审计：重置目标世界，只允许声明的 agent 工件跨任务，并匹配经验暴露和步数。本文证据显示相关经验没有稳定迁移收益。与 EmbodiedCLBench（arxiv:2610.13021）相比，本篇着重隔离物理状态混淆和经验来源归因，后者检验基础任务经验的组合泛化；两篇没有直接比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13285","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13285v1","title":"BoundaryEvo: Data-Model Co-Evolution at the Capability Boundary for Long-Chain Reasoning Distillation","authors":"Jiaming Su; Suorong Yang; Xudong Li; Tengchao Yang; Peng Ye","affiliations":"上海人工智能实验室；南京大学；同济大学；香港中文大学","abstract":"Distilling long-chain reasoning trajectories from large teacher models provides an effective way to improve the reasoning ability of small language models. However, existing methods typically select a fixed training set before distillation, overlooking that the usefulness of a reasoning example changes as the student evolves. This mismatch becomes especially costly when only a small number of teacher trajectories can be used for training. Besides, examples already mastered provide little new supervision, while examples far beyond the capability of student may be difficult to learn from. Training data should therefore adapt as model capability evolves, yet reliable data selection is difficult when the student is initially weak. To address these challenges, our key idea is to first establish the basic reasoning capability and then adapt the training data to the evolving capability boundary of the student. We propose BoundaryEvo, a two-stage data--model co-evolution framework. In Capability Priming, we directly distill a small set of teacher-generated long reasoning trajectories without using a separate model to judge and filter them, allowing the student to acquire an initial reasoning capability before capability-aware data selection. In Capability-Boundary Co-Evolution, we repeatedly select questions that the current student has not mastered but the expert can reliably solve, and update the training data as the student evolves. With only 1,000 training examples, BoundaryEvo consistently outperforms static and dynamic data selection baselines across 11 reasoning benchmarks, raising the original Qwen3.5-4B accuracy from 62.9 to 75.3 on IMO-AnswerBench and from 26.8 to 46.0 on AMO-Bench. The code and data will be made publicly available.","tldr":"背景与问题：固定蒸馏集会随学生能力变化而变得过易或过难；学生很弱时，单看错误也难判断哪些例子能提供有效监督。方法：先直接蒸馏少量教师推理轨迹建立基础能力，再持续选取学生尚未掌握、专家能可靠解决且题目质量合格的样本；学生更新后重新估计边界并刷新训练数据。结果与结论：作者报告只用 1,000 个训练样本，在 11 个基准上优于静态和动态选择基线；Qwen3.5-4B 在 IMO-AnswerBench 从 62.9 升至 75.3，在 AMO-Bench 从 26.8 升至 46.0。Insights：这提示有效课程信号需同时满足学习者有缺口、监督可学且目标可靠；依据是边界筛选机制和多基准结果。专家与分析器仍提供外部判断，不能称为完全自监督。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 推理蒸馏","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称先用少量教师轨迹建立学生初始推理能力，再按学生未掌握、专家可靠可解的边界反复更新数据。本文报告 1,000 例预算、11 个推理基准和多骨干实验。与 SynCo（arxiv:2610.11345）都闭环调整训练分布，但本篇采用学生—专家边界筛选与蒸馏，SynCo 联合强化学习优化合成器与推理器；无直接比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14118","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14118v1","title":"ClawLoop: Self-Improving Agents via Harness-Native Training Loop","authors":"Hansi Yang; Linji Hao; Hongyan Hao; An Wang; Han Wu; Qi Gu; Xunliang Cai","affiliations":"美团；北京大学","abstract":"The rapid advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs) has driven their deployment toward general-purpose harness environments, where LLM-based agents operate in sandbox workspaces and interact directly with file systems and shells. While numerous post-training pipelines exist for tool-use agents, their counterparts for harness-based agents remain scarce and are predominantly one-shot and teacher-dependent: a stronger external model synthesizes tasks and collects trajectories, the target agent is trained once, and evaluation results are consumed by human researchers rather than fed back into the loop. Such pipelines are inherently bounded by the capability of the external model and the scope of human prior, leaving no room for self-improvement. To address these limitations, we propose ClawLoop, a framework that enables self-improving without any external teacher model and with minimal prior dependencies. ClawLoop composes three phases into a self-sustaining cycle: Task Synthesis, which generates a diverse pool of training tasks via two complementary construction routines, applies diagnosis-conditioned difficulty growth followed by both agent-free and agent-based task validation; Training, which updates the agent via SFT and/or RL; and Diagnosis and Feedback, which analyzes the agent's rollout behaviors to produce a capability analysis report that will be used as feedback for task synthesis in the next iteration. Using Qwen3.6-27B as the loop model, ClawLoop yields consistent improvements on SkillsBench, Claw-Eval-Live, and ClawGym-Bench. The iteratively refined tasks are further transferred to smaller-scale Qwen3.5-4B and 9B models with gains across all benchmarks, validating data quality independently of the loop model.","tldr":"背景与问题：Harness agent 的任务空间宽，既有训练常依赖外部强模型造任务或收集轨迹，训练后评估结果又交由人分析，难以持续闭环。方法：系统合成并校验任务，用成功轨迹或强化学习更新模型，再从留出任务 rollout 诊断反复出现的短板，把分析反馈给下一轮任务生成。结果与结论：作者报告 Qwen3.6-27B 在三个基准持续提升；迭代任务转用于 Qwen3.5-4B 与 9B 时，各基准也有增益。摘要未提供具体提升幅度。Insights：这提示闭环的关键不只是生成更多任务，而是把诊断转成合格且针对当前能力的练习；依据是任务合成与能力报告相连。具体泛化范围、预算和长程稳定性仍需更多证据。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; Harness 智能体训练; 诊断反馈闭环","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称在 harness 环境中闭合任务合成、模型训练与能力诊断，不依赖外部教师；诊断结果直接反馈下一轮任务生成。本文证据为 Qwen3.6-27B 基准结果及小模型迁移的作者报告。与 AutoEnvScaling（arxiv:2610.14163）都让训练经验生成进入循环，但 ClawLoop 面向广泛 harness 任务训练，后者专门构建终端 RL 环境；无直接比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13098","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13098v1","title":"VETR: Execution-Grounded Self-Improving Agent for Symbolic Graphics Reasoning","authors":"Yingbo Ma; Kuangshi Ai; Gordon Dai; Chenglong Yu; Chaoli Wang; Hua Shen","affiliations":"纽约大学；圣母大学","abstract":"Visual agents for symbolic graphics reasoning depend on executable world representations, yet continued improvement remains bottlenecked by ambiguous supervision from final renders. Recent agentic systems refine scenes through repeated interaction, but they lack mechanisms to recursively extract actionable evidence from execution traces, overlooking which proposed symbolic edits survived, disappeared, or interfered during program execution. To address this, we propose VETR (Verified Execution Trajectories for Refinement), a framework that enables agentic recursive self-improvement over executable world representations for symbolic graphics reasoning. Within each task, VETR retains aligned program/render records with bounded runtime observations and introduces an execution refiner that compiles observed writes and state changes into constrained alternative programs. The refiner validates their endpoints and preservation conditions against captured runtime state; the ordinary visual verifier then assesses goal relevance. Repair construction makes no additional language-model calls, but can require additional executions. Evaluations on BlenderGym (280 tasks) and BlenderBench (27 released tasks) with GPT-5.6-luna and Qwen3.8-27B show that VETR consistently outperforms existing refinement strategies, including BlenderAlchemy and VIGA. Controlled ablations evaluate the contributions of execution refinement and role-asymmetric evidence organization under fixed generator-interaction caps.","tldr":"背景与问题：程序化图形 agent 主要根据最终渲染修订，图像差异难以说明符号编辑是否生效、被覆盖或互相干扰。方法：保留程序、渲染与运行时状态记录，从实际写入构造受限替代程序；重新执行检查指定端点和保持条件，再由常规视觉反馈判断目标相关性。结果与结论：作者报告在 BlenderGym 280 题与 BlenderBench 27 题上优于所比较的 refinement 方法；消融支持执行修订与证据组织的作用，但修复需额外执行。Insights：这提示改进信号的价值取决于能否观察编辑如何影响执行，而非单纯增加迭代；依据是执行修订消融。结论限于程序化 3D 场景，固定生成交互数也不代表总执行成本相同。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"执行证据驱动改进; 程序级自我修订; 视觉智能体","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称从执行写入和状态变化生成受约束的程序备选，检查运行端点与保持条件后，再由视觉 verifier 判断目标相关性。本文报告 BlenderGym、BlenderBench、两种骨干及消融，并与 BlenderAlchemy、VIGA 比较。其机制差异在于增加执行证据接口，而非仅依赖最终渲染；额外执行带来成本，材料未支持领域级优先性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13021","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13021v1","title":"EmbodiedCLBench: Evaluating Continual Learning for Self-Evolving Embodied Agents","authors":"Jie Huang; Yanan Chen; Ruixun Liu; Kaichen He; Xinyi He; Rui Huang; Zilong Zheng; Zhenliang Zhang; Yiwu Zhong","affiliations":"北京大学；香港大学；BIGAI","abstract":"Continual learning requires models to accumulate past experience and transfer it to new tasks. Despite substantial research on continual learning, existing work remains largely confined to non-embodied settings, without extending to embodied environments. To address this gap, we introduce EmbodiedCLBench, the first benchmark in embodied simulation for evaluating the continual learning capability of self-evolving agents. With compositional generalization as the core evaluation principle, our benchmark evaluates whether agents can first learn from basic tasks and then recombine the acquired skills to solve complex, unseen advanced tasks. Based on EmbodiedCLBench, we conduct extensive experiments across multiple agent harnesses and learning methods, revealing consistent limitations and distinctive behaviors. Our results show that while advanced tasks can be hardly solved under zero-shot setting, the experience from basic tasks enables consistent improvement. Such benefit from the experience remains stable even if the task complexity increases. However, this improvement does not scale accordingly with the number of learning samples, and current agents cannot extract meaningful information from additional experience. Collectively, our findings highlight continual learning as a fundamental yet underexplored capability, and our benchmark offers valuable resources for designing effective self-evolving agents in embodied environments. Our code and dataset are available at https://pku-value-lab.github.io/EmbodiedCLBench-homepage.","tldr":"背景与问题：持续学习研究多限于非具身环境，而常见具身基准也不直接检验既有经验能否迁移到未见任务组合。方法：构造从原子动作、基础家务到未见组合任务的评测，并比较零样本、保留交互轨迹与压缩技能总结。结果与结论：作者报告复杂任务零样本成功率约为 10%，有基础任务经验后可超过 30%；但增加学习样本没有相称的持续收益，ICL 与技能学习也无稳定胜者。Insights：这提示积累经验可能先带来明显收益，之后瓶颈转为提取有效信息，而不是继续增加样本；依据是样本扩张未产生一致增益。任务采用离线状态图，不能直接代表真实在线具身交互。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"具身持续学习评测; 组合泛化; 经验迁移","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出用具身组合泛化测持续学习：先执行基础任务，再测未见复杂任务，比较完整轨迹或技能总结。证据显示经验改善复杂任务，但额外学习样本未带来相称提升。与 MC-EvoBench（arxiv:2610.13829）相比，本篇聚焦组合任务迁移，后者聚焦物理状态重置和经验来源归因；未直接比较，摘要不足以证实首创。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12855","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12855v1","title":"Mitigating Capability Degradation in LLM Self-Improvement via Representation Geometry Regularization","authors":"Jiaqi Tian; Ting Long","affiliations":"吉林大学","abstract":"On-Policy Self-distillation is a self-improvement paradigm that enables large language models (LLMs) to improve their capabilities by leveraging the same model as both teacher and student under different conditioning contexts. However, we find that OPSD methods can progressively degrade previously acquired capabilities: queries that are correctly responded at earlier training stages may become incorrectly responded as optimization proceeds, even the overall performance continues to improve. Further analysis reveals that this degradation coincides with a deterioration of the geometry of hidden representations, characterized by reduced intra-cluster compactness and diminished inter-cluster separation. Motivated by this observation, we propose Representation Geometry Regularization (RGR), which preserves representation geometry during post-training by encouraging compactness within cluster and separation across cluster. RGR can be seamlessly integrated into existing OPSD methods without altering their core optimization procedures. Extensive experiments on multiple OPSD methods and benchmarks show that RGR generally alleviates capability degradation while retaining capability improvements. Our code is available in https://github.com/supermachinelearner/RGR.","tldr":"背景与问题：on-policy 自蒸馏可提升总体能力，但训练推进时，先前答对的问题可能变为答错，单看总体分数会掩盖这种退化。方法：作者观察到能力退化伴随隐藏表征簇结构变模糊，提出在自蒸馏中约束簇内紧致与簇间分离，尽量保留已有表征结构。结果与结论：作者报告在多种自蒸馏方法和基准上，RGR 通常减轻能力退化，同时保留能力提升；摘要没有给出具体效果量。Insights：这提示 RSI 评估应同时追踪新能力与旧题回归，而不能只看平均表现。表征几何是作者提出并分析的关联机制，现有材料不足以断言它是各类自改进的普遍因果瓶颈。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"自改进稳定性; 能力遗忘与回归; 表示几何","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者报告 on-policy 自蒸馏中总体性能上升时，旧题仍可能由对转错；此现象与隐藏表征几何退化相关，并提出保持簇内紧致和簇间分离的正则化。本文证据覆盖多种自蒸馏方法和基准，但摘要未给具体幅度。该工作主要缓解稳定性问题，不提出新的递归闭环；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13912","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13912v1","title":"RSI-Anything: Unlocking Recursive Self-Improvement with World Models","authors":"Taoyong Cui; Pinxian Zeng; Wanghan Xu; Hao Xiao; Shuhan Xue; Qiang Gao; Wanli Ouyang; Pheng Ann Heng; Zhenfei Yin; Yingcheng Wu; Ling Yang","affiliations":"PhAI Labs；香港中文大学；澳门大学；上海交通大学；复旦大学；牛津大学；斯坦福大学；北京大学","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) aims to transform interaction experience into persistent improvements, yet external feedback is costly and world-model predictions may become unreliable as policies evolve. We introduce RSI-Anything, a domain-general framework built on JEPA-Anything that uses predictive world models to guide action and learning-data selection. Observed feedback drives policy or workflow improvement and conditional world-model adaptation, while component and compatibility checks govern the retention of updated policy-model pairs. Across diverse computational and scientific domains, RSI-Anything demonstrates substantial gains. In code repair, with the coder fixed, success increases from 26.3% with a static verifier to 29.2% through predictive selection and 31.2% after world-model adaptation, at comparable test usage. Graphical user interface (GUI) evaluations showed higher task completion, while average actions decrease by 39.4%. Across five successive policy versions, laboratory-planning scores more than double from 21.80% to 46.01%. In reaction optimization, RSI-Anything achieves 96.15% mean best observed yield versus 82.16% for Bayesian optimization under the same 40-experiment budget. An end-to-end immune-science application further connects workflow evolution and predictive modeling with therapeutic hypothesis generation. These results demonstrate how predictive world models and retained system updates enable recursive improvement across diverse environments.","tldr":"背景与问题：RSI 需要把交互经验转成后续能力，但外部评估昂贵；策略更新还可能改变经验分布，使既有世界模型失准。因此，单独改策略或预测器都不能保证下一轮系统仍可靠。\n\n方法：RSI-Anything 用预测模型预判候选行动结果，帮助选择行动和学习数据；真实反馈再驱动策略或工作流更新，并在可靠性、数据和预算条件满足时调整世界模型。组件检查与策略—模型兼容检查决定哪些更新被保留，获准组合进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告，在固定 coder 的代码修复任务中，成功率从静态 verifier 的 26.3% 经预测筛选升至 29.2%，再经世界模型适配升至 31.2%，测试使用量相近；还报告 GUI、实验规划和反应优化结果。这些是作者实验，不是独立复现；材料不足以确认长期稳定性和广泛泛化。\n\nInsights：这提示瓶颈不只是预测准确度，还包括策略变化后模型是否仍适用，以及如何筛选更新组合；依据是论文提出的耦合更新问题和兼容性保留设计。该机制能否延伸至更广任务，仍需长期及统一预算评估。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 反馈驱动更新; 策略—模型联合演化","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者声称 RSI-Anything 将预测引导的行动与数据选择、反馈驱动的策略或工作流改进、条件式世界模型适配及策略—模型对保留连成闭环。本文证据包括摘要中的机制说明，以及作者报告的代码修复、GUI、实验规划和反应优化结果；固定 coder 的代码修复结果显示预测筛选及模型适配阶段分别伴随成功率上升，但不是独立复现。与 corpus 中 Memento 3（arxiv:2610.11794）相比，本篇强调预测器与策略更新的联合保留，Memento 3 则在冻结 LLM 下更新环境规则记忆与可执行模型；两者没有直接比较。编辑推断：相较 JEPA-Anything 的预测基础，本篇把预测接入递归更新与保留机制；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13025","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13025v1","title":"Evo$^2$: Evolving the Evolver through Weight-Harness Co-Evolution","authors":"Chejian Xu; Shujian Zhang; Wenxuan Zhou; John Lambert; Beck Chen; Bo Li; Andrew Hard; Rajiv Mathews","affiliations":"伊利诺伊大学厄巴纳-香槟分校","abstract":"Self-evolving agents are increasingly used to improve language model systems without human intervention through either weight updates or harness improvements. Existing approaches typically pursue these directions separately: some methods update model weights using self-generated experience, while others rewrite the harness that defines how an agent uses prompts, tools, context, and execution feedback. However, these approaches overlook the relationship between model weights and the agent harness. To connect these processes and ensure effective and smooth agent self-evolving, we propose Evo$^2$, a framework for weight-harness co-evolution. For harness updates, we design a unified dual-role pipeline that a single policy serves as both a Proposer, which writes harness edits, and a Reflector, which diagnoses their effects and guides revision. For weight updates, harness modifications and their execution outcomes guide the training of both the Proposer and the Reflector. We further develop EvoTIDE, a training pipeline that recovers usable trajectories through edit extraction and prefix continuation, then combines SFT with interleaved GRPO across the two roles. Extensive experiments across three coding benchmarks demonstrate that Evo$^2$ significantly outperforms existing self-evolution methods. It achieves 82.1% on Polyglot and 48.3% on SWE-bench Verified, compared with 62.6% and 41.0% for the strongest baseline, respectively. We also show that the evolved harnesses transfer to different tasks without further evolution and rank first in cross-benchmark evaluations. Our dual-role harness improvement framework is also able to extend to self-evolution with proprietary models, improving a GPT-5-mini agent's performance from 24.4% to 48.3%. These results demonstrate the applicability of the framework Evo$^2$ across domains and its broad transferability across models and tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：自进化 agent 常分别更新模型权重或修改 harness，忽略了二者的反馈关系：权重影响编辑质量，而编辑执行结果也能提供训练经验。分开优化可能无法让系统学会如何持续改进自身。\n\n方法：Evo² 让同一策略担任 harness 修改者和反思者；修改结果及执行反馈用于训练这两个角色。EvoTIDE 从编辑和反思轨迹中恢复可用训练数据，经监督微调与交错策略优化更新共享权重，再由更新后的策略继续搜索 harness。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告三个编码基准上的表现优于所比较的自进化方法，并称演化出的 harness 可迁移到其他任务；摘要给出 Polyglot 与 SWE-bench Verified 的对照分数。论文指出相关工作机制比较不是匹配性能基准，结果也不是独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示 harness 搜索不只是改善执行脚手架，也可能成为训练“改进者”的数据来源；依据是编辑反馈用于角色训练，更新权重又回到后续搜索。是否优于分别优化或其他联合方案，仍需统一预算、消融和多轮稳定性比较。","published_at":"2026-10-09","topics":"权重—harness 联合演化; 反馈驱动更新; 自进化策略训练","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者声称将 harness 编辑及执行结果用于训练共享的 Proposer–Reflector 策略，更新后的权重再指导后续 harness 搜索，形成相互反馈。本文证据包括机制说明、作者报告的编码基准及迁移结果。corpus 中 SIA（arxiv:2605.27276）与 HASE（arxiv:2607.03935）也涉及权重和 harness 的联合改进；本篇具体强调用编辑结果训练共享修改者与反思者。论文说明相关工作比较是机制比较而非匹配性能基准。编辑推断：这是共演化机制的具体推进，但优先性未确证；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12789","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12789v1","title":"EvoBelief: Falsifiable World Models for Self-Improving LLM Agents","authors":"Janet Wang; Jiang Guo; Yi Xiang; Jiaqing Yuan; Mingwen Dong; Hideo Kobayashi; Shuaichen Chang; Chandan K. Reddy; Jiarong Jiang","affiliations":"杜兰大学；亚马逊","abstract":"Self-evolving LLM agents typically improve how they act through accumulated experience, reflection, or skills. Yet even procedurally capable agents can fail when their beliefs about environment dynamics are incomplete, incorrect, or outdated. We study a complementary axis of self-evolution: evolving those beliefs during deployment. Such beliefs can support multiple tasks, but incorrect ones can also propagate across them. We introduce EvoBelief, a self-evolving world model that represents environment knowledge as falsifiable hypotheses. Unexpected outcomes and decision-relevant unknowns trigger hypothesis formation. Later observations and controlled experiments provide independent validation before a rule can guide predictions or plans within its supported scope. Counterexamples narrow or retire rules as the environment changes. The language model remains frozen, and each rule remains linked to its evidence and the decisions it changes. Across four benchmarks spanning static dynamics, hidden drift, and scientific discovery, EvoBelief improves task performance and reuses learned rules across tasks. On ALFWorld without actor-side transition memory, it improves success over the matched Frozen World Model by 23.9% and 31.3% with Claude Haiku 4.5 and GPT-5.4, respectively. On MiniGrid, it revises stale rules and recovers after unannounced dynamics changes. In DiscoveryWorld's Reactor Lab, it discovers and validates quantitative laws, completing 83.3% of Normal-tier and 58.3% of Challenge-tier instances, versus 0% for each evaluated baseline. These results demonstrate self-improvement through testable, revisable environment knowledge rather than model-parameter updates.","tldr":"背景与问题：Agent 即使会执行步骤，也可能因环境动态信念不完整或过时而失败；错误规则还可能传播到其他任务。方法：冻结语言模型，把环境知识存成带证据、适用范围和检验方式的假设。新观察触发验证，独立证据支持后规则才影响规划；反例会缩窄、降级或撤销规则。结果与结论：作者报告在 ALFWorld 中优于匹配的冻结世界模型，在 MiniGrid 中修订过时规则并适应动态变化；在 DiscoveryWorld Reactor Lab 也报告高于所测基线的完成率。Insights：这提示跨任务记忆要有可检验性、范围约束和撤销机制；依据是规则生命周期与漂移实验。证据来自有限模拟环境的作者实验，不能证明真实环境迁移或独立复现。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 可证伪记忆; 反馈驱动更新","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称将环境知识表示为可证伪假设，经过后续观察或受控实验验证才允许影响规划，并按反例缩窄或撤销规则。本文报告四类基准及冻结语言模型下的作者实验。作者讨论既有世界模型工作，但所给 corpus 未提供可关联的 paper_id，故不列 related；领域优先性未证实。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12367","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12367v1","title":"Which Skill to Distill? SGUID: Selecting a Compact Skill Bank for Model-Skill Co-Evolution","authors":"Yuhan Liu; Xiyao Ma; Zhongkai Sun; Xu Han; Chengyuan Ma; Benjamin Z. Yao; Chenlei Guo","affiliations":"New York University；Amazon","abstract":"Skills, reusable procedural guidance added at inference, can substantially improve LLM downstream performance (Li et al., 2026). Prior work retrieves skills from a bank by semantic relevance, then uses them as inference-time patches or for model distillation. The individual utility of each skill, however, is largely neglected. We first show that, in on-policy distillation where skill-conditioned policies serve as teachers, fewer than 25% of retrieved skills provide useful distillation signals. We then propose SGUID, a method for selecting a compact subset of skills for distillation. SGUID retains a skill only if it consistently yields effective learning signals during training. The selected skills are then distilled to produce a better model. Our results show that not all skills are worth distilling. Across four models from the Olmo and Qwen families, distilling 6 selected skills matches or exceeds full-bank distillation in mean avg@12 on three of the four models, and on all four after a second round that distills 3 newly selected skills, while the full banks are up to 11x larger. Importantly, SGUID supports stable model-skill co-evolution: after a distillation round, a new candidate bank is curated from the updated model's rollouts, and SGUID selects which skills to internalize next. In the second round, this loop selects 3 new skills and improves Qwen3-8B from 64.3% to 66.3%. The selection step is essential for stability: on Qwen3-4B, naively updating the model with unfiltered skills degrades performance, including a 0.3 percentage point drop on HMMT25, whereas SGUID improves HMMT25 by 0.5 points after the first round and 1.1 points after the second. These results identify skill selection as the key mechanism for stable model-skill co-evolution.","tldr":"背景与问题：推理时检索到的技能未必能教会当前模型；论文报告，不到四分之一的检索技能提供有用蒸馏信号，因此语义相关性不足以代表训练价值。\n\n方法：SGUID 观察技能条件教师在学生 rollout 上产生的、与验证器一致的学习信号，只保留训练早晚阶段都持续有效的技能。精简技能蒸馏更新模型后，再从新模型 rollout 整理候选技能并筛选下一轮，形成模型与技能库的反馈闭环。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告，仅蒸馏 6 个技能在四个模型中的多数模型上可匹敌或超过全库；第二轮选出 3 个新技能，Qwen3-8B 的均值由 64.3% 升至 66.3%。结果限于数学推理基准，是作者实验而非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示蒸馏瓶颈可能在监督信号筛选而非技能数量；依据是少量持续有效技能的结果，以及无筛选更新出现退化的报告。该结论仍受任务与验证器范围约束，不能外推到开放任务或缺少可靠验证器的场景。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"技能蒸馏; 模型—数据共演化; 自改进稳定性","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称按蒸馏过程中持续有效的学习信号筛选技能，再用精简技能库更新模型；更新模型的 rollout 用于整理新候选技能并启动下一轮。本文证据为四个 Olmo/Qwen 模型上的作者实验。相对具体已有技能选择与自蒸馏工作，全文讨论了技能有效性问题，但现有 corpus 未提供可核验的匹配性能比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：主要推进在于将筛选依据从语义相关性转到训练动态，领域优先性不能据此确立。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12235","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12235v1","title":"Language Models as AI Research World Models","authors":"Zijun Wang; Zewen Liu; Minhua Lin; Zhaotian Weng; Zhan Shi; Bing He; Yisi Sang; Dakuo Wang; Benoit Dumoulin; Wei Jin; Yuyin Zhou; Cihang Xie; Hanqing Lu","affiliations":"Amazon；UC Santa Cruz；Emory University；Pennsylvania State University；UC Santa Barbara","abstract":"AI research agents automate the cycle of proposing, implementing, and evaluating experiments, opening a path toward recursive self-improvement. Yet their ability to propose experiments outpaces their capacity to execute them in real environments, making outcome prediction a key capability for sustained self-improvement under limited experimental budgets. We investigate language models as Research World Models (RWMs), which predict the outcomes of candidate interventions across research environments. Our evaluation draws on over 2,600 experimental records from nine research environments spanning pretraining, post-training, and inference, representing more than 171,000 H100 GPU-hours of experimentation. Research knowledge acquired from real experimental experience improves RWM predictions of unseen interventions within the same environment (Spearman +0.27), and can be reused across environments. For example, using only pretraining experience from OLMo3, Marin, and Nanochat, an RWM reduces selection regret in the Qwen3 environment by 78% compared with zero-experience setting. These benefits extend to multi-round Autoresearch under a fixed selection budget: RWMs with in-env and cross-env research knowledge increase the best gain achieved by 15.8% and 11.6%, respectively. Ablations across 13 language models used as RWMs show that adding research knowledge can improve intervention ranking more than changing models or increasing reasoning effort alone. These findings support language models as RWMs and motivate accumulating experimental data for future RWM training.","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 能提出实验，却难以在预算有限时判断哪些干预值得执行；仅凭先验推理预测效果，也容易忽略模型、配方和环境差异。\n\n方法：研究世界模型接收环境、候选干预和既往实验记录，预测潜在收益并排序。被选实验执行后形成新记录，可供后续预测复用；因此闭环改善的是实验选择质量，不是本文已证明的模型参数递归训练。\n\n结果与结论：作者汇集九个环境的 2,653 条实验记录。同环境经验提高未见干预的排序相关性，跨环境经验也改善选择；在固定多轮选择预算下，作者报告经验增强的预测器取得更高最佳收益。这些是作者实验，覆盖范围受现有环境与记录限制。\n\nInsights：这提示稀缺实验预算下，积累可迁移的结果记录可能比单纯更换更强模型或增加推理量更关键；依据是跨环境预测和消融结果。边界在于迁移仍依赖目标环境描述与来源覆盖，预测排序也不能替代实际执行和不确定性估计。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"研究世界模型; 实验经验复用; 预算受限搜索","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出用语言模型预测候选研究干预的结果，并将真实实验记录用于后续预测和预算选择。本文证据包括九个研究环境上的记录、跨环境预测及多轮选择实验；描述显示经验通过上下文学习复用，未显示 RWM 权重本身递归更新。相对 corpus 中其他研究搜索工作，未提供直接匹配比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：其重要性在于把实验经验转化为候选干预排序信号，是否能普遍减少试错仍取决于环境覆盖。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12233","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12233v1","title":"ReSI: Recursive Safety Improvement toward Resistant and Resilient AI","authors":"Jingnan Zheng; Dongcheng Zhang; Yi Zhang; Ming Zhang; Qiaosheng Zhang; Youbang Sun; An Zhang; Xiangnan He; Tat-Seng Chua; Xia Hu; Bowen Zhou; Chaochao Lu; Xiang Wang","affiliations":"","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement, the participation of AI systems in improving their own capabilities, is beginning to move from theoretical prospect to practice, posing both challenges and opportunities for safety alignment. Models evolve through frequent updates, and their safety alignment requires continual adaptation to each new checkpoint. Meanwhile, with evolving red-teaming methods exposing new vulnerabilities, safety improvement for each checkpoint needs to mitigate exposed vulnerabilities and generalize to risks not yet revealed. Following R$^2$AI, we term these goals resistance to known threats and resilience to unforeseen risks. Recursive self-improvement, in turn, inspires an approach to both goals: safety alignment could likewise advance through successive rounds of evaluation and update. We therefore introduce ReSI, a recursive safety improvement framework that implements this approach through automated research. In each round, ReSI applies diverse red-teaming methods to identify vulnerabilities in the current target model, develops training recipes, and promotes the update with the largest safety gain among those passing a Pareto gate on capability retention as the next target model. Across four dense and mixture-of-experts models, ReSI matches or exceeds evaluated frontier models on in-distribution and out-of-distribution safety benchmarks, and outperforms alignment baselines on nearly all safety evaluations while largely preserving general capabilities. In particular, ReSI reduces the mean X-Teaming attack success rate across the four models from 86.01% to 31.45%, well below GPT-5.6-Luna's leading frontier result of 56.69%, indicating stronger resilience to attacks unseen during training. These findings support recursive safety improvement as a practical path toward resistant and resilient AI.","tldr":"背景与问题：模型持续更新会使旧安全对齐失效，新红队方法又不断揭示未见漏洞；只针对已知攻击训练，可能修补漏洞却损害能力或无法泛化。\n\n方法：ReSI 每轮攻击当前模型、生成训练配方候选并通过试验筛选，再以安全增益和能力保留门控晋级模型。新模型进入下一轮红队评估，反馈重新驱动配方搜索，形成有明确保留条件的安全更新循环。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告四种稠密及 MoE 模型在多项安全评估上改善，并称 X-Teaming 平均攻击成功率由 86.01% 降至 31.45%，同时大体保留一般能力。结果来自作者实验，外推范围受攻击集、训练预算和轮数限制。\n\nInsights：这提示保留门控不应只看目标安全指标，也需限制能力回归；未见攻击评估则是检验安全泛化的依据。由于搜索流程本身固定，现有证据支持迭代安全改进，不足以证明改进机制也在递归变强。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"递归安全改进; 红队反馈; 能力保留门控","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称每轮对当前模型进行红队探测、搜索安全训练配方，并通过能力保留门控决定是否将更新模型晋级至下一轮。本文证据包括四种模型及已知、未见攻击评估；论文明确搜索程序和评估协议跨轮固定，递归主要发生在目标模型更新。与 corpus 中其他论文没有匹配比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：这是将安全更新接入多轮模型改进流程，而非证明改进算法本身随轮次进化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12190","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12190v1","title":"DataSense-Bench: The First Step Toward an AI Scientist","authors":"Yudi Zhang; Mingyu Cao; Lu Yin; Mykola Pechenizkiy; Shiwei Liu","affiliations":"Eindhoven University of Technology；University of Surrey；ELLIS Institute Tübingen；Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems；Tübingen AI Center","abstract":"As claims about recursive self-improvement (RSI) and artificial general intelligence (AGI) proliferate, we ask a simple question: do frontier AI models have a sense of data, i.e., can they reliably select the right data for training? We introduce DataSense-Bench to study this capability through the fundamental problem of data selection and performance forecasting in machine learning. We ask AI agents to select and rank candidate training subsets that can be used to fine-tune a small LLM model. Agents are allowed to inspect the data, write and execute analysis code, and run model forward passes, but can not train the model or access the actual evaluation tasks. We then fine-tune the base model on each selected subset and evaluate its post-training performance under a standardized protocol. We instantiate the benchmark in terminal problem solving and tool use, selecting trajectories from OpenThoughts-Agent and EnvScaler and evaluating on TBLite and BFCL, respectively. We then evaluate the agents along two complementary dimensions: the post-training performance of the top-ranked subset, reflecting the ability to identify high-value training data, and ranking accuracy, reflecting the ability to predict the relative performance of the selected subsets. In our experiments, selection gains over random selection are limited; agents do not reliably rank their selected groups, and ranking ability does not hold consistently across tasks: Astra identifies the best group in all three tool-use runs but in only one of three terminal runs. Analysis of execution traces on both tasks shows that agents often use similar data signals while interpreting their training value differently.","tldr":"背景与问题：模型能看数据、写分析代码，不代表能判断哪些样本真正有利于训练；数据表面质量、损失或轨迹成功与特定模型的学习收益并非一一对应。\n\n方法：DataSense-Bench 让 agent 在不能训练模型或查看测试题的条件下选择并排序数据子集，随后用固定流程训练同一基座并测量结果，将事前判断与事后训练结果对照。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告相对随机选择的收益有限，代理对所选数据组的排序也不可靠，且跨终端任务与工具使用任务不稳定。材料支持这是一项能力审计，不支持模型已具备可靠数据科学家能力；范围限于两类轨迹任务和小模型微调。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 的数据选择环节可能是瓶颈，必须用训练后的真实结果验证预测，而不能把合理分析过程当作有效信号。依据是排序及跨任务稳定性不足；这不证明所有数据选择方法都无效，也不涵盖在线训练并持续校准选择器的闭环。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"训练数据选择; 收益预测; RSI 评测","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出将训练数据选择与收益排序分开测量，并在提交选择后再训练验证。这是对 RSI 所需能力的基准审计，不是自改进闭环本身。本文证据限于终端任务与工具使用轨迹及指定训练协议；与 corpus 工作没有匹配性能比较，未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：其价值在于把“挑中有用数据”和“能预测候选优劣”拆成不同可检验能力。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12086","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12086v1","title":"EvoAlloc: A Self-Evolving Resource Allocation Agent for Efficient Program Evolution","authors":"Yanning Dai; Yuhui Wang; Nanbo Li; Wenyi Wang; Jürgen Schmidhuber","affiliations":"King Abdullah University of Science and Technology；Sakana AI","abstract":"LLM-based program evolution relies on evaluation feedback to guide the iterative search for high-performing programs. However, evaluation is often computationally expensive, making it essential to allocate limited resources to candidates that can most effectively advance the search. Existing LLM-based methods typically rely on fixed allocation strategies throughout the search, potentially wasting resources on low-value candidates while overlooking promising ones. We propose EvoAlloc, a self-evolving resource-allocation agent that learns from search experience to revise its strategy for allocating computational resources across candidates. EvoAlloc periodically consolidates prior search and allocation outcomes into reusable experience, which informs subsequent strategy revisions. It further uses a counterfactual exploration mechanism to occasionally evaluate candidates denied resources by the allocator, revealing their outcomes to enrich its experience for future strategy updates. Across coding and agent-harness optimization benchmarks, EvoAlloc requires 59-82% fewer full evaluations and 61-89% fewer total LLM tokens to reach baseline-level performance. Moreover, under the same full-evaluation budget, EvoAlloc achieves 8.7-12.0% higher final performance.","tldr":"背景与问题：程序演化的完整评估成本高，固定分配规则可能把预算花在低价值候选上；更深一层的问题是，被跳过的候选没有结果，分配器会因自己的选择而看不到错误。\n\n方法：EvoAlloc 把评估资源分配策略本身设为可修订对象，从搜索与分配结果提炼经验；偶尔完整评估被拒候选，补上反事实反馈，再据共同验证结果决定是否采用新策略。\n\n结果与结论：作者在编码及 agent-harness 优化基准报告，达到基线表现所需完整评估减少 59–82%，同预算下最终表现高 8.7–12.0%。消融支持策略演化和反事实探索的贡献，但结论限于所测搜索任务与预算。\n\nInsights：这提示自适应资源管理的关键不只是更聪明地筛选，还要主动测量被筛选机制隐藏的失败；依据是反事实反馈设计及消融。其收益是否转移到昂贵实验、非程序搜索或不同预算制度，现有材料尚不能确认。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"搜索策略演化; 评估预算分配; 反事实反馈","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称从搜索与分配结果修订资源分配策略，并偶尔评估被拒候选，以揭示选择性反馈隐藏的结果。本文报告程序搜索与 agent-harness 优化基准上的预算收益和消融。与 corpus 中已有搜索策略演化工作，提供的材料不足以核验匹配性能比较或优先性；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：反事实探索是针对分配器自我遮蔽反馈的具体机制补充。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11959","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11959v1","title":"MiMo-V2.6: Scaling Reinforcement Learning Towards Self-Improvement","authors":"Xiaomi LLM-Core Team;  :; Zongming Qiao; Ziyue Hua; Zirui Ou; Zihao Yue; Zihan Jiang; Zhuo Huang; Zhiyang Chen; Zhixian Zheng; Zhipeng Xu; Zhengrui Ma; Yuyang Hu; Yuhang Dong; Yuechen Zhang; Yudong Wang; Yuanxin Liu; Yixin Yang; Yishuo Cai; Yikai Zhao; Yihan Yan; Yifan Zhang; Yifan Song; Xiyu Wei; Xing Zhang; Xin Zhang; Xiaoqian Liu; Xiaodong Ji; Xiangwei Deng; Xueyu Guo; Wenhan Ma; Weimin Xiong; Weikun Wang; Weiji Zhuang; Shuo Liu; Shuhuai Ren; Shuhao Gu; Shimao Chen; Shijie Cao; Shihua Yu; Shicheng Li; Shengjie Zhou; Shaolei Zhang; Rang Li; Qiying Wang; Qingkai Fang; Qianli Chen; Minzheng Wang; Liwen Wang; Linli Yao; Linghao Zhang; Liangyu Cheng; Liang Zhao; Lei Li; Jinhao Dong; Jinyu Xiang; Jianyu Wei; Jiangshan Duo; Huaqiu Liu; Huanjie Fan; Hongyi Guan; Hongshen Xu; Hao Tian; Hanyu Li; Hailin Zhang; Gang Wang; Fuli Luo; Feng Wei; Dong Zhang; Dawei Zhu; Chiheng Lou; Chenhong He; Chenhao He; Chenghua Liu; Bowen Ye; Bowen Shen; Boshen Xu; Bo Yang; Bingquan Xia; Bangjun Xiao; Baixuan Xu; Zhouxiang Mao; Zhiyang Zhang; Zhixiang Xu; Zhenru Lin; Zhengju Tang; Zhaojun Huang; Yuzhe Weng; Yuxing Xiang; Yuxiao Li; Yuheng Yang; Yuhang Wang; Yuchen Liu; Yuanyuan Tian; Yuanliang Dong; Yu Cheng; Yongzhe He; Yongshun Liang; Yong Wang; Yiyan Wang; Yitian Gong; Yijie Zhang; Yanshu Xin; Xun Zhang; Xingjian Zhao; Wenyu Yang; Wenshan Huang; Wenhao Li; Tingwei Huang; Tianyu Yu; Tianyang Lu; Taoyu Yang; Sinan Du; Shutong Tian; Shulin Du; Shengfan Wang; Shanchuan Fang; Qihao Zhang; Qibin Yang; Qian Yu; Qian Tu; Pengrong Xie; Peipei Wang; Peidian Li; Minkun Guo; Mingchen Shao; Luohan Gao; Lijie Wang; Liang Shi; Kaiqi Chen; Kaiming Liu; Kaifei Wang; Kai Yang; Jinlong Xue; Jiechen Zhang; Jiaxuan Liu; Hongxu An; Hao Peng; Hanglong Lü; Guonan Wang; Feiyu Yang; Fanyu Cao; Fangyue Liu; Fan Cui; Cong Wang; Chun Chen; Chenxu Bai; Chengxuan Zhu; Chenghua Wang; Boyi Zeng","affiliations":"Xiaomi LLM-Core Team","abstract":"Reinforcement learning (RL) is the central training paradigm for advancing large foundation models towards self-improvement. This report introduces the MiMo-V2.6 series, an omni-modal family that pushes the frontier of model intelligence by scaling RL compute. Prior to RL, we conduct mid-training on a broad multimodal corpus to provide ample exploration space, and build a solid infrastructure on the pretrained hybrid-SWA architecture to support subsequent scale-up. We scale RL compute along three dimensions: (1) larger batches and higher throughput, with an asynchronous training that consumes 1,568 samples and 2.7-3.7B tokens per step at context lengths of up to 1M; (2) more diverse and complex environments, spanning code, general, visual, and cyber domains under a mixture of agent harnesses; and (3) more grader compute, via groupwise agentic grading that yields more accurate reward signals for long-horizon tasks and steers the model towards shorter, more token-efficient solutions. To keep training stable at scale, we freeze the MoE router and establish a multi-layer defense against reward hacking. We further build infrastructure for mixed-task agentic RL, including a unified trajectory representation, high-concurrency multi-framework rollout, decoupled control and data planes, and training-inference consistency. We open-source the training dynamics, RL environments, and RL framework to facilitate reproduction and further research on scaled RL and model self-improvement.","tldr":"背景与问题：复杂 agent 任务的强化学习受限于探索环境、长程奖励信号及大规模 rollout 基础设施；扩大算力也带来稳定训练与奖励投机风险。\n\n方法：报告扩大 RL 批量与吞吐、丰富环境和 harness，并增加 grader 计算以提供组间细粒度反馈；同时采用稳定性措施应对大规模训练中的路由变化与奖励投机。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称模型在多个领域基准随训练推进而持续提升，并计划开放训练动态、环境和框架。摘要没有提供足以判断相对基线、总成本或关键消融的完整证据，也未展示改进方法自身递归更新。\n\nInsights：这提示规模化 RL 的有效性取决于环境与奖励信号质量，不是算力单变量问题；依据是论文对 grader、环境多样性及稳定性的共同强调。就 RSI 范围而言，这更像推动模型能力的训练报告，而非已证实的自我改进闭环。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"规模化强化学习; Agent 训练基础设施; 奖励信号","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者将主要贡献定位为扩大 RL 计算、环境多样性及 grader 计算，并报告模型训练期间性能提升。摘要未显示模型或训练器在多轮中递归修改自身改进机制；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：可作为规模化 agentic RL 的工程报告关注，但不宜仅凭 RSI 标题纳入递归机制进展。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12536","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12536v1","title":"EliteTable: Self-Improving Program Search for Executable Control Policies","authors":"Stuart Farmer","affiliations":"Casa Dilauro Independent Research","abstract":"EliteTable is a self-improving program-search algorithm guided by large language models (LLMs) that uses a fixed-capacity table of high-scoring solutions to guide new proposals, edits of existing solutions, and remixes of several solutions. Performance was evaluated across six Gymnasium control tasks, each with ten generations and fifty candidate slots per generation. Each task was evaluated across ten independently initialized searches. Candidate-score medians rose between the first and final generations in all six tasks, and selected-winner search-score medians rose in five. In CartPole-v1, the selected winner reached the search-score ceiling in the first generation of all ten searches. All ten paired held-out endpoints improved in four of the six tasks. BipedalWalker-v3 and CarRacing-v3 improved without reaching their reporting targets. Six of ten Acrobot-v1 searches declined on held-out episodes, and the median paired change was negative. The results document improvement during program search and the transfer of selected-winner gains to new episodes in some tasks. Comparisons and ablations are needed to establish EliteTable's relative performance and the contributions of its components.","tldr":"背景与问题：可执行控制策略可以用回报自动评估，但搜索集上保留高分程序并不保证新候选变好，也不保证收益迁移到新 episode。\n\n方法：EliteTable 将高分解保存在固定容量表中，用它们指导新程序生成、编辑和重组；候选经执行评估后再与精英竞争，留出回报不参与搜索决策。\n\n结果与结论：作者在六个 Gymnasium 任务上报告候选分数中位数均随代数上升，但留出端点仅四个任务的十次搜索全部改善；Acrobot 有六次下降且配对中位变化为负。作者承认仍需基线比较与消融，不能据此判断相对性能。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 证据应区分精英保留带来的搜索分数单调性与真正可迁移的能力变化；依据是 Acrobot 的搜索与留出结果分化。现有材料仅支持特定程序搜索的初步观察，不足以主张算法优势。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"程序搜索; 精英档案; 留出泛化","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称以固定容量精英表积累高分程序并用于新提案、编辑和重组，形成程序搜索反馈循环。本文证据是六个控制任务的多轮搜索及部分留出提升；作者明确指出缺少比较和消融。与 corpus 中既有程序演化方法没有匹配比较；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11803","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11803v1","title":"PRAXIS: Learning Dynamics of Self-Improving Models with Symbolic Archives","authors":"Venkat Margapuri; Mustafa Teber","affiliations":"","abstract":"Self-improving learning systems adapt data selection, optimization, and auxiliary symbolic components, inducing nonstationary objectives outside standard learning assumptions. We introduce \\textsc{PRAXIS}, a co-evolutionary framework that models generators, learners, and symbolic archives as interacting dynamical processes. We prove that KL-constrained generator updates and controlled archive-weight movement bound one-step objective drift, that archive updates suppress a program relative to any fixed comparator with a persistent cumulative utility advantage under sub-Gaussian noise, and that stochastic gradient descent achieves an average-stationarity guarantee whose degradation is governed by cumulative objective drift. Experiments across visual robustness, relational graph reasoning, and algorithmic graph reasoning exhibit generator stabilization, decreasing learner loss, and archive concentration consistent with these theoretical mechanisms.","tldr":"背景与问题：当数据生成分布和符号辅助信号也随学习过程变化时，训练目标不再固定；传统稳定性分析可能无法覆盖这种共同演变。\n\n方法：PRAXIS 将生成器、学习器及符号档案建模为耦合动态过程，并以受约束更新控制分布漂移、按效用调整档案权重，再分析学习器在变化目标下的稳定性。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称给出目标漂移界、档案相对固定比较对象的抑制性质及随机梯度平均驻点保证，并报告三类任务实验与理论机制相符。具体实验幅度和理论条件在实际任务中的适用范围，材料不足以确认。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 理论不能只分析模型参数更新，还应把数据分布和外部符号信号的漂移纳入稳定性条件；这是由其联合建模提出的启发，不等于已证明这些保证覆盖大语言模型或开放式自我改进。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"非平稳学习; 符号档案; 稳定性理论","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称以生成器、学习器和符号档案构成联合动力系统，并分析目标漂移、档案抑制和优化稳定性。摘要报告理论保证及三类任务实验，但当前材料包含疑似占位作者与单位信息，无法据此确认论文记录可靠性；实验细节也不足以核验理论假设的适用范围。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11655","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11655v1","title":"Harness Evolution Hits a Ceiling: When Weight Training Should Begin","authors":"Yuan Tian; Bing Hu; Hao Wang; Binghang Lu; Fang Wu","affiliations":"Independent Researcher；University of California, Berkeley；Purdue University；Stanford University","abstract":"Improving a long-horizon LLM agent means evolving the harness around a frozen model or training its weights. We let a self-evolving harness make the system stronger first, then cross seed and evolved harnesses with base and trained weights to learn which gains the trained model keeps and which still need the runtime. We show that the right lever can be read off the agent's failure composition: labelling failed trajectories by the first signal that fires separates process failures (blocked calls, loops, exhausted step budgets) from content failures (a delivered plan that is poor). Harness evolution repairs the former, the behaviour it instils can be trained into the weights, and content failures are what weight training is for. On DeepPlanning, a self-evolving harness loop lifts the held-out score of Qwen3.5-4B from 0.16 to 0.30 and of Qwen3.5-9B from 0.32 to 0.44; for 4B, held-out delivery rises from 55% to 90% while content failures are left for the weights. LoRA adapters trained on evolved-harness trajectories internalise the gain: under the original harness they add +0.13 on held-out tasks for both sizes; on 4B they stack with the harness to more than double the held-out score, and on 9B the adapter alone matches the full evolution line, cutting content failures from a quarter of trajectories to one in twenty. A placebo adapter trained on answer-shuffled trajectories falls below the base model. The loop transfers to WebArena-Lite (+0.09 on 117 unseen tasks), where the gain lives in what the model sees and adapters do not add to it. The result is a diagnose-then-intervene rule applied twice: read the failure composition to choose between harness and weights, then read what the accepted edits changed to decide which gains to train in. Scores are four-rollout means against fresh anchors, same-night except where marked, across eight models from six families and two benchmarks.","tldr":"背景与问题：长程 agent 失败可能来自工具阻塞、循环或步数耗尽，也可能是已交付方案本身质量差；笼统加权或改 harness，难以知道该动运行时还是模型权重。\n\n方法：论文按失败轨迹的首个触发信号区分过程故障与内容故障，先演化 harness 修复执行问题，再用演化轨迹训练 LoRA，测试哪些收益能脱离运行时内化到权重。作者还用 shuffled-answer placebo 和 fresh anchor 控制轨迹价值与选择噪声。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 DeepPlanning 报告 harness 与 adapter 对不同模型规模存在互补或替代关系，并在 WebArena-Lite 观察到迁移；该场景的增益来自运行时所见信息，adapter 未再增加收益。材料也揭示评分噪声、转换器偏差与任务范围等局限；非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示选择干预对象前应先分解失败原因，并进一步判断 harness 改变的是模型写出的内容还是可见信息；依据是两任务的 adapter 结果差异。该诊断规则来自有限基准，失败标签阈值与评估器也会影响归因，尚非普遍定律。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"harness—权重协同; 失败诊断; 收益内化","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称先按失败组成诊断 harness 与权重应分别处理的故障，再用演化 harness 轨迹训练权重，检验收益能否内化。本文在 DeepPlanning 给出多模型、留出集、placebo adapter 和噪声分析，并报告 WebArena-Lite 迁移；具体差异是按失败类型选择干预，但没有匹配基准证明相对优势。未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：失败归因与权重训练的对照提供了可检验的干预选择规则，尚需跨任务验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11345","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11345v1","title":"SynCo: Data Synthesis Co-Training for Self-Evolving LLMs via Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning","authors":"Wei Yang; Shawn Li; Yuehan Qin; Yawei Wang; Mingxi Wang; Shixuan Li; Tiankai Yang; Jiate Li; Jesse Thomason; Xuezhe Ma; Yue Zhao","affiliations":"University of Southern California；The George Washington University；Georgia Institute of Technology","abstract":"Self-evolving LLM agents promise to improve autonomously through continual interaction and learning, reducing their dependence on manually curated supervision. Realizing this promise requires not only updating the agent, but also evolving its training experience as its capabilities change. However, most existing pipelines rely on static datasets or separately updated synthesis models, causing previously useful tasks to become trivial while overly difficult tasks remain uninformative. This growing mismatch between agent capability and training experience limits sustained self-improvement. To address this problem, we propose SynCo, an agentic data synthesis co-training framework for self-evolving LLMs based on multi-agent reinforcement learning. SynCo jointly optimizes two independently parameterized agents: a Synthesizer that constructs training tasks from the Reasoner's evolving capability state, and a Reasoner that learns from the resulting experience. Each synthesized task induces multiple Reasoner rollouts whose outcomes provide complementary rewards to both agents. Correctness feedback improves the Reasoner, while task quality, answer reliability, and outcome-grounded teachability guide the Synthesizer. Their updates are fed back into subsequent synthesis rounds, allowing the task-solving policy and its training distribution to evolve together. Extensive experiments across eight mathematical reasoning benchmarks demonstrate that SynCo substantially outperforms a broad range of existing synthetic-data methods and controlled baselines, achieving the strongest overall performance while deriving most of its gains from previously unsolved problems.","tldr":"背景与问题：静态任务集会随学习者变强而变得过易，远超能力的题目又难以提供有效反馈；只定期刷新数据，仍可能让合成器与推理器各自优化、反馈脱节。\n\n方法：SynCo 让合成器根据推理器能力与任务覆盖生成可验证问题，推理器多次作答；正确性更新推理器，任务质量、可靠性及由实际作答结果估计的可教性更新合成器，之后两者共同影响下一轮课程。\n\n结果与结论：作者在八个数学基准报告优于多类合成数据基线，且多数收益来自先前未解问题；全文片段还报告，相较冻结合成器，联合训练仅略增有效训练任务比例，计算量相近。结果来自作者实验，任务范围主要为数学推理。\n\nInsights：这提示任务价值不应仅靠预估难度，而应由当前学习者的实际交互结果校准；依据是任务可教性信号及合成器对照。反馈依赖题目检查器和学习者自身行为，能否扩展到开放任务与更长训练仍未证实。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"自适应课程与数据合成; 模型—数据共演化; 多智能体强化学习","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称通过多智能体强化学习共同更新任务合成器与推理器；当前推理结果给合成器提供可教性信号，二者更新再改变后续任务分布与学习者。本文报告八个数学推理基准和冻结合成器对照。材料提到相关工作但没有可核验的匹配性能比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：贡献重点是把合成策略作为在线学习对象，而非仅周期性刷新静态训练集。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12176","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.12176v1","title":"Recursive Self-Improvement through Multi-Agent Self-Supervision","authors":"Hyunin Lee; Jinglue Xu; Jeffrey Seely; Donghyun Lee; Somayeh Sojoudi; Matei Zaharia; Yujin Tang","affiliations":"加州大学伯克利分校；Sakana AI","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement (RSI) of a model on non-verifiable tasks, such as open-ended research, faces a supervision bottleneck when its outputs exceed what even human experts can reliably assess, leaving the model itself (optimizee) as the best available optimizer and evaluator. However, a single model instance struggles to critique and improve its own complex reasoning under this homogeneous loop. To address this, we propose Multi-Agent Self-Supervision (MASS), an RSI method that alternates between evolutionary workflow optimization and supervised fine-tuning on self-generated trajectories. Guided by early findings that multi-agent topologies excel at complex reasoning, MASS prompts a single base model to iteratively propose, execute, and self-evaluate multi-agent workflows. Through an evolutionary search constrained by structural guardrails, the model optimizes these computational-graph-like orchestrations, discovering the most effective distinct roles and information routing for a given task. Over two MASS cycles with Qwen3.6-27B, the model achieves 1.2-1.6x higher performance per output tokens on four open-ended public benchmarks. Because the improved model subsequently acts as a better optimizer and evaluator, this alternating framework enables a continuous, recursive bootstrapping of the model's capabilities. Moreover, multi-agent traces are also more training-efficient: a student trained on them outperforms a single-agent student trained on 1.4x more training tokens. These findings suggest that jointly learning orchestration and bounded subagent execution from multi-agent trajectories can provide an effective signal for RSI.","tldr":"背景与问题：开放式研究等任务缺少可靠自动评分，结果可能超出人类专家稳定判断的范围；但让单一模型同时求解、评价和改进自身推理，也容易受同一偏见牵制。\n\n方法：MASS 先让模型搜索多智能体工作流，调整角色分工与信息传递，再把这些工作流生成的求解轨迹用于监督微调。更新后的模型重新担任求解者、工作流优化者和评估者，从而把工作流改进产生的数据带入下一轮能力更新。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告在 Qwen3.6-27B 上经过两轮 MASS，四个开放式基准的每输出 token 表现达到基线的 1.2–1.6 倍；多智能体轨迹训练的学生也优于使用更多 token 的单智能体轨迹学生。模型、任务和轮次有限，结果尚非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示监督瓶颈可能部分来自组织方式：分工和信息路由可产生比单体长轨迹更有效的训练信号。依据是作者报告的轨迹效率结果；由于优化与评估存在同源性，且只展示有限递归轮次，不能据此断言能在开放任务中持续自我纠错。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"多智能体工作流演化; 自生成监督与微调; 递归评估与优化","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者声称 MASS 交替优化多智能体工作流并用自生成轨迹微调共享模型，更新后的模型继续担任任务求解者、工作流优化者和评估者。本文证据包括有限轮次实验及外部强模型评估；附录将其与搜索后蒸馏、工作流搜索及联合改进方法作机制比较，但不是统一匹配性能基准。与 corpus 中 Evo²（arxiv:2610.13025）相比，MASS 优化多智能体工作流并微调模型，Evo² 训练 harness 修改和反思角色；两者没有直接比较。编辑推断：工作流轨迹为共享权重提供信号是具体增量，但同源自评与有限轮次限制递归泛化结论；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11794","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11794v1","title":"Memento 3: Model-Based Recursive Self-Improvement through Reflective Rulebooks","authors":"Haoyu Zhao; Zhengxu Yu; Zhiyuan He; Meng Fang; Rasul Tutunov; Haitham Bou-Ammar; Weilin Luo; Jun Wang","affiliations":"伦敦大学学院；华为诺亚方舟实验室；利物浦大学","abstract":"Learning to act in unfamiliar environments requires agents to infer how the world works and revise that understanding as new evidence arrives. Yet limited observations can support multiple world models that explain past interactions but predict different outcomes in unseen states. We introduce Memento 3, building on the Memento series to enable frozen LLM agents to continually learn explicit world models through external memory. The agent maintains a natural-language rulebook as persistent semantic memory, recording revisable hypotheses about environment dynamics while leaving unknown aspects underspecified. It compiles this rulebook into executable code for prediction and planning. Through a continual loop of observation, reflection, rule revision, compilation, and verification, the agent uses prediction errors to refine both the rulebook and its code. Updated code is accepted only when the LLM judges it faithful to the rulebook and cell-exact replay reproduces the observed transitions. We investigate this process as a model-based route to recursive self-improvement (RSI): the agent autonomously explores the environment, revises its world model, and uses verified updates to guide subsequent interaction and learning, while the underlying LLM remains fixed. A population extension maintains multiple world models in parallel, sharing interaction evidence and using their predictions to guide exploration. On ARC-AGI-3, the single-model agent clears every level of all 25 public games, achieves a mean Relative Human Action Efficiency (RHAE) of 100.0, and uses 44% of the human action count. In an Atari Pong case study, a learned feedback controller wins 21:0 in each of three evaluated episodes with different openings, without further LLM calls.","tldr":"背景与问题：在陌生环境中，少量观察可能同时支持多个世界模型；它们都能解释已发生的转移，却对未见状态作出不同预测。仅靠回放已观察数据，无法判定哪套规则能正确泛化。\n\n方法：Memento 3 让冻结 LLM 把环境假设写成可修订的自然语言规则手册，再编译为用于预测和规划的代码。新观察造成的预测误差促使规则或实现修订；候选代码需符合规则手册，并精确重现已观察转移，才会被接受并用于后续交互。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告其单模型系统在 ARC-AGI-3 的 25 个公开游戏中通过所有关卡，平均 RHAE 为 100，并在 Pong 的三个不同开局案例中以 21:0 获胜。后者是有限案例；回放验证只覆盖已有转移，不能证明对未见状态的模型正确性。\n\nInsights：这提示递归改进可以发生在外部记忆与可执行模型，而不必更新权重；依据是固定 LLM 下规则—代码闭环仍能改变后续规划。关键边界是观测覆盖：通过历史回放不等于掌握环境规律，需检查探索能否区分相互竞争的假设。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"世界模型与递归改进; 外部记忆与规则更新; 预测误差反馈","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者将 Memento 3 定位为 Memento 系列从策略与程序记忆扩展到显式世界模型：冻结 LLM 以规则手册记录可修订假设，将其编译成执行模型，以预测误差更新规则与代码，并通过规则一致性判断和已观察转移回放决定是否接受。本文证据支持该闭环及 ARC-AGI-3、Pong 作者实验。与 corpus 中 RSI-Anything（arxiv:2610.13912）相比，本篇侧重冻结模型下的环境规则记忆与可执行模型，前者侧重预测模型与策略更新的联合保留；两篇未直接比较。编辑推断：回放只能核验已观察转移，未见状态泛化仍未确定；与既有可执行世界模型工作的领域优先关系未证实。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11464","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11464v1","title":"Who Verifies the Verifier? Co-Evolving Inspectable Graders with Self-Improving Agents","authors":"Xing Zhang; Guanghui Wang; Yanwei Cui; Ziyuan Li; Wei Qiu; Bing Zhu; Peiyang He","affiliations":"AWS Forward Deployed Engineering；HSBC Holdings Plc., HSBC Technology Center, China","abstract":"We changed the agent: did it actually get better? Every self-improving agent loop answers this hundreds of times, and every answer comes from a verifier. On open-ended tasks none exists, so the loop is handed a hand-written rubric or a bare LLM judge grading output from a model like itself, inviting reward hacking and shared blind spots. We make the verifier the evolving object: an inspectable expression over small, mostly deterministic drawback detectors, synthesized from clustered failures, gated at birth, and selected for agreement with a ten-item anchored reference set plus consensus over unlabeled outputs, never for the agent's score. On MBPP+ it gains +0.21 held-out agreement over the hand-authored seed composition, on every seed, and ends ahead of the bare LLM judge it contains. One finding should change how co-evolved verifiers are validated: removing the anchor guards collapses the verifier into a vacuous always-pass grader, yet that collapsed verifier trains skills just as well. Downstream task score cannot certify a self-evolved verifier. Score does answer sufficiency, and there an evolved verifier can substitute: Double Ratchet, pairing the verifier with a lifecycle-managed skill loop, retains 88-110% of the lift that ground truth or a rubric buys the same loop, across code generation, enterprise text-to-SQL, and reference-free report generation. When evolved skills gamed the report rubric, an outer judge caught it and one added detector repaired it; the judge itself was wrong until given the task contract.","tldr":"背景与问题：自改进循环每轮都要判断 agent 是否变好，但开放任务往往没有现成 verifier；手写 rubric 或由相似模型担任 judge，可能共享盲点并诱发奖励投机。更关键的是，训练后的任务分数也未必能证明评分器本身可靠。\n\n方法：论文把 verifier 作为演化对象，由失败聚类生成可检查的细粒度缺陷检测器，再以少量锚点参考和未标注输出共识筛选组合，不按 agent 得分选 grader。之后将演化出的 grader 接入技能改进循环，并用外部锁定评估监测结果。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告 MBPP+ 留出一致性较手写初始组合提高约 0.21；消融移除锚点防护后，grader 退化为始终放行，但技能训练表现仍相近。因此，下游任务得分不足以认证自进化 verifier。结果限于指定任务、锚点和实验设置，报告生成场景也没有金标准。\n\nInsights：这提示验证器需要独立于被优化任务表现的有效性检验；依据是退化 grader 仍能支撑相近技能表现的消融。该发现针对特定任务和锚点规模，不能直接证明锚点方案普遍可靠；应将 verifier 的留出一致性与下游收益分别报告。","published_at":"2026-10-08","topics":"评估器递归改进; 锚点监督与验证; 奖励投机与安全","added_on":"2026-10-13","novelty_summary":"作者声称将 verifier 本身作为演化对象，以失败聚类合成可检查的 drawback detectors，并用十项锚点参考与未标注输出共识选择，而非依据 agent 任务得分；Double Ratchet 将其接入技能生命周期循环。本文证据包括 MBPP+ 留出一致性结果，以及移除锚点防护后 verifier 退化为始终放行、技能训练表现却相近的消融。与 corpus 中 MASS（arxiv:2610.12176）同样涉及自评信号，但 MASS 优化工作流并用轨迹微调，本文直接演化 grader；无直接比较。编辑推断：消融揭示了验证器评估的盲点，但不足以证明此类 verifier 首创或可迁移至更广任务；未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10498","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10498v1","title":"EmbodiedRSI: Active Continual Robot Learning Through Hypothesis-Guided Co-Evolution","authors":"Python Song; Zhixuan Liang; Kelsey Fu; Mengdi Wang; Junfeng Yang; Shilong Liu","affiliations":"Columbia University；Princeton University","abstract":"Robot foundation models provide strong visuomotor control, yet their performance can degrade when object positions or task instructions change. Further improvements often require post-training on substantial robot data, which can be costly to collect through methods such as teleoperation. Agentic harnesses can adapt around the model, but current self-evolving harnesses use robot trials inefficiently when deciding which code and skill changes to pursue. We introduce EmbodiedRSI, a self-evolving agentic harness that autonomously decides where to explore next and turns the resulting physical interaction into improved code and skills. EmbodiedRSI realizes this through a Fast-Slow Dual-System Architecture, in which competing code and skill hypotheses are maintained in a Hypothesis Graph. Value-of-Information Experiment Selection chooses physical experiments that can distinguish these hypotheses. Their outcomes guide Code-Skill Co-Evolution. The Slow System builds Hierarchical Memory, and Reward-Grounded Memory Learning selects effective memory according to their value for later Fast-System improvement. On RoboCasa365, EmbodiedRSI reaches 77.0% overall success and 71.3% on Composite-Unseen, compared with 40.1% for the best baseline. EmbodiedRSI also reaches 86.8% overall success on LIBERO-Pro. Beyond benchmark performance, EmbodiedRSI transfers zero-shot to real-world robot, achieving 71.3% overall success across multiple challenging tasks.","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人微调需要昂贵交互数据；仅反复试错修改代码和技能，可能重复探索相近方向，也难判断两者组合是否真的互补。\n\n方法：EmbodiedRSI 将竞争性代码、技能假设与证据存入图中，按预期信息价值选择能区分假设的物理试验；结果驱动代码—技能联合更新，慢速记忆模块再根据后续改进价值学习保留哪些经验。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告 RoboCasa365、LIBERO-Pro 上的成功率高于所列基线，并称从模拟到真实机器人零样本迁移。摘要给出若干比例，但未提供完整任务覆盖、预算和实地重复次数；这是作者报告而非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示昂贵交互应被视为辨别竞争解释的实验，而非单纯收集更多轨迹；依据是信息价值选试验的机制。结论边界在于假设质量、模拟到现实差异及试验预算，尚不能推断长期自主部署会持续改进。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"具身 RSI; 主动实验选择; 代码—技能共演化","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称用假设图表示代码和技能候选，以信息价值选择物理实验，再按匹配试验结果共同更新代码与技能，并按后续收益训练记忆选择。本文报告模拟基准及真实机器人迁移的作者结果；没有与 corpus 论文匹配比较，未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：将物理试验用于区分竞争假设，而非只作为反复试错，是明确的机制设计；实地泛化还需更多证据。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10426","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10426v1","title":"CoTrace: Data Recipes for Training Terminal Agents with Harness-Model Co-Evolution","authors":"Jixuan Chen; Jiaxin Zhang; Qinyuan Ye; Yada Pruksachatkun; Haoxiang Zhang; Jingming Zhuo; Yifan Zhang; Yutong Dai; Juntao Tan; Xiangyu Peng; Silvio Savarese; Zeyuan Chen; Lianhui Qin; Chien-Sheng Wu","affiliations":"University of California, San Diego；Salesforce AI Research；University of Washington","abstract":"Terminal-agent capability depends jointly on model weights and the runtime harness that formats prompts, binds tools, and handles error recovery. Existing harness-model co-evolution approaches improve both components, yet often treat trajectories produced during harness search as an undifferentiated replay buffer. This practice overlooks that a trajectory's value for model training depends on the harness under which it was generated. To systematically analyze this interface, we establish an alternating co-evolution framework that decouples harness search and policy training through component-wise promotion decisions. Within this framework, we introduce CoTrace, a harness-aware data recipe that explicitly governs trajectory routing, provenance matching, and curriculum refresh. Under CoTrace, recurring execution failures guide harness synthesis, while policy training is strictly conditioned on verified rollouts matched to the adopted runtime for supervised fine-tuning (SFT) or fresh online interactions for reinforcement learning (RL). On the Tmax promotion split, CoTrace advances Qwen3.5-9B from 78 to 88 solved tasks under supervised fine-tuning while an online reinforcement variant reaches 90. Specifically, a compact harness-matched corpus produces steady model gains at substantially lower compute than much larger corpora pooled across sibling harnesses. Furthermore, evaluations on Terminal-Bench 2.1 and SWE-bench Lite show that out-of-distribution transfer depends fundamentally on harness compatibility, where maintaining consistency between training and evaluation runtimes prevents procedural execution breakdowns observed under foreign scaffolds.","tldr":"背景与问题：模型和 harness 交替变化时，轨迹的训练价值取决于其生成时的运行时；把不同 harness 的成功轨迹混在回放池里，可能让模型学到部署时不适用的操作程序。\n\n方法：CoTrace 将失败证据用于 harness 合成，只把已验证且与当前采用 harness 匹配的轨迹用于 SFT，或在同一运行时下生成新 RL 交互；分别固定另一组件评估候选，以避免把增益归错对象。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 Tmax promotion split 报告 Qwen3.5-9B 从 78 个解题任务升至 88（SFT）或 90（在线 RL）；紧凑匹配语料在较低计算下比跨 sibling harness 混合的大语料更稳定。外部基准结果也显示运行时兼容性影响迁移。均为作者实验。\n\nInsights：这提示数据规模不是联合演化的唯一瓶颈，轨迹来源与部署 runtime 的一致性可能决定数据是否可学；依据是匹配与混合语料的对照。结论受任务集、晋级划分和所测 harness 限制，长期运行时变化及独立复现仍待验证。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"模型—harness 共演化; 轨迹来源与匹配; 终端智能体","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称显式管理轨迹来源、harness 匹配和课程刷新，将故障轨迹路由至 harness 搜索、经验证且匹配运行时的成功轨迹用于模型训练，并按组件独立晋级。本文在 Tmax 及外部任务报告作者实验。与 corpus 中相关模型—harness 共演化工作机制相邻，但没有匹配实验比较；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：此处强调的数据来源与运行时兼容性是共演化接口的具体细化，不足以主张整体范式首创。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10310","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10310v1","title":"RSIGym: A Flexible Environment for Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Fanqing Meng; Lingxiao Du; Haocheng Lu; Qiguang Chen; Ziqi Zhao; Zijian Wu; Jiayuan Zhuo; Mengkang Hu; Michael Qizhe Shieh","affiliations":"National University of Singapore；Evolvent AI","abstract":"Recursive self-improvement requires carrying accepted changes into later improvement cycles, while studying agent-proposed changes also requires substantial research infrastructure. Existing settings often leave agents to rebuild routine infrastructure or restrict exploration to individual components. We introduce RSIGym, an agent-native research environment based on Everything as a Service (EaaS). RSIGym exposes training, inference, rollout, evaluation, and sandbox execution through reusable services, with shared budget and permission controls supporting Data, Harness, and Joint improvement tracks. This design enables agents to investigate individual interventions and jointly optimize data, training settings, and execution harnesses within the same environment. We define RSI-Index as the mean fraction of the remaining performance gap closed across five benchmarks covering software engineering, terminal interaction, mathematics, scientific reasoning, and skill-based tasks. Comparing six frontier research models in independent Joint runs, Opus 5 achieves the highest RSI-Index of 0.4809 under a $500 platform-service budget per benchmark run. Its selected systems improve all five benchmarks, raising SWE-bench Verified from 17.67% to 50.33% and AIME from 31.67% to 97.78%. Additional experiments examine DSH-harness refinement, budget variation, and restricted network access, while recorded trajectories reveal how agents diagnose failures and select candidates. We open-source the full RSIGym codebase and results to support reproducibility and further research.","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 若每次都需重建训练、推理和评测基础设施，预算会耗在工程准备；只开放单一组件的基准又难检验数据、权重与 harness 的交互。\n\n方法：RSIGym 将训练、推理、rollout、评测和沙箱封装为服务，并统一预算与权限；设置分轨与联合轨道，让 agent 在约束下提出、评估并选择系统修改。\n\n结果与结论：作者比较六个研究模型，报告 Opus 5 在五个基准的 RSI-Index 最高，并给出 SWE-bench Verified、AIME 的提升。关键限制是论文明确承认，所得系统是否改善后续研究循环尚未评估；因此分数表示预算内目标系统改进，不等同递归能力增强。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 基准应把基础设施复用、预算审计与跨轮继承作为实验条件，同时区分“改进目标系统”和“改进产生改进的过程”。该区分来自论文的范围声明；平台可支持后续研究，但当前结果不能证明递归进展。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"RSI 研究环境; 预算与权限审计; RSI 评测","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出共享服务、权限与预算控制的平台，支持 agent 修改数据、训练设置及 harness，并报告单轮研究运行中的系统提升。论文明确指出，所得系统是否改善后续研究循环尚待评估；这是 RSI 环境与基准贡献，不是已证实的递归闭环。与 corpus 中的其他研究环境未进行匹配性能比较。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10120","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10120v1","title":"RewardWeaver: Long-Horizon Interactive Learning for Language Agents via Self-Evolving Reward Adaptation","authors":"Hengbo Xiao; Boyao Zhang; Purui Liu; Yuxuan Zheng; Haoran Yin; Haibo Liu; Fan Zhang","affiliations":"Yoolee.ai；University of Science and Technology of China；Peking University；Tianjin University","abstract":"Reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards (RLVR) has driven substantial progress in domains where task outcomes can be reliably evaluated, but long-horizon interaction remains challenging due to sparse terminal feedback and difficult credit assignment. Process rewards provide denser supervision, yet the capabilities most relevant for training can change as the policy evolves: a behavior that is easy to evaluate or frequently deficient need not be the bottleneck currently limiting task success. We introduce RewardWeaver, a self-evolving reward adaptation framework for language agents in long-horizon interaction. RewardWeaver maintains a validated capability space in which the semantics of admitted Rubrics remain fixed, and closes the loop between policy optimization, task evaluation, failure attribution, and reward adaptation. After each training stage, it performs outcome-grounded backward attribution on low-outcome trajectories, aggregates recurrent and policy-controlled capability bottlenecks, and dynamically selects the corresponding process rewards for the next stage. Recurrent failures not covered by the existing capability space trigger a separate, controlled expansion procedure. We evaluate REWARDWEAVER on SOTOPIA, Amazon?HistoryPrice, and a newly constructed Sales Benchmark. Across social interaction, bilateral bargaining, and domain-specific sales, REWARDWEAVER establishes new state-of-the-art (SOTA) results. Ablations further demonstrate the importance of dynamic reward allocation, failure-grounded attribution, and stable semantics for admitted capabilities.","tldr":"背景与问题：长程互动只有稀疏终局奖励，过程奖励虽更密集，却可能在策略变化后继续优化已不再是瓶颈的行为；频繁缺陷也不必然是失败原因。\n\n方法：RewardWeaver 从低结果轨迹中回溯归因，聚合反复出现且由策略控制的能力瓶颈，动态选择下一阶段过程奖励；已纳入能力的 Rubric 语义保持固定，新能力只有通过独立验证程序才可加入。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告在社交互动、议价与销售任务上优于所比较方法，并以消融支持动态分配、失败归因和语义稳定的重要性。摘要未给效果量、预算或跨模型细节，不能据此判断实际优势幅度。\n\nInsights：这提示过程奖励的关键不是不断改写评分标准，而是稳定定义能力后，随失败瓶颈变化重新分配训练信用；依据是方法对语义与当前相关性的区分。失败归因和 Rubric 评估仍可能有偏，跨领域及独立验证尚不足。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"自适应过程奖励; 失败归因; 长程交互学习","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称以低结果轨迹中的反复、可归因失败决定下一阶段启用哪些固定语义 Rubric，并通过验证程序控制新能力加入。本文摘要给出三类交互基准和消融结论，但没有提供具体量化效果；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑推断：方法区分稳定的评价语义与动态训练优先级，是其相对一般奖励更新的具体设计差异。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09856","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.09856v1","title":"Self-Evolve With a Reference:Anchored Training of Tool-Integrated Agents","authors":"Wenjie Liao; Liangjie Zhao; Zehong Cao","affiliations":"Waseda University；Adelaide University","abstract":"Self-evolving tool-integrated agents learn from tasks and feedback generated within their own training loop. A Curriculum Agent generates tasks, while an Executor Agent learns from self-consistency signals through reinforcement learning. However, relying solely on the current Executor for feedback has two limitations: group-relative advantages vanish under full consensus, while uncertainty-based curriculum rewards favor disagreement without showing whether the generated tasks support further learning. These limitations motivate an additional reference beyond the current Executor. We propose \\textit{AnchorLoop}, which introduces a frozen copy of the previous iteration's Executor as a historical reference and reuses it on both sides of the training loop. For the Executor, the anchor provides a cross-reference advantage that evaluates current outputs against both current and historical majority answers. For the Curriculum, it provides an agreement-based reference based on differences in sampled majority agreement. Since the Executor and anchor have identical parameters during Curriculum training, this comparison serves as a proxy for task selection rather than evidence of inter-version improvement or correctness. Across 13 reasoning benchmarks, AnchorLoop improves over Agent0 by 2.5\\% on mathematical reasoning and 2.8\\% on general reasoning tasks. It also maintains higher effective-advantage variance and continues improving in later iterations as the unanchored baseline shows diminishing gains. These results demonstrate the benefit of introducing a lightweight historical reference into self-evolving tool-integrated agents without external task or answer supervision.","tldr":"背景与问题：依赖当前策略自一致性的训练，在采样答案完全一致时相对优势消失；课程生成若只追求分歧，也无法知道题目是否真的有学习价值。\n\n方法：AnchorLoop 保留上一轮 Executor 作为冻结参考，在求解训练中比较当前答案与当前、历史多数答案；在课程训练中以两组采样一致率差异塑造任务奖励。后者只是选择代理，因为该阶段两模型参数相同，不能当作版本进步或正确性证据。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 13 个推理基准报告较 Agent0 有数学和一般推理增益，并称后续迭代仍改善，而未锚定基线趋于停滞。结果为作者实验；摘要未详列预算和各任务方差。\n\nInsights：这提示历史参照可补充当前自一致性反馈，但参照的解释必须依阶段区分；依据是作者对课程信号局限的明确界定。锚点并不自动提供真值，也不能解决完全共识时优势仍为零的问题，故泛化和抗共同错误能力仍待验证。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"历史参照反馈; 自监督强化学习; 课程生成","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者将前一轮 Executor 冻结为历史锚点，用于当前策略的交叉优势及课程任务反馈。作者明确承认课程阶段模型参数相同，采样差异不能证明跨版本进步或答案正确。本文报告 13 个推理基准结果；与 corpus 中其他工作没有匹配实验，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10623","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10623v1","title":"Recurrent Self-Improvement: Dynamic Cross-Loop On-Policy Distillation for Looped Language Models","authors":"Yi Wang; Rui Qian; Yu Li; Haoyang Yao; Wenjie Wang","affiliations":"ShanghaiTech University；Fudan University；Southeast University；Peking University","abstract":"Looped Language Models (LoopLMs) offer a parameter efficient approach to scaling reasoning by reusing shared parameters across recurrent computation steps. Despite their promise, effective post-training of LoopLMs remains challenging. Existing approaches either provide reward based supervision that is sparse or costly to extend across loops, or rely on external teachers or privileged information, leading to limited teacher availability or teacher-student context mismatch. To address these limitations, we introduce LoopOPD, a cross-loop on-policy distillation framework that uses additional recurrent computation within a LoopLM as its own source of supervision. LoopOPD uses a frozen terminal loop policy as a compute privileged teacher for an intermediate loop student on student generated rollouts, providing dense supervision without an external teacher or privileged information. We further propose Dynamic LoopOPD (D-LoopOPD), which continually refreshes the terminal loop teacher as the shared model parameters are updated, enabling recurrent self-improvement. We characterize how distillation updates propagate across loop depths and derive sufficient conditions under which a single update yields simultaneous local improvement at both loop depths. Experiments on Ouro-Thinking models show that LoopOPD improves mathematical reasoning, while D-LoopOPD yields further gains through dynamic teacher updates. Despite being trained only on mathematical data, the resulting models also improve on general reasoning and code generation benchmarks, demonstrating that recurrent computation can serve as an effective source of supervision for LoopLMs. Our code and model checkpoints will be released upon acceptance.","tldr":"背景与问题：LoopLM 用共享参数反复计算，却难以把稀疏的终局奖励直接分配给中间循环；外部教师可能不可得，带特权信息的自蒸馏又会造成师生上下文不匹配。\n\n方法：LoopOPD 让中间循环在自身生成的轨迹上匹配终端循环的 token 分布，将额外循环计算变成密集监督。D-LoopOPD 每步改用当前终端循环作教师；学生更新共享参数后，终端教师也随之改变，并在后续步骤继续提供监督。\n\n结果与结论：在 Ouro-Thinking 上，作者报告 LoopOPD 改善数学推理，动态教师进一步优于冻结教师；全文片段给出 Ouro-2.6B-Thinking 的 AIME 2024 Avg@16 从 62.08 升至 71.67，并称跨循环深度均有改善。跨任务收益限于数学训练后的指定推理和代码基准。\n\nInsights：这里值得检验的不是“自蒸馏是否有效”，而是共享参数是否能把中间循环的学习稳定传回终端策略；论文的局部改进定理也要求梯度对齐等条件。因此，机制成立依赖特定更新几何，不能推成共享参数更新普遍有益。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"循环语言模型; 跨循环蒸馏; 递归自改进","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称 LoopOPD 以模型的额外循环计算监督中间循环，D-LoopOPD 再利用共享参数更新后的终端循环动态刷新教师。本文证据包括跨循环更新分析及 Ouro-Thinking 作者实验，全文片段报告数学推理改善，并给出 AIME 2024 Avg@16 结果。相对 OPD 与 OPSD，具体差异是教师优势来自额外循环计算，且师生在同一前缀上生成分布；这些是本文对既有机制的比较，不是与 corpus 中独立论文的匹配实验。编辑判断：这是循环模型内部监督的具体推进；未证实领域级新颖性，且没有独立复现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10611","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.10611v1","title":"Verification and Self-Improvement in Agentic AI: Foundations and Limits","authors":"Chien-Ping Lu","affiliations":"","abstract":"Agentic AI systems can improve by searching longer, receiving additional support, or modifying how they propose and verify outputs. A performance score does not distinguish these mechanisms. We compare these changes through bounded verification with hidden terminal randomness. A stage specifies admissible transcripts, polynomial bounds, an alternating verification protocol, and a terminal checker. Its native reach uses default support; its closure frontier permits all support already admitted by the interface. Under a uniform pointwise probability gap and task-relative soundness, these are well-defined languages. We prove that independent majority amplification preserves both languages, whereas existential acceptance over random tapes can admit incorrect outputs. Exact verification is the zero-randomness case, with placement and completeness results. The randomized-verifier classes satisfy $Σ_k^{\\mathrm{P}}\\subseteqΣ_k^{\\mathrm{RV}}\\subseteqΣ_{k+1}^{\\mathrm{P}}$; strict enlargement and depth separation require explicit complexity assumptions, while $\\mathrm{BPP}=\\mathrm{P}$ yields exact companions with the same frontiers. Representation analysis separates invariant acceptance from core-versus-support labels that can change under refactoring. For recursive self-improvement, uniformly bounded self-modification under a common sound interpreter and fixed verification protocol remains within the same verification class. A separate conditional-error budget controls false selection across adaptively chosen candidates. A quota-enforced XOR-synthesis family separates unbounded ratios of search success from changes in the accepted languages; exact and probabilistic audits check the resulting evidence requirements. The framework ties self-improvement claims to obligations on correctness, admissible evidence, verification resources, and selection error.","tldr":"背景与问题：成功率上升可能来自搜索更久、获得更多支持或改变检查器；单看分数无法判断系统只是更容易找到已有解，还是扩展了可接受的正确任务范围。\n\n方法：论文将系统阶段表示为有界交互、支持接口、验证协议与终端检查器，分别定义默认支持下的可达范围和接口许可支持下的范围。它证明独立多数放大保留这两种范围，而随机带上任一次通过可能错误接纳输出；另为自修改和候选选择规定错误预算。\n\n结果与结论：在共同可靠解释器和固定验证协议等条件下，有界递归自修改仍处于同一验证类；有限 XOR 合成例区分搜索成功率提高与接受语言改变。这是条件性理论结果，不是现实 agent 的经验检验。\n\nInsights：该框架把“性能更好”拆成搜索、接口和验证语义三种可分别核查的变化；但其保证依赖明确的可靠性合同，不能直接认证只有经验准确率的学习型评估器。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"RSI 可证伪性与治理; 验证理论; 选择误差","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者提出以有界验证、任务正确性和可容许证据，形式化区分搜索效率改善、支持接口变化与接受边界变化；关于递归自修改的结论依赖共同可靠解释器、固定验证协议和一致有界修改等前提。本文证据是复杂性理论推导及有限 XOR 合成实例，并非 agent 性能实验。corpus 中没有可直接比较的形式化工作；未证实领域级新颖性。编辑判断：其贡献在于明确 RSI 主张需要何种正确性与选择误差证据，不是证明现实系统已满足这些条件。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09426","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.09426v1","title":"RSI-Forge: From Research Papers to Environments for Recursive Self-Improvement","authors":"Renxiong Wang; Darvin Yi; Abril Herrlein; Anas Mahmoud; Advait Gosai; Lisiman Hua; MohammadHossein Rezaei; Xingang Guo; Anisha Gunjal; Utkarsh Tyagi; David J. Lee; Minglai Yang; Haris Riaz; Chenguang Wang; Huaxiu Yao; Daniel Yue Zhang; Aakash Sabharwal; Tong Zhao; Yunzhong He","affiliations":"Scale AI；University of California, Santa Cruz；University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","abstract":"Environments are the foundation of recursive self-improvement: they provide the problems agents work on and the feedback used to evaluate progress. Yet constructing challenging research environments with reliable evaluation still depends on domain experts, limiting their scale and disciplinary coverage. We introduce RSI-Forge, a multi-agent pipeline that turns published papers into executable environments for self-improvement. Three agents coordinate construction, reproduction, and review to produce tasks with automated evaluators; each paper's method is independently reimplemented to establish a baseline score. We present 210 environments across 18 fields, including 90 reviewed by independent human domain experts. Both experts and agent judges give high ratings to the potential for improving the provided starting solutions and the evaluators' ability to distinguish solution quality, whereas experts are more critical of shortcut resistance, faithfulness to the source paper, and whether a single idea can exhaust a task. To validate their use for repeated improvement, we evaluate four models over 3 successive attempts on 120 environments, with each attempt inheriting prior code and notes while model weights remain fixed. At least one model improves after the first attempt in 84% of environments. Models also outperform the reproduced paper methods in 68 of the 120 environments, demonstrating room for gains beyond these baselines. Transcript analysis identifies work beyond parameter tuning in 95% of these successful attempts. Analysis of the resulting trajectories shows that models scoring lower on these tasks explore less, more often accept gains smaller than the reported standard error, and rely more heavily on tuning to the development set. RSI-Forge provides a scalable approach to constructing research environments for training and evaluating self-improving agents.","tldr":"背景与问题：研究型 RSI 需要有挑战的任务、可靠评估和可比较基线，但逐领域依赖专家设计限制了规模；自动生成又可能带来捷径、失真或不可解任务。\n\n方法：RSI-Forge 将任务构建、论文方法复现和环境审查分配给不同角色，分别产出可执行任务与评估器、独立基线，并检查说明和评分是否对应。随后固定模型权重，让 agent 继承先前代码和笔记，检验环境是否支持连续修改。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告构建 210 个、覆盖 18 个领域的环境，其中 90 个经领域专家审阅；在 120 个环境的三次尝试中，至少一个模型在首轮后有所改善的环境占 84%，68 个环境超过复现方法基线。专家对捷径抵抗、来源忠实度及单一想法能否耗尽任务更为审慎。\n\nInsights：环境生成的价值不只是扩充题量，还在于提供可复现基线和分工审查；但专家指出的质量缺口与已观察到的评估材料访问风险，说明环境数量及分数不能单独证明测量可靠。固定权重结果也不代表改进器本身变强。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"RSI 研究环境; 环境生成与评估; Harness 智能体迭代","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者声称 RSI-Forge 将论文转为可执行研究环境，由构建、独立复现和审查环节生成任务、评估器与复现基线。本文证据包括 210 个环境、90 个环境的人类领域专家评审，以及固定权重模型继承代码和笔记的三次尝试；因此测试的是环境支持的工件迭代，而非权重或改进器递归进化。与 corpus 中 RSIGym（arxiv:2610.10310）相比，本篇聚焦从论文构建环境和复现基线；没有匹配性能比较。未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09239","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.09239v1","title":"The Winner's Curse in LLM Self-Improvement Loops: Selection Noise, Lock-in, and Acceptance Rules","authors":"Litao Hu; Yutong Tang","affiliations":"Meta；Microsoft","abstract":"Self-improving LLM systems propose changes to themselves and keep those that score better on a small evaluation set. We treat this keep-if-better step as selection under measurement noise, model the correlated errors of the candidates in a single decision, and study empirically what happens when the evaluation set is reused. In runs where Qwen models rewrite their own instructions and every candidate is also scored on 600 held-out items, most proposals after the first are harmful, and the model gives the size of the winner's curse of a generation's best candidate. With a prior from a separate pilot, it matches the average overstatement of first-generation commits in native loops, though not setting by setting. In a pre-registered study, the final selection-set score of greedy loops exceeded held-out accuracy by 13 to 20 points with 16 selection items and by 1 to 5 points with 256. Held-out gains grew with the selection set on TREC but not on GSM8K, and the tested acceptance rules did not beat greedy acceptance over whole runs. Gains measured on the selection set also exceeded held-out gains when a current model refined a competent instruction, and in the validation scores of GEPA and MIPROv2. Scoring the starting and the current instruction on 64 items never used for selection removes the average bias of a loop's reported gain, but single estimates remain off by about 6 points. Self-improvement studies should report held-out gains with their uncertainty.","tldr":"背景与问题：自改进系统常在小评测集上提出多个修改，再保留分数最高者；被选分数会受选择噪声抬高，重复使用同一集合还会改变后续比较的基线。\n\n方法：论文把保留候选视为相关误差下的噪声选择，并用独立留出集估计真实收益。作者比较多种接受门槛与确认程序，再以预注册实验检验这些规则是否改善完整运行，而非只看单次决策。\n\n结果与结论：预注册研究中，16 项选择集上的贪心循环最终选择分数比留出准确率高 13–20 个百分点；256 项时差距缩至 1–5 点。测试的接受规则在完整运行中没有稳定胜过贪心策略；另用未参与选择的 64 项评分可校正平均偏差，但单次估计仍约有 6 点误差。证据覆盖特定指令改写任务及 GEPA、MIPROv2 验证分数检查。\n\nInsights：结果把研究重点从设计更复杂的接受规则，转向独立报告留出收益和不确定性；依据是接受规则未稳定改善整轮结果，而扩大选择集可缩小高估。它不说明自改进普遍无效，只说明复用评测集上的分数不足以独立证明收益。","published_at":"2026-10-07","topics":"自改进评估可靠性; 选择噪声; 留出评估","added_on":"2026-10-14","novelty_summary":"作者将 keep-if-better 建模为相关候选在有限评测集上的噪声选择，并用 oracle-instrumented 运行、原生循环和预注册研究检验收益高估与接受规则。本文证据显示小型选择集会扩大选择分数与留出表现的差距；未参与选择的 64 项评分能消除平均报告偏差，但单次估计仍有误差。相对 PACE 与 SIREN（仅为本文引用的既有工作，corpus 无对应独立条目），本篇关注循环内部的候选相关误差和整轮接受表现；无 corpus 匹配比较，未证实领域级新颖性。"},{"paper_id":"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=kSuRY5sCuR","url":"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=kSuRY5sCuR","title":"Beyond Majority Voting: Self-Reflective Test-Time Reinforcement Learning for LLM Reasoning","authors":"Sitong Wu; Haoru Tan; Xichen Zhang; Bin Xia; Shaofeng Zhang; Xiaojuan Qi; Bei Yu; Jiaya Jia","affiliations":"原笔记：HKU","abstract":"The core challenge of Test-Time Reinforcement Learning (TTRL) lies in estimating rewards without access to ground-truth supervision. Existing TTRL methods predominantly rely on majority voting to generate pseudo-labels, under the assumption that the most frequent answer among sampled trajectories is correct. However, we observe that this assumption frequently breaks down in complex reasoning tasks, where correct solutions often constitute a logical minority. As a result, rare yet correct trajectories are systematically undervalued by majority-voting-based approaches. To address this limitation, we propose Self-Reflective Test-Time Reinforcement Learning (SR-TTRL), a novel framework that leverages self-reflective verification to produce high-fidelity pseudo-labels. Specifically, given multiple sampled trajectories for a problem, SR-TTRL first groups trajectories according to their final answers and selects one representative from each group to form a candidate pool. Each candidate trajectory is then summarized to preserve its core reasoning steps while reducing verbosity. Finally, the model performs self-reflection over the candidate pool, critically evaluating and selecting the most plausible trajectory as the pseudo-label. Empirically, SR-TTRL achieves substantially higher pseudo-label fidelity and sample efficiency than prior majority-voting-based TTRL methods. Extensive experiments across diverse benchmarks and model families demonstrate that SR-TTRL consistently outperforms majority-voting baselines and significantly improves generalization to novel problems. For example, SR-TTRL improves the Pass@1 accuracy of Qwen3-8B on AIME24 from 29.1 to 55.8 (a gain of +26.7), exceeding standard TTRL by an additional +9.1. The code will be released at: https://github.com/JIA-Lab-research/SR-TTRL.","tldr":"SR-TTRL 将候选推理轨迹按答案分组、提炼关键步骤，再通过自反思选择伪标签，降低多数投票忽略少数正确答案的问题。","published_at":"2026-09-29","topics":"挖掘信号：Test-time Training","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2607.22688","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.22688v1","title":"Co-Harness: Co-Evolving Harnesses and Model Weights for LLM Agents","authors":"Zhengyu Chen; Teng Xiao; Huaisheng Zhu; Yige Yuan; Luan Zhang; Jingang Wang","affiliations":"原笔记：美团","abstract":"Post-training agents for automated AI research requires optimizing not only model parameters, but also the runtime harness that shapes how research trajectories are generated, evaluated, and learned from. Existing pipelines typically train models under a fixed harness, including prompts, tools, skills, middleware, and memory, while leaving the data-generating process outside the optimization objective. This creates a mismatch between model updates and the static scaffolding that determines trajectory quality. We introduce Co-Harness, a framework that jointly optimizes the agent harness and model parameters during post-training. Co-Harness alternates between harness optimization and model optimization. An LLM-based HarnessCritic analyzes failed trajectories, identifies harness-level failure modes, and proposes validated local updates. The model is then fine-tuned on high-quality trajectories generated by the improved harness, distilling effective scaffolding into model parameters. A 200+ hour autonomous case study further shows that Co-Harness can recover from system crashes, improve inference efficiency, and discover ensemble strategies without human intervention. These results suggest that joint harness and model optimization is an effective way to improve agents beyond fixed-harness post-training.","tldr":"Co-Harness 通过交替执行“基于失败轨迹的 HarnessCritic 局部修补”和“利用改进 Harness 生成的高质量轨迹进行 SFT”，让 Agent 的harness与weight共同进化，形成“更好 Harness → 更好训练数据 → 更强模型”的闭环。","published_at":"2026-07-17","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2607.03935","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.03935v1","title":"Harness-Aware Self-Evolving: Co-Evolving Model Weights, Harness, and Task Solutions","authors":"Haochen Luo; Yi Huang; Sichun Luo; Fengyuan Liu; Lei Li; Zefa Hu; Junlan Feng; Qi Liu","affiliations":"原笔记：HKU & China Mobile Jiutian","abstract":"Self-evolving frameworks usually optimize task solutions while treating the surrounding harness as fixed. We introduce Harness-Aware Self-Evolving (HASE), an agentic reinforcement-learning framework in which a single model can generate task solutions or edit selected harness components in a multi-turn action space. HASE enables a single Qwen3-8B model to match the text-classification performance of a GPT-OSS-120B model that uses Claude Code as the harness proposer. In alpha factor mining, HASE outperforms the reported GPT-OSS-120B baseline. HASE also repairs imperfect evaluation components and converges to state-of-the-art performance in circle-packing algorithm discovery. These results show that HASE improves the harness and the solution through one unified agentic process.","tldr":"HASE 将任务解、模型权重与可编辑 Harness 放进同一个 agentic RL action space，使单个小模型能够一边解题，一边持续改进自己的 guidance / evaluation harness。","published_at":"2026-07-04","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.09498","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09498v3","title":"Self-Harness: Harnesses That Improve Themselves","authors":"Hangfan Zhang; Shao Zhang; Kangcong Li; Chen Zhang; Yang Chen; Yiqun Zhang; Lei Bai; Shuyue Hu","affiliations":"原笔记：Shanghai AI lab","abstract":"The performance of LLM-based agents is jointly shaped by their base models and the harnesses that mediate their interaction with the environment. Because different models exhibit distinct behaviors, effective harness design is inherently model-specific. Yet agent harnesses are still largely engineered by human experts, a paradigm that scales poorly as modern LLMs become increasingly diverse and rapidly evolving. In this paper, we introduce Self-Harness, a new paradigm in which an LLM-based agent improves its own operating harness, without relying on human engineers or stronger external agents. We operationalize Self-Harness as an iterative loop with three stages: Weakness Mining, which identifies model-specific failure patterns from execution traces; Harness Proposal, which generates diverse yet minimal harness modifications tied to these failures; and Proposal Validation, which accepts candidate edits only after regression testing. We instantiate Self-Harness across Terminal-Bench-2.0, SWE-bench Verified, and AppWorld using a minimal initial harness and three base models from diverse families: MiniMax M2.5, Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, and GLM-5. Across all nine model--benchmark combinations, every final harness improves both held-in and held-out pass rates, with overall relative gains of up to 132%. Qualitative analyses further show that the retained mechanisms address benchmark-specific bottlenecks in artifact handling and runtime control, software-patch verification, and application-state retrieval. These results suggest a path toward LLM-based agents that are not merely shaped by their harnesses, but can also participate in reshaping them.","tldr":"Self-Harness 使 LLM Agent 能够基于自身执行反馈自主改进自身 Harness，并通过回归验证迭代优化，无需人工或更强外部模型介入。","published_at":"2026-06-08","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.05922","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.05922v3","title":"Evolving Agents in the Dark: Retrospective Harness Optimization via Self-Preference","authors":"Wenbo Pan; Shujie Liu; Chin-Yew Lin; Jingying Zeng; Xianfeng Tang; Xiangyang Zhou; Yan Lu; Xiaohua Jia","affiliations":"原笔记：cityu","abstract":"AI agents rely on a harness of skills, tools, and workflows to solve complex problems. Continually improving this harness is essential for adapting to new tasks. However, existing optimization methods typically require ground-truth validation sets, yet such labeled data is difficult to acquire in practical deployment settings. To address this problem, we introduce Retrospective Harness Optimization (RHO), a self-supervised method that optimizes the agent harness using only past trajectories. Specifically, RHO selects a diverse coreset of challenging tasks from past trajectories and re-solves them in parallel. The agent analyzes these rollouts using self-validation and self-consistency, then generates candidate harness updates and selects the most effective one by its own pairwise self-preference. We evaluate RHO across three diverse domains, spanning software engineering, technical work, and knowledge work. Notably, a single optimization round improves the pass rate on SWE-Bench Pro from 59% to 78% without any external grading. Furthermore, our analysis demonstrates that RHO effectively targets prior failure modes. As a result, the optimized harness alters the agent's behavior patterns and sustains higher accuracy during long-horizon sessions.","tldr":"RHO利用历史轨迹中的自监督信号替代validation feedback，实现无需verifier的Agent harness持续优化。","published_at":"2026-06-04","topics":"挖掘信号：Test-time Training","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.03108","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.03108v2","title":"EvoTrainer: Co-Evolving LLM Policies and Training Harnesses for Autonomous Agentic Reinforcement Learning","authors":"Guhong Chen; Yingcheng Shi; Yongbin Li; Binhua Li; Xander Xu; Hu Wei; Shiwen Ni; Min Yang; Jieping Ye","affiliations":"原笔记：中科院 & 阿里","abstract":"Autonomous LLM training is often framed as recipe search, which leaves the training harness largely static. This limitation sharpens in agentic RL, where shifting bottlenecks and scalar rewards mask diverse failure modes. We introduce EvoTrainer, an autonomous training framework that co-evolves LLM policies and training-side harnesses through empirical feedback: it diagnoses rollout-level evidence, revises diagnostics, backtests interventions, and accumulates reusable skills. Evaluated on mathematical reasoning, competitive-programming code generation, and repository-level software engineering, EvoTrainer matches or exceeds the human-engineered RL references under the same data, codebase, and evaluation protocol, with the largest gain on long-horizon agentic SWE. Trajectory analyses show that retained strategies diverge across domains, evolving diagnostics prevent invalid high-scoring branches from being promoted, and reusable skills shape later search. Autonomous LLM RL should move beyond recipe search toward joint evolution of policies and the training harnesses that interpret them.","tldr":"AutoML的工作，提出了一种让LLM RL中的模型策略与训练诊断流程共同进化的新框架，通过版本化实验、动态诊断升级和技能复用，在数学、编程和软件工程任务上超越了人工设计的RL基线。","published_at":"2026-06-02","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.27276","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27276v2","title":"SIA: Self Improving AI with Harness & Weight Updates","authors":"Prannay Hebbar; Yogendra Manawat; Samuel Verboomen; Alesia Ivanova; Selvam Palanimalai; Kunal Bhatia; Vignesh Baskaran","affiliations":"原笔记：Hexo labs","abstract":"Humans are the bottleneck in building and improving AI. Both the models and the agents that wrap them are written, tuned, and corrected by people. The long-horizon goal of an AI that can figure out how to improve itself remains open. Two largely disjoint research lines attack this bottleneck. The harness-update school has a meta-agent rewrite the scaffold of a task-specific agent (its tools, prompts, retry logic, and search procedure) while the model weights are held fixed. The test-time training school uses hand-written RL pipelines to update the model's own weights on task feedback while the harness is held fixed. These two silos operate in isolation. We propose SIA, a self-improving loop in which a language-model agent (the Feedback-Agent) updates both the harness and the weights of a task-specific agent. We evaluate across three contrasting domains: Chinese legal charge classification, low-level GPU kernel optimisation, and single-cell RNA denoising. Combining both levers outperforms scaffold iteration alone on all three benchmarks. SIA-W+H achieves 25.1% over prior SOTA on LawBench, 12.4% faster GPU kernels than prior SOTA (1,017 vs 1,161 μs), and 20.4% over prior SOTA on denoising. Harness updates make the model agentic, shaping how it searches and acts, while weight updates build the domain intuition that no prompt or scaffold can instil.","tldr":"This paper proposes SIA, a framework that allows an AI agent to improve both its external reasoning system (the harness/scaffold) and its internal model parameters (weights) in a single feedback loop, rather than improving only one of them.","published_at":"2026-05-26","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.11328","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.11328v1","title":"Epistemic Uncertainty for Test-Time Discovery","authors":"Kainat Riaz; Muhammad Ahmed Mohsin; Ahsan Bilal; Muhammad Umer; Ayesha Mohsin; Aqib Riaz; Ali Subhan; John M. Cioffi","affiliations":"原笔记：stanford","abstract":"Automated scientific discovery using large language models relies on identifying genuinely novel solutions. Standard reinforcement learning penalizes high-variance mutations, which leads the policy to prioritize familiar patterns. As a result, the maximum reward plateaus even as the average reward increases. Overcoming this limitation requires a signal that distinguishes unexplored regions from intrinsically difficult problems. This necessitates measuring disagreement across independently adapted weight hypotheses rather than relying on a single network's confidence. UG-TTT addresses this challenge by maintaining a small ensemble of low-rank adapters over a frozen base model. The per-token disagreement, quantified as the mutual information between ensemble predictions and weight hypotheses, isolates epistemic uncertainty and identifies positions where insufficient coverage leads to adapter divergence rather than intrinsic problem difficulty. This measure is incorporated as an exploration bonus into the policy gradient, directing the policy toward positions where persistent adapter disagreement signals low training coverage, the same frontier where genuine discovery is possible. A nuclear norm regularizer ensures the adapters remain distinct from one another, thereby preserving the exploration signal throughout training. Across four scientific discovery benchmarks, UG-TTT increases the maximum reward on three tasks, maintains substantially higher solution diversity, and an ablation study confirms that the regularizer is essential for sustaining this behavior.","tldr":"训练时维护多个模型副本，在ttt-discover的advantage基础上引入“分歧奖励”：对于一个轨迹，如果不同模型（1）各自都很确定，i.e. entropy低 且（2）（原笔记未写完，待补充。）","published_at":"2026-05-11","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.09998","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.09998v1","title":"Continual Harness: Online Adaptation for Self-Improving Foundation Agents","authors":"Seth Karten; Joel Zhang; Tersoo Upaa; Ruirong Feng; Wenzhe Li; Chengshuai Shi; Chi Jin; Kiran Vodrahalli","affiliations":"原笔记：princeton","abstract":"Coding harnesses such as Claude Code and OpenHands wrap foundation models with tools, memory, and planning, but no equivalent exists for embodied agents' long-horizon partial-observability decision-making. We first report our Gemini Plays Pokemon (GPP) experiments. With iterative human-in-the-loop harness refinement, GPP became the first AI system to complete Pokemon Blue, Yellow Legacy on hard mode, and Crystal without a lost battle. In the hardest stages, the agent itself began iterating on its strategy through long-context memory, surfacing emergent self-improvement signals alongside human-in-the-loop refinement. Continual Harness removes the human fully from this loop: a reset-free self-improving harness for embodied agents that formalizes and automates what we observed. Starting from only a minimal environment interface, the agent alternates between acting and refining its own prompt, sub-agents, skills, and memory, drawing on any past trajectory data. Prompt-optimization methods require episode resets; Continual Harness adapts online within a single run. On Pokemon Red and Emerald across frontier models, Continual Harness starting from scratch substantially reduces button-press cost relative to the minimalist baseline and recovers a majority of the gap to a hand-engineered expert harness, with capability-dependent gains, despite starting from the same raw interface with no curated knowledge, no hand-crafted tools, and no domain scaffolding. We then close the loop with the model itself: an online process-reward co-learning loop, in which an open-source agent's rollouts through the refining harness are relabeled by a frontier teacher and used to update the model, drives sustained in-game milestone progress on Pokemon Red without resetting the environment between training iterations.","tldr":"Agent 在任务执行过程中持续演化自身 Harness，而非等任务结束后再优化，使 Agent 能在长期任务中持续积累经验并提升能力。","published_at":"2026-05-11","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.07039","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.07039v1","title":"PACEvolve++: Improving Test-time Learning for Evolutionary Search Agents","authors":"Minghao Yan; Bo Peng; Benjamin Coleman; Ziqi Chen; Zhouhang Xie; Shuo Chen; Zhankui He; Noveen Sachdeva; Weili Wang; Ed H. Chi; Shivaram Venkataraman; Wang-Cheng Kang; Derek Zhiyuan Cheng; Beidou Wang","affiliations":"原笔记：google","abstract":"Large language models have become drivers of evolutionary search, but most systems rely on a fixed, prompt-elicited policy to sample next candidates. This limits adaptation in practical engineering and research tasks, where evaluations are expensive, and progress depends on learning task-specific search dynamics. We introduce PACEvolve++, an advisor-model reinforcement learning framework for test-time policy adaptation in evolutionary search agents. PACEvolve++ decouples strategic search decisions from implementation: a trainable advisor generates, assesses, and selects hypotheses, while a stronger frontier model translates selected hypotheses into executable candidates. To train the advisor under non-stationary feedback, we propose a phase-adaptive approach that adapts its optimization strategy to different phases of the evolutionary process. Early in evolution, it uses group-relative feedback to learn broad search preferences; later, as reward gaps compress, it emphasizes best-of-$k$ frontier contribution to support stable refinement. Across expert-parallel load balancing, sequential recommendation, and protein fitness extrapolation, PACEvolve++ outperforms the state-of-the-art evolutionary search framework with frontier models, achieving faster convergence and stabilizing test-time training during evolutionary search.","tldr":"Test-time RL，提出两点改进：（1）框架上，解耦idea提出和代码实现，将“提出和选择假设”交给可训练的Advisor模型，将代码实现交给更强的frontier model；（2）采用阶段自适应RL信号：早期使用GRPO式组内相对反馈鼓励探索，后期转向Max@k式前沿贡献信号进行精炼，从而兼顾搜索多样性、收敛速度与训练稳定性。","published_at":"2026-05-07","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.25850","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.25850v4","title":"Agentic Harness Engineering: Observability-Driven Automatic Evolution of Coding-Agent Harnesses","authors":"Jiahang Lin; Shichun Liu; Chengjun Pan; Lizhi Lin; Shihan Dou; Zhiheng Xi; Xuanjing Huang; Hang Yan; Zhenhua Han; Tao Gui; Yu-Gang Jiang","affiliations":"原笔记：复旦&北大","abstract":"Harnesses are now central to coding-agent performance, mediating how models interact with tools and execution environments. Yet harness engineering remains a manual craft, because automating it faces a heterogeneous action space across editable components, voluminous trajectories that bury actionable signal, and edits whose effect is hard to attribute. We introduce Agentic Harness Engineering (AHE), a closed loop that addresses these challenges through three matched observability pillars: (1) component observability gives every editable harness component a file-level representation so the action space is explicit and revertible; (2) experience observability distills millions of raw trajectory tokens into a layered, drill-down evidence corpus that an evolving agent can actually consume; and (3) decision observability pairs every edit with a self-declared prediction, later verified against the next round's task-level outcomes. Together, these pillars turn every edit into a falsifiable contract, so harness evolution proceeds autonomously without collapsing into trial-and-error. Empirically, ten AHE iterations lift pass@1 on Terminal-Bench 2 from 69.7% to 77.0%, surpassing the human-designed harness Codex-CLI (71.9%) and the self-evolving baselines ACE and TF-GRPO. The frozen harness transfers without re-evolution: on SWE-bench-verified it tops aggregate success at 12% fewer tokens than the seed, and on Terminal-Bench 2 it yields +5.1 to +10.1pp cross-family gains across three alternate model families, indicating the evolved components encode general engineering experience rather than benchmark-specific tuning. Ablations localize the gain to tools, middleware, and long-term memory rather than the system prompt, suggesting factual harness structure transfers while prose-level strategy does not.","tldr":"AHE shifts Harness evolution from end-to-end coupled program optimization (e.g. Meta-Harness) toward component-aware, evidence-driven engineering with explicit observability and rollback.","published_at":"2026-04-28","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.28052","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.28052v1","title":"Meta-Harness: End-to-End Optimization of Model Harnesses","authors":"Yoonho Lee; Roshen Nair; Qizheng Zhang; Kangwook Lee; Omar Khattab; Chelsea Finn","affiliations":"原笔记：stanford","abstract":"The performance of large language model (LLM) systems depends not only on model weights, but also on their harness: the code that determines what information to store, retrieve, and present to the model. Yet harnesses are still designed largely by hand, and existing text optimizers are poorly matched to this setting because they compress feedback too aggressively. We introduce Meta-Harness, an outer-loop system that searches over harness code for LLM applications. It uses an agentic proposer that accesses the source code, scores, and execution traces of all prior candidates through a filesystem. On online text classification, Meta-Harness improves over a state-of-the-art context management system by 7.7 points while using 4x fewer context tokens. On retrieval-augmented math reasoning, a single discovered harness improves accuracy on 200 IMO-level problems by 4.7 points on average across five held-out models. On agentic coding, discovered harnesses surpass the best hand-engineered baselines on TerminalBench-2. Together, these results show that richer access to prior experience can enable automated harness engineering.","tldr":"将 LLM 系统的 harness 作为优化对象，通过在目标任务上反复执行、保留完整 execution traces 并让 coding agent 直接分析历史代码与日志（依赖强agent分析），实现端到端自动 harness engineering。","published_at":"2026-03-30","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.19461","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.19461v1","title":"Hyperagents","authors":"Jenny Zhang; Bingchen Zhao; Wannan Yang; Jakob Foerster; Jeff Clune; Minqi Jiang; Sam Devlin; Tatiana Shavrina","affiliations":"原笔记：University of British Columbia & Meta","abstract":"Self-improving AI systems aim to reduce reliance on human engineering by learning to improve their own learning and problem-solving processes. Existing approaches to self-improvement rely on fixed, handcrafted meta-level mechanisms, fundamentally limiting how fast such systems can improve. The Darwin Gödel Machine (DGM) demonstrates open-ended self-improvement in coding by repeatedly generating and evaluating self-modified variants. Because both evaluation and self-modification are coding tasks, gains in coding ability can translate into gains in self-improvement ability. However, this alignment does not generally hold beyond coding domains. We introduce \\textbf{hyperagents}, self-referential agents that integrate a task agent (which solves the target task) and a meta agent (which modifies itself and the task agent) into a single editable program. Crucially, the meta-level modification procedure is itself editable, enabling metacognitive self-modification, improving not only the task-solving behavior, but also the mechanism that generates future improvements. We instantiate this framework by extending DGM to create DGM-Hyperagents (DGM-H), eliminating the assumption of domain-specific alignment between task performance and self-modification skill to potentially support self-accelerating progress on any computable task. Across diverse domains, the DGM-H improves performance over time and outperforms baselines without self-improvement or open-ended exploration, as well as prior self-improving systems. Furthermore, the DGM-H improves the process by which it generates new agents (e.g., persistent memory, performance tracking), and these meta-level improvements transfer across domains and accumulate across runs. DGM-Hyperagents offer a glimpse of open-ended AI systems that do not merely search for better solutions, but continually improve their search for how to improve.","tldr":"把\"执行任务的Agent（Task Agent）\"和\"负责修改Agent的Meta Agent\"统一成一个可以修改自己的程序（HyperAgent），再结合Darwin Gödel Machine（DGM）的开放式进化框架，实现任务能力和自我改进能力的共同进化。","published_at":"2026-03-19","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.23413","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23413v2","title":"EvoX: Meta-Evolution for Automated Discovery","authors":"Shu Liu; Shubham Agarwal; Monishwaran Maheswaran; Mert Cemri; Zhifei Li; Qiuyang Mang; Ashwin Naren; Ethan Boneh; Audrey Cheng; Melissa Z. Pan; Alexander Du; Kurt Keutzer; Alvin Cheung; Alexandros G. Dimakis; Koushik Sen; Matei Zaharia; Ion Stoica","affiliations":"原笔记：UCB","abstract":"Recent work such as AlphaEvolve has shown that combining LLM-driven optimization with evolutionary search can effectively improve programs, prompts, and algorithms across domains. In this paradigm, previously evaluated solutions are reused to guide the model toward new candidate solutions. Crucially, the effectiveness of this evolution process depends on the search strategy: how prior solutions are selected and varied to generate new candidates. However, most existing methods rely on fixed search strategies with predefined knobs (e.g., explore-exploit ratios) that remain static throughout execution. While effective in some settings, these approaches often fail to adapt across tasks, or even within the same task as the search space changes over time. We introduce EvoX, an adaptive evolution method that optimizes its own evolution process. EvoX jointly evolves candidate solutions and the search strategies used to generate them, continuously updating how prior solutions are selected and varied based on progress. This enables the system to dynamically shift between different search strategies during the optimization process. Across nearly 200 real-world optimization tasks, EvoX outperforms existing AI-driven evolutionary methods including AlphaEvolve, OpenEvolve, GEPA, and ShinkaEvolve on the majority of tasks.","tldr":"EvoX 提出了一种元演化框架，将搜索策略作为可优化对象，与候选解共同演化，从而实现搜索过程的动态自适应。","published_at":"2026-02-26","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.20133","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.20133v1","title":"AdaEvolve: Adaptive LLM Driven Zeroth-Order Optimization","authors":"Mert Cemri; Shubham Agrawal; Akshat Gupta; Shu Liu; Audrey Cheng; Qiuyang Mang; Ashwin Naren; Lutfi Eren Erdogan; Koushik Sen; Matei Zaharia; Alex Dimakis; Ion Stoica","affiliations":"原笔记：berkely (EvoX同一拨人)","abstract":"The paradigm of automated program generation is shifting from one-shot generation to inference-time search, where Large Language Models (LLMs) function as semantic mutation operators within evolutionary loops. While effective, these systems are currently governed by static schedules that fail to account for the non-stationary dynamics of the search process. This rigidity results in substantial computational waste, as resources are indiscriminately allocated to stagnating populations while promising frontiers remain under-exploited. We introduce AdaEvolve, a framework that reformulates LLM-driven evolution as a hierarchical adaptive optimization problem. AdaEvolve uses an \"accumulated improvement signal\" to unify decisions across three levels: Local Adaptation, which dynamically modulates the exploration intensity within a population of solution candidates; Global Adaptation, which routes the global resource budget via bandit-based scheduling across different solution candidate populations; and Meta-Guidance which generates novel solution tactics based on the previously generated solutions and their corresponding improvements when the progress stalls. We demonstrate that AdaEvolve consistently outperforms the open-sourced baselines across 185 different open-ended optimization problems including combinatorial, systems optimization and algorithm design problems.","tldr":"把 LLM 生成和改进程序的过程视为一种自适应优化：根据近期效果，动态决定是继续精修现有方案、尝试新方向，还是重新调整整体解题思路。其核心是让搜索策略随进展自动变化，而非依赖预先设定的固定流程，本质是harness evolving（演化算法本身是harness，controller相当于一个harness engineer）","published_at":"2026-02-23","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.02919","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.02919v1","title":"DeltaEvolve: Accelerating Scientific Discovery through Momentum-Driven Evolution","authors":"Jiachen Jiang; Tianyu Ding; Zhihui Zhu","affiliations":"原笔记：Ohio State University","abstract":"LLM-driven evolutionary systems have shown promise for automated science discovery, yet existing approaches such as AlphaEvolve rely on full-code histories that are context-inefficient and potentially provide weak evolutionary guidance. In this work, we first formalize the evolutionary agents as a general Expectation-Maximization framework, where the language model samples candidate programs (E-step) and the system updates the control context based on evaluation feedback (M-step). Under this view, constructing context via full-code snapshots constitutes a suboptimal M-step, as redundant implement details dilutes core algorithmic ideas, making it difficult to provide clear inspirations for evolution. To address this, we propose DeltaEvolve, a momentum-driven evolutionary framework that replaces full-code history with structured semantic delta capturing how and why modifications between successive nodes affect performance. As programs are often decomposable, semantic delta usually contains many effective components which are transferable and more informative to drive improvement. By organizing semantic delta through multi-level database and progressive disclosure mechanism, input tokens are further reduced. Empirical evaluations on tasks across diverse scientific domains show that our framework can discover better solution with less token consumption over full-code-based evolutionary agents.","tldr":"Evolutionary agents should remember improvements, not programs.","published_at":"2026-02-02","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2601.16175","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.16175v2","title":"Learning to Discover at Test Time","authors":"Mert Yuksekgonul; Daniel Koceja; Xinhao Li; Federico Bianchi; Jed McCaleb; Xiaolong Wang; Jan Kautz; Yejin Choi; James Zou; Carlos Guestrin; Yu Sun","affiliations":"原笔记：Stanford, NVIDIA,（TextGrad [Nature 2025] 一作）","abstract":"How can we use AI to discover a new state of the art for a scientific problem? Prior work in test-time scaling, such as AlphaEvolve, performs search by prompting a frozen LLM. We perform reinforcement learning at test time, so the LLM can continue to train, but now with experience specific to the test problem. This form of continual learning is quite special, because its goal is to produce one great solution rather than many good ones on average, and to solve this very problem rather than generalize to other problems. Therefore, our learning objective and search subroutine are designed to prioritize the most promising solutions. We call this method Test-Time Training to Discover (TTT-Discover). Following prior work, we focus on problems with continuous rewards. We report results for every problem we attempted, across mathematics, GPU kernel engineering, algorithm design, and biology. TTT-Discover sets the new state of the art in almost all of them: (i) Erdős' minimum overlap problem and an autocorrelation inequality; (ii) a GPUMode kernel competition (up to $2\\times$ faster than prior art); (iii) past AtCoder algorithm competitions; and (iv) denoising problem in single-cell analysis. Our solutions are reviewed by experts or the organizers. All our results are achieved with an open model, OpenAI gpt-oss-120b, and can be reproduced with our publicly available code, in contrast to previous best results that required closed frontier models. Our test-time training runs are performed using Tinker, an API by Thinking Machines, with a cost of only a few hundred dollars per problem.","tldr":"TL;DR: 提出 test-time training to discover 解决 open scientific problems；在数学 (Erdős’ minimum overlap problem and autocorrelation inequalities)、GPU Kernel Engineering (TriMul)、算法 (AtCoder) 和 生物 (denoising problem in single-cell analysis) 四个领域的问题上取得 SOTA，并且经过人类专家审核。","published_at":"2026-01-22","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2511.23473","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.23473v1","title":"ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems","authors":"Yiping Wang; Shao-Rong Su; Zhiyuan Zeng; Eva Xu; Liliang Ren; Xinyu Yang; Zeyi Huang; Xuehai He; Luyao Ma; Baolin Peng; Hao Cheng; Pengcheng He; Weizhu Chen; Shuohang Wang; Simon Shaolei Du; Yelong Shen","affiliations":"原笔记：University of Washington / Microsoft Research","abstract":"Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have enabled breakthroughs in mathematical discovery, exemplified by AlphaEvolve, a closed-source system that evolves programs to improve bounds on open problems. However, it relies on ensembles of frontier LLMs to achieve new bounds and is a pure inference system that models cannot internalize the evolving strategies. We introduce ThetaEvolve, an open-source framework that simplifies and extends AlphaEvolve to efficiently scale both in-context learning and Reinforcement Learning (RL) at test time, allowing models to continually learn from their experiences in improving open optimization problems. ThetaEvolve features a single LLM, a large program database for enhanced exploration, batch sampling for higher throughput, lazy penalties to discourage stagnant outputs, and optional reward shaping for stable training signals, etc. ThetaEvolve is the first evolving framework that enable a small open-source model, like DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B, to achieve new best-known bounds on open problems (circle packing and first auto-correlation inequality) mentioned in AlphaEvolve. Besides, across two models and four open tasks, we find that ThetaEvolve with RL at test-time consistently outperforms inference-only baselines, and the model indeed learns evolving capabilities, as the RL-trained checkpoints demonstrate faster progress and better final performance on both trained target task and other unseen tasks. We release our code publicly: https://github.com/ypwang61/ThetaEvolve","tldr":"TL;DR: ThetaEvolve 将 AlphaEvolve 式的程序进化流水线与 TTRL 结合起来，把“只在推理时搜索”扩展为“在测试时边搜索边学习”。它一方面简化 AlphaEvolve 的复杂系统设计，另一方面让小型开源模型也能在开放优化问题上持续积累改进能力。","published_at":"2025-11-28","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2506.13131","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131v1","title":"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery","authors":"Alexander Novikov; Ngân Vũ; Marvin Eisenberger; Emilien Dupont; Po-Sen Huang; Adam Zsolt Wagner; Sergey Shirobokov; Borislav Kozlovskii; Francisco J. R. Ruiz; Abbas Mehrabian; M. Pawan Kumar; Abigail See; Swarat Chaudhuri; George Holland; Alex Davies; Sebastian Nowozin; Pushmeet Kohli; Matej Balog","affiliations":"原笔记：Deepmind","abstract":"In this white paper, we present AlphaEvolve, an evolutionary coding agent that substantially enhances capabilities of state-of-the-art LLMs on highly challenging tasks such as tackling open scientific problems or optimizing critical pieces of computational infrastructure. AlphaEvolve orchestrates an autonomous pipeline of LLMs, whose task is to improve an algorithm by making direct changes to the code. Using an evolutionary approach, continuously receiving feedback from one or more evaluators, AlphaEvolve iteratively improves the algorithm, potentially leading to new scientific and practical discoveries. We demonstrate the broad applicability of this approach by applying it to a number of important computational problems. When applied to optimizing critical components of large-scale computational stacks at Google, AlphaEvolve developed a more efficient scheduling algorithm for data centers, found a functionally equivalent simplification in the circuit design of hardware accelerators, and accelerated the training of the LLM underpinning AlphaEvolve itself. Furthermore, AlphaEvolve discovered novel, provably correct algorithms that surpass state-of-the-art solutions on a spectrum of problems in mathematics and computer science, significantly expanding the scope of prior automated discovery methods (Romera-Paredes et al., 2023). Notably, AlphaEvolve developed a search algorithm that found a procedure to multiply two $4 \\times 4$ complex-valued matrices using $48$ scalar multiplications; offering the first improvement, after 56 years, over Strassen's algorithm in this setting. We believe AlphaEvolve and coding agents like it can have a significant impact in improving solutions of problems across many areas of science and computation.","tldr":"AlphaEvolve combines state-of-the-art LLMs with evolutionary search to automatically improve algorithms, leading to both engineering optimizations and new mathematical discoveries","published_at":"2025-06-16","topics":"优化上限：Test-time Discovering","added_on":"2026-10-13"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2504.16084","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16084v3","title":"TTRL: Test-Time Reinforcement Learning","authors":"Yuxin Zuo; Kaiyan Zhang; Li Sheng; Shang Qu; Ganqu Cui; Xuekai Zhu; Haozhan Li; Yuchen Zhang; Xinwei Long; Ermo Hua; Biqing Qi; Youbang Sun; Zhiyuan Ma; Lifan Yuan; Ning Ding; Bowen Zhou","affiliations":"原笔记：Tsinghua & AI lab","abstract":"This paper investigates Reinforcement Learning (RL) on data without explicit labels for reasoning tasks in Large Language Models (LLMs). The core challenge of the problem is reward estimation during inference while not having access to ground-truth information. While this setting appears elusive, we find that common practices in Test-Time Scaling (TTS), such as majority voting, yield surprisingly effective rewards suitable for driving RL training. In this work, we introduce Test-Time Reinforcement Learning (TTRL), a novel method for training LLMs using RL on unlabeled data. TTRL enables self-evolution of LLMs by utilizing the priors in the pre-trained models. Our experiments demonstrate that TTRL consistently improves performance across a variety of tasks and models. Notably, TTRL boosts the pass@1 performance of Qwen-2.5-Math-7B by approximately 211% on the AIME 2024 with only unlabeled test data. Furthermore, although TTRL is only supervised by the maj@n metric, TTRL has demonstrated performance to consistently surpass the upper limit of the initial model maj@n, and approach the performance of models trained directly on test data with ground-truth labels. Our experimental findings validate the general effectiveness of TTRL across various tasks and highlight TTRL's potential for broader tasks and domains. GitHub: https://github.com/PRIME-RL/TTRL","tldr":"TTRL shows that LLMs can perform reinforcement learning on unlabeled test data by using their own self-consistency signals as rewards, enabling inference-time self-improvement without human annotations.","published_at":"2025-04-22","topics":"挖掘信号：Test-time Training","added_on":"2026-10-13"}],"reports":[{"date":"2026-10-20","critique":"今天这批材料有实质机制推进，但不足以支持“递归加速已经实现”。LM2LM把实验预测接入提案者训练，再用真实执行纠正策略放大的高估，比单纯累积研究记录更进一步[1]；SpecRSI学习编辑与验证的后续净收益，但目标成本下降不等于总成本下降[2]。评估器共演化值得关注，不过UCoE多数收益仍来自当前回答修补，不能全算作跨任务学习[3]。失败学习审计进一步表明，经验正确仍不保证迁移[4]；预植后门也能借记忆写回放大，静态检查不足[5]。相比之下，分层记忆与技能命名更像既有路线细化。优先精读LM2LM的校准对照和失败学习审计的迁移协议。本次均依据截断全文，部分结果仅见摘要；仍有18篇待分析论文，不是当天全部候选的总结。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.23344","arxiv:2610.16491","arxiv:2610.17609","arxiv:2610.22984","arxiv:2610.15244"],"backlog":18,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18083","tldr":"背景与问题：增加研究agent不一定增加有效进展：早期低分可能掩盖好想法，广播未确认诊断会使探索同质化，单次成功也不会自动变成下一次研究的方法。\n\n方法：AReaL-RSI让leader依据实验记录协调持续研究者，共享时保留发现的条件与不确定性，限制未解决问题的主动传播。活动结束后再把证据提炼成研究方向、知识和技能，供后续团队使用；骨干与leader策略不变。\n\n结果与结论：给定资源配置下，相对Codex-Goal，两种骨干的Terminal Bench成绩均增加2.2个百分点；内核实验中，分工加共享优于独立探索和仅共享。主要实验段落缺失，无法完整核对成本与跨活动继承收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键区别是共享有适用条件的证据，而非共享全部历史。正面标签的程序检查只确认来源，不认证结论；harness发布也不要求未来任务增益，因此配置可继承不能直接算作研究程序已变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17718","tldr":"背景与问题：心电模型的弱点会随训练变化，但定向生成波形可能同时改变其他特征，使问题、答案与实际信号不符；只追着反馈错误补数据也可能过拟合。\n\n方法：ECG-RSI先按目标特征编辑训练波形，再复测目标与受保护特征，合格后才生成监督。构造错误用于修补生成规则，学习者错误用于提出不同数据配方；同父模型训练出的分支在独立选择集比较，获选分支进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：三轮后，四项问答平均准确率由34.57%升至56.04%；保留路径的监督重心转向易混类别对比，但继续纠错的外部收益递减。可见附录另列一组三种子分数，口径未充分说明，不能与主结果混算。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，错误诊断只能提出干预，不能证明该干预有教学价值。独立选择与外部评测使这一区分可检验；波形复测仍依赖特征提取与问答审查，不能等同临床有效性认证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17609","tldr":"背景与问题：开放任务没有答案或可执行测试，错误verifier不仅会把当前回答改坏，还会把误导经验写入后续harness；固定评分标准又可能随任务变化失效。\n\n方法：UCoE构造只破坏一个属性的回答对，选择最弱属性族上辨别力最高的评分程序。该程序指导局部修补、选择交付回答并控制经验写入；完成任务的诊断再提出新程序，经对比测试后替换旧版，所有模型参数固定。\n\n结果与结论：六个开放基准上，两种骨干相对匹配直接生成的平均偏好率为59.00%和57.19%。可见引言明确称多数收益来自当前任务修补，不能把总体优势全部归于跨任务共演化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，评分器应按能否辨别关键退化来选，而非只看平均准确率。但合成退化的偏好方向不等于自然修订的真实优劣；重复使用对比集也留下选择过拟合风险，理论不覆盖任意开放任务。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.17114","tldr":"背景与问题：隐式机器人世界模型预测出错时，难把偏差定位到可修正量；每次重建场景又很昂贵，过度谨慎还会阻止获得辨识模型所需的接触证据。\n\n方法：D-World让冻结LLM编写可执行数字孪生，用实机执行后的测量修订对象状态和物理参数。参数修改须在最新动作段回放中不显著恶化已测残差，下一段动作再经更新后的仿真检查；结构错误则触发重建。\n\n结果与结论：双臂机器人的毛巾与烤面包任务展示局部修订后继续执行，其中面包深度残差由22.4降至1.5毫米。材料没有提供完整成功率、重建成本和受控消融，案例不能证明普遍收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可编辑参数使误差成为行动依据，但本质仍含系统辨识。门控只约束最新可测证据，早期残差不否决更新，仿真通过也不认证实机安全；离线后训练用途尚不能算已验证闭环。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16523","tldr":"背景与问题：多轮用户互动的坏训练信号未必来自策略：模拟用户可能泄露信息，工具或验证器可能出错。只做奖励塑形，无法修复产生这些轨迹的上游过程。\n\n方法：EAU让元agent读取训练轨迹与统计，诊断问题后修改用户规则、交互条件、奖励或训练配置；通过有限完整性检查的变更可在训练中热替换。策略继续按固定RL算法学习，已发现的干预经验跨运行保存。\n\n结果与结论：摘要在三个基准、两种骨干上给出相对最强基线14.7%—15.0%的总体增益。主要结果表被截断；附录说明不少基线来自既有报告，而PPO与EAU自行评测，因此并非全部统一重跑。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，把故障归因到训练系统而非一律归因策略，是有价值的改动。但运行内修补、奖励变化与超参数调整混合发生，需要核对各自增益和总预算；环境可编辑不等于元优化机制也在变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16491","tldr":"背景与问题：每改一版就完整评估，会把预算耗在尚未产生价值的中间状态；只预测当前候选质量，又忽略它还需多少编辑和检查才能成为可采用改进。\n\n方法：SpecRSI允许从未完成评估的版本继续起草，但采用前必须取得完整真实检查。搜索根据后续编辑与验证的预期净收益分配预算；外层用整次搜索的已验证收益减全部成本，训练下一轮改进者，真实评估合同不变。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出编码验证成功率69.4%，对照HGM为64.3%，目标成本指标也下降；但可见图注另显示，相对MetaRSI-v1，目标成本更低时总成本指标略高，不能概括为全面省算力。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，改进者应学习哪些尚未成功的编辑值得继续验证，而非只模仿成功补丁。完整搜索信用回应了这一点；预测器仍可能浪费不可追回的预算，且固定外层算法不意味着改进过程无限自举。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.16078","tldr":"背景与问题：领域专家继续监督训练已达平台时，通用agent仍可能在部分实例上提供帮助；但专家变强后，旧agent策略与交互方式可能不再提供增量。\n\n方法：HACE用任务标签检验agent是否在当前实例上优于专家，探索结果决定专家重点训练哪些样本，专家仍学原始标签。候选专家与harness联合比较后，再收集相对保留专家有正贡献的新回答训练agent，改变下一轮可用贡献。\n\n结果与结论：材料称在推荐、蛋白功能和晶体稳定性预测中优于所比较自改进方法，起点为已收敛专家。主要结果表缺失；蛋白任务实际只更新预测头，不能统称所有领域基础模型权重均被改进。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，平均更弱的agent也可能凭局部互补性帮助专家，关键是验证哪些实例值得投入。这里监督来自原始标签而非纯自生知识；总体联合得分还需拆分专家、agent与harness各自的独立贡献。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15964","tldr":"背景与问题：agent重写harness后，端到端rollout昂贵，原仓库测试又漏掉大量行为变化；更大的生成测试集虽可能更强，却会增加每次准入成本。\n\n方法：TeSearch按测试集大小分区竞争，在每种规模内优化覆盖与变异检测，避免小而强的候选被大集合挤掉；实际生成数量反过来校准搜索。得到的测试集作为harness改写的可执行回归门控。\n\n结果与结论：在mini-swe-agent的470个核验改写上，行为变化拒绝率为59.9%，仓库测试为25.3%；代价是误拒部分等价改写。这里测的是构造改写的行为保持，不是多轮自改进后的任务成功率。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，回归检查是保住已有能力的护栏，不是改进价值本身。若目标本就需要改变行为，强制保持旧实现还可能阻止好更新；后续应把保持合同与允许变化的功能目标分开测试。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15772","tldr":"背景与问题：固定技能库或离线技能生成器会落后于训练中的策略；给教师增加技能也不保证它比学生可靠，统一蒸馏可能强化错误指导。\n\n方法：RSIPO让当前策略从自身轨迹写技能，在同起点回放中与随机留出的无技能轨迹比较执行收益。收益奖励技能生成，噪声校准后的收益则调节学生对技能教师的信任；更新策略再产生下一批轨迹，测试不提供技能。\n\n结果与结论：Qwen2.5-7B在ALFWorld成功率为98.6%，比次优基线高2.5个百分点。但附录显示3B模型在搜索任务只排第二，不能照摘要推广为所有配置均领先；完整成本和消融表未见。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，技能相关不等于具有教学价值，实际回放比教师自信更合适。收益来自同任务重放，还需防止答案泄漏与起点不一致；初始化也使用外部LLM技能监督，不能称全程无教师。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15708","tldr":"背景与问题：代码实体相互依赖，修好一个函数的规格可能改变整个模块生成，使其他函数退化；沿单条修订路径容易反复丢失已有成果。\n\n方法：SpecForge用从规格重建代码后的测试失败修改行为描述，而非直接积累代码补丁。搜索保留各实体上互有优势的规格状态，并优先修订被调用者，减少依赖错误造成的误导；新状态重新生成和测试整个模块。\n\n结果与结论：摘要给出五种骨干上平均比最强基线高5.7个百分点，并称规格可迁移到跨语言翻译和新功能实现。主要实验段落未提供，尚不能核对迁移效果量及完整预算。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，外部知识的质量可用其能否支持行为重建衡量，而非文档相似度。不过测试来自已有参考实现，验证的是捕捉现有行为；这不自动证明新需求正确性，也不证明搜索器自身越来越会优化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15244","tldr":"背景与问题：只在初始记忆下扫描视觉触发器，可能漏掉依赖后续经验状态才激活的后门；部署时权重不变也不保证行为安全不变。\n\n方法：EvolvAttack通过部署前投毒训练预置联合条件：触发图像与载荷相关记忆同时存在才稳定输出恶意行为。早期罕见输出被正常记忆机制写回，后续检索再提高激活机会，形成放大；攻击者部署后不直接修改记忆或权重。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称攻击成功率从演化前0.5%升至百次交互内超过95%。但可见消融中，补充空记忆训练覆盖会降低攻击效果，说明静态隐蔽性与动态强度受具体训练覆盖影响。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，安全审计对象应是带写回的交互轨迹，而非单个权重快照。这是预植后门借记忆放大的证据，不能表述为普通经验学习自然生成恶意；真实部署风险还取决于触发暴露与记忆准入。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23599","tldr":"背景与问题：一条轨迹可能同时暴露规划失误、工具误用和可自动化操作；把它们统一写进技能文档，不能决定该如何验证、维护或何时调用。\n\n方法：CDSE从成功与失败轨迹提取带证据的行为修改建议，按其作用分配维护方式：一般规则与局部经验保留适用条件，可执行程序须经过测试。协调冲突后重写调用描述，让更新后的技能影响后续执行，模型与协议保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准、三模型、两harness的测试表均领先，平均比各设置最强竞争方法高2.6个百分点。训练与测试分开，但完整消融及演化总成本未见，不能单靠总体排名确认功能拆分的独立贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，有意义的是更新的功能决定验证合同，而非认知类比本身。多轮可重复整理固定轨迹，因此轮次增长不代表新增交互学习，更不说明技能更新器本身递归变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23574","tldr":"背景与问题：把用户交互原样塞进记忆或技能，会混淆环境限制与通用操作经验，也难判断哪些补丁应保留、哪些已过时。\n\n方法：Darwin-Claw把有学习信号的轨迹整理成带触发条件的经验单元，写入相关技能；后续轨迹提供效果与无效调用变化，控制试用、晋级和淘汰。LLM判断新轨迹是否相关及改善是否来自经验，底层模型参数不变。\n\n结果与结论：自主后训练场景中，相对只传递上下文报告，技能方案的六项平均分由28.42%升至31.91%。但具体模型—任务组合仍有退化，WildClawBench的完整数值表和消融未见，稳定性主张证据不足。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，限定经验容量与撤销低效补丁比持续追加更可控；但轨迹后的LLM归因不能替代同条件有无记忆对照。还需区分研究目标模型变强与负责优化的agent技能真正获得迁移。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.23344","tldr":"背景与问题：训练研究提案者若逐个运行模型实验，反馈成本过高；改用预测收益后，策略又会集中到预测器高估的方案，使代理奖励上涨而真实收益不涨。\n\n方法：LM2LM用读取真实实验记录的冻结LLM预测收益，训练提案者；定期真实执行当前策略中预测高分的提案，把测量结果补入预测器上下文。提案者权重改变、反馈记录刷新，校准专门针对优化偏爱的区域。\n\n结果与结论：留出任务采用真实执行评价，摘要称优于带实验记录的强模型，数据生成成本低33%。可见案例中，静态记录方案不断强化有害改动，加入真实负结果后该改动比例下降；但主结果表与完整成本口径被截断。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，预测器离线准确不足以支撑在线优化，最需要复测的恰是策略追逐的高分点。证据支持定向纠偏，不证明全空间校准；这里学到改进其他模型的能力，尚非研究者自主改造自身训练算法。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22984","tldr":"背景与问题：很多经验演化方法依赖成功轨迹或验证反馈；若agent空库起步、反复失败又不知道真实评分，能否仅靠反思获得可迁移能力仍不清楚。\n\n方法：论文由控制器只让失败轨迹触发外部记忆、技能或harness更新，隐藏评分且不告知失败筛选。分别测源任务重试恢复与固定未见任务表现，再筛出人工确认正确的经验，并放宽成功轨迹、反馈或额外交互条件。\n\n结果与结论：多个框架与环境中，源任务可部分修复，未见任务却少有持续改善。仅保留正确经验后，五种配置中四种的最终留出成绩仍不高于无经验基线，表明诊断错误不是唯一瓶颈。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应把经验正确性、同题可用性和跨题可迁移性分开验收。成功轨迹带来更强迁移，但成功与失败任务流分别采样，包含难度和内容差异；结果不能推出失败经验普遍无用。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-19","critique":"今天这批材料有实质推进，但主要是改善自改进的证据组织与归因，而非证明递归加速。VideoHarness-SRSI 表明，更丰富的反馈也可能扩大验证集过拟合，搜索需要限制内容暴露并控制机制干扰[1]；SEAR 用预算匹配重启和空技能库对照，区分经验继承与多试几次[2]。STRATA 的反向经验混淆实验，比笼统宣称结构化记忆有效更有解释力[3]。相较之下，ABot-ER 的轮次并非连续继承链，最终语料单次训练即可匹敌迭代结果[4]；APT 去掉反馈循环后部分指标持平，其递归必要性证据弱于自动化主张[5]。优先精读[1][2]，核查预算、选择协议与迁移归因。本次不是当天全部候选的总结，仍有19篇待分析论文；来源多为截断全文，缺失对照不能当作已验证结论。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.19424","arxiv:2610.18792","arxiv:2610.19386","arxiv:2610.18355","arxiv:2610.18097"],"backlog":19,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19799","tldr":"背景与问题：让团队反复修改技能和角色，不保证合作会改善；弱主席可能压制强成员，增加角色也可能只增加等待。论文把团队组成与决策权限作为独立变量，而非默认有效的背景。\n\n方法：固定个体演化机制，改变成员能力配比及信息共享、修改提案和决策规则；执行轨迹与同伴备忘进入下一轮，团队修改经验证集阻止明显退化。权重不变，部分技能和记忆更新由固定强模型完成。\n\n结果与结论：网页搜索中，合适配置较独自演化的强代理最高多25分；但另一模型家族未稳定重现该优势，角色扩张还伴随超时。领导集中并非普遍有效的组织规律。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得检验的是强成员能否获得有效经验并减少协调损耗，而非多代理是否天然更强。竞争条件直接安排按分数轮换主席，不能把全部权力转移解释成演化涌现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19725","tldr":"背景与问题：冻结时序模型不会自动利用节假日等任务知识，也不会自行修正重复误差；人工设计流水线昂贵，而平均最好的方案未必适合每个预测窗口。\n\n方法：编码代理在早期历史窗口执行候选代码，用预测误差和日志指导下一次修订，再用较晚窗口筛选部署方案。部署时根据相似且结果已完整揭晓的历史窗口选择流水线；此时代码固定，仅选择依据更新。\n\n结果与结论：198项任务中，同候选数的非迭代搜索弱于直接推理，反馈修订则改善结果；TIME 的平均绝对缩放误差相对降低1.52%。更换编码代理和预测骨干仍有收益，但候选数匹配未控制全部成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键不是多生成方案，而是让实际误差否定看似合理的领域改动。历史误差能指导部署工程，却不能保证分布突变后的收益，更未证明编码代理自身越来越会优化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19591","tldr":"背景与问题：长期代理若每次等待、协调和恢复都依赖模型推理与人工审批，计算扩张会受人的注意力限制；允许代理写新工具，又可能扩大其操作权限。\n\n方法：L3M 把状态和轨迹持久化，并允许代理将重复程序封装为新工具。程序类型声明所需权限，运行时限制其不超过既有授权；可恢复或权限已限定的操作减少审批，部分检查由 Lean 内核验证。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称仅用无需人工审查的工具，可达到带不安全 shell 配置约三分之二的通过率；可见片段缺少完整实验表，不能据此判断自扩展的独立收益。定理也依赖编译、提供者和操作系统等可信部分。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献是让能力增长与权限增长脱钩，而非认证代理会正确自改进。回滚本地文件不能撤回已经发出的外部请求，安全主张必须逐项对应可恢复范围和可信假设。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19581","tldr":"背景与问题：别的代理学到的经验可能有用，却未必适配接收者的工具和执行历史；只共享语义相似条目，容易合并不兼容经验或重复注入无效指导。\n\n方法：系统分别维护本地与共享经验图，保留来源并避免有歧义的合并。新任务结合相关性、其他代理的使用结果与本地结果选择经验；任务评分随后更新使用统计，并将新轨迹提炼成下一轮经验。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称跨任务和异构框架迁移优于记忆基线，但主要结果表未包含在片段中。跨框架实验增加贡献者时，也同步增加源任务总暴露量，不能将收益全部归于代理多样性。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，迁移价值必须由接收者校准，不能直接照搬贡献者的成功率。不过给所有已注入经验记同一个任务结果，仍无法区分谁真正有用；重复任务的累计成功也不等于未见任务泛化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19424","tldr":"背景与问题：有限验证集同时决定保留哪个 harness、下一步探索什么；视频和题目细节会诱导样本特化，早期噪声还可能让提案者过早放弃有效机制。\n\n方法：固定视觉语言模型，只向提案者开放汇总分数和不含验证内容的执行统计。先做受控预实验，再让机制在独立分支积累证据，最后测试组合及相互作用，减少一次联合修改导致的归因混淆。\n\n结果与结论：四个视频基准上，相对基础演化流程，平均留出得分相对提高6.2%，验证—测试差距缩小37.9%。内容暴露对照支持过拟合诊断，但片段不足以核对完整消融和总成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，更多反馈并非总是更好：能解释已见题目的信息，也能帮助记住验证集。真正应优化的是证据对未见任务的预测力；屏蔽内容仍不能自动消除反复查询汇总分数带来的选择偏差。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19422","tldr":"背景与问题：固定攻击集不会随防御者变强而暴露新弱点；工具代理还会从请求、工具说明和环境观察受到攻击，仅训练安全措辞不足以保证安全行动。\n\n方法：攻击者学习构造完整对抗任务，防御者学习在其中完成合法要求。固定模型分别判断轨迹安全性和效用，反馈更新双方；对同任务多次执行中结果差异较大的任务加权，避免只追求让防御者全败。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称安全鲁棒性改善且保持一般能力；片段提供四类安全基准与通用能力协议，但主要结果和加权消融被省略，无法核对幅度及独立贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可学习攻击应产生可区分的行为后果，而非单纯最难。不过奖励变化也可能来自评判噪声；训练依赖模型判断，尚需独立检查安全评分、合法任务完成与过度拒绝之间的关系。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.19386","tldr":"背景与问题：把具体操作、任务流程和一般原则混在相似度记忆池里，会随规模增长稀释检索；更危险的是，表面相似但方向相反的程序可能被直接执行。\n\n方法：冻结模型，将经验组织成技能、流程和抽象原则，并按任务结果写回：成功产生可复用程序，失败只添加避坑提示。检索同时关注操作与目标，召回相反经验时明确警告，定期压缩和删除冗余流程。\n\n结果与结论：四个互动基准、两个骨干上，摘要称平均表现及效率优于记忆基线；ScienceWorld 同系统加入对比关系后，得分从78.7升至96.7。完整消融表缺失，尚不能核对各机制贡献。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，经验被执行时，错误召回的代价高于一般检索问答。方向识别因此可能比继续扩库更关键；但当前对比关系依赖固定反义操作词表，开放语义下能否覆盖混淆尚未验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18868","tldr":"背景与问题：长程任务里，同组轨迹经常全部失败，终局二元奖励无法区分接近完成和毫无进展，导致组相对强化学习缺少梯度。\n\n方法：先构造已知正确的潜在世界，再从同一世界生成受损输入、目标和阶段检查，按工作区正确程度计进度。训练奖励额外保留最终进度，使未完成轨迹也能产生差异；它不是保证原最优策略不变的传统塑形。\n\n结果与结论：训练所得27B模型在指定长程计算与数学任务上，Pass@5 相对基座提高65%；还报告终端子集迁移。可见材料未给出主要训练消融，不能将全部收益归于稠密奖励。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共同真值来源有助于避免分别生成任务和检查器造成的工件失配。但代理目标仍被改变，部分进度奖励可能影响策略取舍；这属于训练基础，而非已展示的递归自改进。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18845","tldr":"背景与问题：新遥感任务往往需要专家重选模型和训练配方，少标签设置尤其依赖工程经验；论文试图把设计工作交给能运行实验的编码代理。\n\n方法：人固定可用数据、模型与预算，用封闭验证器只返回分数；代理自行写训练代码，并将已训练模型的预测或检查点用于后继模型，按分数选择保留。最终模型另在隐藏测试集评估。\n\n结果与结论：材料称六个遥感基准均超过所列已有方法，部分任务只需少量训练标签；每次运行上限为四张GB200、12小时。实验验证器仍使用基准标签，不能据此证明所有遥感任务都有可靠验证方式。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，减少训练标注不等于消除监督需求，部分成本转移到了验证标签与任务接口。递归发生在目标模型的自训练谱系，尚无证据表明编码代理或产生改进的规则也持续变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18842","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人能自主执行，不代表能自主改进；即使技能越积越多，也可能只是固定更新流程不断运行，而非学习过程本身变得更有效。\n\n方法：论文将执行系统与改进程序分开，用L0—L5区分能力更新、元级更新及跨任务收益。最高等级要求从相同起点和经验出发，在匹配预算下由独立评估比较新旧改进程序；物理反馈可来自真实交互或物理仿真。\n\n结果与结论：这是一项框架与综述工作，不提供达到最高等级的新系统。其判断是所审阅文献尚未满足该定义的物理 RSI 证据要求，不能扩展成对全部机器人研究的否定。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，递归主张最关键的对照是“更新后的改进程序能否产生更好的后续改进”，而非机器人最终更强。独立评测还须防止标准随轮次改变，否则所谓递归增益可能只是目标漂移。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18813","tldr":"背景与问题：提示、记忆、工具实现和运行时控制都可能被称为 harness 演化，但修改边界及风险不同；仅有修订过程，也不代表产生了可保留的性能收益。\n\n方法：论文按被继承的状态分类，分开描述修改对象、候选生成和准入。模型固定，执行反馈驱动候选，获准版本跨运行加载；摘要再提出依赖明确假设的泛化、回归保留及独立验证准入界。\n\n结果与结论：可见正文主要是定义、分类和引用案例，并非新的匹配实验。所给文本虽未标截断，却未包含摘要承诺的理论正文，因此不能核验定理条件；插件成本案例还明确存在两套统计不一致。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，最有用的区分是“发生演化”和“经比较证明改进”。修改解释态、可执行代码与更新算法应分别记账；独立验证数据的理论要求，也不能直接套到反复复用同一验证集的搜索。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18792","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人成功率随时间上升，可能只是多次重试、熟悉初始状态或更大预算，不能直接证明保留了可迁移能力。\n\n方法：SEAR 将写控制程序、在线行动和自主微调纳入同一框架；用空技能库、同总预算短重启和隐藏初始状态评分分离继承与重采样。跨任务只保留代码技能和文字记忆，自动研究产生的权重不延续。\n\n结果与结论：RoboLab 中，一个模型无库成功率46.9%，继承自身库反而退化，改用其他模型的库则达60.6%。经验质量而非有无经验决定收益；硬件上练习成功也高于新场景表现。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，是否值得持续修改，取决于首次成功时间能否落在短尝试预算内，不能只按任务难度决定。封闭评分仍发现资产文件泄露等漏洞，且模型与工具绑定，跨模型排名并非纯模型能力比较。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18484","tldr":"背景与问题：终端代理执行错误后会改变文件和环境，重新从干净状态训练未必教会它恢复；人工注入的错误又可能偏离当前策略真正会犯的错。\n\n方法：先保存学生失败后的环境快照，让强教师生成经验证的恢复示范。在线训练再从当前策略产生的失败状态分叉多次续做，用最终任务验证结果比较恢复行为；近期失败进入队列，随策略变化刷新训练起点。\n\n结果与结论：Terminal-Bench 2.0 的Pass@1 达34.8%，较基座多14.6个百分点；材料称各错误类别恢复率优于普通GRPO。该总增益同时包含教师示范与强化学习，片段缺少完整消融和成本对照。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，失败不只是负样本，也是可复用的训练初始状态。其价值取决于能否准确恢复环境；这训练的是纠错策略，不代表更新算法自身进化，也不能由恢复旧任务直接推断未见故障泛化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18355","tldr":"背景与问题：具身感知、规划与交互定位进步速度不同，固定数据比例会偏离当前短板；语义和动作空间输出共享参数，还可能互相干扰。\n\n方法：评估结果触发能力诊断，修订监督内容与混合比例，经固定规则筛选后训练并再评估；任务条件残差分担异构输出需求。改变的是语料和权重，数据准入规则及学习算法本身不随轮次学习。\n\n结果与结论：材料称十二个基准的各能力汇总领先；更关键的是，最终语料单次训练能匹敌六轮模型，累计后训练量仅五分之一。历史包含重启、跳过检查点和污染修复，不是一条连续增强链。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，证据更支持发现了可复用的数据配方，而非每轮继承权重不可替代。应分开计算数据清洗、预算扩大和反馈适配的贡献；交互定位得分也不能等同真实机器人运动控制能力。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.18097","tldr":"背景与问题：不同图像模型的计数、文字和空间关系短板不同，统一人工训练集未必适配；模型变强后，训练优先级也应重新判断。\n\n方法：预先生成固定的提示—评分准则诊断集，用同一视觉语言评估器诊断与给训练奖励。数据代理据当前失败生成下一轮提示，主要针对弱项，也保留其他能力；强化学习更新图像模型后再次诊断。\n\n结果与结论：Lens 上，保留反馈循环的GenEval 为0.859，去掉后为0.844，但OneIG均值持平；只练难项在后者甚至更高。实验支持部分收益，不能据此宣称反馈循环或混合采样在所有指标上必要。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，自适应训练价值应由跨指标权衡检验，而非自动化程度代替证据。诊断与奖励共用评估器，可能共同放大其盲点；这里更新的是生成器和课程，不是诊断者或教学策略本身。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-18","critique":"今天这批材料有实质推进，但不是“递归加速”已获证明。变化集中在改进信号的校准：RRI 用攻击样本修补奖励，却仍接纳未彻底修好的任务[1]；AdaRSI 以同状态重试区分调用问题与动作缺口，比笼统联合训练更有解释力[2]。MetaExp 将经验学习能力与携带已有经验分开测量[3]，技能漂移审计则揭示原配高分可能掩盖部署脆弱性[4]。Athanor 展示真实算力上的自主后训练，但没有让研究者自身递归变强[5]。单纯交替训练再冠以 RSI，更像增量组织而非新范式。最值得精读 AdaRSI 的干预对照和技能漂移审计的理论前提。本次仅覆盖关键词候选与截断全文，部分比较仍属摘要级判断；尚有26篇待分析论文，并非当天全部候选的总结，也未验证代码或复现实验。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.21040","arxiv:2610.20474","arxiv:2610.21492","arxiv:2610.20845","arxiv:2610.21055"],"backlog":26,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22362","tldr":"背景与问题：物理上有效的仿真场景未必值得训练；只按成功率生成难题，分不清当前短板究竟可学，还是继续投入也无收益。\n\n方法：CoDA 用轨迹诊断提出困难因素，再比较定向扰动与其他因素扰动，验证诊断后存入共享记忆。同一困难生成针对性场景和密集势函数；机器可检查的任务成功条件保持独立，训练后的实际进步指导下一轮生成。\n\n结果与结论：四类操作任务中，同接受环境预算下，分布外成功率为27.6%，高于成功率引导生成的18.1%。这支持超越标量难度的反馈有价值，但不代表总计算成本相等，实机迁移仍未建立。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，关键不只是找失败，而是验证失败原因并测量能否学会。生成引擎靠记忆适配、策略靠梯度学习，两者共演化不等于生成算法自身变强；势函数保留最优策略也依赖标准塑形假设。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22344","tldr":"背景与问题：机器学习实验返回结果前，agent 已作出多轮分析和代码修改；等整段研究结束才训练，既浪费中间反馈，也难把结果归给相关决策。\n\n方法：MLExpert 先从按结果筛选的轨迹学习，再把相邻实验结果之间的决策视为一个窗口，用实验结果及局部进步共同奖励窗口内行为。实验完成即可异步更新，不必等待整个任务结束，并修正采样策略与训练策略的差异。\n\n结果与结论：MLE-Bench Lite 平均获牌率从基座的37.9%升至72.7%；算法优化迁移中也有收益，但部分任务持平或退化。窗口共享奖励并未实现窗口内部的精细归因。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，贡献是让研究者从真实实验节奏学习，而非证明研究流程递归自造。脚手架优化实验中，进一步强化学习同时增加调用量，准确率收益不能全解释为调用效率提高。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.22192","tldr":"背景与问题：终端任务的冗长日志会让按 token 衰减的信用偏离实际决策距离；监督重写改变策略后，旧价值估计也可能失准。通过局部检查更不等于完成整个任务。\n\n方法：Terminal-RSI 交替学习经验证的重写轨迹与强化学习精炼，保留价值网络但在新阶段重新校准；信用按交互轮衰减，并限制失败轨迹的部分奖励，避免局部进展压过严格完成。\n\n结果与结论：长程终端测试的严格完成从0/46增至5/46，说明收益不只体现在过程奖励；但绝对完成率仍低。阶段还同时改变数据、奖励和学习率，现有曲线不能单独归因于价值继承。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，值得借鉴的是把检查覆盖、塑形奖励和终局成功分开报告。这里递归的是训练数据与策略继承，并无证据说明信用分配算法自身学会了如何改进；被丢弃分支也反对单调变强的叙事。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21791","tldr":"背景与问题：改权重、改 harness 或修任务产物各自有效，却未必对应当前瓶颈；固定的干预选择方式也不会自动从过去的改进尝试中受益。\n\n方法：RSIFlow 根据轨迹和环境反馈选择一个组件更新，固定其余组件比较候选。之后把成功、失败及回归提炼为带适用条件的技能和跨组件原则，修改元 agent 的接口与指令，让下一轮诊断和选择使用这些经验。\n\n结果与结论：六个基准、两种骨干的12种设置中，11种领先所比较基线。材料称消融支持自适应编排和元 harness 演化，但消融表被截断，无法核对独立贡献及完整成本。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，比最终任务分数更关键的是元经验能否在相同预算下改善下一次干预。方法确实改变了改进者的外部状态，但五轮结果尚不能证明持续加速；还应区分任务产物修补与可迁移能力增长。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21646","tldr":"背景与问题：自修改系统希望自动门控既不放过坏更新，也不阻止好更新；但门控必须停机，真正的行为改进却可能依赖无界运行，二者要求并不相容。\n\n方法：论文把 agent 与候选更新表示为程序，分别研究判断单次更新和从提案中寻找改进。利用自指构造证明普遍可靠且完备的停机程序不存在，再限制评估时域与提案数量，恢复相对于有界分数的可判定保证。\n\n结果与结论：可见证明支持认证器的不可能性；材料还给出搜索及随机门控的对应结果，并构造代理每轮上升、真实目标反而下降的更新链。这不是现实系统失败率的测量。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，工程意义是声明保证究竟针对哪个有限目标，而非宣布自改进不可行。经典不可判定性不能替代统计审计；有限测试恢复的正确性也不能自动覆盖未测输入和长期目标。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21492","tldr":"背景与问题：会解任务不等于会从任务中积累经验；独立任务训练难以告诉模型哪些知识应跨回合保留，部署时加记忆甚至可能使表现下降。\n\n方法：MetaExp 构造共享工具或潜在流程、但具体答案不能直接复用的任务族，用连续求解和反馈后修订技能的轨迹训练模型。测试时参数冻结、经验库清空，从新分布逐步积累技能，再在不参与更新的固定目标集测量收益。训练反馈以执行检查为主，模型复核失败项。\n\n结果与结论：SpreadsheetBench 中经验积累带来8.5分增长，匹配基座在同协议下反降2.2分；排除相关训练领域后仍有收益，支持经验学习不只是携带目标领域知识。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，较有力的变化是把初始解题水平与经验带来的增量拆开。训练过滤仍主要确认当前任务成功，尚未直接验证每次技能修改能改善后续任务；经验积累也不等于更新算法持续递归增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21055","tldr":"背景与问题：自主后训练不仅要提出配方，还要完成耗时且易失败的 GPU 实验，同时防止开发集搜索和数据污染冒充通用能力增长。\n\n方法：Athanor 将作业、数据去污染和固定评估做成服务，把研究记录与模型谱系持久化；四个固定前沿 agent 自选数据、算法和模型组合，训练另一个基础模型。最终隐藏套件不向研究者开放，也不允许调用外部教师模型。\n\n结果与结论：104小时活动后，隐藏套件均分为48.2，官方指令版为47.9，支持接近其平均水平，而非可靠超越。论文区分活动期间协议与事后统一重测，结果不能混为同一条曲线。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，这说明低摩擦执行设施能支撑已知方法的自主重组，但尚无基础设施消融证明它是决定性瓶颈。单次活动也未显示研究者自身变强，运营者仍承担节点恢复等基础设施职责。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.21040","tldr":"背景与问题：开放式专家任务缺少答案键，模型自写评分准则容易奖励关键词覆盖而非实质内容；求解器会把这些漏洞放大成训练方向。\n\n方法：RRI 从检索资料生成任务与准则，先写故意钻评分漏洞的答案，再与同一模型不看准则写出的诚实答案比较，由模型 judge 评分并指导修补。漏洞还改写未来任务和准则的生成指令，求解器用修补后的奖励学习。\n\n结果与结论：9B 设置相对只生成任务的基线提高10.9分，但相对已共演化任务与奖励的基线，攻击修补额外贡献为2.7分。修补次数受限，仍能被攻破的任务也进入训练，不能称为可靠奖励认证。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，主张应落在减少已发现的可利用性，而非无参考地建立真值。诚实答案和 judge 仍可能共享错误；专业基准收益不代表临床有效性，后续应独立测量修补后的排序可靠性。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20845","tldr":"背景与问题：技能—策略共演化通常只测最终配对；部署后技能库比权重更新更频繁，原配高分可能掩盖对特定措辞和内容的依赖。\n\n方法：论文固定任务和策略，在固定检索下分别改写技能措辞、删除必要步骤或注入误导，并另测增删技能与撤库。沿训练检查点追踪敏感性，再以任务成功、语义一致性和抗损坏性审计交付系统；语义保持改写另经模型及部分人工检查。\n\n结果与结论：四种方法、六种设置中，所测最差成功率比原配低5—13个百分点；五种设置的内容漂移敏感性随训练增加。理论依赖理想选择与候选覆盖，不意味着任意共演化必然退化。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，共演化应优化技能变化下的可靠使用，而非只优化原配峰值。意义保持改写也会造成损失，说明问题不全是技能变坏；但所测最差值不是所有部署变化的全局最坏保证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20809","tldr":"背景与问题：固定小型领域语言只能回答已有算子可组合的问题；让 agent 自写新算子又会引入计算错误，运行成功或模型自信不足以决定保留。\n\n方法：冻结模型先用独立表达式的一致结果扩展问题覆盖，再针对反复出现的能力缺口生成算子。新算子需通过第二实现的差分测试和基于可信原语的守恒关系检查，获准后进入后续组合；解释器与准入规则保持固定。\n\n结果与结论：独立参考条件下，门控拒绝全部138个错误变体；人为让两实现共享错误时仍会漏放。团队盲评中仅89%的问题表达式忠实于问题，说明算得一致不代表理解正确。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，可信扩展需要同时检查执行关系与问题语义。无 oracle 指在线准入不看答案键，不代表实验没有外部金标准；有限输入上的一致性也不是所有输入正确的形式证明。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20474","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人子步骤失败可能是调用姿态或指令不当，也可能是执行器不会所需动作；直接微调所有失败既浪费数据，也可能损坏原本可用的能力。\n\n方法：AdaRSI 先修 harness，再从保存状态重试不同调用方式，只为仍不可靠的子步骤自采示范并微调。示范来自成功 rollout 或读取特权状态的脚本；训练起点取自实际到达状态，新策略经比较后仅在受益位置推荐使用。\n\n结果与结论：未见组合任务中，相对 harness-only 的9.9%，完整系统达到13.8%。同预算下只挑最低成功率步骤训练没有额外收益，支持训练状态与归因的重要性；结果限于仿真及单一执行器。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，harness 不只是廉价替代品，还决定训练数据来自哪些状态。保存状态重试提供受控干预，但有限重试找不到有效调用，并不严格证明动作不可实现；跨任务经验也尚未独立证明调度能力递归增强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20431","tldr":"背景与问题：科学实验失败不说明假设错还是实现错；按整体得分淘汰程序，还会丢掉对其他研究分支有用的局部组件。\n\n方法：SwarmRSI 将假设、程序、执行证据与未解决需求写入共享图，用其他分支反馈决定改研究方向还是修实现。保留假设可迁到另一程序上验证，互补组件也可重组；每次执行及评分结果进入下一轮继承状态。\n\n结果与结论：NatureBench 上删除程序修订后，匹配既有最佳结果的比例从44.4%降至31.1%，支持实现修复有贡献。跨任务经验结果仍受源任务数量混淆，生物学家复用程序不等于复现整套方法。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，负结果应保留可复用结构，而非只有一个失败标签。但重组后得分上升不能证明原科学假设成立；固定搜索规则下状态越来越丰富，也不能直接当作改进算法自身递归变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20312","tldr":"背景与问题：空间任务只能看到部分环境，答错可能来自看错、探索不够或规划失误；不区分原因就总结经验，容易固化错误策略。\n\n方法：HiMeco 在执行结束后利用轨迹、答案真值与特权仿真信息诊断三类问题，比较多次尝试并提炼适用策略。程序片段抽象成参数化技能后，经证据合同和实际调用验证再保留；模型冻结，记忆只在轮间更新。\n\n结果与结论：材料称其在 ESI-Bench 领先，但结果表和关键消融未提供。EmbSpatial-Bench 的3.94个百分点收益发生在没有演化时，不能据此证明记忆更新有效。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，应优先核查去掉分类诊断后是否仍能取得同样收益，而非接受脑机制类比。诊断分数不是校准概率，离线特权信息也是重要监督来源；推广到无真值或真实机器人反馈时，归因可靠性尚未确定。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20294","tldr":"背景与问题：改变策略状态或写入记忆，只能说明发生适配；要证明递归改进，还须显示当前适配规则参与产生更好的继任规则，并由后者继续承担同一角色。\n\n方法：MMLA-RSI 分别规定数值更新器和记忆管理器的继任流程：前者训练提出后继的策略，后者选择该过程能读取的记录。候选锁定后由独立评估器准入，固定解释器和可信提交器限制可改范围，并记录更新先于新尝试的证据。\n\n结果与结论：现有组件研究有正有负：程序选择受益，连续集成回放保留状态却增加损失，SQL 未证实额外在线收益。论文明确表示，有益递归链及发现效率尚未评估。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，其价值在于把功能参与、任务收益和搜索效率分开。固定随机带下输出改变也不必然证明动作分布改变；这些证据要求比组件增益更接近真正递归主张，但目前仍是待验证方案。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.20665","tldr":"背景与问题：游戏在推理期间继续运行时，正确动作也可能来得太晚；暂停评测会掩盖这一点，在线调用更强教师反而可能破坏控制。\n\n方法：TORSI 让快学生独立行动，慢教师在回合之间读取失败，从保存状态练习替代动作，再让学生按真实延迟检验指导。只有在独立验证任务上改善的指导才替换旧版，下一轮处理更新后的残余失败，双方权重和行动接口不变。\n\n结果与结论：两轮后按游戏分别选出的指导，使测试平均进度分从13.51升至24.19；这不是统一采用第二轮候选的结果。消融显示仅写指导或缺少任一侧练习均不足以取得完整收益。\n\nInsights：编辑判断，慢推理适合用于控制间隙的学习，而非每次动作决策。证据限于文本状态接口、六类游戏和两轮，进度分不等于通关率；这里变强的是指导，不是教师或教学算法自身。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-17","critique":"本次巡检没有待分析的新材料，因此没有新增已核实的研究进展。此前的判断保留在论文库中。","source_ids":[],"backlog":0,"papers":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16","critique":"今天这批材料有实质变化，但主要是改进机制与证据标准的细化，尚不足以确立新范式。LoopOPD 把额外循环计算变成中间循环的密集监督，并用共享参数让更新后的终端循环继续提供反馈；关键证据是数学推理对照，但结论仍限于 Ouro-Thinking 及作者实验。[1] 理论论文严格区分搜索效率、支持接口与验证边界的变化，说明分数上涨不等于正确任务范围扩大；它提供的是有条件的形式化框架，不是现实系统验证。[2] RSI-Forge 扩大研究环境供给并测试固定权重下的工件迭代，但专家对捷径抵抗、论文忠实度和任务饱和度更谨慎；这支持其作为评测基础设施，而非改进器递归变强的证据。[3] 今日最值得精读的是赢家诅咒研究：预注册对照量化了复用小型评测集造成的收益高估，也发现所测接受规则未稳定胜过贪心策略；这直接影响如何解释 RSI 实验结果。[4] 当前判断基于四篇所给全文片段，没有独立复现，不能外推为领域整体结论。本次 arXiv 检索未能连接，因此这是已有论文库的巡检点评，并非当天全部候选论文的总结；目前没有待分析论文积压。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.10623","arxiv:2610.10611","arxiv:2610.09426","arxiv:2610.09239"],"backlog":0,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10623","tldr":"背景与问题：LoopLM 用共享参数反复计算，却难以把稀疏的终局奖励直接分配给中间循环；外部教师可能不可得，带特权信息的自蒸馏又会造成师生上下文不匹配。\n\n方法：LoopOPD 让中间循环在自身生成的轨迹上匹配终端循环的 token 分布，将额外循环计算变成密集监督。D-LoopOPD 每步改用当前终端循环作教师；学生更新共享参数后，终端教师也随之改变，并在后续步骤继续提供监督。\n\n结果与结论：在 Ouro-Thinking 上，作者报告 LoopOPD 改善数学推理，动态教师进一步优于冻结教师；全文片段给出 Ouro-2.6B-Thinking 的 AIME 2024 Avg@16 从 62.08 升至 71.67，并称跨循环深度均有改善。跨任务收益限于数学训练后的指定推理和代码基准。\n\nInsights：这里值得检验的不是“自蒸馏是否有效”，而是共享参数是否能把中间循环的学习稳定传回终端策略；论文的局部改进定理也要求梯度对齐等条件。因此，机制成立依赖特定更新几何，不能推成共享参数更新普遍有益。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10611","tldr":"背景与问题：成功率上升可能来自搜索更久、获得更多支持或改变检查器；单看分数无法判断系统只是更容易找到已有解，还是扩展了可接受的正确任务范围。\n\n方法：论文将系统阶段表示为有界交互、支持接口、验证协议与终端检查器，分别定义默认支持下的可达范围和接口许可支持下的范围。它证明独立多数放大保留这两种范围，而随机带上任一次通过可能错误接纳输出；另为自修改和候选选择规定错误预算。\n\n结果与结论：在共同可靠解释器和固定验证协议等条件下，有界递归自修改仍处于同一验证类；有限 XOR 合成例区分搜索成功率提高与接受语言改变。这是条件性理论结果，不是现实 agent 的经验检验。\n\nInsights：该框架把“性能更好”拆成搜索、接口和验证语义三种可分别核查的变化；但其保证依赖明确的可靠性合同，不能直接认证只有经验准确率的学习型评估器。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09426","tldr":"背景与问题：研究型 RSI 需要有挑战的任务、可靠评估和可比较基线，但逐领域依赖专家设计限制了规模；自动生成又可能带来捷径、失真或不可解任务。\n\n方法：RSI-Forge 将任务构建、论文方法复现和环境审查分配给不同角色，分别产出可执行任务与评估器、独立基线，并检查说明和评分是否对应。随后固定模型权重，让 agent 继承先前代码和笔记，检验环境是否支持连续修改。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告构建 210 个、覆盖 18 个领域的环境，其中 90 个经领域专家审阅；在 120 个环境的三次尝试中，至少一个模型在首轮后有所改善的环境占 84%，68 个环境超过复现方法基线。专家对捷径抵抗、来源忠实度及单一想法能否耗尽任务更为审慎。\n\nInsights：环境生成的价值不只是扩充题量，还在于提供可复现基线和分工审查；但专家指出的质量缺口与已观察到的评估材料访问风险，说明环境数量及分数不能单独证明测量可靠。固定权重结果也不代表改进器本身变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09239","tldr":"背景与问题：自改进系统常在小评测集上提出多个修改，再保留分数最高者；被选分数会受选择噪声抬高，重复使用同一集合还会改变后续比较的基线。\n\n方法：论文把保留候选视为相关误差下的噪声选择，并用独立留出集估计真实收益。作者比较多种接受门槛与确认程序，再以预注册实验检验这些规则是否改善完整运行，而非只看单次决策。\n\n结果与结论：预注册研究中，16 项选择集上的贪心循环最终选择分数比留出准确率高 13–20 个百分点；256 项时差距缩至 1–5 点。测试的接受规则在完整运行中没有稳定胜过贪心策略；另用未参与选择的 64 项评分可校正平均偏差，但单次估计仍约有 6 点误差。证据覆盖特定指令改写任务及 GEPA、MIPROv2 验证分数检查。\n\nInsights：结果把研究重点从设计更复杂的接受规则，转向独立报告留出收益和不确定性；依据是接受规则未稳定改善整轮结果，而扩大选择集可缩小高估。它不说明自改进普遍无效，只说明复用评测集上的分数不足以独立证明收益。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-15","critique":"今天这批材料有实质变化，但主要是把 RSI 闭环做得更可选择、更可控，尚未证明自我改进能力本身递归增强。SGUID 按蒸馏期间实际产生的有效信号筛技能，而非把检索相关性当训练价值；研究世界模型则显示，历史实验记录可帮助排序未执行干预，跨环境复用尤其值得关注 [1][2]。ReSI 把红队发现、训练配方搜索和能力保留门控接成多轮安全更新，但论文说明搜索程序本身固定，支持的是目标模型迭代，不是改进机制递归进化 [3]。反向证据也直接：DataSense-Bench 中数据选择与排序仍不稳定，说明会分析数据不等于能预测训练收益 [4]；EvoAlloc 的预算收益来自特定程序搜索基准，不能外推为普遍优势 [5]。本次只处理已有论文库，仍有待分析论文；虽有部分全文片段，判断仍主要受摘要及截断材料限制，作者实验均非独立复现。最值得精读 [2]：其大规模实验记录和跨环境选择设置，为检验经验能否减少昂贵试错提供了具体证据，也值得审视环境覆盖、预测不确定性与多轮稳健性。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.12367","arxiv:2610.12235","arxiv:2610.12233","arxiv:2610.12190","arxiv:2610.12086"],"backlog":4,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12367","tldr":"背景与问题：推理时检索到的技能未必能教会当前模型；论文报告，不到四分之一的检索技能提供有用蒸馏信号，因此语义相关性不足以代表训练价值。\n\n方法：SGUID 观察技能条件教师在学生 rollout 上产生的、与验证器一致的学习信号，只保留训练早晚阶段都持续有效的技能。精简技能蒸馏更新模型后，再从新模型 rollout 整理候选技能并筛选下一轮，形成模型与技能库的反馈闭环。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告，仅蒸馏 6 个技能在四个模型中的多数模型上可匹敌或超过全库；第二轮选出 3 个新技能，Qwen3-8B 的均值由 64.3% 升至 66.3%。结果限于数学推理基准，是作者实验而非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示蒸馏瓶颈可能在监督信号筛选而非技能数量；依据是少量持续有效技能的结果，以及无筛选更新出现退化的报告。该结论仍受任务与验证器范围约束，不能外推到开放任务或缺少可靠验证器的场景。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12235","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 能提出实验，却难以在预算有限时判断哪些干预值得执行；仅凭先验推理预测效果，也容易忽略模型、配方和环境差异。\n\n方法：研究世界模型接收环境、候选干预和既往实验记录，预测潜在收益并排序。被选实验执行后形成新记录，可供后续预测复用；因此闭环改善的是实验选择质量，不是本文已证明的模型参数递归训练。\n\n结果与结论：作者汇集九个环境的 2,653 条实验记录。同环境经验提高未见干预的排序相关性，跨环境经验也改善选择；在固定多轮选择预算下，作者报告经验增强的预测器取得更高最佳收益。这些是作者实验，覆盖范围受现有环境与记录限制。\n\nInsights：这提示稀缺实验预算下，积累可迁移的结果记录可能比单纯更换更强模型或增加推理量更关键；依据是跨环境预测和消融结果。边界在于迁移仍依赖目标环境描述与来源覆盖，预测排序也不能替代实际执行和不确定性估计。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12233","tldr":"背景与问题：模型持续更新会使旧安全对齐失效，新红队方法又不断揭示未见漏洞；只针对已知攻击训练，可能修补漏洞却损害能力或无法泛化。\n\n方法：ReSI 每轮攻击当前模型、生成训练配方候选并通过试验筛选，再以安全增益和能力保留门控晋级模型。新模型进入下一轮红队评估，反馈重新驱动配方搜索，形成有明确保留条件的安全更新循环。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告四种稠密及 MoE 模型在多项安全评估上改善，并称 X-Teaming 平均攻击成功率由 86.01% 降至 31.45%，同时大体保留一般能力。结果来自作者实验，外推范围受攻击集、训练预算和轮数限制。\n\nInsights：这提示保留门控不应只看目标安全指标，也需限制能力回归；未见攻击评估则是检验安全泛化的依据。由于搜索流程本身固定，现有证据支持迭代安全改进，不足以证明改进机制也在递归变强。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12190","tldr":"背景与问题：模型能看数据、写分析代码，不代表能判断哪些样本真正有利于训练；数据表面质量、损失或轨迹成功与特定模型的学习收益并非一一对应。\n\n方法：DataSense-Bench 让 agent 在不能训练模型或查看测试题的条件下选择并排序数据子集，随后用固定流程训练同一基座并测量结果，将事前判断与事后训练结果对照。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告相对随机选择的收益有限，代理对所选数据组的排序也不可靠，且跨终端任务与工具使用任务不稳定。材料支持这是一项能力审计，不支持模型已具备可靠数据科学家能力；范围限于两类轨迹任务和小模型微调。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 的数据选择环节可能是瓶颈，必须用训练后的真实结果验证预测，而不能把合理分析过程当作有效信号。依据是排序及跨任务稳定性不足；这不证明所有数据选择方法都无效，也不涵盖在线训练并持续校准选择器的闭环。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12086","tldr":"背景与问题：程序演化的完整评估成本高，固定分配规则可能把预算花在低价值候选上；更深一层的问题是，被跳过的候选没有结果，分配器会因自己的选择而看不到错误。\n\n方法：EvoAlloc 把评估资源分配策略本身设为可修订对象，从搜索与分配结果提炼经验；偶尔完整评估被拒候选，补上反事实反馈，再据共同验证结果决定是否采用新策略。\n\n结果与结论：作者在编码及 agent-harness 优化基准报告，达到基线表现所需完整评估减少 59–82%，同预算下最终表现高 8.7–12.0%。消融支持策略演化和反事实探索的贡献，但结论限于所测搜索任务与预算。\n\nInsights：这提示自适应资源管理的关键不只是更聪明地筛选，还要主动测量被筛选机制隐藏的失败；依据是反事实反馈设计及消融。其收益是否转移到昂贵实验、非程序搜索或不同预算制度，现有材料尚不能确认。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11959","tldr":"背景与问题：复杂 agent 任务的强化学习受限于探索环境、长程奖励信号及大规模 rollout 基础设施；扩大算力也带来稳定训练与奖励投机风险。\n\n方法：报告扩大 RL 批量与吞吐、丰富环境和 harness，并增加 grader 计算以提供组间细粒度反馈；同时采用稳定性措施应对大规模训练中的路由变化与奖励投机。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称模型在多个领域基准随训练推进而持续提升，并计划开放训练动态、环境和框架。摘要没有提供足以判断相对基线、总成本或关键消融的完整证据，也未展示改进方法自身递归更新。\n\nInsights：这提示规模化 RL 的有效性取决于环境与奖励信号质量，不是算力单变量问题；依据是论文对 grader、环境多样性及稳定性的共同强调。就 RSI 范围而言，这更像推动模型能力的训练报告，而非已证实的自我改进闭环。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12536","tldr":"背景与问题：可执行控制策略可以用回报自动评估，但搜索集上保留高分程序并不保证新候选变好，也不保证收益迁移到新 episode。\n\n方法：EliteTable 将高分解保存在固定容量表中，用它们指导新程序生成、编辑和重组；候选经执行评估后再与精英竞争，留出回报不参与搜索决策。\n\n结果与结论：作者在六个 Gymnasium 任务上报告候选分数中位数均随代数上升，但留出端点仅四个任务的十次搜索全部改善；Acrobot 有六次下降且配对中位变化为负。作者承认仍需基线比较与消融，不能据此判断相对性能。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 证据应区分精英保留带来的搜索分数单调性与真正可迁移的能力变化；依据是 Acrobot 的搜索与留出结果分化。现有材料仅支持特定程序搜索的初步观察，不足以主张算法优势。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11803","tldr":"背景与问题：当数据生成分布和符号辅助信号也随学习过程变化时，训练目标不再固定；传统稳定性分析可能无法覆盖这种共同演变。\n\n方法：PRAXIS 将生成器、学习器及符号档案建模为耦合动态过程，并以受约束更新控制分布漂移、按效用调整档案权重，再分析学习器在变化目标下的稳定性。\n\n结果与结论：摘要称给出目标漂移界、档案相对固定比较对象的抑制性质及随机梯度平均驻点保证，并报告三类任务实验与理论机制相符。具体实验幅度和理论条件在实际任务中的适用范围，材料不足以确认。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 理论不能只分析模型参数更新，还应把数据分布和外部符号信号的漂移纳入稳定性条件；这是由其联合建模提出的启发，不等于已证明这些保证覆盖大语言模型或开放式自我改进。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11655","tldr":"背景与问题：长程 agent 失败可能来自工具阻塞、循环或步数耗尽，也可能是已交付方案本身质量差；笼统加权或改 harness，难以知道该动运行时还是模型权重。\n\n方法：论文按失败轨迹的首个触发信号区分过程故障与内容故障，先演化 harness 修复执行问题，再用演化轨迹训练 LoRA，测试哪些收益能脱离运行时内化到权重。作者还用 shuffled-answer placebo 和 fresh anchor 控制轨迹价值与选择噪声。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 DeepPlanning 报告 harness 与 adapter 对不同模型规模存在互补或替代关系，并在 WebArena-Lite 观察到迁移；该场景的增益来自运行时所见信息，adapter 未再增加收益。材料也揭示评分噪声、转换器偏差与任务范围等局限；非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示选择干预对象前应先分解失败原因，并进一步判断 harness 改变的是模型写出的内容还是可见信息；依据是两任务的 adapter 结果差异。该诊断规则来自有限基准，失败标签阈值与评估器也会影响归因，尚非普遍定律。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11345","tldr":"背景与问题：静态任务集会随学习者变强而变得过易，远超能力的题目又难以提供有效反馈；只定期刷新数据，仍可能让合成器与推理器各自优化、反馈脱节。\n\n方法：SynCo 让合成器根据推理器能力与任务覆盖生成可验证问题，推理器多次作答；正确性更新推理器，任务质量、可靠性及由实际作答结果估计的可教性更新合成器，之后两者共同影响下一轮课程。\n\n结果与结论：作者在八个数学基准报告优于多类合成数据基线，且多数收益来自先前未解问题；全文片段还报告，相较冻结合成器，联合训练仅略增有效训练任务比例，计算量相近。结果来自作者实验，任务范围主要为数学推理。\n\nInsights：这提示任务价值不应仅靠预估难度，而应由当前学习者的实际交互结果校准；依据是任务可教性信号及合成器对照。反馈依赖题目检查器和学习者自身行为，能否扩展到开放任务与更长训练仍未证实。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10498","tldr":"背景与问题：机器人微调需要昂贵交互数据；仅反复试错修改代码和技能，可能重复探索相近方向，也难判断两者组合是否真的互补。\n\n方法：EmbodiedRSI 将竞争性代码、技能假设与证据存入图中，按预期信息价值选择能区分假设的物理试验；结果驱动代码—技能联合更新，慢速记忆模块再根据后续改进价值学习保留哪些经验。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告 RoboCasa365、LIBERO-Pro 上的成功率高于所列基线，并称从模拟到真实机器人零样本迁移。摘要给出若干比例，但未提供完整任务覆盖、预算和实地重复次数；这是作者报告而非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示昂贵交互应被视为辨别竞争解释的实验，而非单纯收集更多轨迹；依据是信息价值选试验的机制。结论边界在于假设质量、模拟到现实差异及试验预算，尚不能推断长期自主部署会持续改进。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10426","tldr":"背景与问题：模型和 harness 交替变化时，轨迹的训练价值取决于其生成时的运行时；把不同 harness 的成功轨迹混在回放池里，可能让模型学到部署时不适用的操作程序。\n\n方法：CoTrace 将失败证据用于 harness 合成，只把已验证且与当前采用 harness 匹配的轨迹用于 SFT，或在同一运行时下生成新 RL 交互；分别固定另一组件评估候选，以避免把增益归错对象。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 Tmax promotion split 报告 Qwen3.5-9B 从 78 个解题任务升至 88（SFT）或 90（在线 RL）；紧凑匹配语料在较低计算下比跨 sibling harness 混合的大语料更稳定。外部基准结果也显示运行时兼容性影响迁移。均为作者实验。\n\nInsights：这提示数据规模不是联合演化的唯一瓶颈，轨迹来源与部署 runtime 的一致性可能决定数据是否可学；依据是匹配与混合语料的对照。结论受任务集、晋级划分和所测 harness 限制，长期运行时变化及独立复现仍待验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10310","tldr":"背景与问题：研究 agent 若每次都需重建训练、推理和评测基础设施，预算会耗在工程准备；只开放单一组件的基准又难检验数据、权重与 harness 的交互。\n\n方法：RSIGym 将训练、推理、rollout、评测和沙箱封装为服务，并统一预算与权限；设置分轨与联合轨道，让 agent 在约束下提出、评估并选择系统修改。\n\n结果与结论：作者比较六个研究模型，报告 Opus 5 在五个基准的 RSI-Index 最高，并给出 SWE-bench Verified、AIME 的提升。关键限制是论文明确承认，所得系统是否改善后续研究循环尚未评估；因此分数表示预算内目标系统改进，不等同递归能力增强。\n\nInsights：这提示 RSI 基准应把基础设施复用、预算审计与跨轮继承作为实验条件，同时区分“改进目标系统”和“改进产生改进的过程”。该区分来自论文的范围声明；平台可支持后续研究，但当前结果不能证明递归进展。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.10120","tldr":"背景与问题：长程互动只有稀疏终局奖励，过程奖励虽更密集，却可能在策略变化后继续优化已不再是瓶颈的行为；频繁缺陷也不必然是失败原因。\n\n方法：RewardWeaver 从低结果轨迹中回溯归因，聚合反复出现且由策略控制的能力瓶颈，动态选择下一阶段过程奖励；已纳入能力的 Rubric 语义保持固定，新能力只有通过独立验证程序才可加入。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告在社交互动、议价与销售任务上优于所比较方法，并以消融支持动态分配、失败归因和语义稳定的重要性。摘要未给效果量、预算或跨模型细节，不能据此判断实际优势幅度。\n\nInsights：这提示过程奖励的关键不是不断改写评分标准，而是稳定定义能力后，随失败瓶颈变化重新分配训练信用；依据是方法对语义与当前相关性的区分。失败归因和 Rubric 评估仍可能有偏，跨领域及独立验证尚不足。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.09856","tldr":"背景与问题：依赖当前策略自一致性的训练，在采样答案完全一致时相对优势消失；课程生成若只追求分歧，也无法知道题目是否真的有学习价值。\n\n方法：AnchorLoop 保留上一轮 Executor 作为冻结参考，在求解训练中比较当前答案与当前、历史多数答案；在课程训练中以两组采样一致率差异塑造任务奖励。后者只是选择代理，因为该阶段两模型参数相同，不能当作版本进步或正确性证据。\n\n结果与结论：作者在 13 个推理基准报告较 Agent0 有数学和一般推理增益，并称后续迭代仍改善，而未锚定基线趋于停滞。结果为作者实验；摘要未详列预算和各任务方差。\n\nInsights：这提示历史参照可补充当前自一致性反馈，但参照的解释必须依阶段区分；依据是作者对课程信号局限的明确界定。锚点并不自动提供真值，也不能解决完全共识时优势仍为零的问题，故泛化和抗共同错误能力仍待验证。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-14","critique":"本批更有价值的推进，是把“如何改进”拆成可检验的信号与闭环。Marvo 用工具的边际收益构造学习信号，但长轮次退化提醒我们：自生成信号未必越迭代越可靠。[1] Harness² 连接任务内行为对比与跨任务经验积累，AutoEnvScaling 把环境生成纳入训练，值得看的是反馈如何塑造下一轮改进。[3][4] EvoBelief 强调可证伪世界模型，Genesis Accounting 尝试审计新机制生成；后者仍有人工触发、盲测零计数，不能当作自主发明的证据。[5][2] 建议优先精读 Harness²，再看 Marvo 的信号失效分析。这些是作者基于所给摘要或全文片段报告的结果，历史基线有限，仍有待分析论文；不同任务和预算下的收益不能直接横比，也不等于独立复现。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.15084","arxiv:2610.14843","arxiv:2610.14224","arxiv:2610.14163","arxiv:2610.12789"],"backlog":19,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.15084","tldr":"背景与问题：视觉工具调用训练常依赖昂贵的标注问答或专家演示；仅按不确定性出题，也不能保证工具确实有用。方法：challenger 从无标注图像造题，solver 通过强化学习作答；solver 有无工具时的表现差作为出题反馈，使课程追踪工具的实际边际收益。结果与结论：作者报告覆盖 11,691 题的多基准评估中，Qwen2.5-VL-7B 平均准确率提高 7.1%；所给全文片段还报告八轮扩展中题目质量与表现后期下降。Insights：这提示课程信号应对准待学能力的边际贡献，而不是难度本身；依据是工具增益奖励及后期标签质量同步下滑。结论限于所测视觉任务，作者实验未经独立复现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14843","tldr":"背景与问题：性能提升可能来自复用设计者提供的机制，也可能来自系统写出新机制；若不区分来源，RSI 声称难以证伪。方法：预注册区分机制实例与新算子，要求候选通过留出数据证书后才登记，并进入可复用注册表。结果与结论：作者报告氢谱与开普勒两次算子生成；氢谱协议修复循环性漏洞后，未见能级外推相对误差约为 10⁻⁶。盲选考试至今为零，事件触发仍需人工。Insights：这提示 RSI 应分别记录机制来源、验证与复用；依据是协议审计和诚实报告的零 tally。边界明确：结果支持受限语法下的机制生成能力，不证明系统能自主启动或持续进化。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14828","tldr":"背景与问题：办公工作流要求文档、表格和演示文件既正确、可编辑又彼此一致；单一文件类型上的修补成功，不代表形成可复用流程。方法：构建四类办公任务基准，对产物内容、原生结构、公式和跨文件一致性评分，并将反馈集、选择集与最终测试分离，控制初始 harness 与预算。结果与结论：在 GLM 5.3 与共同初始 harness 下，ACE/AHE 域内分别提高 4.90/2.64 分，跨办公任务却只变化 +0.03/-1.72 分。作者据此指出，域内收益不保证协调工作流迁移。Insights：这提示迁移目标应直接进入 RSI 测试，而不能用总体分数替代；依据是单模态与跨文件结果分化。边界是离线办公产物、有限配置及有限方法运行。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14730","tldr":"背景与问题：检索嵌入需要训练数据符合具体领域和相关性标准；人工设计查询、标签与合成指令难以随任务扩展。方法：系统从少量相关查询—文档示例推断任务要求，在小样本试产出上获取诊断反馈并修订共享合成指令，再用改进后的指令大规模生成数据。结果与结论：作者报告覆盖 24 个检索集、15 个领域；六项任务的自改进均提升训练数据效果，其中四项超过人工校准，MS MARCO 数据扩至初始规模 32 倍时性能仍提升。Insights：这提示递归改进对象也可以是产生训练经验的规则，而不只是模型参数；依据是指令修订与下游检索结果相联系。材料未提供独立复现，少量示例依赖、标签质量与长程闭环稳定性仍待验证。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14625","tldr":"背景与问题：RSI 工作涉及不同更新对象、反馈与保留机制，宽泛分类难以揭示设计差异及其交互。方法：论文提出九维设计空间，并从优化、正则化、数据增强、持续学习与进化计算等机制中归纳可能的研究方向，同时梳理在线与离线评测。结果与结论：材料支持其分类框架和研究议程；没有本文系统的递归改进实验或性能结果。Insights：这提示比较 RSI 时可分别追问改什么、谁提出、依据何种反馈保留；这是框架可能提供的分析工具，材料未证明它本身改善系统或研究产出。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14495","tldr":"背景与问题：解释视频既要视觉呈现，也要事实、推导和动画正确；只看像素难定位程序缺陷，偏好评审还可能把展示偏差当成改进。方法：把作品作为可读、可测试的程序记录；复盘将检查发现与修复差异配对，可静态检测的经验编译成带正反例的规则，并回查旧作品；playbook 更新需盲评且经人批准。结果与结论：作者报告一条规则在旧作品中发现四处潜在缺陷；研究也揭示盲评有明显顺序偏差。经验缩短修订循环，但没有形成累积改进或改变 judge。Insights：这提示可执行产物有助于把经验变成可审计检查，但偏好评分不能单独决定记忆保留；依据是回溯发现与位置偏差。证据限于单系统、有限作品和人工门控。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14224","tldr":"背景与问题：开放世界任务往往没有真值 verifier，按单一任务改出的 harness 又未必适用于后续新任务；直接继承任务专用修改还可能放大噪声。方法：先提出编辑并在相同任务和条件下探测行为变化，再据对比证据组合修改；随后从编辑过程提取适用条件与经验，更新未来任务的改进 harness。结果与结论：作者报告单步在多个专业基准和配置上有增益，增加任务级递归预算也带来提升。行为差异可帮助选择编辑，但不等于验证任务正确性。Insights：这提示应分别衡量“当前任务改得怎样”与“下一次是否更会改”；依据是双层循环及跨任务经验设计。证据限于特定基准、模型和预算，尚非独立复现。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14163","tldr":"背景与问题：终端 agent 的强化学习依赖多样且可验证的环境；人工设计限制供给，固定任务池也会随 solver 进步而失去训练价值。方法：proposer 阅读 solver 轨迹，在沙箱终端中编写、运行和修复环境；环境通过有效性与难度校准后入池，solver 的新表现再指导下一轮生成，形成数据飞轮。结果与结论：作者报告相较纯提示生成，有效环境率最高提升 25 倍、单个有效环境成本最高降低 75%；同一模型兼任 proposer 与 solver 时，Terminal-Bench 2.1 提升 12.2 分。Insights：这提示训练经验生成本身可成为 agent 能力的一部分；依据是环境构建与 solver 学习相互反馈。边界是生成者也参与构造测试，仍需审查测试漏洞、长期稳定性与外部分布迁移。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13829","tldr":"背景与问题：保存记忆或在一次任务中成功，不足以证明获得可迁移能力；后续表现可能受携带资源、源任务暴露量和早期执行失败影响。方法：用任务状态图和阶段验证器记录进度，重置目标世界与库存，只让声明的 agent 工件跨任务；在匹配预算下比较相关、不相关、打乱经验与无经验条件。结果与结论：作者报告控制器的直接能力优于规划器变体，但相关经验未显示稳定迁移，微小收益受单个种子影响且区间含零；早期采集、制作瓶颈还会使后续能力未被观察。Insights：这提示具身 RSI 的首要难点是把能力变化与环境状态、执行机会分开归因；依据是严格重置后仍无稳定迁移。结论限于 Minecraft 探针和所测代理，不能外推到所有具身环境。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13285","tldr":"背景与问题：固定蒸馏集会随学生能力变化而变得过易或过难；学生很弱时，单看错误也难判断哪些例子能提供有效监督。方法：先直接蒸馏少量教师推理轨迹建立基础能力，再持续选取学生尚未掌握、专家能可靠解决且题目质量合格的样本；学生更新后重新估计边界并刷新训练数据。结果与结论：作者报告只用 1,000 个训练样本，在 11 个基准上优于静态和动态选择基线；Qwen3.5-4B 在 IMO-AnswerBench 从 62.9 升至 75.3，在 AMO-Bench 从 26.8 升至 46.0。Insights：这提示有效课程信号需同时满足学习者有缺口、监督可学且目标可靠；依据是边界筛选机制和多基准结果。专家与分析器仍提供外部判断，不能称为完全自监督。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.14118","tldr":"背景与问题：Harness agent 的任务空间宽，既有训练常依赖外部强模型造任务或收集轨迹，训练后评估结果又交由人分析，难以持续闭环。方法：系统合成并校验任务，用成功轨迹或强化学习更新模型，再从留出任务 rollout 诊断反复出现的短板，把分析反馈给下一轮任务生成。结果与结论：作者报告 Qwen3.6-27B 在三个基准持续提升；迭代任务转用于 Qwen3.5-4B 与 9B 时，各基准也有增益。摘要未提供具体提升幅度。Insights：这提示闭环的关键不只是生成更多任务，而是把诊断转成合格且针对当前能力的练习；依据是任务合成与能力报告相连。具体泛化范围、预算和长程稳定性仍需更多证据。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13098","tldr":"背景与问题：程序化图形 agent 主要根据最终渲染修订，图像差异难以说明符号编辑是否生效、被覆盖或互相干扰。方法：保留程序、渲染与运行时状态记录，从实际写入构造受限替代程序；重新执行检查指定端点和保持条件，再由常规视觉反馈判断目标相关性。结果与结论：作者报告在 BlenderGym 280 题与 BlenderBench 27 题上优于所比较的 refinement 方法；消融支持执行修订与证据组织的作用，但修复需额外执行。Insights：这提示改进信号的价值取决于能否观察编辑如何影响执行，而非单纯增加迭代；依据是执行修订消融。结论限于程序化 3D 场景，固定生成交互数也不代表总执行成本相同。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13021","tldr":"背景与问题：持续学习研究多限于非具身环境，而常见具身基准也不直接检验既有经验能否迁移到未见任务组合。方法：构造从原子动作、基础家务到未见组合任务的评测，并比较零样本、保留交互轨迹与压缩技能总结。结果与结论：作者报告复杂任务零样本成功率约为 10%，有基础任务经验后可超过 30%；但增加学习样本没有相称的持续收益，ICL 与技能学习也无稳定胜者。Insights：这提示积累经验可能先带来明显收益，之后瓶颈转为提取有效信息，而不是继续增加样本；依据是样本扩张未产生一致增益。任务采用离线状态图，不能直接代表真实在线具身交互。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12855","tldr":"背景与问题：on-policy 自蒸馏可提升总体能力，但训练推进时，先前答对的问题可能变为答错，单看总体分数会掩盖这种退化。方法：作者观察到能力退化伴随隐藏表征簇结构变模糊，提出在自蒸馏中约束簇内紧致与簇间分离，尽量保留已有表征结构。结果与结论：作者报告在多种自蒸馏方法和基准上，RGR 通常减轻能力退化，同时保留能力提升；摘要没有给出具体效果量。Insights：这提示 RSI 评估应同时追踪新能力与旧题回归，而不能只看平均表现。表征几何是作者提出并分析的关联机制，现有材料不足以断言它是各类自改进的普遍因果瓶颈。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12789","tldr":"背景与问题：Agent 即使会执行步骤，也可能因环境动态信念不完整或过时而失败；错误规则还可能传播到其他任务。方法：冻结语言模型，把环境知识存成带证据、适用范围和检验方式的假设。新观察触发验证，独立证据支持后规则才影响规划；反例会缩窄、降级或撤销规则。结果与结论：作者报告在 ALFWorld 中优于匹配的冻结世界模型，在 MiniGrid 中修订过时规则并适应动态变化；在 DiscoveryWorld Reactor Lab 也报告高于所测基线的完成率。Insights：这提示跨任务记忆要有可检验性、范围约束和撤销机制；依据是规则生命周期与漂移实验。证据来自有限模拟环境的作者实验，不能证明真实环境迁移或独立复现。"}]},{"date":"2026-10-13","critique":"这批论文的推进集中在“改进过程如何产生下一轮训练信号”：Evo² 联合优化权重与 harness，MASS 将多智能体轨迹用于递归微调。[2][3] RSI-Anything 与 Memento 3 把世界模型纳入闭环，但后者主要更新外部规则记忆，不能把两者都视为权重自进化。[1][4] 最值得精读的是评估器共演化：退化 grader 仍能带来相近任务表现，说明下游分数不足以认证反馈信号可靠。[5] 真正的瓶颈正在从“会不会更新”转向“更新依据是否可信”。这些是机制推进，尚无完整历史基线、统一预算比较或长期稳定性证据；判断限于所给摘要与全文片段，作者实验不等于独立复现。","source_ids":["arxiv:2610.13912","arxiv:2610.13025","arxiv:2610.12176","arxiv:2610.11794","arxiv:2610.11464"],"backlog":0,"papers":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13912","tldr":"背景与问题：RSI 需要把交互经验转成后续能力，但外部评估昂贵；策略更新还可能改变经验分布，使既有世界模型失准。因此，单独改策略或预测器都不能保证下一轮系统仍可靠。\n\n方法：RSI-Anything 用预测模型预判候选行动结果，帮助选择行动和学习数据；真实反馈再驱动策略或工作流更新，并在可靠性、数据和预算条件满足时调整世界模型。组件检查与策略—模型兼容检查决定哪些更新被保留，获准组合进入下一轮。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告，在固定 coder 的代码修复任务中，成功率从静态 verifier 的 26.3% 经预测筛选升至 29.2%，再经世界模型适配升至 31.2%，测试使用量相近；还报告 GUI、实验规划和反应优化结果。这些是作者实验，不是独立复现；材料不足以确认长期稳定性和广泛泛化。\n\nInsights：这提示瓶颈不只是预测准确度，还包括策略变化后模型是否仍适用，以及如何筛选更新组合；依据是论文提出的耦合更新问题和兼容性保留设计。该机制能否延伸至更广任务，仍需长期及统一预算评估。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.13025","tldr":"背景与问题：自进化 agent 常分别更新模型权重或修改 harness，忽略了二者的反馈关系：权重影响编辑质量，而编辑执行结果也能提供训练经验。分开优化可能无法让系统学会如何持续改进自身。\n\n方法：Evo² 让同一策略担任 harness 修改者和反思者；修改结果及执行反馈用于训练这两个角色。EvoTIDE 从编辑和反思轨迹中恢复可用训练数据，经监督微调与交错策略优化更新共享权重，再由更新后的策略继续搜索 harness。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告三个编码基准上的表现优于所比较的自进化方法，并称演化出的 harness 可迁移到其他任务；摘要给出 Polyglot 与 SWE-bench Verified 的对照分数。论文指出相关工作机制比较不是匹配性能基准，结果也不是独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示 harness 搜索不只是改善执行脚手架，也可能成为训练“改进者”的数据来源；依据是编辑反馈用于角色训练，更新权重又回到后续搜索。是否优于分别优化或其他联合方案，仍需统一预算、消融和多轮稳定性比较。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.12176","tldr":"背景与问题：开放式研究等任务缺少可靠自动评分，结果可能超出人类专家稳定判断的范围；但让单一模型同时求解、评价和改进自身推理，也容易受同一偏见牵制。\n\n方法：MASS 先让模型搜索多智能体工作流，调整角色分工与信息传递，再把这些工作流生成的求解轨迹用于监督微调。更新后的模型重新担任求解者、工作流优化者和评估者，从而把工作流改进产生的数据带入下一轮能力更新。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告在 Qwen3.6-27B 上经过两轮 MASS，四个开放式基准的每输出 token 表现达到基线的 1.2–1.6 倍；多智能体轨迹训练的学生也优于使用更多 token 的单智能体轨迹学生。模型、任务和轮次有限，结果尚非独立复现。\n\nInsights：这提示监督瓶颈可能部分来自组织方式：分工和信息路由可产生比单体长轨迹更有效的训练信号。依据是作者报告的轨迹效率结果；由于优化与评估存在同源性，且只展示有限递归轮次，不能据此断言能在开放任务中持续自我纠错。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11794","tldr":"背景与问题：在陌生环境中，少量观察可能同时支持多个世界模型；它们都能解释已发生的转移，却对未见状态作出不同预测。仅靠回放已观察数据，无法判定哪套规则能正确泛化。\n\n方法：Memento 3 让冻结 LLM 把环境假设写成可修订的自然语言规则手册，再编译为用于预测和规划的代码。新观察造成的预测误差促使规则或实现修订；候选代码需符合规则手册，并精确重现已观察转移，才会被接受并用于后续交互。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告其单模型系统在 ARC-AGI-3 的 25 个公开游戏中通过所有关卡，平均 RHAE 为 100，并在 Pong 的三个不同开局案例中以 21:0 获胜。后者是有限案例；回放验证只覆盖已有转移，不能证明对未见状态的模型正确性。\n\nInsights：这提示递归改进可以发生在外部记忆与可执行模型，而不必更新权重；依据是固定 LLM 下规则—代码闭环仍能改变后续规划。关键边界是观测覆盖：通过历史回放不等于掌握环境规律，需检查探索能否区分相互竞争的假设。"},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2610.11464","tldr":"背景与问题：自改进循环每轮都要判断 agent 是否变好，但开放任务往往没有现成 verifier；手写 rubric 或由相似模型担任 judge，可能共享盲点并诱发奖励投机。更关键的是，训练后的任务分数也未必能证明评分器本身可靠。\n\n方法：论文把 verifier 作为演化对象，由失败聚类生成可检查的细粒度缺陷检测器，再以少量锚点参考和未标注输出共识筛选组合，不按 agent 得分选 grader。之后将演化出的 grader 接入技能改进循环，并用外部锁定评估监测结果。\n\n结果与结论：作者报告 MBPP+ 留出一致性较手写初始组合提高约 0.21；消融移除锚点防护后，grader 退化为始终放行，但技能训练表现仍相近。因此，下游任务得分不足以认证自进化 verifier。结果限于指定任务、锚点和实验设置，报告生成场景也没有金标准。\n\nInsights：这提示验证器需要独立于被优化任务表现的有效性检验；依据是退化 grader 仍能支撑相近技能表现的消融。该发现针对特定任务和锚点规模，不能直接证明锚点方案普遍可靠；应将 verifier 的留出一致性与下游收益分别报告。"}]}],"progress":[{"title":"将预测模型与规则记忆纳入改进闭环","topic":"世界模型与递归改进","description":"RSI-Anything 将预测筛选、反馈更新和策略—模型保留串联；Memento 3 以规则手册和可执行模型构成误差驱动闭环。两篇作者报告了各自特定任务实验，但彼此未比较，不能据此确立共同增益。","kind":"watch","limitations":"实验限于特定代码、GUI、科学规划或公开游戏场景；长期稳定性、未见环境泛化、预算敏感性和统一对照仍待检验。Memento 3 的回放只核验已观察转移；给定材料不足以确认领域级优先性。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.13912","arxiv:2610.11794"]},{"title":"权重与 agent harness 共演化","topic":"权重—harness 联合演化","description":"Evo² 将 harness 编辑及执行反馈用于更新进化策略权重，再以更新权重指导后续搜索；作者报告编码基准与跨任务迁移结果。这是权重与 harness 相互反馈的具体机制，但相关工作比较并非匹配性能基准。","kind":"advance","limitations":"需核对训练与评估预算、组件消融、不同模型和任务上的迁移及多轮稳定性；作者报告不能替代独立复现或统一基准比较。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.13025"]},{"title":"把多智能体协调轨迹转为递归自监督","topic":"多智能体工作流演化","description":"MASS 交替优化多智能体工作流并微调共享模型，使执行轨迹成为自监督信号；更新权重再用于求解、优化和评估。作者报告有限轮次实验与外部评估，但机制差异不等于相对既有方法的匹配性能优势。","kind":"advance","limitations":"证据限于特定基座模型、有限训练轮次和任务集；工作流筛选依赖同源模型反馈，需检验自评偏差、外部评估稳健性、训练预算和更广泛泛化。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12176"]},{"title":"演化评估器并检验锚点防护","topic":"评估器递归改进","description":"论文以锚点一致性而非 agent 得分选择演化 grader；消融显示退化 grader 也可能支撑相近的技能训练表现，提示下游任务分数不能单独证明 verifier 有效。","kind":"advance","limitations":"实验覆盖指定任务、十项锚点和三种子；报告生成缺少金标准，技能侧结果也可能受评估与回滚设置影响。需检验更多任务、锚点规模、预算及长期 grader 漂移。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.11464"]},{"title":"训练经验随当前能力调整","topic":"自适应课程与数据合成","description":"Marvo 以工具有无的表现差生成适配当前能力的视觉问题；BoundaryEvo 先启动弱学生，再按学生—专家能力边界更新蒸馏数据；SYNTRA 迭代合成指令以改善检索训练数据；ClawLoop 将诊断反馈用于后续任务合成。共同变化是让训练经验随学习者状态调整，但各自反馈、任务与更新对象不同，不能视为统一机制已验证。","kind":"advance","limitations":"均为作者报告实验，缺少独立复现和匹配比较；任务分别限于视觉工具调用、推理蒸馏、检索和 harness 训练。长程闭环中的标签质量、错误累积、预算与跨域迁移仍待验证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.15084","arxiv:2610.14730","arxiv:2610.13285","arxiv:2610.14118"]},{"title":"把改进过程纳入后续学习","topic":"Harness 递归演化","description":"Harness² 将任务内编辑的行为对比与跨任务改进经验积累连接；AutoEnvScaling 与 ClawLoop 则把任务或环境生成纳入训练循环。变化在于改进过程本身成为下一轮学习信号，但三者的验证器、角色来源和权重更新方式不同。","kind":"advance","limitations":"基准、预算和任务分布不同，报告增益不可横向比较；开放任务的行为对比不等于真值验证，环境生成还可能受到自建测试与目标偏差影响。多轮稳定性及外部分布迁移证据有限。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.14224","arxiv:2610.14163","arxiv:2610.14118"]},{"title":"把迁移与可归因能力变化单独测量","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"EvoCowork 显示单模态 harness 增益未必迁移到跨文件工作流；MC-EvoBench 未发现相关经验的稳定具身迁移；EmbodiedCLBench 则以组合任务检验经验收益。它们把迁移和能力归因从附加分析提升为 RSI 评测的核心问题。","kind":"watch","limitations":"评测分别限于离线办公产物、Minecraft 和离线具身状态图；模型、任务与方法有限，缺少独立复现。后续需共同控制源任务暴露、训练预算、样本量和目标任务难度。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.14828","arxiv:2610.13829","arxiv:2610.13021"]},{"title":"让改进建立在可核查的环境证据上","topic":"世界模型与递归改进","description":"EvoBelief 用可检验、带范围且可撤销的环境规则改变后续预测；VETR 从执行轨迹提取受约束的程序备选。两者将改进依据从最终分数或偏好判断，推进到更具体的环境状态与执行证据。","kind":"advance","limitations":"任务类型差异大且未直接比较；EvoBelief 限于若干模拟环境，VETR 的保持检查只覆盖已观测运行时性质并增加执行成本。规则泛化和长时稳定性仍待评估。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12789","arxiv:2610.13098"]},{"title":"从任务得分转向机制与反馈审计","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"Genesis Accounting 预注册区分机制复用与新机制生成；Reels-RSI 把可检查经验编译成可回溯规则，并报告偏好 judge 的位置偏差。共同指向 RSI 需要独立于任务得分的审计证据，但现有材料没有证明稳定的自主递归。","kind":"watch","limitations":"Genesis 依赖人工触发和观察者注入语法，盲选 tally 为零；Reels-RSI 有人工审批且为单系统小规模研究。治理指标可能受到 Goodhart 影响，需扩大盲测与独立评估。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.14843","arxiv:2610.14495"]},{"title":"训练信号筛选与任务分布共演化","topic":"自适应训练经验","description":"SGUID 按训练期间持续有效的技能信号压缩蒸馏库；SynCo 联合更新任务合成器与推理器，让实际解题结果改变后续训练分布。两者共同体现训练经验随学习者状态适配，但反馈机制和任务不同，作者实验不构成彼此复现。","kind":"advance","limitations":"SGUID 限于带验证器的数学蒸馏及四个模型；SynCo 限于数学推理任务且依赖任务检查器。均为作者实验，无独立复现或匹配比较；长期训练稳定性、数据质量与跨域迁移仍待检验。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12367","arxiv:2610.11345"]},{"title":"让实验经验改进后续预算决策","topic":"预算受限研究搜索","description":"研究世界模型将历史实验记录用于预测未执行干预并辅助固定预算选择；EvoAlloc 将程序搜索中的评估分配策略纳入经验更新，并用反事实评估补足选择性反馈。两者都把昂贵实验决策作为改进对象，但一个预测干预效果、一个调整评估投入，证据不可直接横比。","kind":"advance","limitations":"均为作者报告，分别依赖有限实验环境与程序搜索基准。跨环境迁移、预测不确定性、不同成本结构下的预算优势及长期稳定性仍待验证；没有独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12235","arxiv:2610.12086"]},{"title":"从失败反馈调整下一轮安全与训练目标","topic":"失败驱动的递归更新","description":"ReSI 将模型更新纳入多轮红队—配方搜索，并以能力保留门控晋级；RewardWeaver 从低结果轨迹归因当前能力瓶颈，调整下一阶段过程奖励。共同变化是让训练配方或目标随失败证据改变，但两者任务和更新对象不同，尚无直接比较。","kind":"advance","limitations":"ReSI 受红队池、模型和安全基准约束；RewardWeaver 摘要未提供完整效果量及成本。失败归因、评估器偏差、长期能力保持和独立复现均是证据缺口。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.12233","arxiv:2610.10120"]},{"title":"将循环计算转化为跨深度监督","topic":"循环语言模型与跨循环蒸馏","description":"LoopOPD 将循环模型的额外计算转化为中间循环在自身轨迹上的密集分布监督；D-LoopOPD 再让共享参数更新后的终端循环继续充当教师。作者报告 Ouro-Thinking 数学推理与跨深度结果改善，并给出局部同时改进的条件分析。这推进了循环深度内部的反馈机制，但不是改进器自身递归进化的证据。","kind":"advance","limitations":"证据限于 Ouro-Thinking 作者实验及指定数据、循环结构和基准；理论结果依赖梯度对齐等条件。缺少独立复现、不同循环架构和统一预算比较；代码与检查点尚待发布。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.10623"]},{"title":"从论文自动构建可执行 RSI 环境","topic":"RSI 研究环境与评测","description":"RSI-Forge 从论文构建可执行研究环境，并用独立复现建立基线；作者在 120 个环境上测试固定权重 agent 继承代码和笔记的多轮改进。它扩展研究环境供给和工件迭代评测，未检验权重或改进器递归进化。","kind":"watch","limitations":"专家对捷径抵抗、论文忠实度和任务饱和度更为审慎；部分环境存在评估材料访问风险。结果限于作者构建的数据集、三次尝试和固定权重；仍需独立审计、预算匹配、长期稳定性与泛化测试。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.09426"]},{"title":"用受控失败诊断决定改哪里、练什么","topic":"失败驱动的递归更新","description":"AdaRSI 将已有诊断后选择 harness 或权重的思路落实到具身子步骤：同状态改变调用方式，确定训练对象及起点，再验证新策略的调用范围。CoDA 则用定向场景与控制扰动验证困难诊断，将其编译为生成程序与训练势函数，并按实际学习进步分配后续生成。二者分别推进干预对象与训练经验的选择，是对既有失败驱动更新主题的补充，不是同一机制的相互复现。","kind":"advance","limitations":"AdaRSI 限于单一执行器和 RoboCasa365 仿真，有限重试不能证明执行器绝对缺能；CoDA 的同环境预算不等于同总算力，真实机器人迁移未建立。诊断、训练和验证都有额外成本，长期稳定性与改进调度自身增强尚无独立证据。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.20474","arxiv:2610.22362","arxiv:2610.11655"]},{"title":"从设计经验库转向训练跨任务经验学习能力","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"MetaExp 用保留共享因素、变化具体实现的任务族训练经验获取和更新行为；在新分布空库起步、冻结权重，并将适配任务与固定目标评测分开。相对已有记忆结构设计和经验迁移评测，变化是训练产生经验的能力，而非预装目标经验；同协议下基座退化而训练模型获益，为这种区分提供直接对照。","kind":"advance","limitations":"证据限于指定大模型、三个下游基准和有限任务流；训练过滤尚未直接按技能更新的未来效用选择，反馈还含模型对失败检查的复核。需核对全部消融、训练预算、顺序敏感性和更长任务流稳定性，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.21492"]},{"title":"将共演化交付后的技能漂移纳入审计","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"技能漂移审计固定策略与检索，改变被使用的技能内容，将共演化原配峰值拆成措辞一致性、抗损坏性和所测最差成功率。它补充既有跨任务迁移审计及 CoTrace 的运行时兼容性问题：不仅任务会变，系统内部被依赖的技能也会变。四种方法六设置的结果显示，原配能力增长可伴随漂移敏感性增加。","kind":"advance","limitations":"理论依赖理想化候选最优选择和覆盖，只保证覆盖改写族内不能改善，并不普遍证明大幅退化。实验证据来自有限内容扰动和训练轨迹，最差值不是全空间保证；更多技能规模、真实版本更新、审计成本和长期鲁棒训练仍需验证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.20845","arxiv:2610.10426"]},{"title":"用已确认攻击修补逐任务奖励及其生成规则","topic":"评估器递归改进","description":"RRI 在已有评估器演化路线之外，加入逐任务评分准则的攻击—修补循环，并让已发现漏洞修改未来生成规则。相对只生成任务的总体增益，和已共演化任务与奖励相比的额外收益，更能检验攻击修补本身。该工作将奖励可利用性作为训练前应测量的对象，但没有把修补视为彻底认证。","kind":"advance","limitations":"判断仍依赖模型生成的诚实答案和 judge，修补两次后仍可被攻击的任务也进入训练。专业基准不能代表真实临床结果，部分跨域样本少；计算预算、长期奖励漂移及独立评估器一致性仍待核验，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.21040","arxiv:2610.11464","arxiv:2610.17609"]},{"title":"在封存评估下展示长时自主通用模型后训练","topic":"RSI 研究环境与评测","description":"Athanor 将已有研究服务平台推进到真实 GPU 上的长时自主后训练活动：固定研究者自选数据、修改算法并组合检查点，隐藏套件检验所得通用模型。相对 RSIGym 的多轨目标系统搜索，本篇给出单个原始基座被自主后训练至接近官方指令版平均水平的具体案例；没有展示研究者自身递归升级。","kind":"advance","limitations":"主要证据为一次104小时、四研究者各一台八卡节点的活动；隐藏集仅覆盖既定能力，略高均分不能证明统计优势。活动中与事后重测协议不同，基础设施和人工运营职责仍存在，缺少服务消融、跨模型重复与预算匹配研究者对照。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.21055","arxiv:2610.10310"]},{"title":"限制反馈暴露并组织可归因的 harness 搜索","topic":"Harness 递归演化","description":"VideoHarness-SRSI 对既有完整轨迹驱动搜索作出具体修正：内容暴露对照显示反馈越丰富，验证—测试差距可能越大；继而限制内容反馈、隔离机制搜索并测试组合，四基准平均留出得分相对基础流程提高6.2%。这补充既有迁移审计，推进点是改变搜索使用证据的方式，而非新增一次验证门控。","kind":"advance","limitations":"作者实验集中于视频理解和固定骨干；主要结果及消融部分被截断，无法完整核对预算、重复次数与分阶段成本。屏蔽内容不消除汇总分数的适应性复用偏差；没有独立复现或改进器持续增强证据。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.19424","arxiv:2603.28052"]},{"title":"将经验继承与重复尝试分开审计","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"SEAR 将既有具身迁移审计扩展至机器人控制代码、多模拟器和真实硬件，以同开发时间的短重启、空技能库及隐藏状态评分，分离持续努力和经验继承。观察到自身技能库可能伤害表现、他人技能库反而有益；Physical RSI 框架进一步要求匹配起点与预算比较新旧改进程序，避免把任务收益当成元级收益。","kind":"advance","limitations":"SEAR 模型与工具配置绑定，部分自动研究设置只有一次运行，真实任务和场景数量有限，封闭评判仍存在信息旁路。Physical RSI 是规范框架，非递归收益实验；没有统一跨论文预算或独立复现，完整共演化仍未实现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.18792","arxiv:2610.18842","arxiv:2610.13829"]},{"title":"把经验混淆和接收者适配纳入记忆维护","topic":"经验迁移","description":"在已有经验学习与迁移主题内，STRATA 提供同系统方向混淆修复的具体证据：分层维护并显式警告相反程序，ScienceWorld 得分由78.7升至96.7。XferAgent 则保留跨代理来源，结合其他代理与本地使用结果校准经验选择。两者分别处理库内负迁移与异构共享，不构成彼此复现，也不替代 MetaExp 对经验学习行为的训练。","kind":"advance","limitations":"STRATA 对比边依赖固定反向操作词表，关键消融表不全；XferAgent 贡献者数量与源任务总暴露同步增加，经验使用结果尚非因果贡献。总预算、长期记忆漂移、任务顺序和开放语义泛化仍需评估，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.19386","arxiv:2610.19581","arxiv:2610.21492"]},{"title":"以固定权限边界支持代理自扩展","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"L3M 将自扩展约束落实到运行时代码：代理可生成后续工具，但类型和能力令牌限制权限，部分核心检查有内核核验的定理；可恢复性及预先限定的影响范围决定审查层级。相对 harness 分类与准入原则，它提供具体实现，尚不能按已验证的多轮自改进收益入账。","kind":"watch","limitations":"关键评测表未提供，约三分之二通过率来自摘要，缺少自扩展独立消融、成本和长期部署证据。保证依赖可信编译、提供者、操作系统等，并非全系统语义安全；局部回滚不能撤回外部影响，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.19591","arxiv:2610.18813"]},{"title":"用当前失败状态与对抗任务刷新训练经验","topic":"失败驱动的递归更新","description":"在已有失败驱动更新主题内，ReTerm 把当前策略的自然失败保留为可恢复训练状态，从同一快照分叉并用任务验证器训练纠错；AgentSafeEvo 则直接更新对抗任务生成者和防御策略，以安全、效用反馈及任务内奖励变化调整训练。两者都让后续训练经验适配当前弱点，但只有后者明确训练经验生成策略，反馈可靠性也不同。","kind":"advance","limitations":"ReTerm 总体收益混合强教师冷启动与在线 RL，完整预算及机制消融未见；快照恢复增加工程成本。AgentSafeEvo 依赖模型安全与效用判断，主结果表缺失，奖励方差可能含评判噪声。均无独立复现、长期稳定性或训练算法自我改写证据。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.18484","arxiv:2610.19422","arxiv:2610.12233"]},{"title":"训练研究提案与验证调度，并用真实结果纠偏","topic":"预算受限研究搜索","description":"在已有研究世界模型与预算决策主题内，LM2LM进一步用预测收益训练提案者，并执行当前策略偏爱的高分方案来纠正反馈高估；SpecRSI则学习后续编辑与检查的净验证收益，用整次搜索结果训练改进者。两者分别改变提案生成与验证调度，不是同一机制的相互复现，也不是仅增加并行尝试。","kind":"advance","limitations":"两篇均为截断全文下的作者实验，主结果及完整预算表未见。LM2LM的33%降低针对数据生成成本，不能当作全流程成本；定向校准的覆盖和长期稳定性未确定。SpecRSI目标成本下降时总成本可略升，跨任务预算优势与改进者迁移仍需独立验证。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.23344","arxiv:2610.16491","arxiv:2610.12235","arxiv:2610.13025"]},{"title":"将反馈质量与回归保持拆成可测试对象","topic":"评估器递归改进","description":"补充已有评估器改进主题：UCoE在固定模型下演化评分程序，以最弱属性对比族筛候选，再控制回答修补与经验准入；TeSearch优化小型可执行回归测试，对核验过的harness改写提升行为变化检出率。前者测试开放任务反馈的辨别力，后者检验行为保持，不能将两类检查统称为真实改进认证。","kind":"advance","limitations":"UCoE多数收益来自当前任务修补，合成属性对比向自然修订的泛化、重复校准集选择偏差及总成本仍待核验。TeSearch限于Python模块及构造的改写池，测试生成成本需摊销，仍有漏检和误拒；没有展示长期自演化收益或稳定性，也没有独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.17609","arxiv:2610.15964","arxiv:2606.09498"]},{"title":"经验正确仍可能不迁移，维护机制需接受独立验收","topic":"RSI 评测与迁移","description":"CFOE将既有迁移审计推进到无成功轨迹、无显式验证反馈的冷启动条件：局部修复不带来稳定留出收益，人工筛出正确经验也不足以消除缺口。CDSE、SpecForge与Darwin-Claw分别提出功能化维护、依赖约束和情境补丁；这些可作为应对缺口的候选机制，但没有在CFOE同协议下比较，不能当作已解决。","kind":"advance","limitations":"CFOE采用骨干特定的失败密集流，成功条件比较又分别采样任务，限制因果解释和普遍化。技能维护工作的完整消融、统一总预算、顺序敏感性与长期稳定性不足；SpecForge依赖参考实现测试，Darwin-Claw的LLM归因不等于因果识别。没有独立复现或跨方法统一迁移对照。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.22984","arxiv:2610.23599","arxiv:2610.15708","arxiv:2610.23574","arxiv:2610.21492","arxiv:2610.13829"]},{"title":"以执行反馈和学习者状态调整训练经验","topic":"自适应训练经验","description":"在自适应训练经验主题内，RSIPO用技能回放相对控制组的收益训练技能生成并校准蒸馏；ECG-RSI把信号有效性、弱点诊断与干预选择分离；HACE用标签验证局部贡献并双向选择训练经验；EAU进一步修改产生互动反馈的用户与环境配置。变化是让经验适配当前学习者，而非仅积累更多数据；各自监督来源和可变组件不同，不能合并为同一共演化机制。","kind":"advance","limitations":"均依赖有限任务和作者实验，未统一控制总算力、验证开销或干预次数。RSIPO的同题回放不直接证明跨任务技能价值；ECG-RSI完整消融与部分结果口径未能核对；HACE蛋白任务只更新预测头；EAU部分基线引用既有成绩。长程稳定性、开放反馈泛化和元更新机制自身增强均未建立。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.15772","arxiv:2610.17718","arxiv:2610.16078","arxiv:2610.16523","arxiv:2610.12367","arxiv:2610.11345"]},{"title":"将记忆写回后的延迟后门纳入轨迹级安全审计","topic":"RSI 可证伪性与治理","description":"EvolvAttack为已有自改进治理主题增加动态威胁证据：预植于权重的后门可在初始记忆检查中休眠，再由普通记忆写回与检索放大。其贡献不是提高自改进能力，而是说明安全状态取决于交互历史；静态权重或空记忆扫描不足以覆盖这种联合激活。","kind":"advance","limitations":"结论受部署前投毒能力、触发器暴露、检索与写回规则限制，不代表良性系统自然形成后门。空记忆训练覆盖改变攻击效果，完整跨设置结果被截断；现实流中的触发频率、审计预算、长期攻击稳定性及防御泛化未充分建立，无独立复现。","paper_ids":["arxiv:2610.15244"]}]};
